window.CET6_LESSONS = [{"id":"cet6_2016_06_1-p1","title":"CET6 2016年06月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2016年06月 第1套","examDate":"2016年06月","year":"2016","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2016-06-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"互动电视广告多年被看好却始终未达预期；Cablevision推出该服务遭遇怀疑，但业界仍寄望它能像Axe广告那样吸引观众，把流向网络的广告费拉回电视。","mainIdeaEn":"Interactive TV advertising, long hyped but never living up to expectations, met skepticism when Cablevision rolled it out; still, the industry hopes it can engage viewers and lure ad dollars back from the Internet.","answerCode":"DCCBA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先没达到预期，再大家有点怀疑，然后电视广告吃亏，接着擅长吸引观众，最后归功新颖广告。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What does Colin Dixon mean by saying \"It's been the year of interactive television advertising for the last ten or twelve years\" (Line 4, Para. 1)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Interactive television advertising will become popular in 10-12 years."},{"label":"B","text":"Interactive television advertising has been under debate for the last decade or so."},{"label":"C","text":"Interactive television advertising is successful when incorporated into situation comedies."},{"label":"D","text":"Interactive television advertising has not achieved the anticipated results."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Interactive television advertising has not achieved the anticipated results.","answerZh":"互动电视广告并未取得预期的效果。","explanation":"这是一道词义猜测题。Colin Dixon的话'It's been the year of interactive television advertising for the last ten or twelve years'意味着互动电视广告被预测将会流行起来已经有十年到十二年的时间，但实际上并没有达到预期的效果。","questionZh":"Colin Dixon 说 \"It's been the year of interactive television advertising for the last ten or twelve years\"(第1段第4行)是什么意思?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What is the public's response to Cablevision's planned interactive TV advertising program?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pretty positive."},{"label":"B","text":"Totally indifferent."},{"label":"C","text":"Somewhat doubtful."},{"label":"D","text":"Rather critical."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Somewhat doubtful.","answerZh":"有些怀疑。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章提到Cablevision推出互动广告的消息'was greeted with some skepticism'，说明公众对此持怀疑态度。","questionZh":"公众对 Cablevision 计划推出的互动电视广告项目有何反应?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What is the impact of the wide use of digital video recorders on TV advertising?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has made TV advertising easily accessible to viewers."},{"label":"B","text":"It helps advertisers to measure the click-through rates."},{"label":"C","text":"It has placed TV advertising at a great disadvantage."},{"label":"D","text":"It enables viewers to check the sales items with ease."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It has placed TV advertising at a great disadvantage.","answerZh":"它使电视广告处于极为不利的境地。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文中提到数字视频录像机的普及导致广告商担心他们的广告会被跳过，这对电视广告来说是一个很大的不利。","questionZh":"数字录像机的广泛使用对电视广告有什么影响?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What do we learn about Unilever's interactive campaign?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It proves the advantage of TV advertising."},{"label":"B","text":"It has done well in engaging the viewers."},{"label":"C","text":"It helps attract investments in the company."},{"label":"D","text":"It has boosted the TV advertising industry."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It has done well in engaging the viewers.","answerZh":"它在吸引观众参与方面表现出色。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章提到联合利华的互动广告活动'kept viewers engaged for more than three minutes on average'，说明它在吸引观众方面做得很好。","questionZh":"关于 Unilever 的互动广告活动,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"How does the author view the hitherto high click-through rates?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They may be due to the novel way of advertising."},{"label":"B","text":"They signify the popularity of interactive advertising."},{"label":"C","text":"They point to the growing curiosity of TV viewers."},{"label":"D","text":"They indicate the future direction of media reform."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They may be due to the novel way of advertising.","answerZh":"这可能归因于这种新颖的广告方式。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后提到'Click-through rates have been high so far (around 3-4%, compared with less than 0.3% online), but that may be a result of the novelty'，说明迄今为止的高点击率可能是由于广告方式的新颖性。","questionZh":"作者如何看待迄今为止的高点击率?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2016_06_1-p2","title":"CET6 2016年06月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2016年06月 第1套","examDate":"2016年06月","year":"2016","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2016-06-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"面对大规模失业，结构性失业、无捷径的说法流行却毫无依据；作者认为美国失业实因需求不足，只要有决心即可迅速解决，结构论不过是不作为的借口。","mainIdeaEn":"Amid mass unemployment, the fashionable claim of structural, no-easy-answer joblessness is baseless; the author argues U.S. unemployment stems from inadequate demand and could be cured quickly given the will to act.","answerCode":"BDAAC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先是需求不足，再毫无根据，然后国防工业兴旺，接着强烈反对刺激，最后表明须紧急行动。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author think is the root cause of mass unemployment in America?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Corporate mismanagement."},{"label":"B","text":"Insufficient demand."},{"label":"C","text":"Technological advances."},{"label":"D","text":"Workers' slow adaptation."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Insufficient demand.","answerZh":"需求不足。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段明确指出'all the facts suggest that high unemployment in America is the result of inadequate demand'，即美国大规模失业的根源在于需求不足。因此，B选项'Insufficient demand'是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者认为美国大规模失业的根本原因是什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does the author think of the experts' claim concerning unemployment?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Self-evident."},{"label":"B","text":"Thought-provoking."},{"label":"C","text":"Irrational."},{"label":"D","text":"Groundless."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Groundless.","answerZh":"毫无根据。","explanation":"这是一道观点态度题。文章第二段指出'But don't bother asking for evidence that justifies this bleak view. There isn't any.'，表明作者认为专家关于失业的观点没有证据支持，即'Groundless'。因此，D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者如何看待专家们关于失业问题的说法?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does the author say helped bring down unemployment during the Great Depression?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The booming defense industry."},{"label":"B","text":"The wise heads, benefit package."},{"label":"C","text":"Nationwide training of workers."},{"label":"D","text":"Thorough restructuring of industries."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"The booming defense industry.","answerZh":"蓬勃发展的国防工业。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第三段提到'A few years later, a large defense buildup finally provided a fiscal stimulus adequate to the economy's needs—and suddenly industry was eager to employ those \"unadaptable and untrained\" workers.'，说明在大萧条期间，是国防工业的蓬勃发展帮助降低了失业率。因此，A选项'The booming defense industry'是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者认为是什么帮助降低了大萧条时期的失业率?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What has caused claims of huge structural problems to multiply?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Powerful opposition to governments stimulus efforts."},{"label":"B","text":"Very Serious People's attempt to cripple the economy."},{"label":"C","text":"Evidence gathered from many sectors of the industries."},{"label":"D","text":"Economists' failure to detect the problems in time."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Powerful opposition to governments stimulus efforts.","answerZh":"对政府刺激措施的强烈反对。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段指出'But now, as then, powerful forces are ideologically opposed to the whole idea of government action on a sufficient scale to jump-start the economy.'，说明对政府刺激经济行动的强大反对是导致大规模结构性问题说法增多的原因。因此，A选项'Powerful opposition to governments stimulus efforts'是正确答案。","questionZh":"是什么导致关于巨大结构性问题的说法层出不穷?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What is the author's purpose in writing the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"To testify to the experts, analysis of America's problems."},{"label":"B","text":"To offer a feasible solution to the structural unemployment."},{"label":"C","text":"To show the urgent need for the government to take action."},{"label":"D","text":"To alert American workers to the urgency for adaptation."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"To show the urgent need for the government to take action.","answerZh":"表明政府迫切需要采取行动。","explanation":"这是一道写作目的题。文章最后一段作者强调'So what you need to know is that there's no evidence whatsoever to back these claims. ... it's an excuse -- a reason not to act on America's problems at a time when action is desperately needed.'，表明作者写作的目的是展示政府迫切需要采取行动的必要性。因此，C选项'To show the urgent need for the government to take action'是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者写这篇文章的目的是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2016_06_2-p1","title":"CET6 2016年06月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2016年06月 第2套","examDate":"2016年06月","year":"2016","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2016-06-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"面对缺水与化肥涨价，发展中国家农民用未经处理的污水灌溉施肥；尽管带来细菌感染等健康风险，但其社会经济效益更大，风险可通过教育来化解。","mainIdeaEn":"Facing water shortages and costly fertilizer, farmers in developing countries irrigate with raw sewage; despite bacterial health risks, the social and economic benefits outweigh them and risks can be addressed through education.","answerCode":"CCABA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先益处大于危害，再农民消费者染菌，然后作者表示赞成，接着靠教育化解风险，最后认同Drechsel观点。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What does the author say about the use of raw sewage for farming?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its risks cannot be overestimated."},{"label":"B","text":"It should be forbidden altogether."},{"label":"C","text":"Its benefits outweigh the hazards involved."},{"label":"D","text":"It is polluting millions of acres of cropland."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Its benefits outweigh the hazards involved.","answerZh":"其益处大于所涉及的危害。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'those dangers are outweighed by the social and economic gains for poor urban farmers and consumers who need affordable food'可知，作者认为使用生污水灌溉和施肥的好处大于其带来的风险，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于将未处理污水用于农业,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What is the main problem caused by the use of waste water for irrigation?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rivers and lakes nearby will gradually become contaminated."},{"label":"B","text":"It will drive producers of chemical fertilizers out of business."},{"label":"C","text":"Farmers and consumers may be affected by harmful bacteria."},{"label":"D","text":"It will make the farm produce less competitive on the market."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Farmers and consumers may be affected by harmful bacteria.","answerZh":"农民和消费者可能受到有害细菌的影响。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'When this water is used for agricultural irrigation, farmers risk absorbing disease-causing bacteria, as do consumers who eat the produce raw and unwashed'可知，使用废水灌溉的主要问题是农民和消费者可能会受到有害细菌的影响，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"用废水灌溉造成的主要问题是什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What is environmental scientist Pay Drechsel's attitude towards the use of untreated human waste in agriculture?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Favorable."},{"label":"B","text":"Skeptical."},{"label":"C","text":"Indifferent."},{"label":"D","text":"Responsible."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Favorable.","answerZh":"赞成。","explanation":"这是一道观点态度题。根据文章第五段'But Pay Drechsel, an environmental scientist, argues that the social and economic benefits of using untreated human waste to grow food outweigh the health risks'可知，环境科学家Pay Drechsel认为使用未经处理的人类废物种植食物的社会和经济效益大于健康风险，因此他对这种做法持支持态度，A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"环境科学家 Pay Drechsel 对在农业中使用未处理的人类排泄物持什么态度?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What does Pay Drechsel think of the risks involved in using untreated human waste for farming?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They have been somewhat exaggerated."},{"label":"B","text":"They can be dealt with through education."},{"label":"C","text":"They will be minimized with new technology."},{"label":"D","text":"They can be addressed by improved sanitation."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They can be dealt with through education.","answerZh":"这些风险可以通过教育来应对。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第五段'Those dangers can be addressed with farmer and consumer education, he said'可知，Pay Drechsel认为通过教育可以解决使用未经处理的人类废物种植食物所涉及的风险，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Pay Drechsel 如何看待用未处理的人类排泄物务农所涉及的风险?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What do we learn about James Bartram's position on the use of human waste for farming?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"He echoes Pay Drechsel's opinion on the issue."},{"label":"B","text":"He challenges Liqa Raschid-Sally's conclusion."},{"label":"C","text":"He thinks it the only way out of the current food crisis."},{"label":"D","text":"He deems it indispensable for combating global poverty."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"He echoes Pay Drechsel's opinion on the issue.","answerZh":"他在这一问题上赞同 Pay Drechsel 的观点。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'Overly strict standards often... We need to accept that fact across much of the planet, so waste with little or no treatment will be used in agriculture for good reason'可知，James Bartram认为过于严格的标准往往不切实际，我们需要接受这样一个事实：在地球上的大部分地区，未经处理或处理很少的废物将因充分的理由被用于农业，这与Pay Drechsel的观点相呼应，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于 James Bartram 对用人类排泄物务农的立场,我们可以了解到什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2016_06_2-p2","title":"CET6 2016年06月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2016年06月 第2套","examDate":"2016年06月","year":"2016","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2016-06-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"如今很少有人下厨，厨房却成了现代住宅的中心；从藏于地下的仆役重地到彰显身份的设计舞台，厨房的地位变迁折射出一个世纪的社会变革。","mainIdeaEn":"Though few people cook anymore, the kitchen has become the heart of the modern home; its rise from a hidden servants' space to a status-defining design showcase reflects a century of social change.","answerCode":"DBDAB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先是现代家中心，再世上独一无二，然后折射社会变迁，接着让女性更高效，最后核心仍似1920年代。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author say about the kitchen of today?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is where housewives display their cooking skills."},{"label":"B","text":"It is where the family entertains important guests."},{"label":"C","text":"It has become something odd in a modern house."},{"label":"D","text":"It is regarded as the center of a modern home."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is regarded as the center of a modern home.","answerZh":"它被视为现代家庭的中心。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'the kitchen has become the heart of the modern house'，说明现代家庭中厨房被视为中心。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于当今的厨房,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"Why does the Georgian-style kitchen sell at a very high price?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is believed to have tremendous artistic value."},{"label":"B","text":"No duplicate is to be found in any other place."},{"label":"C","text":"It is manufactured by a famous British company."},{"label":"D","text":"No other manufacturer can produce anything like it."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"No duplicate is to be found in any other place.","answerZh":"在其他任何地方都找不到相同的复制品。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章提到'Robinson & Cornish...offers a Georgian-style one which would cost £145,000-155,000...Its big selling point is that nobody else will have it'，说明这种厨房之所以昂贵是因为其独一无二，没有其他地方能找到相同的设计。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"乔治王朝风格的厨房为什么卖价很高?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does the change in the status of the kitchen reflect?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Improved living conditions."},{"label":"B","text":"Women's elevated status."},{"label":"C","text":"Technological progress."},{"label":"D","text":"Social change."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Social change.","answerZh":"社会变迁。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'The elevation of the room that once belonged only to the servants to that of a design showcase for the modern family tells the story of a century of social change'，说明厨房地位的提升反映了一个世纪以来的社会变迁。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"厨房地位的变化反映了什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What was the Beecher sisters' idea of a kitchen?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A place where women could work more efficiently."},{"label":"B","text":"A place where high technology could be applied."},{"label":"C","text":"A place of interest to the educated people."},{"label":"D","text":"A place to experiment with new ideas."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"A place where women could work more efficiently.","answerZh":"一个能让女性更高效工作的地方。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章提到'In American Woman's Home, published in 1869, the Beecher sisters recommended a scientific approach to household management, designed to enhance the efficiency of a woman's work and promote order'，说明Beecher姐妹认为厨房应该是女性工作更高效的场所。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Beecher 姐妹心目中的厨房是什么样的?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What do we learn about today's kitchen?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It represents the rapid technological advance in people's daily life."},{"label":"B","text":"Many of its central features are no different from those of the 1920s."},{"label":"C","text":"It has been transformed beyond recognition."},{"label":"D","text":"Many of its functions have changed greatly."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Many of its central features are no different from those of the 1920s.","answerZh":"它的许多核心特征与20世纪20年代的并无不同。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一句提到'many elements remain central features of today's kitchen'，说明今天厨房的许多核心特征与1920年代没有太大不同。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于当今的厨房,我们可以了解到什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2016_06_3-p1","title":"CET6 2016年06月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2016年06月 第3套","examDate":"2016年06月","year":"2016","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2016-06-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"美国联邦贸易委员会修订绿色指南，要求环保广告不得笼统宣称，须具体说明产品哪方面环保；此前环保标签泛滥、消费者困惑，还引发误导认证的诉讼。","mainIdeaEn":"The FTC's revised Green Guides require eco-friendly ads to specify how a product is environmentally beneficial rather than make broad claims, following a surge of confusing, sometimes misleading eco-labels and lawsuits.","answerCode":"CDCAB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说清哪里环保，再消费者分不清，然后误导第三方认证，接着当时没有准则，最后各企业各行其是。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do the revised \"Green Guides\" require businesses to do?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Manufacture as many green products as possible."},{"label":"B","text":"Indicate whether their products are recyclable."},{"label":"C","text":"Specify in what way their products are green."},{"label":"D","text":"Attach green labels to all of their products."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Specify in what way their products are green.","answerZh":"具体说明其产品在哪些方面是环保的。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段中的'Marketers must qualify their claims on the product packaging and limit them to a specific benefit, such as how much of the product is recycled'，可以确定修订后的'Green Guides'要求商家具体说明其产品在哪些方面是环保的，因此选项C是正确答案。","questionZh":"修订后的 \"Green Guides\" 要求企业做什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the author say about consumers facing an explosion of green claims?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They can easily see through the businesses' tricks."},{"label":"B","text":"They have to spend lots of time choosing products."},{"label":"C","text":"They have doubt about current green certification."},{"label":"D","text":"They are not clear which products are truly green."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They are not clear which products are truly green.","answerZh":"他们不清楚哪些产品是真正环保的。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第五段中的'In the last five years or so, there has been an explosion of green claims and environmental claims. It is clear that consumers don't always know what they are getting'，可以确定作者认为消费者面对大量的绿色声明时，并不清楚哪些产品是真正的绿色产品，因此选项D是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于面对铺天盖地环保宣传的消费者,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What was SC Johnson accused of in the class-action lawsuits?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It gave consumers the impression that all its products were truly green."},{"label":"B","text":"It gave a third party the authority to label its products as environmentally friendly."},{"label":"C","text":"It misled consumers to believe that its products had been certified by a third party."},{"label":"D","text":"It sold cleaning products that were not included in the official \"Greenlist\"."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It misled consumers to believe that its products had been certified by a third party.","answerZh":"它误导消费者相信其产品已获得第三方认证。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段中的'The lawsuits said that the label was misleading because it gave the impression that the products had been certified by a third party when the certification was the company's own'，可以确定SC Johnson被控误导消费者相信其产品是由第三方认证的，而实际上认证是公司自己的，因此选项C是正确答案。","questionZh":"在集体诉讼中,SC Johnson 被指控什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"How did Christopher Beard defend his company's labeling practice?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"There were no clear guidelines concerning green labeling."},{"label":"B","text":"His company's products had been well received by the public."},{"label":"C","text":"It was in conformity to the prevailing practice in the market."},{"label":"D","text":"No law required the involvement of a third party in certification."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"There were no clear guidelines concerning green labeling.","answerZh":"当时没有关于环保标签的明确准则。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。Christopher Beard在为公司辩护时承认'this has been an area that is difficult to navigate'（这是一个难以驾驭的领域），即绿色标签领域缺乏明确的指导方针，这正是他为公司标签做法辩护的依据，因此选项A正确。 - 关键句：while acknowledging that \"this has been an area that is difficult to navigate\".","questionZh":"Christopher Beard 如何为其公司的标签做法辩护?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does Kevin Wilhelm imply by saying \"It's kind of a Wild West\" (Lines 2-3, Para. 11)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Businesses compete to produce green products."},{"label":"B","text":"Each business acts its own way in green labeling."},{"label":"C","text":"Consumers grow wild with products labeled green."},{"label":"D","text":"Anything produced in the West can be labeled green."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Each business acts its own way in green labeling.","answerZh":"在环保标签方面各企业各行其是。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章最后一段中的'it's kind of a Wild West, anybody can claim themselves to be green'，可以推断出Kevin Wilhelm意味着在绿色标签方面，每个企业都按照自己的方式行事，因此选项B是正确答案。","questionZh":"Kevin Wilhelm 说 \"It's kind of a Wild West\"(第11段第2-3行)是在暗示什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2016_06_3-p2","title":"CET6 2016年06月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2016年06月 第3套","examDate":"2016年06月","year":"2016","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2016-06-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"美国教育体系正把不平等代代相传，学校改革刻不容缓；作者指出教师效能对学生影响巨大，而芝加哥教师工会却在牺牲学生利益、庇护不称职的教师。","mainIdeaEn":"America's schools transmit inequality across generations, making reform urgent; the author argues teacher effectiveness hugely affects students, yet Chicago's union protects weak teachers at students' expense.","answerCode":"BBCDA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先难消除不平等，再不利学习环境，然后要求涨薪，接着表现全看老师，最后护庸师坑学生。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn about America's education system?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It provides a ladder of opportunity for the wealthy."},{"label":"B","text":"It contributes little to the elimination of inequality."},{"label":"C","text":"It has remained basically unchanged for generations."},{"label":"D","text":"It has brought up generations of responsible citizens."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It contributes little to the elimination of inequality.","answerZh":"它对消除不平等几乎没有贡献。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一句提到'America's education system has become less a ladder of opportunity than a structure to transmit inequality from one generation to the next'，说明美国教育系统对消除不平等贡献不大，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于美国的教育体系,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What is chiefly responsible for the undesirable performance of inner-city schools?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Unqualified teachers."},{"label":"B","text":"Unfavorable learning environment."},{"label":"C","text":"Lack of financial resources."},{"label":"D","text":"Subconscious racial discrimination."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Unfavorable learning environment.","answerZh":"不利的学习环境。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段指出'the main reason inner-city schools do poorly isn't teachers' unions, but poverty'，即内城学校表现差的主因是'贫困'。贫困造成的是不利的学习环境（unfavorable learning environment），B选项正是对'poverty'这一根源的概括，因此B正确。 - 关键句：the main reason inner-city schools do poorly isn't teachers' unions, but poverty.","questionZh":"内城区学校表现不佳的主要原因是什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does the author think the union should do to win popular support?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Assist the city government in reforming schools."},{"label":"B","text":"Give constructive advice to inner-city schools."},{"label":"C","text":"Demand higher pay for teachers."},{"label":"D","text":"Help teachers improve teaching."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Demand higher pay for teachers.","answerZh":"要求提高教师薪酬。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章倒数第二段提到'Teachers need to be much better paid to attract the best college graduates to the nation's worst schools'，说明作者认为教师应该获得更高的薪酬以吸引优秀大学毕业生到全国最差的学校任教，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者认为工会应该怎么做才能赢得公众支持?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What is the finding of the gold standard study by Harvard and Columbia University scholars?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Many inner-city school teachers are not equal to their jobs."},{"label":"B","text":"A large proportion of inner-city children often miss classes."},{"label":"C","text":"Many students are dissatisfied with their teachers."},{"label":"D","text":"Student performance has a lot to do with teachers."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Student performance has a lot to do with teachers.","answerZh":"学生的表现与教师有很大关系。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第五段提到'The gold standard study by Harvard and Columbia University scholars found that even in high-poverty schools, teachers consistently had a huge positive or negative impact'，说明哈佛大学和哥伦比亚大学的黄金标准研究发现，即使在高贫困学校，教师也始终对学生产生巨大积极或消极影响，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"哈佛大学和哥伦比亚大学学者的黄金标准研究有什么发现?"},{"number":"55","stem":"Why does the author say the Chicago union's demand is an insult to students?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It protects incompetent teachers at the expense of students."},{"label":"B","text":"It underestimates students' ability to tell good teachers from poor ones."},{"label":"C","text":"It makes students feel that they are discriminated against in many ways."},{"label":"D","text":"It totally ignores students' initiative in the learning process."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It protects incompetent teachers at the expense of students.","answerZh":"它以牺牲学生利益为代价保护不称职的教师。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到'the union in Chicago is insisting that teachers who are laid off—often for being ineffective—should get priority in new hiring'，说明芝加哥工会坚持认为被解雇的教师（通常是因为表现不佳）应该在新招聘中优先考虑，这实际上是在牺牲学生的利益来保护不称职的教师，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者为什么说芝加哥工会的要求是对学生的侮辱?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2016_12_2-p1","title":"CET6 2016年12月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2016年12月 第2套","examDate":"2016年12月","year":"2016","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2016-12-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"政府拟立法统一香烟包装，意在剥离香烟吸引力、阻止新一代入坑，而非让老烟民戒烟；烟草业强烈反对，政治游说使这项措施一再拖延。","mainIdeaEn":"The government plans to legislate standardized cigarette packaging to strip cigarettes of appeal and deter new smokers rather than make addicts quit; the tobacco industry fiercely opposes it, and lobbying has repeatedly delayed action.","answerCode":"DABAC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先对戒烟没影响，再立法统一包装，然后降幅比英国更大，接着首相迟迟不动，最后竟让更多人变胖。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do chain smokers think of cigarette packaging?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fancy packaging can help to engage new smokers."},{"label":"B","text":"It has little to do with the quality or taste of cigarettes."},{"label":"C","text":"Plain packaging discourages non-smokers from taking up smoking."},{"label":"D","text":"It has little impact on their decision whether or not to quit smoking."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It has little impact on their decision whether or not to quit smoking.","answerZh":"它对他们是否戒烟的决定几乎没有影响。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段中的描述，'Any veteran nicotine addict will testify that fancy packaging plays no role in the decision to keep smoking'，表明老烟民认为香烟包装对于他们是否继续吸烟几乎没有影响，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"老烟民如何看待香烟包装?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What has the UK government agreed to do concerning tobacco packaging?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pass a law to standardise cigarette packaging."},{"label":"B","text":"Rid cigarette cartons of all advertisements."},{"label":"C","text":"Subsidise companies to adopt plain packaging."},{"label":"D","text":"Reclassify cigarettes according to packaging."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Pass a law to standardise cigarette packaging.","answerZh":"立法统一香烟包装。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到，'The government...has agreed to legislate for standardised packaging'，即政府同意通过立法来标准化香烟包装，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"英国政府同意在烟草包装方面做什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What has happened in Australia where plain packaging is implemented?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Premature death rates resulting from smoking have declined."},{"label":"B","text":"The number of smokers has dropped more sharply than in the UK."},{"label":"C","text":"The sales of tobacco substitutes have increased considerably."},{"label":"D","text":"Cigarette sales have been falling far more quickly than in the UK."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"The number of smokers has dropped more sharply than in the UK.","answerZh":"吸烟者数量的下降幅度比英国更大。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段指出英国吸烟人数自20世纪70年代以来大致减半（'a fall in smoking with numbers having roughly halved since the 1970s'），第四段紧接着说'Evidence from Australia suggests plain packaging pushes society further along that road'，即朴素包装让（澳大利亚）社会在吸烟人数下降这条路上走得比英国更远，对应选项B'The number of smokers has dropped more sharply than in the UK'。A项把英国的'过早死亡'误植到澳大利亚且文中并未说死亡率下降，属过度推断。故正确答案是B。","questionZh":"实行平装包装的澳大利亚发生了什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"Why has it taken so long for the UK government to consider plain packaging?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Prime Minister Cameron has been reluctant to take action."},{"label":"B","text":"There is strong opposition from veteran nicotine addicts."},{"label":"C","text":"Many Members of Parliament are addicted to smoking."},{"label":"D","text":"Pressure from tobacco manufacturers remains strong."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Prime Minister Cameron has been reluctant to take action.","answerZh":"卡梅伦首相一直不愿采取行动。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到，'But strength of will is the missing ingredient where Mr. Cameron and public health are concerned'，表明卡梅伦在公共卫生问题上缺乏决心，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"英国政府为什么迟迟才考虑平装包装?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What did Cameron say about chocolate oranges at supermarket checkouts?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They fueled a lot of controversy."},{"label":"B","text":"They attracted a lot of smokers."},{"label":"C","text":"They made more British people obese."},{"label":"D","text":"They had certain ingredients missing."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They made more British people obese.","answerZh":"它们使更多英国人变得肥胖。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到卡梅伦在2006年曾表示，'chocolate oranges placed seductively at supermarket check-outs fueled obesity'，即他认为超市结账处诱人的巧克力橙子助长了肥胖问题，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于超市收银台旁的巧克力橙,Cameron 说了什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2016_12_2-p2","title":"CET6 2016年12月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2016年12月 第2套","examDate":"2016年12月","year":"2016","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2016-12-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"尽管学费高、负债重、就业无保障，上大学依然划算：低薪者可少还或免还贷款，课外同学交流、人脉与名校声望都会带来长远回报。","mainIdeaEn":"Despite high fees, heavy debt and no job guarantee, university still pays off: low earners repay little, and peer interaction, lifelong contacts and a prestigious degree bring lasting returns.","answerCode":"ADCBD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先上大学终究值，再多数干非学位活，然后课外同学互学，接着结识贵人，最后名校声望影响招聘。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What is the author's opinion of going to university?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is worthwhile after all."},{"label":"B","text":"It is simply a waste of time."},{"label":"C","text":"It is hard to say whether it is good or bad."},{"label":"D","text":"It is too expensive for most young people."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is worthwhile after all.","answerZh":"终究还是值得的。","explanation":"这是一道观点态度题。文章最后一段提到'Perhaps the reason why so many universities offer their students so little is they know studying at a top university remains a brilliant investment even if you don't learn anything'，表明作者认为上大学是一项值得的投资。同时，文章也提到了上大学的诸多好处，如'studies show they go on to be healthier and happier than non-graduates'，'far more likely to vote'，'forming contacts for life'等，进一步印证了作者的正面态度。","questionZh":"作者对上大学持什么看法?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does the author say about the employment situation of British university graduates?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Few of them are satisfied with the jobs they are offered."},{"label":"B","text":"It usually takes a long time for them to find a decent job."},{"label":"C","text":"Graduates from elite universities usually can get decent jobs."},{"label":"D","text":"Most of them take jobs which don't require a college degree."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Most of them take jobs which don't require a college degree.","answerZh":"他们中大多数人从事不需要大学学位的工作。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'six in ten graduates today are in non-graduate jobs'，即60%的大学毕业生从事的是非大学毕业即可从事的工作，说明大多数毕业生从事的工作并不需要大学学位。","questionZh":"关于英国大学毕业生的就业状况,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does the author say is important for university students besides classroom instruction?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Making sure to obtain an upper-second class degree."},{"label":"B","text":"Practical skills they will need in their future careers."},{"label":"C","text":"Interactions among themselves outside the classroom."},{"label":"D","text":"Developing independent and creative thinking abilities."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Interactions among themselves outside the classroom.","answerZh":"课堂之外学生之间的相互交流。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'Education is the sum of what students teach each other in between lectures and seminars'，强调了学生在课堂之外的互动对他们的教育同样重要。","questionZh":"作者认为除课堂教学外,什么对大学生很重要?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What is said to be an advantage of going to university?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Learning how to take risks in an ever-changing world."},{"label":"B","text":"Meeting people who will be helpful to you in the future."},{"label":"C","text":"Having opportunities of playing a leading role in society."},{"label":"D","text":"Gaining up-to-date knowledge in science and technology."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Meeting people who will be helpful to you in the future.","answerZh":"结识将来会对你有帮助的人。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'Students at university also meet those likely to be in leading jobs in the future, forming contacts for life'，说明在大学期间结识未来可能在重要职位的人，对个人未来发展有帮助。","questionZh":"据说上大学有什么好处?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What can we infer from the last paragraph?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is natural for students to make complaints about university education."},{"label":"B","text":"Few students are willing to bear the burden of debt incurred at university."},{"label":"C","text":"University education is becoming attractive to students who can afford it."},{"label":"D","text":"The prestige of the university influences employers' recruitment decisions."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The prestige of the university influences employers' recruitment decisions.","answerZh":"大学的声望会影响雇主的招聘决定。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到'Studying at university will only become less attractive if employers shift their focus away from where someone went to university — and there is no sign of that happening anytime soon'，说明雇主对大学背景的重视是大学教育吸引力的关键因素。","questionZh":"从最后一段我们可以推断出什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2016_12_3-p1","title":"CET6 2016年12月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2016年12月 第3套","examDate":"2016年12月","year":"2016","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2016-12-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"先进电池正从专门市场走向主流，被视为通向更清洁、高效、公平能源未来的关键；储能已成庞大产业，甚至让无电地区首次用上太阳能照明。","mainIdeaEn":"Advanced batteries are moving into the mainstream as a key to a cleaner, more efficient and equitable energy future; energy storage is now a huge industry, even bringing first light to off-grid communities.","answerCode":"BDCAA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先是能源大方向，再世界天翻地覆，然后储太阳能照明，接着利好电力公司，最后旧电网成往事。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What does Dr. Sadoway think of energy storage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It involves the application of sophisticated technology."},{"label":"B","text":"It is the direction energy development should follow."},{"label":"C","text":"It will prove to be a profitable business."},{"label":"D","text":"It is a technology benefiting everyone."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It is the direction energy development should follow.","answerZh":"它是能源发展应当遵循的方向。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'Dr. Donald Sadoway at MIT started his own battery company with the hope of changing the world's energy future.'可知，Sadoway博士认为能源存储技术是能源发展应该遵循的方向，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Sadoway 博士如何看待储能?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What is most likely to happen when advanced batteries become widely used?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Mobile-first lifestyles will become popular."},{"label":"B","text":"The globalization process will be accelerated."},{"label":"C","text":"Communications will take more diverse forms."},{"label":"D","text":"The world will undergo revolutionary changes."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The world will undergo revolutionary changes.","answerZh":"世界将发生革命性的变化。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章第二段提到'Advanced batteries are moving out of specialized markets and creeping into the mainstream, signaling a tipping point for forward-looking technologies such as electric cars and rooftop solar panels.'以及'Having already enabled a communications revolution, the battery is now poised to transform just about everything else.'可以推断，当先进的电池被广泛使用时，世界将经历革命性的变化，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"先进电池得到广泛应用后,最可能发生什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"In some rural communities of emerging economies, people have begun to.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"find digital devices simply indispensable."},{"label":"B","text":"communicate primarily by mobile phone."},{"label":"C","text":"light their homes with stored solar energy."},{"label":"D","text":"distribute power with wires and wooden poles."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"light their homes with stored solar energy.","answerZh":"用储存的太阳能为家里照明。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'In emerging economies, rural communities are bypassing the wires and wooden poles that spread power. Instead, some in Africa and Asia are seeing their first light-bulbs illuminated by the power of sunlight stored in batteries.'可知，在新兴经济体的一些农村社区，人们已经开始使用储存的太阳能点亮他们的家，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"在一些新兴经济体的农村社区,人们已经开始做什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"Utility companies have begun to realize that battery technologies.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"benefit their business."},{"label":"B","text":"transmit power faster."},{"label":"C","text":"promote innovation."},{"label":"D","text":"encourage competition."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"benefit their business.","answerZh":"有利于它们的业务。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段'Even utility companies, which have long viewed batteries and alternative forms of energy as a threat, are learning to embrace the technologies as enabling rather than disrupting.'可知，公用事业公司开始意识到电池技术对他们的业务是有益的，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"公用事业公司开始意识到电池技术怎么样?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does the author imply about the centralized electric grid?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It might become a thing of the past."},{"label":"B","text":"It might turn out to be a \"prosumer\"."},{"label":"C","text":"It will be easier to operate and maintain."},{"label":"D","text":"It will have to be completely transformed."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It might become a thing of the past.","answerZh":"它可能会成为过去。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章最后一段'What happens to the centralized electric grid, which took decades and billions of dollars to build, as more and more people become \"prosumers,\" who produce and consume their own energy onsite?'可以推断，随着越来越多的人成为'产销者'，集中式电网可能会成为过去，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于集中式电网,作者暗示了什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2016_12_3-p2","title":"CET6 2016年12月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2016年12月 第3套","examDate":"2016年12月","year":"2016","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2016-12-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"百余年前杜波依斯就质疑用种族作生物学解释；如今主流科学认为种族是没有生物学意义的社会建构，界定含糊、易致临床误判，学界呼吁淘汰种族分类。","mainIdeaEn":"Over a century after Du Bois questioned race as biology, mainstream science holds race is a social construct without biological meaning, a poorly defined marker that misleads clinical predictions, and scholars urge phasing it out.","answerCode":"CBCAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先解释社会文化差异，再种族界定不清，然后分类致临床误判，接着用词该更精确，最后某些领域仍有用。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"Du Bois was opposed to the use of race as.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"a basis for explaining human genetic diversity."},{"label":"B","text":"an aid to understanding different populations."},{"label":"C","text":"an explanation for social and cultural differences."},{"label":"D","text":"a term to describe individual human characteristics."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"an explanation for social and cultural differences.","answerZh":"对社会和文化差异的一种解释。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'He spoke out against the idea of 'white' and 'black' as distinct groups, claiming that these distinctions ignored the scope of human diversity'可知，Du Bois反对使用种族作为解释社会和文化差异的依据，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Du Bois 反对把种族用作什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"The study by Svante Paabo served as an example to show.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"modern genetics research is likely to fuel racial conflicts."},{"label":"B","text":"race is a poorly defined marker of human genetic diversity."},{"label":"C","text":"race as a biological term can explain human genetic diversity."},{"label":"D","text":"genetics research should consider social and cultural variables."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"race is a poorly defined marker of human genetic diversity.","answerZh":"种族是人类遗传多样性的一个界定不清的标志。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段'In one example that demonstrated genetic differences were not fixed along racial lines'可知，Svante Paabo的研究是为了展示种族并不是人类遗传多样性的一个明确标志，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Svante Paabo 的研究作为例子说明了什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"The example of the disease cystic fibrosis underdiagnosed in people of African ancestry demonstrates that.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"it is absolutely necessary to put race aside in making diagnosis."},{"label":"B","text":"it is important to include social variables in genetics research."},{"label":"C","text":"racial categories for genetic diversity could lead to wrong clinical predictions."},{"label":"D","text":"discrimination against black people may cause negligence in clinical treatment."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"racial categories for genetic diversity could lead to wrong clinical predictions.","answerZh":"用种族类别衡量遗传多样性可能导致错误的临床预测。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段'If you make clinical predictions based on somebody's race, you're going to be wrong a good chunk of the time'可知，基于种族的临床预测可能会导致错误的诊断，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"非洲裔人群中囊性纤维化被漏诊的例子表明了什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What is Yudell's suggestion to scientists?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They be more precise with the language they use."},{"label":"B","text":"They refrain from using politically sensitive terms."},{"label":"C","text":"They throw out irrelevant concepts in their research."},{"label":"D","text":"They examine all possible variables in their research."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They be more precise with the language they use.","answerZh":"他们应更精确地使用语言。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第三段'Yudell said scientists need to get more specific with their language'可知，Yudell建议科学家们在使用语言时需要更精确，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Yudell 对科学家们有什么建议?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What can be inferred from Yudell's remark in the last paragraph?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Clinging to racism prolongs inequity and discrimination."},{"label":"B","text":"Physiological disparities are quite striking among races."},{"label":"C","text":"Doing away with racial discrimination is challenging."},{"label":"D","text":"Racial terms are still useful in certain fields of study."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Racial terms are still useful in certain fields of study.","answerZh":"种族术语在某些研究领域仍然有用。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章最后一段'we also acknowledge that using race as a political or social category to study racism... remains necessary'可知，尽管存在挑战，但在某些研究领域，种族术语仍然有用，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"从 Yudell 在最后一段的话中可以推断出什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2017_06_1-p1","title":"CET6 2017年06月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2017年06月 第1套","examDate":"2017年06月","year":"2017","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2017-06-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"尽管公开共享原始数据能加速科学，多数研究者仍不愿公开自己的成果；随着期刊和资助方推动，障碍正在消失，而共享其实能让分享者与使用者双赢。","mainIdeaEn":"Although open data sharing would accelerate science, most researchers resist posting their own results; as journals and funders push for it, barriers are falling, and sharing benefits both sharers and users.","answerCode":"DACCB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先共享利于科学，再多数人反对，然后视数据为私产，接着期刊资助方转向，最后共享者用者双赢。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do many researchers generally accept?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is imperative to protect scientists' patents."},{"label":"B","text":"Repositories are essential to scientific research."},{"label":"C","text":"Open data sharing is most important to medical science."},{"label":"D","text":"Open data sharing is conducive to scientific advancement."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Open data sharing is conducive to scientific advancement.","answerZh":"开放数据共享有利于科学进步。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段中的'Although many researchers broadly agree that public access to raw data would accelerate science'，可以确定大多数研究者普遍接受的观点是开放数据共享有助于科学进步。","questionZh":"许多研究人员普遍接受什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What is the attitude of most researchers towards making their own data public?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Opposed."},{"label":"B","text":"Ambiguous."},{"label":"C","text":"Liberal."},{"label":"D","text":"Neutral."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Opposed.","answerZh":"反对。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'most are reluctant to post the results of their own labors online'，表明大多数研究者对于将自己的数据公开是反对的。","questionZh":"大多数研究人员对公开自己的数据持什么态度?"},{"number":"48","stem":"According to the passage, what might hinder open data sharing?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The fear of massive copying."},{"label":"B","text":"The lack of a research culture."},{"label":"C","text":"The belief that research data is private intellectual property."},{"label":"D","text":"The concern that certain agencies may make a profit out of it."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"The belief that research data is private intellectual property.","answerZh":"认为研究数据是私人知识产权的观念。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'scientists have objected to sharing for many reasons: ... it has been difficult to agree on standards for formatting data; and there is no agreed way to assign credit for data'，其中提到了科学家反对共享的原因之一是他们认为研究数据是私人的知识产权。","questionZh":"根据文章,什么可能阻碍开放数据共享?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What helps lift some of the barriers to open data sharing?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The ever-growing demand for big data."},{"label":"B","text":"The advancement of digital technology."},{"label":"C","text":"The changing attitude of journals and funders."},{"label":"D","text":"The trend of social and economic development."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"The changing attitude of journals and funders.","answerZh":"期刊和资助方态度的转变。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'But the barriers are disappearing, in part because journals and funding agencies worldwide are encouraging scientists to make their data public'，说明期刊和资助机构的态度变化有助于消除开放数据共享的障碍。","questionZh":"什么有助于消除开放数据共享的部分障碍?"},{"number":"50","stem":"Dryad serves as an example to show how open data sharing_______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"is becoming increasingly popular"},{"label":"B","text":"benefits sharers and users alike"},{"label":"C","text":"makes researchers successful"},{"label":"D","text":"saves both money and labor"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"benefits sharers and users alike","answerZh":"使共享者和使用者都受益。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'Researchers who share get plenty of personal benefits, including more connections with colleagues, improved visibility and increased citations'以及'For example, one of the most popular data sets on multidisciplinary repository Dryad... it has been downloaded 5,700 times'，说明开放数据共享对共享者和使用者双方都有好处。","questionZh":"Dryad 作为例子说明了开放数据共享怎么样?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2017_06_1-p2","title":"CET6 2017年06月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2017年06月 第1套","examDate":"2017年06月","year":"2017","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2017-06-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"梅西百货假日季销售大跌，公司归咎于暖冬，但真正病根更深——强势美元削减游客消费；为此它大幅裁员、关店，并押注美容连锁以图翻身。","mainIdeaEn":"Macy's holiday sales plunged; it blamed warm weather, but its troubles run deeper: a strong dollar cut tourist spending, prompting major layoffs, store closures and a bet on its beauty chain.","answerCode":"ABDDA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先怪罪美元升值，再不能只怪天气，然后大幅裁员，接着为美容更能拼，最后实体店销量暴跌。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author say about the shrinking spending of international tourists in the U.S.?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is attributable to the rising value of the U.S. dollar."},{"label":"B","text":"It is a direct result of the global economic recession."},{"label":"C","text":"It reflects a shift of their interest in consumer goods."},{"label":"D","text":"It poses a potential threat to the retail business in the U.S."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is attributable to the rising value of the U.S. dollar.","answerZh":"这归因于美元的升值。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段中的信息，'Its flagship stores in major U.S. cities depend heavily on international tourist spending, which shrank at many retailers due to a strong dollar.' 可知，国际游客在美国的消费减少是由于美元的升值导致的，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于国际游客在美国消费的缩减,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does Macy's believe about its problems?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They can be solved with better management."},{"label":"B","text":"They cannot be attributed to weather only."},{"label":"C","text":"They are not as serious in its online stores."},{"label":"D","text":"They call for increased investments."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They cannot be attributed to weather only.","answerZh":"这些问题不能仅仅归咎于天气。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到，'However, it's clear that Macy's believes its troubles run deeper than a temporary aberration off the thermometer.' 表明Macy's认为其问题不仅仅是天气导致的，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Macy's 认为自己的问题出在哪里?"},{"number":"53","stem":"In order to cut costs, Macy's decided to_______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"cut the salary of senior executives"},{"label":"B","text":"relocate some of its chain stores"},{"label":"C","text":"adjust its promotion strategies"},{"label":"D","text":"reduce the size of its staff"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"reduce the size of its staff","answerZh":"裁减员工规模。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到，'The company pledged to cut 600 back-office positions, though some 150 workers in those roles would be reassigned to other jobs. It also plans to offer 'voluntary separation' packages to 165 senior executives. It will slash staffing at its fleet of 770 stores, a move affecting some 3,000 employees.' 表明Macy's决定减少员工人数以降低成本，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"为了削减成本,Macy's 决定做什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"Why does Macy's plan to expand Bluemercury in 2016?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"To experiment on its new business concept."},{"label":"B","text":"To focus more on beauty products than clothing."},{"label":"C","text":"To promote sales of its products by lowering prices."},{"label":"D","text":"To be more competitive in sales of beauty products."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"To be more competitive in sales of beauty products.","answerZh":"为了在美容产品销售上更具竞争力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到，'Macy's hopes Bluemercury will help strengthen its position in the category.' 表明Macy's希望通过扩展Bluemercury来加强其在美容产品类别中的竞争力，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Macy's 为什么计划在2016年扩张 Bluemercury?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What can we learn about Macy's during the holiday season?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sales dropped sharply in its physical stores."},{"label":"B","text":"Its retail sales exceeded those of T.J. Maxx."},{"label":"C","text":"It helped Bluemercury establish its position worldwide."},{"label":"D","text":"It filled its stores with abundant supply of merchandise."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Sales dropped sharply in its physical stores.","answerZh":"其实体店销售额急剧下降。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到，'While Thanksgiving, Black Friday and Cyber Monday all saw record spending online, in-store sales plunged over the holiday weekend.' 表明在假日季节，Macy's的实体店销售急剧下降，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于假日购物季期间的 Macy's,我们可以了解到什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2017_06_2-p1","title":"CET6 2017年06月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2017年06月 第2套","examDate":"2017年06月","year":"2017","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2017-06-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"田纳西州社区与技术学院依据开支分析拒绝将设施管理外包：自管更省钱，外包恐致员工失业，校长莫根还因反对州长重组方案辞职。","mainIdeaEn":"Citing a spending analysis showing campuses already manage facilities cost-effectively, Tennessee's colleges rejected the governor's outsourcing plan, and Chancellor Morgan resigned over his board reorganization proposal.","answerCode":"ABCAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先拿开支分析撑腰拒外包，再证自管更省钱，然后外包恐砸员工饭碗，接着州里说方案未定，最后校长因重组辞职抗议。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do we learn about the decision of technical and community colleges in Tennessee?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is backed by a campus spending analysis."},{"label":"B","text":"It has been flatly rejected by the governor."},{"label":"C","text":"It has neglected their faculty's demands."},{"label":"D","text":"It will improve their financial situation."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is backed by a campus spending analysis.","answerZh":"该决定有一项校园开支分析作为依据。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段内容，Tennessee的技术与社区学院决定不将设施管理外包给私人公司，这一决定得到了校园支出分析的支持。","questionZh":"关于田纳西州技术学院和社区学院的决定,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the campus spending analysis reveal?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Private companies play a big role in campus management."},{"label":"B","text":"Facilities management by colleges is more cost-effective."},{"label":"C","text":"Facilities management has greatly improved in recent years."},{"label":"D","text":"Colleges exercise full control over their own financial affairs."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Facilities management by colleges is more cost-effective.","answerZh":"由学院自行管理设施更具成本效益。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到，内部分析显示每个校园在设施管理上的支出远低于州确定的行业标准，这表明学院自己管理设施更具成本效益。","questionZh":"校园开支分析揭示了什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"Workers' supporters argue that Bill Haslam's proposal would_______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"deprive colleges of the right to manage their facilities"},{"label":"B","text":"make workers less motivated in performing duties"},{"label":"C","text":"render a number of campus workers jobless"},{"label":"D","text":"lead to the privatization of campus facilities"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"render a number of campus workers jobless","answerZh":"使一批校园员工失业。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到，工人的支持者批评Haslam的计划，认为这将意味着一些校园工人将失去工作或福利。","questionZh":"工人的支持者们认为 Bill Haslam 的提案会带来什么后果?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What do we learn from the state spokeswoman's response to John Morgan's decision?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The outsourcing plan is not yet finalized."},{"label":"B","text":"The outsourcing plan will be implemented."},{"label":"C","text":"The state officials are confident about the outsourcing plan."},{"label":"D","text":"The college spending analysis justifies the outsourcing plan."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"The outsourcing plan is not yet finalized.","answerZh":"外包计划尚未最终确定。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到，州发言人Michelle R. Martin表示，外包计划尚未最终确定，目前正在分析数据。","questionZh":"从州政府女发言人对 John Morgan 决定的回应中,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"Why did John Morgan decide to resign?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"He had lost confidence in the Tennessee state government."},{"label":"B","text":"He disagreed with the governor on higher education policies."},{"label":"C","text":"He thought the state's outsourcing proposal was simply unworkable."},{"label":"D","text":"He opposed the governor's plan to reconstruct the college board system."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"He opposed the governor's plan to reconstruct the college board system.","answerZh":"他反对州长重组学院董事会体系的计划。","explanation":"原文倒数第二段明确指出Morgan将退休是'because of the governor's proposal to split off six universities of the Board of Regents system and create separate governing boards for each of them'，并在辞职信中称这一改组'unworkable'。即他辞职是因为反对州长重组高校董事会系统的计划，故选D。B过于笼统，C错把'unworkable'归到外包提案（原文指的是改组而非外包）。","questionZh":"John Morgan 为什么决定辞职?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2017_06_2-p2","title":"CET6 2017年06月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2017年06月 第2套","examDate":"2017年06月","year":"2017","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2017-06-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章介绍16世纪末兴起的壮游：欧洲贵族青年赴法意尤其罗马完成古典教育，游历中习得古典艺术与建筑，并深深影响了英国建筑风格。","mainIdeaEn":"The passage describes the Grand Tour, a costly rite in which young aristocrats traveled to France and Italy—above all Rome—to absorb classical art and architecture, ultimately shaping English building styles.","answerCode":"BCDBA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说穷人游不起，再看游子通文学爱艺术，然后一路学古典艺术建筑，接着没博物馆只好看私藏，最后英国盖满罗马风。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What is said about the Grand Tour?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It was fashionable among young people of the time."},{"label":"B","text":"It was unaffordable for ordinary people."},{"label":"C","text":"It produced some famous European artists."},{"label":"D","text":"It made a compulsory part of college education."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It was unaffordable for ordinary people.","answerZh":"普通人负担不起。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'Travel was arduous and costly throughout the period, possible only for a privileged class'，说明大旅行对于普通人来说是负担不起的，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于 Grand Tour,文中说了什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What did Grand Tourists have in common?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They had much geographic knowledge."},{"label":"B","text":"They were courageous and venturesome."},{"label":"C","text":"They were versed in literature and interested in art."},{"label":"D","text":"They had enough travel and outdoor-life experience."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They were versed in literature and interested in art.","answerZh":"他们精通文学并对艺术感兴趣。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'The Grand Tourist was typically a young man with a thorough grounding in Greek and Latin literature as well as some interest in art'，说明大旅行者通常具有文学基础并对艺术感兴趣，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Grand Tour 的旅行者们有什么共同点?"},{"number":"53","stem":"How did Grand Tourists benefit from their travel?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They found inspiration in the world's greatest masterpieces."},{"label":"B","text":"They got a better understanding of early human civilization."},{"label":"C","text":"They developed an interest in the origin of modern art forms."},{"label":"D","text":"They gained some knowledge of classical art and architecture."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They gained some knowledge of classical art and architecture.","answerZh":"他们获得了一些古典艺术和建筑方面的知识。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'expected to return home with souvenirs of their travels as well as an understanding of art and architecture formed by exposure to great masterpieces'，说明大旅行者通过接触伟大的艺术作品，获得了对古典艺术和建筑的了解，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Grand Tour 的旅行者们从旅行中获得了什么益处?"},{"number":"54","stem":"Why did many Grand Tourists visit the private collections?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They could buy unique souvenirs there to take back home."},{"label":"B","text":"Europe hardly had any museums before the 19th century."},{"label":"C","text":"They found the antiques there more valuable."},{"label":"D","text":"Private collections were of greater variety."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Europe hardly had any museums before the 19th century.","answerZh":"19世纪以前欧洲几乎没有博物馆。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'Since there were few museums anywhere in Europe before the close of the eighteenth century, Grand Tourists often saw paintings and sculptures by gaining admission to private collections'，说明由于18世纪末之前欧洲几乎没有博物馆，大旅行者通过参观私人收藏来观赏绘画和雕塑，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"许多 Grand Tour 旅行者为什么参观私人收藏?"},{"number":"55","stem":"How did the Grand Tour influence the architecture in England?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"There appeared more and more Roman-style buildings."},{"label":"B","text":"Many aristocrats began to move into Roman-style villas."},{"label":"C","text":"Aristocrats' country houses all had Roman-style gardens."},{"label":"D","text":"Italian architects were hired to design houses and gardens."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"There appeared more and more Roman-style buildings.","answerZh":"出现了越来越多罗马风格的建筑。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'noble men often applied what they learned from the villas of Palladio in the Veneto and the evocative ruins of Rome to their own country houses and gardens'，说明贵族们将从罗马废墟中学到的知识应用到自己的乡村住宅和花园中，导致出现了越来越多的罗马风格建筑，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Grand Tour 如何影响了英国的建筑?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2017_06_3-p1","title":"CET6 2017年06月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2017年06月 第3套","examDate":"2017年06月","year":"2017","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2017-06-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章赞颂美国女设计师把时装从巴黎束缚中解放：她们原创运动装，确立实用、易打理的美式着装规范，证明时装是服务需求的设计艺术。","mainIdeaEn":"The passage celebrates American women designers who freed fashion from Parisian dictates, inventing practical, easy-care sportswear that prized utility over pure beauty and pioneered gender equity.","answerCode":"BDCAC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先立美式着装新规，再夸运动装纯属原创，然后衣服好洗好打理，接着重心从美转实用，最后力挺男女平等。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What contribution did the women designers make to American fashion?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They made some improvements on the traditional Parisian design."},{"label":"B","text":"They formulated a dress code with distinctive American features."},{"label":"C","text":"They came up with a brand new set of design procedures."},{"label":"D","text":"They made originality a top priority in their fashion design."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They formulated a dress code with distinctive American features.","answerZh":"她们制定了具有鲜明美国特色的着装规范。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到这些设计师'established the modern dress code'，并且'letting play suits and other active wear outfits suffice for casual clothing, allowing pants to enter the wardrobe'，表明他们制定了具有独特美国特色的着装规范。","questionZh":"这些女设计师对美国时尚做出了什么贡献?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What do we learn about American designer sportswear?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It imitated the European model."},{"label":"B","text":"It laid emphasis on women's beauty."},{"label":"C","text":"It represented genuine American art."},{"label":"D","text":"It was a completely new invention."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It was a completely new invention.","answerZh":"它是一项全新的发明。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段指出'Designer sportswear was not modeled on that of Europe... it was genuinely invented and developed in America'，即美国设计师运动装并非模仿欧洲，而是在美国真正发明和发展出来的，因此D'一项全新的发明'与原文'genuinely invented and developed'直接对应。 - 关键句：Designer sportswear was not modeled on that of Europe, as \"modern art\" would later be; it was genuinely invented and developed in America.","questionZh":"关于美国设计师运动装,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What characterized American designer sportswear?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pursuit of beauty."},{"label":"B","text":"Decorative closings."},{"label":"C","text":"Ease of care."},{"label":"D","text":"Fabric quality."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Ease of care.","answerZh":"易于打理。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'Ease of care was most important'，表明美国设计师运动装的特点是易于护理。","questionZh":"美国设计师运动装有什么特点?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What occurred in the design of women's apparel in America during the 1930s-40s?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A shift of emphasis from beauty to utility."},{"label":"B","text":"The emulation of traditional Parisian design."},{"label":"C","text":"A search for balance between tradition and novelty."},{"label":"D","text":"The involvement of more women in fashion design."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"A shift of emphasis from beauty to utility.","answerZh":"设计重点从美观转向实用。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'If Paris was cast aside, the tradition of beauty was also to some degree slighted'，表明在1930-40年代，美国女装设计从美丽转向实用性。","questionZh":"上世纪三四十年代,美国女装设计发生了什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What do we learn about designers of American sportswear?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They catered to the taste of the younger generation."},{"label":"B","text":"They radically changed people's concept of beauty."},{"label":"C","text":"They advocated equity between men and women."},{"label":"D","text":"They became rivals of their Parisian counterparts."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They advocated equity between men and women.","answerZh":"她们倡导男女平等。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'They were the pioneers of gender equity, in their useful, adaptable clothing'，表明美国运动装设计师倡导男女平等。","questionZh":"关于美国运动装的设计师们,我们可以了解到什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2017_06_3-p2","title":"CET6 2017年06月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2017年06月 第3套","examDate":"2017年06月","year":"2017","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2017-06-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"研究发现垃圾填埋场改变了部分白鹳的迁徙习性：留在垃圾场过冬短期死亡率更低，但可能误食有害物，还或给生态系统埋下隐患。","mainIdeaEn":"GPS tracking shows landfills are changing white storks' migration: birds wintering on dumps survive better short-term, but risk eating harmful waste, and disrupted routes may harm ecosystems.","answerCode":"DDBCA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先是垃圾场改了鸟迁徙，再看走老路更易丧命，然后捡食垃圾恐中毒，接着西班牙鸟不恋沿途垃圾，最后忧心生态遭殃。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What is the impact of rubbish dumps on wildlife?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They have forced white storks to search for safer winter shelters."},{"label":"B","text":"They have seriously polluted the places where birds spend winter."},{"label":"C","text":"They have accelerated the reproduction of some harmful insects."},{"label":"D","text":"They have changed the previous migration habits of certain birds."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They have changed the previous migration habits of certain birds.","answerZh":"它们改变了某些鸟类以往的迁徙习性。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到，rubbish dumps have led some birds to give up on migration，说明垃圾场改变了某些鸟类的迁徙习惯。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"垃圾场对野生动物有什么影响?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What do we learn about birds following the traditional migration routes?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They can multiply at an accelerating rate."},{"label":"B","text":"They can better pull through the winter."},{"label":"C","text":"They help humans kill harmful insects."},{"label":"D","text":"They are more likely to be at risk of dying."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They are more likely to be at risk of dying.","answerZh":"它们死亡的风险更高。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到，birds following traditional migration routes were more likely to die than German storks that flew only as far as northern Morocco，说明按照传统迁徙路线飞行的鸟类死亡风险更高。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于沿传统路线迁徙的鸟类,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does Andrea Flack say about the birds overwintering on rubbish dumps?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They may end up staying there permanently."},{"label":"B","text":"They may eat something harmful."},{"label":"C","text":"They may evolve new feeding habits."},{"label":"D","text":"They may have trouble getting adequate food."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They may eat something harmful.","answerZh":"它们可能吃到有害的东西。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到，'It's very risky. The birds can easily eat pieces of plastic or rubber bands and they can die,' said Flack. 'And we don't know about the long-term consequences. They might eat something toxic and damage their health.' 说明Flack认为在垃圾场上过冬的鸟类可能会吃到有害物质。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于在垃圾场越冬的鸟类,Andrea Flack 说了什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What can be inferred about the Spanish birds tagged in the study?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They gradually lose the habit of migrating in winter."},{"label":"B","text":"They prefer rubbish dumps far away to those at home."},{"label":"C","text":"They are not attracted to the rubbish dumps on their migration routes."},{"label":"D","text":"They join the storks from Germany on rubbish dumps in Morocco."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They are not attracted to the rubbish dumps on their migration routes.","answerZh":"它们不会被迁徙路线上的垃圾场所吸引。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到，'Landfill sites on the Iberian peninsula have long attracted local white storks, but all of the Spanish birds tagged in the study flew across the Sahara desert to the western Sahel.' 说明参与研究的西班牙鸟类没有被家门口的垃圾场吸引，而是飞越撒哈拉沙漠去了西非萨赫勒地区。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于研究中被标记的西班牙鸟类,可以推断出什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What is scientists' other concern about white storks feeding on landfills?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The potential harm to the ecosystem."},{"label":"B","text":"The genetic change in the stork species."},{"label":"C","text":"The spread of epidemics to their homeland."},{"label":"D","text":"The damaging effect on bio-diversity."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"The potential harm to the ecosystem.","answerZh":"对生态系统的潜在危害。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到，'Migrating birds affect ecosystems both at home and at their winter destinations, and disrupting the traditional routes could have unexpected side effects.' 说明科学家担心迁徙鸟类对生态系统有影响，改变传统迁徙路线可能会带来意外的后果。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"对于在垃圾填埋场觅食的白鹳,科学家们的另一个担忧是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2017_12_1-p1","title":"CET6 2017年12月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2017年12月 第1套","examDate":"2017年12月","year":"2017","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2017-12-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章追溯可口可乐的演变：它从含古柯与可乐果的药饮起家，随可卡因声名败坏而走红，此后口味百年间几乎未变，成为标志饮品。","mainIdeaEn":"The passage traces Coca-Cola's evolution from a coca-and-kola tonic invented to skirt alcohol bans into today's iconic drink, whose taste has stayed nearly unchanged for over a century.","answerCode":"BCADA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先有药剂师巧避禁酒令，再运可乐果进欧当药，然后可卡因臭名远扬，接着口味百年没大变，最后串成可乐进化史。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do we learn about chemist John Pemberton?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"He used a strangely potent ingredient in a food supplement."},{"label":"B","text":"He created a drink containing alcohol without breaking law."},{"label":"C","text":"He became notorious because of the coca drink he developed."},{"label":"D","text":"He risked breaking local law to make a drink with coca leaves."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"He created a drink containing alcohol without breaking law.","answerZh":"他在不违法的情况下创制出一种含酒精的饮料。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段，chemist John Pemberton mixed extracts of coca leaf with his sugary syrup to create Coca-Cola, as a way to get around local laws prohibiting the sale of alcohol。因此，B选项正确。","questionZh":"关于化学家 John Pemberton,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the passage say about kola nuts?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Their commercial value was first discovered by Portuguese settlers."},{"label":"B","text":"They contain some kind of energy boost not found in any other food."},{"label":"C","text":"Many were shipped to Europe in the late 19th century for medicinal use."},{"label":"D","text":"They were strange to the Europeans when first imported from West Africa."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Many were shipped to Europe in the late 19th century for medicinal use.","answerZh":"19世纪末有大量可乐果被运往欧洲作药用。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段，By the late 19th century, kola nuts were being shipped by the tonne to Europe and the US, many made their way into medicines, intended as a kind of energy boost。因此，C选项正确。","questionZh":"关于可乐果,文章说了什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"How come kola-extract colas became popular?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cocaine had become notorious."},{"label":"B","text":"Alcoholic drinks were prohibited."},{"label":"C","text":"Fountains were set up to sell them."},{"label":"D","text":"Rights were sold to bottle the soda."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Cocaine had become notorious.","answerZh":"可卡因已经声名狼藉。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段，When cocaine eventually fell from grace as a beverage ingredient, kola-extract colas became popular。因此，A选项正确。","questionZh":"含可乐果提取物的可乐为什么会流行起来?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What is known about the taste of Coca-Cola?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It was so designed as to create addiction in consumers."},{"label":"B","text":"It still relies on traditional kola nut extract."},{"label":"C","text":"It has become more popular among the old."},{"label":"D","text":"It has remained virtually unchanged since its creation."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It has remained virtually unchanged since its creation.","answerZh":"自问世以来几乎没有改变。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段，But it's said to no longer contain kola nut extract, relying instead on artificial imitations to achieve the flavour。说明Coca-Cola的味道自其诞生以来基本保持不变，因此D选项正确。","questionZh":"关于可口可乐的味道,我们知道什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What is the passage mainly about?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The evolution of Coca-Cola."},{"label":"B","text":"The medicinal value of Coca-Cola."},{"label":"C","text":"The success story of Coca-Cola."},{"label":"D","text":"The business strategy of Coca-Cola."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"The evolution of Coca-Cola.","answerZh":"可口可乐的演变历程。","explanation":"这是一道主旨大意题。文章从Coca-Cola的起源讲起，介绍了其成分、发展历程、流行原因以及味道的变化，因此A选项正确。","questionZh":"这篇文章主要讲的是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2017_12_1-p2","title":"CET6 2017年12月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2017年12月 第1套","examDate":"2017年12月","year":"2017","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2017-12-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章介绍美国18小时城市的兴起：中型城市兼取大城活力与小城安宁，改造市中心住房与设施，吸引投资并带来就业与房价上涨。","mainIdeaEn":"The passage explains the rise of America's 18-hour cities—mid-sized cities blending big-city vibrancy with small-city calm—whose revitalized downtowns attract investment, jobs and rising property values.","answerCode":"CBDCD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先看大小城泾渭分明，再见新城房价上扬，然后旧市中心夜里空城，接着新居新设施齐上阵，最后好工作留住人。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn about American cities twenty years ago?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They were divided into residential and business areas."},{"label":"B","text":"Their housing prices were linked with their prosperity."},{"label":"C","text":"There was a clear divide between large and small cities"},{"label":"D","text":"They were places where large investment capital flowed."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"There was a clear divide between large and small cities","answerZh":"大城市与小城市之间存在明显差距。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'Twenty years ago, the Urban Land Institute defined the two types of cities that dominated the US landscape: smaller cities that operated around standard 9-5 business hours and large metropolitan areas that ran all 24 hours of the day.'可知，二十年前美国城市存在明显的大都市和小城市之分，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于二十年前的美国城市,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What can be inferred from the passage about 18-hour cities?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They especially appeal to small businesses."},{"label":"B","text":"They have seen a rise in property prices."},{"label":"C","text":"They have replaced quiet with excitement."},{"label":"D","text":"They have changed America's landscape."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They have seen a rise in property prices.","answerZh":"它们的房价出现了上涨。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章最后一段'The right urban mix has propped up home occupancy, increased property values, and attracted significant investment capital.'可以推断，18小时城市房价上涨，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于18小时城市,从文章中可以推断出什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"Years ago, many downtown cores in small to mid-sized cities().","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Had hardly any business activity."},{"label":"B","text":"Were crowded in business hours."},{"label":"C","text":"Exhibited no signs of prosperity."},{"label":"D","text":"Looked deserted in the evenings."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Looked deserted in the evenings.","answerZh":"一到晚上就显得空无一人。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段'For decades, many downtown cores in small to mid-sized cities were abandoned after work hours by workers who lived in the suburbs.'可知，过去小到中等城市的市中心在下班后被居住在郊区的工人遗弃，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"多年前,许多中小城市的市中心区是什么状况?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What characterizes the new downtown areas in 18-hour cities?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sudden emergence of the knowledge industry."},{"label":"B","text":"Flooding in large crowds of migrant workers."},{"label":"C","text":"Modernized housing and improved infrastructure."},{"label":"D","text":"More comfortable life and greater upward mobility."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Modernized housing and improved infrastructure.","answerZh":"现代化的住房和改善的基础设施。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'Transforming downtown areas so that they incorporate modern housing and improved walkability to local restaurants, retail, and entertainment -especially when combined with improved infrastructure for cyclists and public transit-makes them appeal to a more affluent demographic.'可知，18小时城市的新市中心特点是现代化住宅和改善的基础设施，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"18小时城市新的市中心区有什么特点?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What have 18-hour cities brought to the local residents?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"More chances for promotion."},{"label":"B","text":"Healthier living environment."},{"label":"C","text":"Greater cultural diversity."},{"label":"D","text":"Better job opportunities."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Better job opportunities.","answerZh":"更好的就业机会。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'In many of these cities such as Denver, a diverse and vigorous economy attracted to the urban core has offered stable employment for residents.'可知，18小时城市为当地居民带来了更好的工作机会，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"18小时城市给当地居民带来了什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2017_12_2-p1","title":"CET6 2017年12月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2017年12月 第2套","examDate":"2017年12月","year":"2017","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2017-12-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章借电影中机器人救人抉择探讨机器道德难题：阿西莫夫定律回避了道德，抽象概念难以编程，机器人在复杂情境中难做决断。","mainIdeaEn":"Using a movie rescue dilemma, the passage argues robot morality is hard to program: Asimov's laws sidestep ethics, abstract concepts resist coding, and robots struggle to decide in complex situations.","answerCode":"ADBAC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先问机器人能否决断更好，再叹定律没谈道德，然后程序写死不许伤人，接着抽象概念难编码，最后复杂情境机器抓瞎。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What question does the example in the movie raise?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Whether robots can reach better decisions."},{"label":"B","text":"Whether robots follow Asimov's \"zero\" law."},{"label":"C","text":"How robots may make bad judgments."},{"label":"D","text":"How robots should be programmed."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Whether robots can reach better decisions.","answerZh":"机器人能否做出更好的决定。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。机器人通过计算生存概率（45% vs 11%）做出了救人的选择，由此引出'would humans make the same choice? And which choice would we want our robotic counterparts to make?'，即这种基于计算的机器人决策是否比人类更好、机器人能否做出更好的决策，因此选A。 - 关键句：The robot's decision and its calculated approach raise an important question: would humans make the same choice? And which choice would we want our robotic counterparts to make?","questionZh":"电影中的例子提出了什么问题?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the author think of Asimov's three laws of robotics?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are apparently divorced from reality."},{"label":"B","text":"They did not follow the coding system of robotics."},{"label":"C","text":"They laid a solid foundation for robotics."},{"label":"D","text":"They did not take moral issues into consideration."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They did not take moral issues into consideration.","answerZh":"它们没有把道德问题考虑在内。","explanation":"这是一道观点态度题。文章中提到Asimov的三大定律并没有涉及道德问题，'They don't have to think, judge, or value'，表明作者认为Asimov的三大定律没有考虑到道德问题，因此正确答案是D，'They did not take moral issues into consideration'。","questionZh":"作者如何看待 Asimov 的机器人三定律?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does the author say about Asimov's robots?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They know what is good or bad for human beings."},{"label":"B","text":"They are programmed not to hurt human beings."},{"label":"C","text":"They perform duties in their owners' best interest."},{"label":"D","text":"They stop working when a moral issue is involved."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They are programmed not to hurt human beings.","answerZh":"它们被编入了不得伤害人类的程序。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到Asimov的机器人被编程为不伤害人类，'Robots cannot harm humans or allow humans to come to harm'，因此正确答案是B，'They are programmed not to hurt human beings'。","questionZh":"关于 Asimov 笔下的机器人,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What does the author want to say by mentioning the word \"harm\" in Asimov's laws?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Abstract concepts are hard to program."},{"label":"B","text":"It is hard for robots to make decisions."},{"label":"C","text":"Robots may do harm in certain situations."},{"label":"D","text":"Asimov's laws use too many vague terms."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Abstract concepts are hard to program.","answerZh":"抽象概念很难编入程序。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。作者以'harm'为例说明'A word such as \"harm\" is vague... and abstract concepts present coding problems'，举'harm'这一抽象模糊词正是为了说明抽象概念难以编程实现，因此选A，与紧随其后的'abstract concepts present coding problems'直接呼应。 - 关键句：A word such as \"harm\" is vague (what about emotional harm? Is replacing a human employ harm?), and abstract concepts present coding problems.","questionZh":"作者提到 Asimov 定律中的 \"harm\" 一词想表达什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What has the roboticist at the Bristol Robotics Laboratory found in his experiment?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Robots can be made as intelligent as human beings some day."},{"label":"B","text":"Robots can have moral issues encoded into their program."},{"label":"C","text":"Robots can have trouble making decisions in complex scenarios."},{"label":"D","text":"Robots can be programmed to perceive potential perils."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Robots can have trouble making decisions in complex scenarios.","answerZh":"机器人在复杂情境中可能难以做出决定。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后提到了Bristol Robotics Laboratory的机器人学家的实验，发现机器人在复杂情况下做决定时会遇到麻烦，'the robot choked 42 percent of the time, unable to decide which to save'，因此正确答案是C，'Robots can have trouble making decisions in complex scenarios'。","questionZh":"Bristol Robotics Laboratory 的机器人专家在实验中发现了什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2017_12_2-p2","title":"CET6 2017年12月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2017年12月 第2套","examDate":"2017年12月","year":"2017","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2017-12-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章展望物联网前景：设备互联将催生智能家居、智能建筑与智慧城市，关键挑战是善用海量数据创造效益，从而大幅提升生活质量。","mainIdeaEn":"The passage predicts the Internet of Things will bring smart homes, buildings and cities; the key challenge is creatively turning the flood of connected data into savings and tangible benefits.","answerCode":"DBCAA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先叹科技几年大飞跃，再看智能家居进万家，然后老板加码智能楼城，接着琢磨海量数据变现，最后联网随处可办公。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the example of iPhone 6s serve to show?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The huge capacity of the smartphones people now use."},{"label":"B","text":"The widespread use of smartphones all over the world."},{"label":"C","text":"The huge impact of new technology on people's everyday life."},{"label":"D","text":"The rapid technological progress in a very short period of time."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The rapid technological progress in a very short period of time.","answerZh":"极短时间内技术的飞速进步。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'The latest iPhone 6s, for example, has a dual-core processor and fits nicely into your pocket. By comparison, you would expect to find a technological specification like this on your standard laptop in an office anywhere in the world.'，说明iPhone 6s的技术规格与过去只能在笔记本电脑上找到的相媲美，体现了技术在短时间内的快速进步。","questionZh":"iPhone 6s 的例子是用来说明什么的?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What can we expect to see by the year 2020?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Apps for the internet of Things."},{"label":"B","text":"The popularization of smart homes."},{"label":"C","text":"The emergence of Millennials."},{"label":"D","text":"Total globalization of the world."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"The popularization of smart homes.","answerZh":"智能家居的普及。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'All researches agree that close to 25 billion devices, things and sensors will be connected by 2020... the fully connected home become a reality for large numbers of people worldwide.'，说明到2020年智能家居将普及。","questionZh":"到2020年,我们可以预见什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What will business owners do when they become aware of the benefits of the internet of Things?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Employ fewer workers in their operations."},{"label":"B","text":"Gain automatic control of their businesses."},{"label":"C","text":"Invest in more smart buildings and cities."},{"label":"D","text":"Embrace whatever new technology there is."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Invest in more smart buildings and cities.","answerZh":"投资更多的智能建筑和智慧城市。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章倒数第二段提到'leaders and business owners begin to wake up to the massive savings that technology can deliver...'，说明商业领袖和业主意识到技术带来的巨大节省，因此他们会投资于更多的智能建筑和城市。","questionZh":"当企业主意识到物联网的好处时,他们会怎么做?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What is the most exciting challenge when we possess more and more data?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"How to turn it to profitable use."},{"label":"B","text":"How to do real time data analysis."},{"label":"C","text":"How to link the actionable systems."},{"label":"D","text":"How to devise new ways to store it."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"How to turn it to profitable use.","answerZh":"如何将其转化为有利可图的用途。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'The biggest and most exciting challenge of this technology is how to creatively leverage this ever-growing amount of data to deliver cost savings, improvements and tangible benefits to both businesses and citizens of these smart cities.'，说明最令人兴奋的挑战是如何将越来越多的数据转化为利润。","questionZh":"当我们拥有越来越多的数据时,最令人兴奋的挑战是什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author think about working from anywhere and at any time?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is feasible with a connection to the internet."},{"label":"B","text":"It will thrive in smart buildings, cities and homes."},{"label":"C","text":"It is still a distant utopian dream for ordinary workers."},{"label":"D","text":"It will deliver tangible benefits to both boss and worker."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is feasible with a connection to the internet.","answerZh":"只要连上互联网就是可行的。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'Let's face it, it wasn't too long ago that the idea of working from anywhere and at any time was some form of a distant utopian dream, and yet now we can perform almost any office-based task from any location in the world as long as we have access to the internet.'，说明只要有互联网连接，就可以在任何地方和任何时间工作。","questionZh":"作者如何看待随时随地办公?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2017_12_3-p1","title":"CET6 2017年12月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2017年12月 第3套","examDate":"2017年12月","year":"2017","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2017-12-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"坦桑尼亚纳特龙湖盐碱致命却是全球火烈鸟主要繁殖地，火烈鸟与部分鱼类靠独特适应存活，而政府采碱计划或威胁这一独特生态。","mainIdeaEn":"Tanzania's deadly, caustic Lake Natron paradoxically hosts most of the world's flamingo breeding thanks to unique adaptations, but a planned soda-ash mining project may threaten this fragile ecosystem.","answerCode":"ACBAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先见毒湖万物难活，再挑水位躲开天敌，然后火烈鸟咸水安家，接着鱼儿躲进淡水湖，最后担心采矿毁生态。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What can we learn about Lake Natron?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is simply uninhabitable for most animals."},{"label":"B","text":"It remains little known to the outside world."},{"label":"C","text":"It is a breeding ground for a variety of birds."},{"label":"D","text":"It makes an ideal habitat for lots of predators."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is simply uninhabitable for most animals.","answerZh":"它根本不适合大多数动物生存。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段描述，Lake Natron的水具有极强的腐蚀性，可以烧伤未适应的动物的皮肤和眼睛，因此大多数动物都无法在此生存。选项A正确。","questionZh":"关于 Lake Natron,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"Flamingos nest only when the lake water is at a specific level so that their babies can.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"find safe shelter more easily."},{"label":"B","text":"grow thick feathers on their feet."},{"label":"C","text":"stay away from predators."},{"label":"D","text":"get accustomed to the salty water."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"stay away from predators.","answerZh":"远离捕食者。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到，火烈鸟只在湖水达到特定水平时筑巢，这样它们的幼鸟可以远离捕食者。因此选项C正确。","questionZh":"火烈鸟只在湖水处于特定水位时筑巢,这样它们的幼鸟才能怎么样?"},{"number":"48","stem":"Flamingos in the Rift Valley are unique in that .","options":[{"label":"A","text":"they can move swiftly across lagoons."},{"label":"B","text":"they can survive well in salty water."},{"label":"C","text":"they breed naturally in corrosive ditches."},{"label":"D","text":"they know where and when to nest."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"they can survive well in salty water.","answerZh":"它们能在咸水中很好地生存。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到火烈鸟的腿部皮肤非常坚韧，可以忍受盐水，这是它们在盐湖中生存的独特之处。因此选项B正确。","questionZh":"东非大裂谷的火烈鸟独特之处在于什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"Why can certain species of tilapia sometimes survive around Lake Natron?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They can take refuge in the less salty waters."},{"label":"B","text":"They can flee quickly enough from predators."},{"label":"C","text":"They can move freely from lagoon to lagoon."},{"label":"D","text":"They can stand the heat of the spring water."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They can take refuge in the less salty waters.","answerZh":"它们可以躲进盐度较低的水域。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到，某些罗非鱼物种能够在Lake Natron周围的泻湖中生存，因为这些泻湖的盐分较低。因此选项A正确。","questionZh":"为什么某些种类的罗非鱼有时能在 Lake Natron 周边存活?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What may be the consequence of the Tanzanian government's planned operation?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The accelerated extinction of flamingos."},{"label":"B","text":"The change of flamingos' migration route."},{"label":"C","text":"The overmining of Lake Natron's soda ash."},{"label":"D","text":"The disruption of Lake Natron's ecosystem."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The disruption of Lake Natron's ecosystem.","answerZh":"纳特龙湖生态系统遭到破坏。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到坦桑尼亚政府计划从Lake Natron开采苏打灰，环保人士担心这可能会破坏自然水循环和繁殖地，因此选项D正确。","questionZh":"坦桑尼亚政府计划中的工程可能带来什么后果?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2017_12_3-p2","title":"CET6 2017年12月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2017年12月 第3套","examDate":"2017年12月","year":"2017","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2017-12-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章讨论社会地位象征从有闲转向忙碌：知识经济下显得忙碌意味着被市场抢手、地位更高，但作者提醒人们仍应留出时间放松。","mainIdeaEn":"The passage examines how busyness has replaced leisure as a status symbol in knowledge economies, since being busy signals being in demand—yet the author still urges saving time to relax.","answerCode":"BCADC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先是年底不休接着干，再想当年闲人才高贵，然后越显忙越受敬，接着知识经济捧红忙碌，最后再忙也得留空歇。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do most employees plan to do towards the end of the year?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Go for a vacation."},{"label":"B","text":"Keep on working."},{"label":"C","text":"Set an objective for next year."},{"label":"D","text":"Review the year's achievements."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Keep on working.","answerZh":"继续工作。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'More than half of American workers don't use up all of their allotted vacation days each year'可知，超过一半的美国工人每年不用完他们所有的假期。因此，大多数员工计划在年底继续工作，答案为B。","questionZh":"大多数员工打算在年底做什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"How would people view dedication to work in the past?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They would regard it as a matter of course."},{"label":"B","text":"They would consider it a must for success."},{"label":"C","text":"They would look upon it with contempt."},{"label":"D","text":"They would deem it a trick of businessmen."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They would look upon it with contempt.","answerZh":"人们过去会对此嗤之以鼻。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'Not so long ago, people would have turned up their noses at that kind of dedication to the job'，说明过去人们会鄙视对工作的这种奉献，答案为C。","questionZh":"过去人们如何看待对工作的投入?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What did the researchers find through a series of experiments?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The busier one appears, the more respect one earns."},{"label":"B","text":"The more one works, the more one feels exploited."},{"label":"C","text":"The more knowledge one has, the more competent one will be."},{"label":"D","text":"The higher one's status, the more vacation time one will enjoy."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"The busier one appears, the more respect one earns.","answerZh":"一个人显得越忙碌,赢得的尊重就越多。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'The researchers illustrated just how much we've come to admire busyness, or at least the appearance of it'，说明人们越来越欣赏忙碌，或者至少是忙碌的外表。因此，A选项'The busier one appears, the more respect one earns'是正确答案。","questionZh":"研究人员通过一系列实验发现了什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What may account for the change of people's attitude towards being busy?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The fast pace of life in modern society."},{"label":"B","text":"The fierce competition in the job market."},{"label":"C","text":"The widespread use of computer technology."},{"label":"D","text":"The role of knowledge in the modern economy."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The role of knowledge in the modern economy.","answerZh":"知识在现代经济中的作用。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'the shift from leisure-as-status to busyness-as-status may be linked to the development of knowledge-intensive economics'，说明从休闲作为地位的象征转变为忙碌作为地位的象征可能与知识密集型经济的发展有关。因此，D选项'The role of knowledge in the modern economy'是正确答案。","questionZh":"什么可以解释人们对忙碌态度的转变?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author advise us to do at the end of the passage ?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Schedule our time properly for efficiency."},{"label":"B","text":"Plan our weekends in a meaningful way."},{"label":"C","text":"Plan time to relax however busy we are."},{"label":"D","text":"Avoid appearing busy when we are not."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Plan time to relax however busy we are.","answerZh":"无论多忙都要安排时间放松。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'at least consider leaving your weekends unscheduled. It's for your own good'，说明作者建议我们无论多忙都要计划时间来放松，答案为C。","questionZh":"在文章结尾,作者建议我们做什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2018_06_1-p1","title":"CET6 2018年06月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2018年06月 第1套","examDate":"2018年06月","year":"2018","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2018-06-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"西班牙埃布罗河三角洲稻农面临福寿螺与海水盐化双重威胁，科学家借咸水灭螺并培育抗盐水稻，以保欧洲稻米生产与湿地健康。","mainIdeaEn":"Facing invasive apple snails and rising salinity, scientists in Spain's Ebro Delta are harnessing seawater against the pest and breeding salt-tolerant rice to safeguard European rice production.","answerCode":"CDCBA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先看稻农打场大仗，再借海水以害制害，然后当务之急先治虫，接着蜗牛迟早侵全欧，最后育出抗盐良种。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"Why does the author mention the Spanish Civil War at the beginning of the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It had great impact on the life of Spanish rice farmers."},{"label":"B","text":"It is of great significance in the records of Spanish history."},{"label":"C","text":"Rice farmers in the Ebro Delta are waging a battle of similar importance."},{"label":"D","text":"Rice farmers in the Ebro Delta are experiencing as hard a time as in the war."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Rice farmers in the Ebro Delta are waging a battle of similar importance.","answerZh":"埃布罗河三角洲的稻农正在进行一场同样重要的战斗。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。作者在文章开头提到西班牙内战，是为了引出现在Ebro Delta地区稻农面临的不同战斗，即与巨型苹果蜗牛和海平面上升的斗争。'one that is pitting rice farmers against two enemies'与选项C中的'Rice farmers in the Ebro Delta are waging a battle of similar importance'相对应，因此C是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者为什么在文章开头提到西班牙内战?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What may be the most effective strategy for rice farmers to employ in fighting their enemies?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Striking the weaker enemy first."},{"label":"B","text":"Eliminating the enemy one by one."},{"label":"C","text":"Killing two birds with one stone."},{"label":"D","text":"Using one evil to combat the other."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Using one evil to combat the other.","answerZh":"以一害制另一害。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章提到，'The most promising strategy has become to harness one foe against the other.'，即利用一个敌人对抗另一个敌人，与选项D中的'Using one evil to combat the other'相对应，因此D是正确答案。","questionZh":"对稻农来说,对付敌害最有效的策略可能是什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What do we learn about \"Project Neurice\"?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its goals will have to be realized at a cost."},{"label":"B","text":"It aims to increase the yield of Spanish rice."},{"label":"C","text":"Its immediate priority is to bring the pest under control."},{"label":"D","text":"It tries to kill the snails with the help of climate change."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Its immediate priority is to bring the pest under control.","answerZh":"其当务之急是控制住这种害虫。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到，'The project has two sides,' says Xavier Serrat, Neurice project manager and researcher at the University of Barcelona. 'The short-term fight against the snail, and a mid- to long-term fight against climate change.' 说明项目的当务之急是控制害虫，与选项C中的'Its immediate priority is to bring the pest under control'相对应，因此C是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于 \"Project Neurice\",我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What does Neurice project manager say about the giant apple snail?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It can survive only on southern European wetlands."},{"label":"B","text":"It will invade other rice-growing regions of Europe."},{"label":"C","text":"It multiplies at a speed beyond human imagination."},{"label":"D","text":"It was introduced into the rice fields on purpose."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It will invade other rice-growing regions of Europe.","answerZh":"它将入侵欧洲其他水稻种植区。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到，'But the snail continues its march to new territory, says Serrat. 'The question is not if it will reach other rice-growing areas of Europe, but when.' 说明巨型苹果蜗牛将会入侵欧洲其他稻米种植区，与选项B中的'It will invade other rice-growing regions of Europe'相对应，因此B是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于福寿螺,Neurice 项目经理说了什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What is the ultimate goal of the EU-funded program?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cultivating ideal salt-resistant rice varieties."},{"label":"B","text":"Increasing the absorbency of the Spanish rice."},{"label":"C","text":"Introducing Spanish rice to the rest of Europe."},{"label":"D","text":"Popularizing the rice crossbreeding technology."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Cultivating ideal salt-resistant rice varieties.","answerZh":"培育理想的抗盐水稻品种。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到，'As an EU-funded effort, the search for salt-tolerant varieties of rice is taking place in all three countries.' 说明欧盟资助的项目旨在寻找耐盐的稻米品种，与选项A中的'Cultivating ideal salt-resistant rice varieties'相对应，因此A是正确答案。","questionZh":"这个由欧盟资助的项目的最终目标是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2018_06_1-p2","title":"CET6 2018年06月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2018年06月 第1套","examDate":"2018年06月","year":"2018","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2018-06-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"人们常说拍照会打断体验，但研究发现拍照让人更留心寻找想捕捉的画面，反而更投入、更享受，甚至只是想着拍照也有同样效果。","mainIdeaEn":"Contrary to the belief that photo-taking spoils experiences, experiments show it actually makes people more engaged and enjoy activities more—even merely planning to take a photo boosts enjoyment.","answerCode":"ADCBD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先忆当年拍照费劲记大事，再问拍照碍不碍享受，然后镜头让人更专注，接着看展拍照更入神，最后光想拍也添乐。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author say about photo-taking in the past?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It was a painstaking effort for recording life's major events."},{"label":"B","text":"It was a luxury that only a few wealthy people could enjoy."},{"label":"C","text":"It was a good way to preserve one's precious images."},{"label":"D","text":"It was a skill that required lots of practice to master."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It was a painstaking effort for recording life's major events.","answerZh":"过去拍照是为记录人生大事而付出的费力之举。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'Photography was once an expensive, laborious ordeal reserved for life's greatest milestones'可以得知，过去拍照是一种费力且昂贵的活动，仅用于记录生命中的重大事件。因此，选项A 'It was a painstaking effort for recording life's major events' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于过去的拍照,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"Kristin Diehl conducted a series of experiments on photo-taking to find out_________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"what kind of pleasure it would actually bring to photo-takers"},{"label":"B","text":"whether people enjoyed it when they did sightseeing"},{"label":"C","text":"how it could help to enrich people's life experiences"},{"label":"D","text":"whether it prevented people enjoying what they were doing"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"whether it prevented people enjoying what they were doing","answerZh":"拍照是否妨碍人们享受正在做的事情。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'But is there another cost, a deeper cost, to documenting a life experience instead of simply enjoying it?'和'Diehl and her fellow researchers wanted to find out if that was true'可以得知，Kristin Diehl 进行一系列实验是为了探究拍照是否会阻止人们享受他们正在做的事情。因此，选项D 'whether it prevented people enjoying what they were doing' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"Kristin Diehl 就拍照进行了一系列实验,是为了弄清什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What do the results of Diehl's experiments show about people taking pictures?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are distracted from what they are doing."},{"label":"B","text":"They can better remember what they see or do."},{"label":"C","text":"They are more absorbed in what catches their eye."},{"label":"D","text":"They can have a better understanding of the world."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They are more absorbed in what catches their eye.","answerZh":"他们更专注于吸引自己目光的东西。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段'Taking photos actually makes people enjoy what they're doing more, not less'和'That gets people more engaged in the experience, and they tend to enjoy it more'可以得知，拍照使人们更加专注于他们所做的事情，并且更加享受。因此，选项C 'They are more absorbed in what catches their eye' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于拍照的人,Diehl 的实验结果表明了什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What is found about museum visitors with the aid of eye-tracking glasses?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They come out with better photographs of the exhibits."},{"label":"B","text":"They focus more on the exhibits when taking pictures."},{"label":"C","text":"They have a better view of what are on display."},{"label":"D","text":"They follow the historical events more easily."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They focus more on the exhibits when taking pictures.","answerZh":"拍照时他们更加专注于展品。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第五段'People look longer at things they want to photograph'和'They report liking the exhibits more, too'可以得知，使用眼动追踪眼镜的博物馆参观者在拍照时更加关注展品。因此，选项B 'They focus more on the exhibits when taking pictures' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"借助眼动追踪眼镜,研究者对博物馆参观者有什么发现?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What do we learn from the last paragraph?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is better to make plans before taking photos."},{"label":"B","text":"Mental photos can be as beautiful as snapshots."},{"label":"C","text":"Photographers can derive great joy from the click of the camera."},{"label":"D","text":"Even the very thought of taking a photo can have a positive effect."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Even the very thought of taking a photo can have a positive effect.","answerZh":"即使只是想到要拍照也能产生积极的效果。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'just the act of planning to take a photo—and not actually taking it—had the same joy-boosting effect'可以得知，即使是拍照的想法也能产生积极的效果。因此，选项D 'Even the very thought of taking a photo can have a positive effect' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"从最后一段我们可以了解到什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2018_06_2-p1","title":"CET6 2018年06月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2018年06月 第2套","examDate":"2018年06月","year":"2018","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2018-06-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"机器人脸识别虽远胜人类记忆，但仍有局限：研究者用百万级MegaFace数据库测试发现，库越大准确率越低、难辨相似面孔，而公开的大规模人脸数据仍稀缺。","mainIdeaEn":"Machines outperform human memory at facial recognition, yet the MegaFace study shows accuracy drops as databases grow and lookalikes confuse algorithms, while researchers lack large public datasets to fix these limits.","answerCode":"ACDAB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先机器认脸又快又准，再建超大库摸清机器软肋，然后库越大准确率越掉，接着双胞胎脸分不清，最后缺公开大库没法练。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"Compared with human memory, machines can .","options":[{"label":"A","text":"identify human faces more efficiently"},{"label":"B","text":"tell a friend from a mere acquaintance"},{"label":"C","text":"store an unlimited number of human faces"},{"label":"D","text":"perceive images invisible to the human eye"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"identify human faces more efficiently","answerZh":"更高效地识别人脸。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'Give the right computer a massive database of faces, and it can process what it sees-then recognize a face it's told to find-with remarkable speed and precision'，说明机器在处理和识别人脸方面比人类记忆更有效。","questionZh":"与人类记忆相比,机器能做到什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"Why did researchers create MegaFace?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"To enlarge the volume of the facial-recognition database"},{"label":"B","text":"To increase the variety of facial-recognition software"},{"label":"C","text":"To understand computers' problems with facial recognition"},{"label":"D","text":"To reduce the complexity of facial-recognition algorithms"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"To understand computers' problems with facial recognition","answerZh":"为了理解计算机在人脸识别上的问题。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'To begin to figure out how computers are struggling, researchers at the University of Washington created a massive database of faces- they call it MegaFace'，说明研究人员创建MegaFace是为了理解计算机在面部识别上的问题。","questionZh":"研究人员为什么创建 MegaFace?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does the passage say about machine accuracy?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It falls short of researchers' expectations."},{"label":"B","text":"It improves with added computing power."},{"label":"C","text":"It varies greatly with different algorithms."},{"label":"D","text":"It decreases as the database size increases."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It decreases as the database size increases.","answerZh":"它随着数据库规模的扩大而下降。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第五段提到'As the databases grew, machine accuracy dipped across the board'，说明随着数据库规模的增加，机器的准确度下降了。","questionZh":"关于机器的准确率,文章说了什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What is said to be a shortcoming of facial-recognition machines?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They cannot easily tell apart people with near-identical appearances."},{"label":"B","text":"They have difficulty identifying changes in facial expressions"},{"label":"C","text":"They are not sensitive to minute changes in people's mood"},{"label":"D","text":"They have problems distinguishing people of the same age"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They cannot easily tell apart people with near-identical appearances.","answerZh":"它们难以区分外貌几乎相同的人。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到机器在区分长相极为相似的人时存在困难，说明面部识别机器的一个缺点是它们不能轻易区分长相几乎相同的人。","questionZh":"据说人脸识别机器有什么缺点?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What is the difficulty confronting researchers of facial-recognition machines?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"No computer is yet able to handle huge datasets of human faces"},{"label":"B","text":"There do not exist public databases with sufficient face sampler"},{"label":"C","text":"There are no appropriate algorithms to process the face samples"},{"label":"D","text":"They have trouble converting face datasets into the right format."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"There do not exist public databases with sufficient face sampler","answerZh":"目前没有拥有足够人脸样本的公共数据库。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'The trouble is, for many of the researchers who'd like to design systems to address these challenges, massive datasets for experimentation just don't exist'，说明研究人员面临的困难是缺乏足够大的公共数据库来处理人脸样本。","questionZh":"面部识别机器的研究者面临的困难是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2018_06_2-p2","title":"CET6 2018年06月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2018年06月 第2套","examDate":"2018年06月","year":"2018","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2018-06-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"针对“免费大学”呼声，作者指出教育成本不会消失：若由纳税人埋单，学生就该按起薪反映的社会需要选专业；结论是大学费用无论如何应由学生自己承担。","mainIdeaEn":"Rebutting calls for free college, the author argues costs never vanish: if taxpayers pay, they should dictate majors by market value, so either way students should fund their own education.","answerCode":"BACCD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先借巨债上学不理智，再免费大学根本不现实，然后花公款就该选实用专业，接着起薪高低见专业价值，最后学费还得自己掏。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author think of college students funding their education through loans?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They only expect to get huge returns."},{"label":"B","text":"They are acting in an irrational way."},{"label":"C","text":"They benefit at taxpayers expense."},{"label":"D","text":"They will regret doing so someday."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They are acting in an irrational way.","answerZh":"他们的做法是不理性的。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'many students are far from sensible'，表明作者认为学生通过贷款支付大学费用的行为是不合理的。因此，B选项'They are acting in an irrational way.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者如何看待大学生靠贷款支付学费?"},{"number":"52","stem":"In the author's opinion, free college education is .","options":[{"label":"A","text":"impractical"},{"label":"B","text":"unsustainable"},{"label":"C","text":"a goal to strive for"},{"label":"D","text":"a way to social equality"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"impractical","answerZh":"不切实际的","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'But the only way college could be free is if... As long as it's impossible to produce something from nothing, costs are absolutely a barrier.'，表明作者认为免费大学教育是不切实际的。因此，A选项'impractical'是正确答案。","questionZh":"在作者看来,免费大学教育______。"},{"number":"53","stem":"What should students do if taxpayers are to bear their college costs?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Work even harder to repay society."},{"label":"B","text":"Choose their subjects more carefully."},{"label":"C","text":"Choose majors that will serve society's practical needs."},{"label":"D","text":"Allow taxpayers to participate in college administration."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Choose majors that will serve society's practical needs.","answerZh":"选择能满足社会实际需求的专业。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'If we're going to force taxpayers to foot the bill for college degrees, students should only study those subjects that're of greatest benefit to taxpayers.'，表明如果纳税人承担大学费用，学生应该选择对社会最有益的专业。因此，C选项'Choose majors that will serve society's practical needs.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"如果由纳税人承担大学费用,学生应该做什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does the author say about the value of a student's college education?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is underestimated by profit-seeking employers."},{"label":"B","text":"It is to be proved by what they can do on the job."},{"label":"C","text":"It is well reflected in their average starting salary."},{"label":"D","text":"It is embodied in how they remove social barriers."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It is well reflected in their average starting salary.","answerZh":"它在学生的平均起薪中得到了很好的体现。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第五段提到'Average starting salaries give a clear indication of what type of training society needs its new workers to have... the value of what the student can produce is reflected in the wage employers are willing to pay the student to produce it.'，表明作者认为学生的大学教育价值反映在他们的平均起薪中。因此，C选项'It is well reflected in their average starting salary.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于学生大学教育的价值,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What message does the author want to convey in the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Students should think care fully whether to go to college"},{"label":"B","text":"Taxpayers should only finance the most gifted students."},{"label":"C","text":"The worth of a college education is open to debate."},{"label":"D","text":"College students should fund their own education."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"College students should fund their own education.","answerZh":"大学生应该自己承担教育费用。","explanation":"这是一道主旨大意题。文章最后一段提到'Or we can allow students both to choose their majors and pay for their education themselves. But in the end, one of two things is true: Either a college major is worth its cost or it isn't. If yes, taxpayer financing isn't needed If not taxpayer financing isn't desirable. Either way, taxpayers have no business paying for students' college education.'，表明作者认为大学生应该自己支付大学教育费用。因此，D选项'College students should fund their own education.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者想通过这篇文章传达什么信息?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2018_06_3-p1","title":"CET6 2018年06月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2018年06月 第3套","examDate":"2018年06月","year":"2018","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2018-06-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者认为普查局收入数据有缺陷，转而推介Jones-Klenow更全面的经济福祉衡量法：兼顾消费、闲暇、寿命与不平等，可跨国跨时期比较，揭示福祉是多维的。","mainIdeaEn":"Criticizing the Census Bureau's flawed income statistic, the author endorses the Jones-Klenow measure, which incorporates consumption, leisure, life expectancy, and inequality to assess economic welfare across countries and over time.","answerCode":"ADBDC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先普查报告数据靠不住，再新方法量福祉更全面，然后光比消费漏了闲暇寿命，接着还能纵向比年代，最后美国改善没报的多。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What does the author think of the 2015 report by the Census Bureau?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is based on questionable statistics."},{"label":"B","text":"It reflects the economic changes."},{"label":"C","text":"It evidences the improved welfare."},{"label":"D","text":"It provides much food for thought."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is based on questionable statistics.","answerZh":"它建立在可疑的统计数据之上。","explanation":"这是一道观点态度题。文章第二段提到了Census Bureau的报告存在问题，'Unfortunately, that conclusion puts too much weight on a useful, but flawed and incomplete, statistic'，表明作者认为该报告基于有问题的统计数据。","questionZh":"作者如何看待人口普查局2015年的报告?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the author say about the Jones-Klenow method?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is widely used to compare the economic growth across countries."},{"label":"B","text":"It revolutionizes the way of measuring ordinary people's livelihood."},{"label":"C","text":"It focuses on people's consumption rather than their average income."},{"label":"D","text":"It is a more comprehensive measure of people's economic well-being."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is a more comprehensive measure of people's economic well-being.","answerZh":"它是衡量人们经济福祉的一种更全面的方法。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到Jones-Klenow方法比平均收入更全面，'it is considerably more comprehensive than average income'，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于 Jones-Klenow 方法,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What do Jones and Klenow think of the comparison between France and the U.S. in terms of real consumption per person?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It reflected the existing big gap between the two economies."},{"label":"B","text":"It neglected many important indicators of people's welfare."},{"label":"C","text":"It covered up the differences between individual citizens."},{"label":"D","text":"It failed to count their difference in natural resources."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It neglected many important indicators of people's welfare.","answerZh":"这种比较忽略了许多衡量人们福祉的重要指标。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到比较法国和美国人均实际消费时忽略了休闲时间、寿命和经济不平等等因素，'that comparison omits other relevant factors'，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Jones 和 Klenow 如何看待法国与美国在人均实际消费上的比较?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What is an advantage of the Jones-Klenow method?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It can accurately pinpoint a country's current economic problems."},{"label":"B","text":"It can help to raise people's awareness of their economic well-being."},{"label":"C","text":"It can diagnose the causes of a country's slowing pace of economic improvement."},{"label":"D","text":"It can compare a country's economic conditions between different periods of time."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It can compare a country's economic conditions between different periods of time.","answerZh":"它可以比较一个国家不同时期的经济状况。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到Jones-Klenow方法可以用于比较不同时期一个国家的经济状况，'it can be used to assess economic performance both across countries and over time'，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Jones-Klenow 方法的一个优点是什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What can we infer from the passage about American people's economic well-being?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is much better than that of their European counterparts."},{"label":"B","text":"It has been on the decline ever since the turn of the century."},{"label":"C","text":"It has not improved as much as reported by the Census Bureau."},{"label":"D","text":"It has not been accurately assessed and reported since the mid-2000s."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It has not improved as much as reported by the Census Bureau.","answerZh":"其改善程度并不像人口普查局报告的那么大。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到根据Jones-Klenow方法，美国的经济福利自2007年以来持续改善，但改善的步伐明显放缓，'However, the pace of improvement has slowed markedly'，可以推断出美国人民的经济福利并没有像Census Bureau报告的那样改善那么多，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于美国人的经济福祉,我们能从文中推断出什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2018_06_3-p2","title":"CET6 2018年06月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2018年06月 第3套","examDate":"2018年06月","year":"2018","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2018-06-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章解释“决策疲劳”现象：连续做决定会耗尽判断力、让人守旧或做出糟糕选择，而替他人做决定则轻松无此负担；适度冒险对达成目标至关重要。","mainIdeaEn":"The passage explains decision fatigue: making many choices depletes judgment and breeds inaction, but deciding for others feels liberating and avoids the pitfall, while some risk-taking remains essential to achieving desired outcomes.","answerCode":"ACBDA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先自己拍板太多会累垮，再决策疲劳让人犯糊涂，然后替别人选反而轻松，接着累了就守旧不敢试新，最后想成事总得冒点险。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author say about people making decisions?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They may become exhausted by making too many decisions for themselves."},{"label":"B","text":"They are more cautious in making decisions for others than for themselves."},{"label":"C","text":"They tend to make decisions the way they think advantageous to them."},{"label":"D","text":"They show considerable differences in their decision-making abilities."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They may become exhausted by making too many decisions for themselves.","answerZh":"自己做太多决定可能会让人精疲力竭。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'Our own decision-making abilities can become depleted over the course of the day causing indecision or poor choices'，说明人们在一天中做太多决策后可能会感到疲惫。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于人们做决定,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does the example about the physicians illustrate?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Patients seldom receive due care towards the end of the day."},{"label":"B","text":"Prescription of antibiotics can be harmful to patients'health."},{"label":"C","text":"Decision fatigue may prevent people making wise decisions."},{"label":"D","text":"Medical doctors are especially susceptible to decision fatigue."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Decision fatigue may prevent people making wise decisions.","answerZh":"决策疲劳可能妨碍人们做出明智的决定。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'Physicians who have been on the job for several hours, for example, are more likely to prescribe antibiotics to patients when it's unwise to do so'，说明决策疲劳可能导致人们做出不明智的决策。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"医生的例子说明了什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"When do people feel less decision fatigue?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"When they take decision shortcuts."},{"label":"B","text":"When they help others to make decisions."},{"label":"C","text":"When they have major decisions to make."},{"label":"D","text":"When they have advisers to turn to."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"When they help others to make decisions.","answerZh":"在帮助别人做决定的时候。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'But decision fatigue goes away when you are making the decision for someone else'，说明当人们帮助他人做决策时，会感到较少的决策疲劳。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"人们在什么时候较少感到决策疲劳?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What are people likely to do when decision fatigue sets in?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They turn to physicians for advice."},{"label":"B","text":"They tend to make risky decisions."},{"label":"C","text":"They adopt a totally new perspective."},{"label":"D","text":"They refrain from trying anything new."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They refrain from trying anything new.","answerZh":"他们会避免尝试任何新事物。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'when people experience decision fatigue-when they are tired of making choices-they have a tendency to choose to go with status quo'，说明当决策疲劳发生时，人们倾向于不尝试新事物，维持现状。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"决策疲劳出现时,人们可能会怎么做?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the passage say about taking some risk in decision making?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is vital for one to reach the goal desired."},{"label":"B","text":"It is likely to entail serious consequences."},{"label":"C","text":"It will enable people to be more creative."},{"label":"D","text":"It will more often than not end in regret."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is vital for one to reach the goal desired.","answerZh":"冒一些风险对实现预期目标至关重要。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'In order to achieve a successful outcome or reward, some level of risk is almost always essential'，说明在决策中承担一定风险对于实现目标至关重要。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于在决策中承担一些风险,文章说了什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2018_12_1-p1","title":"CET6 2018年12月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2018年12月 第1套","examDate":"2018年12月","year":"2018","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2018-12-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章介绍农业机器人如何放牧、监测牲畜健康、查作物除杂草：面对大农场偏远难管与劳动力短缺，农民正推动这类技术，未来农场将越来越自动化。","mainIdeaEn":"Farm robots now herd livestock, monitor animal health, and inspect crops; driven by vast isolated farms and worsening labor shortages, farmers are embracing them, and future farms will grow increasingly autonomous.","answerCode":"BACDA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先农民能翘脚享清闲，再机器人包揽日常农活，然后实时直播农场动静，接着缺人手才催着上机器，最后未来农场越来越自动。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What may farmers be able to do with robots appearing on the farming scene?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Upgrade farm produce"},{"label":"B","text":"Enjoy more leisure hours."},{"label":"C","text":"Modify the genes of crops."},{"label":"D","text":"Cut down farming costs."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Enjoy more leisure hours.","answerZh":"享受更多闲暇时光。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到，由于劳动力短缺，农民推动了农业机器人技术的发展，使得他们能够更有效地维持大规模的农场运营，从而可以享受更多的休闲时间。因此，B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"随着机器人进入农业领域,农民或许能够做什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What will \"farmbots\" be expected to do?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Take up many of the farmers' routines."},{"label":"B","text":"Provide medical treatments for livestock."},{"label":"C","text":"Lead the trend in farming the world over."},{"label":"D","text":"Improve the quality of pastures for grazing."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Take up many of the farmers' routines.","answerZh":"承担农民的许多日常工作。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章提到，'Robots are currently under a two-year trial in Wales which will train \"farmbots\" to herd, monitor the health of livestock, and make sure there is enough pasture for them to graze on.' 这表明农场机器人将承担许多农民的日常任务，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"“farmbots” 将被期望做什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What can robots do when equipped with high-tech sensors and complex learning algorithms?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Help farmers choose the most efficient and safest passages."},{"label":"B","text":"Help farmers simplify their farming tasks and management."},{"label":"C","text":"Allow farmers to learn instantly what is occurring on the farm."},{"label":"D","text":"Allow farmers to give them real-time instructions on what to do."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Allow farmers to learn instantly what is occurring on the farm.","answerZh":"让农民即时了解农场里正在发生的情况。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到，'The robots also learn the most efficient and safest passages, and allow engineers and farmers to analyze and better optimize the attributes and tasks of the robot, as well as provide a live stream giving real-time feedback on exactly what is happening on the farms.' 这表明机器人可以实时反馈农场情况，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"配备高科技传感器和复杂学习算法后,机器人能做什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"Why are farmers pressing for robotic farming?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Farming costs are fast increasing."},{"label":"B","text":"Robotics technology is maturing."},{"label":"C","text":"Robotic farming is the trend."},{"label":"D","text":"Labor short is worsening"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Labor short is worsening","answerZh":"劳动力短缺日益严重。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到，'However, it is farmers that are pushing for the advancements due to ever-increasing labor vacancies, making it difficult to maintain large-scale operations.' 这表明农民由于劳动力短缺而推动农业机器人技术的发展，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"农民为什么迫切要求推行机器人农业?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does the author think future farms will be like?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"More and more automated."},{"label":"B","text":"More and more productive."},{"label":"C","text":"Larger and larger in scale."},{"label":"D","text":"Better and better in condition."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"More and more automated.","answerZh":"越来越自动化。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到，'Future farms will likely experience a greater deal of autonomy as robots take up more and more farm work efficiently.' 这表明未来农场将更加自动化，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者认为未来的农场会是什么样子?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2018_12_1-p2","title":"CET6 2018年12月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2018年12月 第1套","examDate":"2018年12月","year":"2018","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2018-12-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章强调公众理解科学对决策与政策的重要性：科学新闻是科普主渠道却可能失真夸大，作者认为科学家也应接受传播训练、提升与公众沟通的能力。","mainIdeaEn":"Public understanding of science shapes personal and policy decisions; since science journalism can distort findings, the author argues scientists themselves need communication training to convey research effectively to diverse audiences.","answerCode":"DBACD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先民众科学素养左右政策，再普通人得懂点医学常识，然后搭好媒体线利传播，接着报道跑偏会误导大众，最后科学家自己练沟通。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the example of climate change serve to show?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The importance of climate data is increasingly recognized."},{"label":"B","text":"Adequate government funding is vital to scientific research."},{"label":"C","text":"Government regulation helps the public understand science."},{"label":"D","text":"Common folks' scientific knowledge can sway policy making."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Common folks' scientific knowledge can sway policy making.","answerZh":"普通民众的科学素养可以影响政策制定。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'The issue of climate change also illustrates how the public acceptance and understanding of science (or the lack of it) can influence governmental decision-making with regard to regulation, science policy and research funding'，表明公众对科学的理解和接受程度可以影响政策制定。因此，D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"气候变化的例子旨在说明什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What should non-scientists do to ensure their quality of life?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Seek personalized medical assistance from doctors."},{"label":"B","text":"Acquire a basic understanding of medical science."},{"label":"C","text":"Have their individual genome sequenced."},{"label":"D","text":"Make informed use of animal models."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Acquire a basic understanding of medical science.","answerZh":"掌握基本的医学科学知识。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'more non-scientists will need to be comfortable analyzing complex scientific information to make decisions that directly affect their quality of life'，说明非科学家需要具备基本的医学科学知识来确保他们的生活质量。因此，B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"非科学工作者应该做什么来保障自己的生活质量?"},{"number":"53","stem":"Why is it important for scientists to build a good relationship with the media?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It helps them to effectively popularize new scientific information."},{"label":"B","text":"It enables the public to develop a positive attitude toward science."},{"label":"C","text":"It helps them to establish a more positive public image."},{"label":"D","text":"It enables them to apply their findings to public health."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It helps them to effectively popularize new scientific information.","answerZh":"这有助于他们有效地普及新的科学信息。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第五段提到'Good science journalists are specialists in making complex topics accessible to a general audience, while adhering to scientific accuracy'，说明科学家与媒体建立良好关系有助于有效地向公众普及新的科学信息。因此，A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"科学家与媒体建立良好关系为什么重要?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does the author say is the problem with science journalism?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is keen on transmitting sensational information."},{"label":"B","text":"It tends to oversimplify people's health problems."},{"label":"C","text":"It may give inaccurate or distorted information to the public."},{"label":"D","text":"It may provide information open to different interpretations."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It may give inaccurate or distorted information to the public.","answerZh":"它可能向公众传递不准确或被歪曲的信息。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第五段提到'Unfortunately, pieces of science journalism can also oversimplify and generalize their subject material to the point that the basic information conveyed is obscured or at worst, obviously wrong'，说明科学新闻可能会向公众提供不准确或扭曲的信息。因此，C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者认为科学新闻报道存在什么问题?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What should scientists do to impart their latest findings to the public more effectively?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Give training to science journalists."},{"label":"B","text":"Stimulate public interest in science."},{"label":"C","text":"Seek timely assistance from the media."},{"label":"D","text":"Improve their communication skills."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Improve their communication skills.","answerZh":"提高他们的沟通能力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'for one thing we underestimate how difficult it is for scientists to communicate effectively with a diversity of audiences, and for another most scientists do not receive formal training in science communication'，说明科学家需要提高他们的沟通技巧以更有效地向公众传达他们的最新发现。因此，D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"科学家应该怎么做才能更有效地向公众传播最新发现?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2018_12_2-p1","title":"CET6 2018年12月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2018年12月 第2套","examDate":"2018年12月","year":"2018","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2018-12-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"面对数学挂科率上升，美国教育界争论数学教学改革：Hacker主张削减高等数学、多教实用统计，其他教育者则认为应让数学更有趣易懂，帮助学生理解世界。","mainIdeaEn":"Amid rising math failure rates, American educators debate reform: Hacker wants less advanced math and more practical numeracy, while others argue math should be made accessible and engaging to help learners understand the world.","answerCode":"CABDA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先大众觉得高数用不上，再总被念叨不如中国，然后开课教实用基础数学，接着有人主张点燃好奇心，最后数学该帮人看懂世界。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What does the author say about ordinary Americans?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They struggle to solve math problems."},{"label":"B","text":"They think math is a complex subject."},{"label":"C","text":"They find high-level math of little use."},{"label":"D","text":"They work hard to learn high-level math."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They find high-level math of little use.","answerZh":"他们觉得高等数学没什么用处。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段中的描述，许多非数学专业或工程领域的美国人可能很难回忆起他们最后一次使用微积分是什么时候，这表明他们认为高级数学对他们的实际生活帮助不大。因此，选项C 'They find high-level math of little use' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于普通美国人,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What is the general complaint about America's math education according to Hacker?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"America is not doing as well as China."},{"label":"B","text":"Math professors are not doing a good job."},{"label":"C","text":"It doesn't help students develop their literacy."},{"label":"D","text":"There has hardly been any innovation for years."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"America is not doing as well as China.","answerZh":"美国做得不如中国好。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。题目问的是 Hacker 转述的'普遍抱怨'。原文 Hacker 说 'We hear on all sides that we're not teaching enough mathematics, and the Chinese are running rings around us.'（我们从各方面听到我们教的数学不够，中国人在绕着我们跑），这正是他所引述的、社会上普遍存在的抱怨——美国数学教育不如中国。故选项 A 'America is not doing as well as China' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"据 Hacker 所说,人们对美国数学教育的普遍抱怨是什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does Andrew Hacker's Numeracy 101 aim to do?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Allow students to learn high-level math step by step."},{"label":"B","text":"Enable students to make practical use of basic math."},{"label":"C","text":"Lay a solid foundation for advanced math studies."},{"label":"D","text":"Help students to develop their analytical abilities."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Enable students to make practical use of basic math.","answerZh":"让学生能够实际运用基础数学。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章中对Numeracy 101课程的描述，该课程旨在让学生分析公共信息，如联邦预算和公司报告，因此选项B 'Enable students to make practical use of basic math' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"Andrew Hacker 的 Numeracy 101 课程旨在做什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What does Maria Droujkova suggest math teachers do in class?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Make complex concepts easy to understand."},{"label":"B","text":"Start teaching children math at an early age."},{"label":"C","text":"Help children work wonders with calculus."},{"label":"D","text":"Try to arouse students' curiosity in math."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Try to arouse students' curiosity in math.","answerZh":"设法激发学生对数学的好奇心。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据Maria Droujkova的观点，她认为数学教育应该激发儿童的好奇心，所以选项D 'Try to arouse students' curiosity in math' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"Maria Droujkova 建议数学老师在课堂上做什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does Pamela Harris think should be the goal of math education?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"To enable learners to understand the world better."},{"label":"B","text":"To help learners to tell fake math from real math."},{"label":"C","text":"To broaden Americans' perspectives on math."},{"label":"D","text":"To exert influence on world development."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"To enable learners to understand the world better.","answerZh":"让学习者更好地理解世界。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据Pamela Harris的观点，她认为数学教育的目标应该是帮助学习者更好地理解世界，所以选项A 'To enable learners to understand the world better' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"Pamela Harris 认为数学教育的目标应该是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2018_12_2-p2","title":"CET6 2018年12月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2018年12月 第2套","examDate":"2018年12月","year":"2018","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2018-12-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"面对护士短缺，文章介绍日本领先的护理机器人：从送药查房到远程陪伴、拟人互动各有分工，它们承担琐碎劳务、解放护士，是协作而非取代人力。","mainIdeaEn":"Facing a nursing shortage, hospitals are turning to care robots, with Japan leading in delivery carts, telepresence companions, and humanlike helpers that handle routine tasks and free nurses, promising collaboration rather than replacement.","answerCode":"BCDAC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先日本机器人护理领跑，再送药车少碰病人先上岗，然后远程机器人牵线医患家属，接着有的像真人般陪聊，最后不抢护士饭碗。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author say about Japan?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It delivers the best medications for the elderly."},{"label":"B","text":"It takes the lead in providing robotic care."},{"label":"C","text":"It provides retraining for registered nurses."},{"label":"D","text":"It sets the trend in future robotics technology."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It takes the lead in providing robotic care.","answerZh":"它在提供机器人护理方面处于领先地位。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段中的信息，'Japan is ahead of the curve when it comes to this trend'，说明日本在提供机器人护理方面处于领先地位，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于日本,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What do we learn about the robot Terapio?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has been put to use in many Japanese hospitals."},{"label":"B","text":"It provides specific individualized care to patients."},{"label":"C","text":"It does not have much direct contact with patients."},{"label":"D","text":"It has not revolutionized medical service in Japan."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It does not have much direct contact with patients.","answerZh":"它与病人没有太多直接接触。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段中的信息，'This type of robot will likely be one of the first to be implemented in hospitals because it has fairly minimal patient contact'，说明Terapio机器人与病人的直接接触很少，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于机器人 Terapio,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What are telepresence robots designed to do?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Directly interact with patients to prevent them from feeling lonely."},{"label":"B","text":"Cater to the needs of patients for recovering their cognitive capacity."},{"label":"C","text":"Closely monitor the patients' movements and conditions around the clock."},{"label":"D","text":"Facilitate communication between patients and doctors or family members."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Facilitate communication between patients and doctors or family members.","answerZh":"促进病人与医生或家人之间的沟通。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段中的信息，'Telepresence robots such as MantaroBot, Vgo, and Giraff can be controlled through a computer, smartphone, or tablet, allowing family members or doctors to remotely monitor patients or Skype them'，说明远程呈现机器人的设计目的是促进病人与医生或家庭成员之间的沟通，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"远程临场机器人被设计来做什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What is one special feature of the robot Actroid F?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It interacts with patients just like a human companion."},{"label":"B","text":"It operates quietly without patients realizing its presence."},{"label":"C","text":"It likes to engage in everyday conversations with patients."},{"label":"D","text":"It uses body language even more effectively than words."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It interacts with patients just like a human companion.","answerZh":"它像人类伙伴一样与病人互动。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段中的信息，'This conversational robot companion has cameras in its eyes, which allow it to track patients and use appropriate facial expressions and body language in its interactions'，说明Actroid F机器人与病人的互动就像人类伴侣一样，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"机器人 Actroid F 的一个特别之处是什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What can we infer from the last paragraph?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Doctors and surgeons will soon be laid off."},{"label":"B","text":"The robotics industry will soon take off."},{"label":"C","text":"Robots will not make nurses redundant."},{"label":"D","text":"Collaboration will not replace competition."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Robots will not make nurses redundant.","answerZh":"机器人不会让护士变得多余。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章最后一段中的信息，'This is one industry where it seems the integration of robots will lead to collaboration, not replacement'，可以推断出机器人不会使护士失业，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"从最后一段我们可以推断出什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2018_12_3-p1","title":"CET6 2018年12月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2018年12月 第3套","examDate":"2018年12月","year":"2018","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2018-12-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"杜克大学研究发现，幼年注意力是学业成功最稳定的预测因素，早期注意力问题使高中毕业率降低四成，同伴接纳也影响成绩，故教育应兼顾学业与社交软技能。","mainIdeaEn":"A Duke study finds early attention skills most consistently predict academic success, with attention problems cutting graduation rates by 40 percent; peer acceptance also matters, so education should take a comprehensive approach.","answerCode":"BCDAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先研究找学业成功预测器，再控住无关变量保靠谱，然后走神一点也拖成绩，接着人缘好的分更高，最后教育得全面兼顾。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What is the focus of the new study from Duke University?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The contributors to children's early attention."},{"label":"B","text":"The predictors of children's academic success."},{"label":"C","text":"The factors that affect children's emotional well-being."},{"label":"D","text":"The determinants of children's development of social skills."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"The predictors of children's academic success.","answerZh":"预测儿童学业成功的因素。","explanation":"这是一道主旨大意题。文章第一段提到'early academic attention and socio-emotional skills and how each contributed to academic success into young adulthood'，明确指出研究关注的是影响儿童学业成功的早期因素。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"杜克大学这项新研究的焦点是什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"How did the researchers ensure that their findings are valid?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"By attaching equal importance to all possible variables examined."},{"label":"B","text":"By collecting as many typical samples as were necessary."},{"label":"C","text":"By preventing them from being affected by factors not under study."},{"label":"D","text":"By focusing on the family background of the children being studied."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"By preventing them from being affected by factors not under study.","answerZh":"通过防止研究对象受到研究范围之外因素的影响。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'This was after controlling for IQ, socio-economic status and academic skills at school entry'，说明研究者通过控制其他变量来确保研究结果的有效性。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"研究人员如何确保他们的研究结果有效?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What do we learn from the findings of the Duke study?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Modest students are generally more attentive than their contemporaries."},{"label":"B","text":"There are more children with attention difficulties than previously thought."},{"label":"C","text":"Attention deficit hyperactivity disorder accounts for most academic failures."},{"label":"D","text":"Children's academic performance may suffer from even slight inattention."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Children's academic performance may suffer from even slight inattention.","answerZh":"即使是轻微的注意力不集中也可能损害儿童的学业表现。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'early attention skills were the most consistent predictor of academic success'，说明即使是轻微的注意力不集中也会影响学业表现。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"从杜克大学研究的结果中我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What does the Duke study find about children better accepted by peers?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They do better academically."},{"label":"B","text":"They are easy to get on with."},{"label":"C","text":"They are teachers' favorites."},{"label":"D","text":"They care less about grades."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They do better academically.","answerZh":"他们的学业表现更好。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'Children not as liked by their first-grade peers had slightly lower grades in fifth grade, while those with higher social acceptance had higher grades'，说明被同伴更接受的孩子学业表现更好。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"杜克大学的研究发现,更受同伴接纳的孩子怎么样?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What can we conclude from the Duke study?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Children's success is related to their learning environment."},{"label":"B","text":"School curriculum should cover a greater variety of subjects."},{"label":"C","text":"Social skills are playing a key role in children's development."},{"label":"D","text":"An all-round approach should be adopted in school education."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"An all-round approach should be adopted in school education.","answerZh":"学校教育应采取全面发展的方式。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到'student success requires a more comprehensive approach, one that incorporates not only academic skills but also social, self-regulatory and attention skills'，说明儿童成功需要全面的方法，包括学业技能和社会技能等。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"从杜克大学的研究中我们可以得出什么结论?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2018_12_3-p2","title":"CET6 2018年12月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2018年12月 第3套","examDate":"2018年12月","year":"2018","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2018-12-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"在iPhone问世十周年之际，作者指出智能手机一个不那么显眼的好处：它能持续记录人的行为与环境，正在革新行为科学，推动心理学研究走向真实生活情境。","mainIdeaEn":"Marking the iPhone's tenth anniversary, the author highlights a less obvious benefit of smartphones: by continuously recording behavior and context, they are revolutionizing behavioral science and pushing psychology toward real-world research.","answerCode":"CDBAB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先负面影响隐蔽却惹忧，再手机大大革新行为研究，然后老方法靠实验室加自述，接着帮人揪出异常苗头，最后研究越来越贴近生活。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author say about the negative impact of smartphones?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has been overshadowed by the positive impact."},{"label":"B","text":"It has more often than not been taken for granted."},{"label":"C","text":"It is not so obvious but has caused some concern."},{"label":"D","text":"It is subtle but should by no means be overstated."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It is not so obvious but has caused some concern.","answerZh":"它不那么明显,但已引起一些担忧。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'often the advantages of convenient mobile technology are both obvious and taken for granted, leaving more subtle topics for concerned discussion'，说明智能手机的负面影响并不是显而易见的，但确实引起了人们的担忧。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于智能手机的负面影响,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What is considered a less obvious advantage of smartphone technology?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It systematically records real human interactions."},{"label":"B","text":"It helps people benefit from technological advances."},{"label":"C","text":"It brings people into closer contact with each other."},{"label":"D","text":"It greatly improves research on human behavior."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It greatly improves research on human behavior.","answerZh":"它极大地改进了对人类行为的研究。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'the potential for smartphone technology to revolutionize behavioral science'，说明智能手机技术对人类行为研究的巨大影响是一个不太明显的优势。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"智能手机技术有什么不太明显的优势?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What characterizes traditional psychological research?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is based on huge amounts of carefully collected data."},{"label":"B","text":"It relies on lab observations and participants' reports."},{"label":"C","text":"It makes use of the questionnaire method."},{"label":"D","text":"It is often expensive and time-consuming."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It relies on lab observations and participants' reports.","answerZh":"它依赖实验室观察和参与者的自我报告。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'in which people report how they behaved in real life or participate in relatively short and artificial laboratory-based tasks'，说明传统心理学研究依赖于实验室观察和参与者报告。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"传统心理学研究有什么特点?"},{"number":"54","stem":"How will future psychological studies benefit individuals?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"By helping them pin down their unusual behaviors."},{"label":"B","text":"By helping them maintain a positive state of mind."},{"label":"C","text":"By helping them live their lives in a unique way."},{"label":"D","text":"By helping them cope with abnormal situations."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"By helping them pin down their unusual behaviors.","answerZh":"通过帮助人们准确发现自己的异常行为。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'the right combination of data and analysis can also help individuals identify unique characteristics of their own behavior'，说明未来心理学研究将帮助个体识别自己行为的独特特征，包括可能需要干预的情况。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"未来的心理学研究将如何使个人受益?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What do we learn about current psychological studies?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are going through a period of painful transition."},{"label":"B","text":"They are increasingly focused on real-life situations."},{"label":"C","text":"They are conducted in a more rigorous manner."},{"label":"D","text":"They are mainly targeted towards undergraduates."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They are increasingly focused on real-life situations.","answerZh":"它们越来越关注现实生活情境。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'Today, the field is in transition, moving away from a focus on laboratory studies with undergraduate participants towards more complex, real-world situations studied with more diverse groups of people'，说明当前心理学研究越来越关注现实生活情境。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于当前的心理学研究,我们可以了解到什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2019_06_2-p1","title":"CET6 2019年06月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2019年06月 第2套","examDate":"2019年06月","year":"2019","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2019-06-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"美国演员工会因谈判破裂对多家游戏公司罢工：游戏业利润丰厚，配音演员要求按销量获得追加酬金并提高透明度，公司方则称改薪酬制度会带来更多问题。","mainIdeaEn":"After failed negotiations, SAG-AFTRA voice actors struck against major video game publishers, demanding sales-based secondary compensation and transparency, while the companies warn changing the pay system would create more problems.","answerCode":"DACAB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先谈判谈崩宣布罢工，再游戏业赚得盆满钵满，然后配音员要销量分成，接着接活连演啥都不知道，最后厂方说改薪制麻烦更多。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"Why did SAG-AFTRA declare a strike against some video game publishers?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The labor contract between them had been violated."},{"label":"B","text":"Its appeal to renegotiate the contract had been rejected."},{"label":"C","text":"It had been cheated repeatedly in the 19 months of talks."},{"label":"D","text":"The negotiations between them had broken down."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The negotiations between them had broken down.","answerZh":"双方之间的谈判破裂了。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段中的'The strike comes in light of an unsuccessful 19 months of negotiations after the existing labor contract known as the Interactive Media Agreement expired in late 2014'，可以确定SAG-AFTRA宣布罢工是因为与视频游戏发行商之间的谈判破裂。","questionZh":"SAG-AFTRA 为什么宣布对一些电子游戏发行商罢工?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about the video gaming industry?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has reaped huge profits in recent years."},{"label":"B","text":"It has become more open and transparent."},{"label":"C","text":"It has attracted many famous voice actors."},{"label":"D","text":"It has invested a lot in its domestic market."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It has reaped huge profits in recent years.","answerZh":"它近年来获得了巨额利润。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章中'The Los Angeles Times reports that the industry is in the midst of an intense increase in cash flow. In 2015, gaming produced $23.5 billion in domestic revenue.'，可以知道视频游戏行业近年来获得了巨大的利润。","questionZh":"关于电子游戏行业,我们能从文中了解到什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What are the voice actors demanding?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"More regular employment."},{"label":"B","text":"A non-discriminatory contract."},{"label":"C","text":"Extra pay based on sales revenues."},{"label":"D","text":"A limit on the maximum work hours."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Extra pay based on sales revenues.","answerZh":"基于销售收入的额外报酬。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章中'So the voice actors are pushing for the idea of secondary compensation—a performance bonus every time a game sells 2 million copies or downloads, or reaches 2 million subscribers, with a cap at 8 million.'，可以知道配音演员要求根据销售收入获得额外的报酬。","questionZh":"配音演员们在要求什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What does Keythe Farley say about voice actors?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are kept in the dark about many details of their job."},{"label":"B","text":"They are discriminated against in the gaming industry."},{"label":"C","text":"They are not paid on a regular basis."},{"label":"D","text":"They are not employed full-time."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They are kept in the dark about many details of their job.","answerZh":"他们对自己工作的许多细节一无所知。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章中'Another major complaint from the actors is the secrecy of the industry... I can't imagine if there's any other acting job in the world where you don't know what show you're in, when you're hired...'，可以知道配音演员对于工作的许多细节一无所知。","questionZh":"关于配音演员,Keythe Farley 说了什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What is the argument of lawyer Scott Witlin?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Voice actors should have a pay raise if they prove to be top craftsmen."},{"label":"B","text":"Changing the pay system would cause the industry more problems."},{"label":"C","text":"Voice actors are mere craftsmen, not professional performers."},{"label":"D","text":"Paying voice actors on an hourly basis is in line with the law."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Changing the pay system would cause the industry more problems.","answerZh":"改变薪酬制度会给这个行业带来更多问题。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章中'Scott Witlin... says, \"if we pay them under a vastly different system than the people who do the 99.9 percent of the work, that's going to create far more problems for the video game companies.\"'，可以知道律师Scott Witlin认为改变薪酬体系会给游戏公司带来更多问题。","questionZh":"律师 Scott Witlin 的论点是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2019_06_2-p2","title":"CET6 2019年06月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2019年06月 第2套","examDate":"2019年06月","year":"2019","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2019-06-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"白宫发布新太空政策，由商务部管理太空交通、规范卫星发射，要求发射方分析碎片风险，旨在缓解太空垃圾与碰撞隐患，并期望为全球商业航天树立标准。","mainIdeaEn":"A new White House space policy tasks the Commerce Department with managing space traffic and satellite launches, tightening debris analysis requirements to prevent collisions and hopefully setting norms for the global spaceflight industry.","answerCode":"DCADB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先新政策要理顺太空交通，再商务部管卫星发射，然后盼定出全球航天规范，接着发射前彻查添不添碎片，最后研发技术清垃圾。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What is the purpose of the new U.S. space policy?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"To lay out general guidelines for space exploration."},{"label":"B","text":"To encourage companies to join in space programs."},{"label":"C","text":"To make the best use of satellites in space."},{"label":"D","text":"To improve traffic conditions in space."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"To improve traffic conditions in space.","answerZh":"改善太空中的交通状况。","explanation":"这是一道主旨大意题。文章第一段提到了新空间政策的目的是缓解空间碎片的影响并管理空间交通，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"美国新太空政策的目的是什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What is the Department of Commerce expected to do under the new policy?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Reduce debris in space."},{"label":"B","text":"Monitor satellite operations."},{"label":"C","text":"Regulate the launching of new satellites."},{"label":"D","text":"Update satellite communications technology."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Regulate the launching of new satellites.","answerZh":"监管新卫星的发射。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段，商务部将确保新发射的卫星不会使用会干扰现有卫星的无线电频率，并安排新卫星的发射时间，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"根据新政策,商务部被期望做什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does the U.S. government hope to do with the new space policy?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Set international standards for the space flight industry."},{"label":"B","text":"Monopolize the space industry by developing a set of norms."},{"label":"C","text":"Facilitate commercial space flights throughout the world."},{"label":"D","text":"Promote international collaboration in space exploration."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Set international standards for the space flight industry.","answerZh":"为太空飞行产业制定国际标准。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章第二段提到希望该政策将有助于在全球范围内标准化商业太空飞行行业的一套规范，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"美国政府希望通过新太空政策做什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What is a space vehicle launching entity required to do according to the current U.S. Government Orbital Debris Mitigation Standard Practices?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Give an estimate of how long its debris will stay in space."},{"label":"B","text":"Account for the debris it has released into space at any time."},{"label":"C","text":"Provide a detailed plan for managing the space debris it creates."},{"label":"D","text":"Make a thorough analysis of any possible addition to space debris."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Make a thorough analysis of any possible addition to space debris.","answerZh":"对任何可能新增的太空碎片进行彻底分析。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段，发射实体需要对任何可能增加的空间碎片进行彻底分析，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"按照现行美国政府轨道碎片减缓标准做法,航天器发射实体须做什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What are space agencies and companies aiming to do at present?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Recycle used space vehicles before they turn into debris."},{"label":"B","text":"Develop technology to address the space debris problem."},{"label":"C","text":"Limit the amount of debris entering space."},{"label":"D","text":"Cooperate closely to retrieve space debris."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Develop technology to address the space debris problem.","answerZh":"开发技术以解决太空碎片问题。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段，全球的机构和公司正在开发技术来处理或捕获空间碎片，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"目前各航天机构和公司的目标是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2019_06_3-p1","title":"CET6 2019年06月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2019年06月 第3套","examDate":"2019年06月","year":"2019","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2019-06-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者结合自身经历与新研究提出，职场中“无所谓的关系”并非坏事：不必与同事亲密无间，保持中性疏淡的关系反而有效率、自尊与专注等实证好处。","mainIdeaEn":"Drawing on personal experience and new research, the author argues workplace indifferent relationships are legitimate: colleagues need not be close friends, and emotionally neutral ties bring proven benefits like efficiency and focus.","answerCode":"DABCD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先发现同事情谊没那么要紧，再不和睦拖累效率，然后职场关系可有可无，接着社交懒人懒得经营，最后淡淡之交反提效。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What did the author realize when he re-entered the corporate world?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Making new friends with his workmates was not as easy as he had anticipated."},{"label":"B","text":"Cultivating positive interpersonal relationships helped him expel solitary feelings."},{"label":"C","text":"Working in the corporate world requires more interpersonal skills than self-employment."},{"label":"D","text":"Building close relationships with his colleagues was not as important as he had expected."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Building close relationships with his colleagues was not as important as he had expected.","answerZh":"与同事建立密切关系并不像他原先预想的那么重要。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到作者重新进入全职工作后，意识到与同事建立朋友关系并不像他预期的那样重要。因此，正确答案是D选项。","questionZh":"作者重返企业界时意识到了什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What do we learn from many studies about collegial relationships?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Inharmonious relationships have an adverse effect on productivity."},{"label":"B","text":"Harmonious relationships are what many companies aim to cultivate."},{"label":"C","text":"Close collegial relationships contribute very little to product quality."},{"label":"D","text":"Conflicting relationships in the workplace exist almost everywhere."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Inharmonious relationships have an adverse effect on productivity.","answerZh":"不和谐的关系会对生产效率产生不利影响。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到许多研究探讨了同事关系如何帮助解决影响生产力和工作质量的一系列工作场所问题，如团队冲突、嫉妒、破坏、愤怒等。因此，正确答案是A选项，不和谐的关系对生产力有负面影响。","questionZh":"关于同事关系,我们能从许多研究中了解到什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What can be inferred about relationships at work from an academic analysis?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They should be cultivated."},{"label":"B","text":"They are virtually irrelevant."},{"label":"C","text":"They are vital to corporate culture."},{"label":"D","text":"They should be reasonably intimate."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They are virtually irrelevant.","answerZh":"职场关系实际上无关紧要。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章第三段提到了'indifferent relationships'的概念，即工作关系可以合理地是非亲密的、无关紧要的、不重要的，甚至是可以替代的。因此，可以推断出工作关系实际上是几乎无关紧要的，正确答案是B选项。","questionZh":"从一项学术分析中,关于职场关系可以推断出什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What does the author say about people who are socially lazy?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They feel uncomfortable when engaging in social interactions."},{"label":"B","text":"They often find themselves in confrontation with their colleagues."},{"label":"C","text":"They are Unwilling to make efforts to maintain Workplace relationships."},{"label":"D","text":"They lack basic communication skills in dealing with interpersonal issues."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They are Unwilling to make efforts to maintain Workplace relationships.","answerZh":"他们不愿意花力气去维系职场关系。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'Indifference is also the preferred option among those who are socially lazy. Maintaining relationships over the long term takes effort. For some of us, too much effort.'，表明社交懒惰的人不愿意努力维持工作关系。因此，正确答案是C选项。","questionZh":"关于社交上懒惰的人,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What is one of the benefits of indifferent relationships?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They provide fun at Work."},{"label":"B","text":"They help control emotions."},{"label":"C","text":"They help resolve differences."},{"label":"D","text":"They improve Work efficiency."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They improve Work efficiency.","answerZh":"它们能提高工作效率。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'One of those is efficiency. Less time chatting and socializing means more time working and churning.'，表明冷漠关系的一个好处是提高工作效率。因此，正确答案是D选项。","questionZh":"淡漠关系的好处之一是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2019_06_3-p2","title":"CET6 2019年06月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2019年06月 第3套","examDate":"2019年06月","year":"2019","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2019-06-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"作者担忧人工智能将超越许多人类独有能力，主张人类不应与机器比拼理性，而要培养机器难以模仿的创造力，用创意提供价值来证明自身存在的意义。","mainIdeaEn":"As AI surpasses abilities once uniquely human, the author argues we should complement machine rationality rather than compete with it, fostering creativity that AI cannot yet emulate to keep providing value.","answerCode":"BCDAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先愁人类本领不再独有，再看谷歌自驾猛进，然后AI还学不会创造力，接着学校该养原创思维，最后靠创意供价值保住饭碗。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What is the author's greatest concern about the use of AI?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Computers are performing lots of creative tasks."},{"label":"B","text":"Many abilities will cease to be unique to human beings."},{"label":"C","text":"Computers may become more rational than humans."},{"label":"D","text":"Many human skills are fast becoming outdated."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Many abilities will cease to be unique to human beings.","answerZh":"许多能力将不再为人类所独有。","explanation":"这是一道观点态度题。文章中作者表达了对人工智能发展的担忧，特别是在'I worry about my six-year-old son. What will his place be in a world where machines beat us in one area after another?'这句话中，作者担心的是人类的许多能力将不再是独一无二的，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者对 AI 应用最大的担忧是什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What impresses the author most in the field of AI?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Google's experimental driverless cars require little human intervention."},{"label":"B","text":"Google's cars have surpassed his driving ability in just a single year."},{"label":"C","text":"Google has made huge progress in autonomous driving in a short time."},{"label":"D","text":"Google has become a world leader in the field of autonomous driving."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Google has made huge progress in autonomous driving in a short time.","answerZh":"Google 在短时间内在自动驾驶领域取得了巨大进展。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到'But even more impressive is the progress in just a single year: human interventions fell from 0.8 times per thousand miles to 0.2, a 400% improvement.'这句话强调了谷歌在自动驾驶领域短时间内取得的巨大进步，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"在 AI 领域,最让作者印象深刻的是什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about creativity?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is rational."},{"label":"B","text":"It is predictable."},{"label":"C","text":"It is human specific."},{"label":"D","text":"It is yet to be emulated by AI."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is yet to be emulated by AI.","answerZh":"人工智能尚无法模仿创造力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到'So far, machines have a pretty hard time emulating creativity, arbitrary enough not to be predicted by a computer, and yet more than simple randomness.'这句话说明创造力是人工智能尚未模仿的人类特质，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于创造力,我们能从文中了解到什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What should schools help children do in the era of AI?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cultivate original thinking."},{"label":"B","text":"Learn to work independently."},{"label":"C","text":"Compete with smart machines."},{"label":"D","text":"Understand howAI works."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Cultivate original thinking.","answerZh":"培养原创性思维。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到'So we must aim to complement the rationality of the machine, rather than to compete with it. If I'm right, we should foster a creative spirit because a dose of illogical creativity will complement the rationality of the machine.'这句话强调了在人工智能时代，学校应该帮助孩子们培养原创思维，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"在 AI 时代,学校应该帮助孩子做什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"How can we humans justify our future existence?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"By constantly outsmarting computers."},{"label":"B","text":"By adopting a long-term perspective."},{"label":"C","text":"By rationally compromising with AI."},{"label":"D","text":"By providing value with our creativity."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"By providing value with our creativity.","answerZh":"通过用我们的创造力提供价值。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到'Because if we aren't, we won't be providing much value in future ecosystems, and that may put in question the foundation for our existence.'这句话暗示了如果我们不能通过创造力提供价值，我们的存在基础可能会受到质疑，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"我们人类如何证明自己未来存在的价值?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2019_12_1-p1","title":"CET6 2019年12月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2019年12月 第1套","examDate":"2019年12月","year":"2019","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2019-12-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章探讨撒谎的心理机制：撒谎需要复杂的心理活动，受诱惑、疲劳、旁人注视等条件影响；研究还显示撒谎会改变大脑，不受惩罚时谎言会越来越大。","mainIdeaEn":"The passage explores the psychology of lying: it takes complex mental work, depends on temptation and social conditions, and dishonesty rewires the brain so unpunished lies grow bigger over time.","answerCode":"ADCBB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先小孩撒谎算会换位思考，再撒谎烧脑费工夫，然后诱惑太大就想骗，接着有人盯着就不敢，最后没惩罚谎越撒越大。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"Why do some experts consider lying a milestone in a child's development?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It shows they have the ability to view complex situations from different angles."},{"label":"B","text":"It indicates they have an ability more remarkable than crawling and walking."},{"label":"C","text":"It represents their ability to actively interact with people around them."},{"label":"D","text":"It involves the coordination of both their mental and physical abilities."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It shows they have the ability to view complex situations from different angles.","answerZh":"这表明他们有能力从不同角度看待复杂情况。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段，'Some experts even consider lying a developmental milestone, like crawling and walking, because it requires sophisticated planning, attention and the ability to see a situation from someone else's perspective to manipulate them.' 这句话说明了专家认为说谎是儿童发展中的一个里程碑，因为它需要复杂的计划、注意力以及从他人视角看问题的能力，因此选项A是正确答案。","questionZh":"为什么一些专家认为说谎是儿童发育的一个里程碑?"},{"number":"47","stem":"Why does the Harvard neuroscientist say that lying takes work?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is hard to choose from several options."},{"label":"B","text":"It is difficult to sound natural or plausible."},{"label":"C","text":"It requires speedy blood flow into one's brain."},{"label":"D","text":"It involves lots of sophisticated mental activity."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It involves lots of sophisticated mental activity.","answerZh":"撒谎涉及大量复杂的心理活动。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段，'But others opted to lie, and they showed increased activity in their frontal parietal control network, which is involved in difficult or complex thinking.' 这句话说明了说谎需要复杂的思考，因此选项D是正确答案。","questionZh":"哈佛神经科学家为什么说说谎很费力?"},{"number":"48","stem":"Under what circumstances do people tend to lie?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"When they become too emotional."},{"label":"B","text":"When they face too much peer pressure."},{"label":"C","text":"When the temptation is too strong."},{"label":"D","text":"When the consequences are not imminent."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"When the temptation is too strong.","answerZh":"当诱惑太大的时候。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段，'We are more likely to lie, when we are able to rationalise it, when we are stressed and fatigued or see others being dishonest.' 这句话说明了当诱惑很强时，人们更倾向于说谎，因此选项C是正确答案。","questionZh":"人们在什么情况下倾向于说谎?"},{"number":"49","stem":"When are people less likely to lie?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"When they are worn out and stressed."},{"label":"B","text":"When they are under watchful eyes."},{"label":"C","text":"When they think in a rational way."},{"label":"D","text":"When they have a clear conscience."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"When they are under watchful eyes.","answerZh":"当他们处于他人的注视之下时。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段，'And we are less likely to lie when we have moral reminders or when we think others are watching.' 这句话说明了当人们处于监视之下时，他们不太可能说谎，因此选项B是正确答案。","questionZh":"人们在什么时候不太可能说谎?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does the author say will happen when a liar does not get punished?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They may feel justified."},{"label":"B","text":"They will tell bigger lies."},{"label":"C","text":"They will become complacent."},{"label":"D","text":"They may mix lies and truths."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They will tell bigger lies.","answerZh":"他们会撒更大的谎。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段，'This means that if you give people multiple opportunities to lie for their own benefit, they start with little lies which get bigger over time.' 这句话说明了如果说谎者没有受到惩罚，他们会从较小的谎言开始，随着时间的推移，谎言会变得越来越严重，因此选项B是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者说,说谎者不受惩罚时会发生什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2019_12_1-p2","title":"CET6 2019年12月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2019年12月 第1套","examDate":"2019年12月","year":"2019","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2019-12-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章介绍美国西北太平洋卡斯卡迪亚地区两万人参与的地震海啸演习：该断层的特大地震迟早会来，官方希望通过演练协调应对、把伤亡降到最低。","mainIdeaEn":"The Pacific Northwest is running a massive earthquake-and-tsunami drill for the inevitable megathrust quake on the Cascadia fault, hoping coordinated preparation will minimize casualties when The Big One strikes.","answerCode":"CADBC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先大家伙是场超级天灾，再演习备战强震海啸，然后断层积压应力猛释放，接着官方想着少死伤，最后它早晚要来只等时间。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does \"The Big One\" refer to?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A gigantic geological fault."},{"label":"B","text":"A large-scale exercise to prepare for disasters."},{"label":"C","text":"A massive natural catastrophe."},{"label":"D","text":"A huge tsunami on the Caledonia coast."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"A massive natural catastrophe.","answerZh":"一场巨大的自然灾难。","explanation":"这是一道词义猜测题。根据文章第一段'Here's how the Pacific Northwest is preparing for 'The Big One'. It's the mother of all disaster drills for what could be the worst disaster in American history.'可知，'The Big One'指的是一场可能发生的最严重的灾难，即一场大规模的自然灾害。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"“The Big One” 指的是什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What is the purpose of the Cascadia Rising drill?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"To prepare people for a major earthquake and tsunami."},{"label":"B","text":"To increase residents' awareness of imminent disasters."},{"label":"C","text":"To teach people how to adapt to post-disaster life."},{"label":"D","text":"To cope with the aftermath of a possible earthquake."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"To prepare people for a major earthquake and tsunami.","answerZh":"让人们为大地震和海啸做好准备。","explanation":"这是一道写作目的题。文章第二段提到'The Cascadia Rising drill gives area residents and emergency responders a chance to practice what to do in case of a 9.0-magnitude earthquake and tsunami along one of the nation's dangerous—and underestimated—faults.'说明Cascadia Rising演习的目的是为了让当地居民和紧急救援人员为可能发生的大地震和海啸做好准备。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Cascadia Rising 演习的目的是什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What happens in case of a megathrust earthquake according to the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Two plates merge into one."},{"label":"B","text":"A variety of forces converge."},{"label":"C","text":"Boundaries blur between plates."},{"label":"D","text":"Enormous stress is released."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Enormous stress is released.","answerZh":"巨大的应力会被释放出来。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'During a megathrust event, all of that stress releases and some of the world's most powerful earthquakes occur.'可知，在一场megathrust地震中，长期积累的压力会释放，导致一些世界上最强烈的地震发生。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"据文章所述,发生大型逆冲地震时会怎样?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What do the officials hope to achieve through the drills?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Coordinating various disaster-relief efforts."},{"label":"B","text":"Reducing casualties in the event of a disaster."},{"label":"C","text":"Minimizing property loss caused by disaster."},{"label":"D","text":"Establishing disaster and emergency management."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Reducing casualties in the event of a disaster.","answerZh":"在灾难发生时减少人员伤亡。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'Not all casualties can necessarily be prevented—but by coordinating across local, state, and even national borders, officials hope that the worst-case scenario can be averted.'可知，通过跨地区、州甚至国家边界的协调，官员们希望避免最坏的情况发生，即减少灾难造成的伤亡。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"官员们希望通过演习达到什么目的?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author say about \"The Big One\"?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Whether it will occur remains to be seen."},{"label":"B","text":"How it will arrive is too early to predict."},{"label":"C","text":"Its occurrence is just a matter of time."},{"label":"D","text":"It keeps haunting Cascadia residents."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Its occurrence is just a matter of time.","answerZh":"它的发生只是时间问题。","explanation":"这是一道观点态度题。根据文章最后一段'For hundreds of thousands of Cascadia residents. 'The Big One' isn't a question of if, only when.'可知，对于成千上万的Cascadia居民来说，'The Big One'不是会不会发生的问题，而是何时发生的问题，说明作者认为'The Big One'的发生只是时间问题。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于 “The Big One”,作者说了什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2019_12_2-p1","title":"CET6 2019年12月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2019年12月 第2套","examDate":"2019年12月","year":"2019","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2019-12-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章以先天心脏缺陷婴儿母亲为例说明态度的力量：态度是后天习得并可改变的，想法未必等于行动，改变态度最有效的办法是先按理想的方式去行动。","mainIdeaEn":"Attitudes, our learned ways of interpreting and reacting to the world, are powerful but do not always predict behavior; the best way to change an attitude is to start acting as you wish to feel.","answerCode":"CAADB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先态度决定怎么应对环境，再偶像言行塑造它，然后想法未必变行动，接着只怪缺乏意志力，最后照理想的样子先做起来。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about attitude?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It shapes our beliefs and ideologies."},{"label":"B","text":"It improves our psychological wellbeing."},{"label":"C","text":"It determines how we respond to our immediate environment."},{"label":"D","text":"It changes the way we think, feel and interact with one another."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It determines how we respond to our immediate environment.","answerZh":"态度决定我们如何应对身边的环境。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。第二段指出'We use our attitudes to filter, interpret and react to the world around us'，说明态度决定我们如何回应周围环境。因此选项C正确。 - 关键句：We use our attitudes to filter, interpret and react to the world around us.","questionZh":"关于态度,我们能从文中了解到什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What can contribute to the refinement of one's attitude, according to the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Their idols' behaviors."},{"label":"B","text":"Their educational level."},{"label":"C","text":"Their contact with the opposite gender."},{"label":"D","text":"Their interaction with different cultures."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Their idols' behaviors.","answerZh":"他们偶像的行为。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。第三段提到态度受到自己认同的人的行为影响，包括'the people you admire'，对应偶像的行为。因此选项A正确。 - 关键句：your attitudes are further refined by the behavior of those with whom you identify—your family, those of your gender and culture, and the people you admire.","questionZh":"据文章所述,什么有助于完善一个人的态度?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What do many studies find about people's feelings and thoughts?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They may not suggest how a person is going to behave."},{"label":"B","text":"They are in a way consistent with a person's mentality."},{"label":"C","text":"They may not find expression in interpersonal relations."},{"label":"D","text":"They are in line with a person's behavior no matter what."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They may not suggest how a person is going to behave.","answerZh":"它们可能无法预示一个人将如何行动。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。第四段指出'feelings and thoughts don't necessarily predict behavior'，即感受与想法不一定能预示行为。因此选项A正确。 - 关键句：many studies have found that feelings and thoughts don't necessarily predict behavior.","questionZh":"关于人们的情感和思想,许多研究发现了什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"How come many people don't do what they believe is good?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They can't afford the time."},{"label":"B","text":"They have no idea how to."},{"label":"C","text":"They are hypocritical."},{"label":"D","text":"They lack willpower."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They lack willpower.","answerZh":"他们缺乏意志力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。第四段指出'it takes awareness, effort and courage'才能把信念付诸行动，缺乏意志力是关键原因。因此选项D正确。 - 关键句：it takes awareness, effort and courage to go beyond merely stating that you believe something is a good idea.","questionZh":"为什么许多人不去做自己认为好的事情?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What is proposed as a strategy to change attitudes?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Changing things that require one's immediate attention."},{"label":"B","text":"Starting to act in a way that embodies one's aspirations."},{"label":"C","text":"Adjusting one's behavior gradually over a period of time."},{"label":"D","text":"Considering ways of reducing one's psychological burdens."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Starting to act in a way that embodies one's aspirations.","answerZh":"开始以体现自己抱负的方式行动。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。最后一段建议'start behaving as if you already feel and think the way you'd prefer to'，即按照希望具有的态度去行动。因此选项B正确。 - 关键句：One of the most effective ways to change an attitude is to start behaving as if you already feel and think the way you'd prefer to.","questionZh":"文中提出了什么改变态度的策略?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2019_12_2-p2","title":"CET6 2019年12月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2019年12月 第2套","examDate":"2019年12月","year":"2019","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2019-12-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"绿色和平报告指出南极磷虾捕捞逼近企鹅与鲸鱼栖息地、威胁生态，呼吁渔业退出拟议保护区；管理机构CCAMLR则称要在保护与可持续捕捞间求平衡。","mainIdeaEn":"A Greenpeace report warns krill fishing near Antarctic penguin and whale habitats threatens the ecosystem and urges the industry to quit proposed sanctuaries, while regulator CCAMLR seeks balance between conservation and sustainable fishing.","answerCode":"CBADC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先捕虾船贴着企鹅鲸鱼转，再全球呼吁建保护区，然后劝渔业避开候选区，接着管委会想护着生态捕，最后自称出知识出经验。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does Greenpeace's study find about krill fishing?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It caused a great many penguins and whales to migrate."},{"label":"B","text":"It was depriving penguins and whales of their habitats."},{"label":"C","text":"It was carried out too close to the habitats of penguins and whales."},{"label":"D","text":"It posed an unprecedented threat to the wildlife around Antarctica."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It was carried out too close to the habitats of penguins and whales.","answerZh":"捕捞磷虾的地点离企鹅和鲸鱼的栖息地太近。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'The study by Greenpeace analysed the movements of krill fishing vessels in the region and found they were increasingly operating in the immediate vicinity of penguin colonies and whale-feeding grounds'，可以确定C选项'It was carried out too close to the habitats of penguins and whales.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于磷虾捕捞,Greenpeace 的研究发现了什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"For what purpose has a global campaign been launched?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"To reduce the impact of climate change on Antarctica."},{"label":"B","text":"To establish conservation areas in the Antarctic region."},{"label":"C","text":"To regulate krill fishing operations in the Antarctic seas."},{"label":"D","text":"To publicise the concern about the impact of krill fishing."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"To establish conservation areas in the Antarctic region.","answerZh":"为了在南极地区建立保护区。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'A global campaign has been launched to turn a huge tract of Antarctic seas into ocean sanctuaries protecting wildlife and banning not just krill fishing, but all fishing.'，可以确定B选项'To establish conservation areas in the Antarctic region.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"发起这场全球运动的目的是什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What is Greenpeace's recommendation to the krill industry?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Opting to operate away from the suggested conservation areas."},{"label":"B","text":"Volunteering to protect the endangered species in the Antarctic."},{"label":"C","text":"Refraining from krill fishing throughout the breeding season."},{"label":"D","text":"Showing its sense of responsibility by leading the global campaign."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Opting to operate away from the suggested conservation areas.","answerZh":"选择在拟议保护区以外的海域作业。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'Frida Bengtsson from Greenpeace's Protect the Antarctic campaign said: If the krill industry wants to show it's a responsible player, then it should be voluntarily getting out of any area which is being proposed as an ocean sanctuary, and should instead be backing the protection of these huge tracts of the Antarctic.'，可以确定A选项'Opting to operate away from the suggested conservation areas.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"Greenpeace 对磷虾产业提出了什么建议?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What did CCAMLR aim to do according to its science manager?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Raise public awareness of the vulnerability of Antarctic species."},{"label":"B","text":"Ban all commercial fishing operations in the Southern Ocean."},{"label":"C","text":"Keep the penguin colonies from all fishing interference."},{"label":"D","text":"Sustain fishing without damaging the Antarctic ecosystem."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Sustain fishing without damaging the Antarctic ecosystem.","answerZh":"在不破坏南极生态系统的前提下维持捕捞。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段'He said although more fishing was taking place nearer penguin colonies it was often happening later in the season when these colonies were empty. The creation of a system of marine protected areas is a key part of ongoing scientific and policy discussions in CCAMLR, he added. Our long-term operation in the region depends on a healthy and thriving Antarctic marine ecosystem, which is why we have always had an open dialogue with the environmental non-governmental organisations.'，可以确定D选项'Sustain fishing without damaging the Antarctic ecosystem.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"据其科学主管所说,CCAMLR 的目标是什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"How does CCAMLR define its role in the conservation of the Antarctic environment?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A coordinator in policy discussions."},{"label":"B","text":"An authority on big data analysis."},{"label":"C","text":"A provider of the needed expertise."},{"label":"D","text":"An initiator of marine sanctuaries."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"A provider of the needed expertise.","answerZh":"所需专业知识的提供者。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'Keith Reid, a science manager at CCAMLR, said that the organisation sought a balance between protection, conservation and sustainable fishing in the Southern Ocean. We are not the ones to decide on the establishment of marine protected areas, but we hope to contribute positively with our knowledge and experience.'，可以确定C选项'A provider of the needed expertise.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"CCAMLR 如何界定自己在南极环境保护中的角色?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2019_12_3-p1","title":"CET6 2019年12月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2019年12月 第3套","examDate":"2019年12月","year":"2019","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2019-12-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者批评英国学校日益流行的昂贵游学在贫富学生间制造分化，认为学校应通过全员筹款等方式扩大机会，至少不应加剧弱势学生的被排斥感。","mainIdeaEn":"The author criticizes increasingly expensive school trips for deepening divides between rich and poor pupils, arguing schools must extend opportunities to all and at least avoid fostering new divisions.","answerCode":"BBDAC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先护娃又教他面对世界，再贵游学拉大贫富差，然后全员活动养社区，接着没觉多好也让娃去，最后别再造新差距。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What does the author say the best schools should do?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Prepare students to both challenge and change the divided unequal society."},{"label":"B","text":"Protect students from social pressures and enable them to face the world."},{"label":"C","text":"Motivate students to develop their physical as well as intellectual abilities."},{"label":"D","text":"Encourage students to be ambitious and help them to achieve their goals."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Protect students from social pressures and enable them to face the world.","answerZh":"保护学生免受社会压力,并使他们能够面对世界。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'The best seek to alleviate the external pressures on their pupils while equipping them better to understand and handle the world outside-at once sheltering them and broadening their horizons'，可以看出作者认为最好的学校应该在保护学生免受社会压力的同时，帮助他们更好地理解和面对外部世界。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者认为最好的学校应该做什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the author think about school field trips?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They enable students from different backgrounds to mix with each other."},{"label":"B","text":"They widen the gap between privileged and disadvantaged students."},{"label":"C","text":"They give the disadvantaged students a chance to see the world."},{"label":"D","text":"They only benefit students with rich relatives and neighbors."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They widen the gap between privileged and disadvantaged students.","answerZh":"它们扩大了优越学生与弱势学生之间的差距。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'Introducing a fundraising requirement for students does not help, as better-off children can tap up richer aunts and neighbors'和第五段'Educational outings help bright but disadvantaged students to get better scores in A-level tests'，可以看出学校郊游加剧了特权和弱势学生之间的差距。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者如何看待学校的实地考察活动?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does the author suggest can help build community spirit?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Events aiming to improve community services."},{"label":"B","text":"Activities that help to fuel students' ingenuity."},{"label":"C","text":"Events that require mutual understanding."},{"label":"D","text":"Activities involving all students on campus."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Activities involving all students on campus.","answerZh":"让校内所有学生都参与的活动。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段'Methods such as whole-school fundraising, with the proceeds pooled, can help to extend opportunities and fuel community spirit'，可以看出作者认为全校性的筹款活动，将收益集中起来，可以帮助扩大机会并激发社区精神。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者建议用什么来培养社区精神?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What do we learn about low-income parents regarding school field trips?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They want their children to participate even though they don't see much benefit."},{"label":"B","text":"They don't want their kids to participate but find it hard to keep them from going."},{"label":"C","text":"They don't want their kids to miss any chance to broaden their horizons despite."},{"label":"D","text":"They want their children to experience adventures but they don't want them to run risks."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They want their children to participate even though they don't see much benefit.","answerZh":"他们希望孩子参加,尽管自己并不觉得有多大好处。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。证据句为'Even parents who can see that a trip is little more than a party or celebration may well feel guilt that their child is left behind'——即便那些看清旅行不过是聚会、没什么实际价值（don't see much benefit）的家长，也会因孩子被落下而内疚，说明他们仍希望孩子参加。这与A'They want their children to participate even though they don't see much benefit'完全吻合。故选A。 - 关键句：Even parents who can see that a trip is little more than a party or celebration may well feel guilt that their child is left behind.","questionZh":"关于低收入家长与学校实地考察,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What is the author's expectation of schools?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bringing a community together with ingenuity."},{"label":"B","text":"Resolving the existing discrepancies in society."},{"label":"C","text":"Avoiding creating new gaps among students."},{"label":"D","text":"Giving poor students preferential treatment."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Avoiding creating new gaps among students.","answerZh":"避免在学生之间制造新的差距。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'But the least we should expect is that they do not foster divisions and exclude those who are already disadvantaged'，可以看出作者期望学校不要制造新的鸿沟，排除那些已经处于不利地位的人。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者对学校的期望是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2019_12_3-p2","title":"CET6 2019年12月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2019年12月 第3套","examDate":"2019年12月","year":"2019","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2019-12-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"新研究警告：若变暖与过度捕捞持续，本世纪末七成王企鹅将被迫迁移繁殖地或灭绝；企鹅作为生态指示物种，其困境预示整个南极海洋环境的未来。","mainIdeaEn":"A new study warns that global warming and overfishing could force 70 percent of Antarctic king penguins to relocate or face extinction by 2100, signaling danger for the whole marine ecosystem.","answerCode":"ACDAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先王企鹅要濒临灭绝，再捕捞变暖害惨磷虾，然后大多数得另找繁殖地，接着幼崽等不到吃的，最后适合安家的岛没几个。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What will happen by 2100, according to the new study?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"King penguins in the Antarctic will be on the verge of dying out."},{"label":"B","text":"Sea water will rise to a much higher level around the Antarctic."},{"label":"C","text":"The melting ice cover will destroy the great Antarctic wilderness."},{"label":"D","text":"The pristine waters around the Antarctic will disappear forever."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"King penguins in the Antarctic will be on the verge of dying out.","answerZh":"南极的王企鹅将濒临灭绝。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段的'Unless current greenhouse gas emissions drop, 70 percent of king penguins—1.1 million breeding pairs—will be forced to relocate their breeding grounds, or face extinction by 2100'可知，到2100年，如果不减少温室气体排放，70%的帝企鹅将被迫迁移繁殖地或面临灭绝。因此，A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"根据这项新研究,到2100年会发生什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What do we learn from the findings of a separate study?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Shrinking krill population and rising temperatures could force Antarctic whales to migrate."},{"label":"B","text":"Human activities have accelerated climate change in the Antarctic region in recent years."},{"label":"C","text":"Industrial fishing and climate change are threatening the Antarctic krill population."},{"label":"D","text":"Krill fishing in the Antarctic has worsened the pollution of the pristine waters."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Industrial fishing and climate change are threatening the Antarctic krill population.","answerZh":"工业捕捞和气候变化正威胁着南极磷虾的数量。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。证据句为'Earlier this month a separate study found that a combination of climate change and industrial fishing is threatening the krill population in Antarctic waters'——另一项研究发现气候变化与工业捕捞共同威胁着南极水域的磷虾种群。这与C'Industrial fishing and climate change are threatening the Antarctic krill population'吻合。故选C。 - 关键句：a combination of climate change and industrial fishing is threatening the krill population in Antarctic waters","questionZh":"从另一项研究的结果中我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does the passage say about king penguins?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They will turn out to be the second-largest species of birds to become extinct."},{"label":"B","text":"Many of them will have to migrate to isolated islands in the Southern Ocean."},{"label":"C","text":"They feed primarily on only a few kinds of krill in the Antarctic Polar Front."},{"label":"D","text":"The majority of them may have to find new breeding grounds in the future."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The majority of them may have to find new breeding grounds in the future.","answerZh":"它们中的大多数将来可能不得不寻找新的繁殖地。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段的'Unless current greenhouse gas emissions drop, 70 percent of king penguins—1.1 million breeding pairs—will be forced to relocate their breeding grounds, or face extinction by 2100'可知，未来大多数帝企鹅可能需要寻找新的繁殖地。因此，D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于王企鹅,文章说了什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What happens when sea levels rise in the Antarctic?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Many baby king penguins can't have food in time."},{"label":"B","text":"Many king penguins could no longer live on krill."},{"label":"C","text":"Whales will invade king penguins' breeding grounds."},{"label":"D","text":"Whales will have to travel long distances to find food."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Many baby king penguins can't have food in time.","answerZh":"许多王企鹅幼崽无法及时获得食物。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段的'As the ocean warms, a body of water called the Antarctic Polar Front—an upward movement of nutrient-rich sea that supports a huge abundance of marine life—is being pushed further south. This means that king penguins, which feed on fish and krill in this body of water, have to travel further to their feeding grounds, leaving their hungry chicks for longer'可知，随着海平面上升，帝企鹅需要更远地前往觅食地，导致它们的幼崽长时间得不到食物。因此，A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"南极海平面上升时会发生什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What do we learn about the Southern Ocean?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The king penguins there are reluctant to leave for new breeding grounds."},{"label":"B","text":"Its conversation is key to the sustainable propagation of Antarctic species."},{"label":"C","text":"It is most likely to become the ultimate retreat for species like the king penguin."},{"label":"D","text":"Only a few of its islands can serve as huge breeding grounds for king penguins."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Only a few of its islands can serve as huge breeding grounds for king penguins.","answerZh":"其中只有少数岛屿能成为王企鹅的大型繁殖地。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第三段的'Only a handful of islands in the Southern Ocean are suitable for sustaining large breeding colonies'可知，南大洋只有少数岛屿适合维持大型繁殖群。因此，D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于南大洋,我们可以了解到什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2020_07_1-p1","title":"CET6 2020年07月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2020年07月 第1套","examDate":"2020年07月","year":"2020","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2020-07-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章介绍“积极压力”运动：以科技圈人士为主的追随者通过冰浴、极端锻炼等自我施压来增强耐受与健康，但医学专家警告这类做法并非人人适用。","mainIdeaEn":"The positive stress movement, popular among tech workers, embraces extreme practices like ice baths to build tolerance and wellbeing, though medical professionals warn such stress may be risky for some people.","answerCode":"BDADB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先这群人偏说压力是好事，再用冰浴苦行走极端，然后靠它扛住工作压力，接着日常压力练不出耐受，最后医生提醒别忽视副作用。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do we learn about followers of the positive stress movement?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are usually quite sensitive to different types of stress."},{"label":"B","text":"They hold a different view on stress from the popular one."},{"label":"C","text":"They derive much pleasure from living a very hectic life."},{"label":"D","text":"They gain a competitive edge by enjoying good health."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They hold a different view on stress from the popular one.","answerZh":"他们对压力的看法与流行观点不同。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'a very different view of stress is gaining popularity'，表明积极压力运动的追随者持有与普遍观点不同的对压力的看法。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于积极压力运动的追随者,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What do followers of the positive stress movement usually do to put their ideas into practice?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They keep changing their living habits."},{"label":"B","text":"They network with influential figures."},{"label":"C","text":"They seek jobs in tech industries."},{"label":"D","text":"They apply extreme tactics."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They apply extreme tactics.","answerZh":"他们采用极端的手段。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'positive stress practitioners seek out some combination of extreme temperatures, restrictive diets, punishing exercise routines and general discomfort'，说明积极压力运动的追随者通过应用极端手段来实践他们的理念。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"积极压力运动的追随者通常怎样将他们的理念付诸实践?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does Zachary Rapp say about his unconventional practices?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They help him combat stress from work."},{"label":"B","text":"They enable him to cut down living expenses."},{"label":"C","text":"They enable him to recover from injuries and illnesses."},{"label":"D","text":"They help him get three companies enlisted all at once."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They help him combat stress from work.","answerZh":"这些做法帮助他对抗工作压力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'He believes that these practices, which put stress on his body, actually make him feel less stress from work'，说明Rapp认为这些非常规做法有助于他应对工作压力。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于自己的非常规做法,Zachary Rapp 说了什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What can be inferred from the passage about day-to-day stress?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is harmful to one's physical and mental health."},{"label":"B","text":"It does not differ in essence from positive stress."},{"label":"C","text":"It is something everybody has to live with."},{"label":"D","text":"It does not help build up one's tolerance."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It does not help build up one's tolerance.","answerZh":"它无助于增强人的抗压能力。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章倒数第二段提到'the difference between day-to-day stress, like the kind we feel when moving apartments, and positive stress is that the latter involves pushing the body to extremes and forcing it to build up a tolerance'，说明日常压力与积极压力的区别在于后者通过将身体推向极端来建立耐受力，而日常压力并不涉及建立耐受力。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于日常压力,可以从文中推断出什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What do some medical professionals think of positive stress?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its true effect remains to be verified."},{"label":"B","text":"Its side effects should not be ignored."},{"label":"C","text":"Its effect varies considerably from person to person."},{"label":"D","text":"Its practitioners should not take it as a form of therapy."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Its side effects should not be ignored.","answerZh":"其副作用不应被忽视。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'some medical professionals argue that positive stress is not for everyone, and that it might even be dangerous for people who are unhealthy or older'，说明一些医学专业人士认为积极压力并非适合每个人，对不健康或年长的人来说甚至可能是危险的。这暗示了积极压力的副作用不应被忽视。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"一些医学专业人士如何看待积极压力?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2020_07_1-p2","title":"CET6 2020年07月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2020年07月 第1套","examDate":"2020年07月","year":"2020","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2020-07-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章围绕狩猎对环境是好是坏展开正反争论：有人视其为控制种群的自然手段，反对者斥其残忍且破坏生态，作者最后指出绿色领袖正倡导猎人与环保组织合作。","mainIdeaEn":"The passage weighs arguments over whether hunting helps or harms the environment, from population control to cruelty and ecological damage, noting green leaders now urge cooperation between hunters and environmentalists.","answerCode":"BCAAC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先讽刺狩猎反成解药，再骂执照费搅乱生态，然后多数猎物根本不过剩，接着利于生态才算正当，最后倡猎人环保派联手。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author say sounds ironic?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Some predators may often turn out to be prey of other predators."},{"label":"B","text":"Hunting may also be a solution to the problem caused by hunting."},{"label":"C","text":"The species of prey animals continue to vary despite humans' hunting."},{"label":"D","text":"The number of prey animals keeps rising despite environmental change."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Hunting may also be a solution to the problem caused by hunting.","answerZh":"狩猎或许也是解决狩猎所造成问题的一种办法。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到，一些人认为由于人类消灭了许多动物捕食者，狩猎成为了减少那些现在繁殖超过环境承载能力的猎物种群的一种自然方式，这听起来很讽刺。因此，B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者说什么听起来具有讽刺意味?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does Glenn Kirk think of charging hunters' license fees?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It keeps the game population under control."},{"label":"B","text":"It turns hunting into a sport of the rich."},{"label":"C","text":"It leads to ecological imbalance."},{"label":"D","text":"It helps stop killing for pleasure."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It leads to ecological imbalance.","answerZh":"它会导致生态失衡。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到Glenn Kirk认为，尽管猎人声称狩猎可以保持野生动物种群平衡，但实际上猎人的执照费用被用来'操纵一些猎物种群过度繁殖，牺牲了更多非猎物种群，导致生物多样性、遗传完整性和生态平衡的丧失'，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Glenn Kirk 如何看待收取猎人执照费?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What is the argument of the Humane Society of the United States against hunting?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Overpopulation is not an issue for most hunted animals."},{"label":"B","text":"Hunting deprives animal populations of their food sources."},{"label":"C","text":"Many birds and small animals are being irrationally killed."},{"label":"D","text":"Hunting is universally acknowledged as a savage behavior."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Overpopulation is not an issue for most hunted animals.","answerZh":"对大多数被猎杀的动物来说,数量过剩并不是问题。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到，根据美国人文协会的说法，大多数被猎杀的物种——如水禽、兔子、丘陵鸟类和哀鸽——'提供的营养很少，不需要种群控制'。因此，A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"美国人道协会反对狩猎的论点是什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"When is hunting morally justifiable according to Gary E. Varner?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"When it benefits animals and their ecosystem."},{"label":"B","text":"When it serves both human and animal interests."},{"label":"C","text":"When it is indispensable to humans' subsistence."},{"label":"D","text":"When it stabilizes the population of animal species."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"When it benefits animals and their ecosystem.","answerZh":"当狩猎有益于动物及其生态系统时。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第五段提到Gary E. Varner在他的书中提到，'therapeutic hunting'——旨在确保目标物种的总体福利、其生态系统的完整性或两者——是可辩护的，而仅为人类利益服务的生计和运动狩猎则不可辩护。因此，A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"在 Gary E. Varner 看来,狩猎在什么情况下在道德上是正当的?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What concept are green leaders trying to promote?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Effective protection of animal habitats."},{"label":"B","text":"Strict control over urban development."},{"label":"C","text":"Coordinated efforts of hunters and environmentalists."},{"label":"D","text":"A compromise between development and animal protection."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Coordinated efforts of hunters and environmentalists.","answerZh":"猎人与环保主义者的协同努力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到，绿色领袖越来越多地倡导猎人和环保组织之间的合作，因为双方都反对城市扩张和栖息地破坏。因此，C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"环保领袖们正试图推广什么理念?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2020_09_1-p1","title":"CET6 2020年09月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2020年09月 第1套","examDate":"2020年09月","year":"2020","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2020-09-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章讨论英国肥胖危机为何难解：责任之争与行业游说阻碍行动，作者主张政府应设计良好的干预、扩大民众获得健康选择的途径，与个人动力结合才能奏效。","mainIdeaEn":"Britain's obesity crisis stalls in ideological disputes over responsibility; the author argues well-designed government intervention that builds social capacity, combined with motivated individuals, is the way forward.","answerCode":"BABDC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先吵谁该负责没个准，再看历史知政府得出手，然后批评者拿不出好招，接着不平等坐实干预有理，最后个人有动力政策才灵。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"Why is the obesity problem in Britain so difficult to solve?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Government health budgets are depleted."},{"label":"B","text":"People disagree as to who should do what."},{"label":"C","text":"Individuals are not ready to take their responsibilities."},{"label":"D","text":"Industry lobbying makes it hard to get healthy foods."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"People disagree as to who should do what.","answerZh":"人们对谁该做什么意见不一。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'the quest for solutions gets diverted by ideological arguments around responsibility and choice'，说明肥胖问题难以解决的原因是人们对于责任和选择的意识形态争论。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"英国的肥胖问题为什么如此难以解决?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What can we learn from the past experience in tackling public health emergencies?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Governments have a role to play."},{"label":"B","text":"Public health is a scientific issue."},{"label":"C","text":"Priority should be given to deprived regions."},{"label":"D","text":"Businesses' responsibility should be stressed."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Governments have a role to play.","answerZh":"政府应当发挥作用。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'Historical precedent suggests that science and politics can overcome resistance from businesses'，说明政府在应对公共卫生紧急情况中扮演着重要角色。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"从过去应对公共卫生紧急事件的经验中我们能学到什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does the author imply about some critics of bans and taxes concerning unhealthy drinks?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are not aware of the consequences of obesity."},{"label":"B","text":"They have not come up with anything more constructive."},{"label":"C","text":"They are uncomfortable with parliament's anti-obesity debate."},{"label":"D","text":"They have their own motives in opposing government regulation."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They have not come up with anything more constructive.","answerZh":"他们并没有提出更有建设性的办法。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章第四段提到'Bans and taxes can be blunt instruments, but their harshest critics can rarely suggest better methods'，说明一些批评者并没有提出更有建设性的方法。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"对于批评针对不健康饮品的禁令和征税的人,作者暗示了什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"Why does the author stress the relationship between poor health and inequality?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"To demonstrate the dilemma of people living in deprived areas."},{"label":"B","text":"To bring to light the root cause of widespread obesity in Britain."},{"label":"C","text":"To highlight the area deserving the most attention from the public."},{"label":"D","text":"To justify government intervention in solving the obesity problem."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"To justify government intervention in solving the obesity problem.","answerZh":"为政府干预解决肥胖问题提供正当理由。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章倒数第二段提到'The relationship between poor health and inequality is too pronounced for governments to be passive'，说明作者强调健康与不平等的关系是为了证明政府干预解决肥胖问题的必要性。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者为什么强调健康不良与不平等之间的关系?"},{"number":"50","stem":"When will government action be effective?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"When the polarised debate is abandoned."},{"label":"B","text":"When ideological differences are resolved."},{"label":"C","text":"When individuals have the incentive to act accordingly."},{"label":"D","text":"When the private sector realises the severity of the crisis."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"When individuals have the incentive to act accordingly.","answerZh":"当个人有相应行动的动力时。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到'Government action works when individuals are motivated to respond'，说明政府行动在个人有动力采取行动时才会有效。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"政府的行动在什么情况下才会有效?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2020_09_1-p2","title":"CET6 2020年09月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2020年09月 第1套","examDate":"2020年09月","year":"2020","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2020-09-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"澳大利亚拟建全球最大的珊瑚海海洋保护区，但科学家和环保组织批评方案禁渔范围不足、只保护几乎无商业威胁的海域，认为政府保护力度还不够。","mainIdeaEn":"Australia proposes the world's largest marine reserve in the Coral Sea, but scientists and conservationists criticize the plan for insufficient no-take zones and for protecting areas that face little real threat.","answerCode":"ADADC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先看珊瑚海生物超丰富，再政府要建成环岸保护区，然后科学家嫌保护不够，接着有人赞共护栖息地，最后批只护无需护的海域。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about the Coral Sea?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is exceptionally rich in marine life."},{"label":"B","text":"It is the biggest marine protected area."},{"label":"C","text":"It remains largely undisturbed by humans."},{"label":"D","text":"It is a unique haven of endangered species."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is exceptionally rich in marine life.","answerZh":"它的海洋生物异常丰富。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'Home to virgin reefs, rare sharks and vast numbers of exotic fish, the Coral Sea is a unique haven of biodiversity off the northeastern coast of Australia'，说明珊瑚海是澳大利亚东北部沿海生物多样性的独特天堂，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于珊瑚海,我们能从文中了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does the Australian government plan to do according to Tony Burke?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Make a new proposal to protect the Coral Sea."},{"label":"B","text":"Revise its conservation plan owing to criticisms."},{"label":"C","text":"Upgrade the established reserves to protect marine life."},{"label":"D","text":"Complete the series of marine reserves around its coast."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Complete the series of marine reserves around its coast.","answerZh":"建成环绕澳大利亚海岸的一系列海洋保护区。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'the proposal would be the last in a series of proposed marine reserves around Australia's coast'，说明澳大利亚政府计划完成沿海一系列海洋保护区的建设，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"据 Tony Burke 所说,澳大利亚政府计划做什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What is scientists' argument about the Coral Sea proposal?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The government has not done enough for marine protection."},{"label":"B","text":"It will not improve the marine reserves along Australia's coast."},{"label":"C","text":"The government has not consulted them in drawing up the proposal."},{"label":"D","text":"It is not based on sufficient investigations into the ecological system."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"The government has not done enough for marine protection.","answerZh":"政府在海洋保护方面做得还不够。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'the scheme is attracting criticism from scientists and conservation groups, who argue that the government hasn't gone far enough in protecting the Coral Sea'，说明科学家和保护组织认为政府在保护珊瑚海方面做得不够，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"科学家们对珊瑚海提案的论点是什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does marine geologist Robin Beaman say about the Coral Sea plan?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It can compare with the British government's effort in the Indian Ocean."},{"label":"B","text":"It will result in the establishment of the world's largest marine reserve."},{"label":"C","text":"It will ensure the sustainability of the fishing industry around the coast."},{"label":"D","text":"It is a tremendous joint effort to protect the range of marine habitats."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is a tremendous joint effort to protect the range of marine habitats.","answerZh":"这是保护多样海洋栖息地的一项巨大的共同努力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'the reserve does broadly protect the range of habitats in the sea'和'I can testify to the huge effort that government agencies and other organisations have put into trying to understand the ecological values of this vast area'，说明珊瑚海计划是保护海洋栖息地范围的巨大联合努力，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于珊瑚海计划,海洋地质学家 Robin Beaman 说了什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What do critics think of the Coral Sea plan?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It will do more harm than good to the environment."},{"label":"B","text":"It will adversely affect Australia's fishing industry."},{"label":"C","text":"It will protect regions that actually require little protection."},{"label":"D","text":"It will win little support from environmental organisations."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It will protect regions that actually require little protection.","answerZh":"它将保护那些实际上几乎不需要保护的区域。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'Critics say that the southwestern reserve offers the greatest protection to the offshore areas where commercial opportunities are fewest and where there is little threat to the environment'，说明批评者认为珊瑚海计划将保护那些实际上需要很少保护的区域，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"批评者如何看待珊瑚海计划?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2020_09_2-p1","title":"CET6 2020年09月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2020年09月 第2套","examDate":"2020年09月","year":"2020","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2020-09-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章以小说家斯蒂尔自称每天工作20小时引发追捧为切入点，指出这类说法可疑：缺觉严重损害效率，标榜不眠已成地位象征，专家告诫大众切勿效仿。","mainIdeaEn":"Novelist Danielle Steel's claimed 20-hour workdays drew admiration, but experts doubt them: sleep loss wrecks productivity, self-imposed sleeplessness has become a status symbol, and encouraging others to copy such schedules is irresponsible.","answerCode":"CAACB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先有读者惊叹她的作息，再被捧成勤奋榜样，然后遭质疑真假难辨，接着熬夜成了成功勋章，最后专家劝大家别学。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about Glamour magazine readers?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are intrigued by the exotic romance in Danielle Steel's novels."},{"label":"B","text":"They are amazed by the number of books written by Danielle Steel."},{"label":"C","text":"They are deeply impressed by Danielle Steel's daily work schedule."},{"label":"D","text":"They are highly motivated by Danielle Steel's unusual productivity."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They are deeply impressed by Danielle Steel's daily work schedule.","answerZh":"他们对 Danielle Steel 的日常工作安排印象深刻。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段中的描述，'a passing reference in a recent profile by Glamour magazine to her 20-hour workdays prompted an outpouring of admiration'，可以看出Glamour杂志的读者对Danielle Steel每天工作20小时的日程安排印象深刻。","questionZh":"关于 Glamour 杂志的读者,我们能从文中了解到什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What did the business news website Quartz say about Danielle Steel?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"She could serve as an example of industriousness."},{"label":"B","text":"She proved we could liberate ourselves from sleep."},{"label":"C","text":"She could be an inspiration to novelists all over the world."},{"label":"D","text":"She showed we could get all our work done without sleep."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"She could serve as an example of industriousness.","answerZh":"她可以作为勤奋的典范。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到，'The business news website Quartz held Steel up as an inspiration, writing that if only we all followed her \"actually extremely liberating\" example of industrious sleeplessness, we would be quick to see results.' 因此，Quartz网站认为Steel可以作为勤奋的榜样。","questionZh":"商业新闻网站 Quartz 对 Danielle Steel 有何评论?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What do sceptics think of Danielle Steel's work schedule claims?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are questionable."},{"label":"B","text":"they are alterable."},{"label":"C","text":"They are irresistible."},{"label":"D","text":"They are verifiable."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They are questionable.","answerZh":"这些说法值得怀疑。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到，'With research results showing the cumulative effects of sleep loss and its impact on productivity, doubt has been voiced about the accuracy of Steel's self-assessment.' 表明怀疑者对Steel的工作日程声明表示怀疑。","questionZh":"怀疑者如何看待 Danielle Steel 声称的工作日程?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What does Maryanne Taylor think of self-imposed sleeplessness?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It may turn out to be key to a successful career."},{"label":"B","text":"It may be practiced only by certain tech heads."},{"label":"C","text":"It may symbolise one's importance and success."},{"label":"D","text":"It may well serve as a measure of self-discipline."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It may symbolise one's importance and success.","answerZh":"它可能象征着一个人的重要性和成功。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到，'Self-imposed sleeplessness has \"become a bit of a status symbol\", says Taylor, a misguided measure to prove how powerful and productive you are.' 因此，Taylor认为自我强加的失眠可能象征着个人的重要性和成功。","questionZh":"Maryanne Taylor 如何看待自我强加的不睡觉行为?"},{"number":"50","stem":"How does Dr. Sophie Bostock look at the 20-hour daily work schedule?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"One should not adopt it without consulting a sleep expert."},{"label":"B","text":"The general public should not be encouraged to follow it."},{"label":"C","text":"One must be duly self-disciplined to adhere to it."},{"label":"D","text":"The minority must adjust their body clock for it."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"The general public should not be encouraged to follow it.","answerZh":"不应鼓励普通大众效仿这种作息。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到，'Even if Steel does happen to be among that tiny minority, says Bostock, it's \"pretty irresponsible\" to suggest that 20-hour days are simply a question of discipline for the rest of us.' 因此，Bostock认为公众不应该被鼓励遵循20小时的工作日程。","questionZh":"Dr. Sophie Bostock 如何看待每天工作20小时的日程?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2020_09_2-p2","title":"CET6 2020年09月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2020年09月 第2套","examDate":"2020年09月","year":"2020","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2020-09-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"作者回顾四十年研究后认为，有机农业虽产量略低，但在环境与经济等可持续目标上优于常规农业，是应对全球粮食与气候挑战的未被充分利用的资源。","mainIdeaEn":"Reviewing 40 years of research, the author argues that despite lower yields, organic agriculture outperforms conventional farming on sustainability and is an untapped resource for feeding the world amid climate change.","answerCode":"BDCBD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说有机能解粮食难题，再有人嫌产量低，然后指出分配不均，接着批常规农业难持续，最后夸有机长远利生态。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn from the conclusion of the author's review study?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"More resources should be tapped for feeding the world's population."},{"label":"B","text":"Organic farming may be exploited to solve the global food problem."},{"label":"C","text":"The long-term prospects of organic farming are yet to be explored."},{"label":"D","text":"Organic farming is at least as promising as conventional farming."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Organic farming may be exploited to solve the global food problem.","answerZh":"有机农业或可用来解决全球粮食问题。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到作者得出的结论是'Organic agriculture is a relatively untapped resource for feeding the Earth's population'，说明有机农业是一个未被充分利用的资源，可以用来解决全球粮食问题。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"从作者综述研究的结论中我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What is the critics' argument against organic farming?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It cannot meet the need for food."},{"label":"B","text":"It cannot increase farm yields."},{"label":"C","text":"It is not really practical."},{"label":"D","text":"It is not that productive."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is not that productive.","answerZh":"它的产量不高。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到批评者认为有机农业效率低下，需要更多的土地来生产同样数量的食物，说明有机农业的生产力不如传统农业。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"批评者反对有机农业的论点是什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does the author think should be taken into account in arguing about organic farming?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Growth in world population."},{"label":"B","text":"Deterioration in soil fertility."},{"label":"C","text":"Inequality in food distribution."},{"label":"D","text":"Advance in farming technology."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Inequality in food distribution.","answerZh":"粮食分配的不平等。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'Sometimes excluded from these arguments is the fact that we already produce enough food to more than feed the world's 7.4 billion people but do not provide adequate access to all individuals'，说明在讨论有机农业时应该考虑食物分配不均的问题。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者认为在争论有机农业时应该考虑什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does science tell us about conventional farming?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It will not be able to meet global food demand."},{"label":"B","text":"It is not conducive to sustainable development."},{"label":"C","text":"It will eventually give way to organic farming."},{"label":"D","text":"It is going mainstream throughout the world."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It is not conducive to sustainable development.","answerZh":"它不利于可持续发展。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到传统农业虽然可以生产更多食物，但往往以牺牲其他可持续性目标为代价，如生物多样性丧失、环境退化等。说明传统农业不利于可持续发展。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于传统农业,科学告诉了我们什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"Why does the author think higher prices of organic farm produce are justifiable?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They give farmers going organic a big competitive edge."},{"label":"B","text":"They motivate farmers to upgrade farming technology."},{"label":"C","text":"Organic farming costs more than conventional farming."},{"label":"D","text":"Organic farming does long-term good to the ecosystem."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Organic farming does long-term good to the ecosystem.","answerZh":"有机农业对生态系统有长远的好处。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到有机农业对生态系统长期有益，因此消费者愿意支付更高的价格，作为对农民提供生态系统服务和避免环境损害的补偿。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者为什么认为有机农产品价格更高是合理的?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2020_12_1-p1","title":"CET6 2020年12月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2020年12月 第1套","examDate":"2020年12月","year":"2020","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2020-12-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者忧虑大众旅游时代艺术欣赏被走马观花取代：真正领会作品需要时间凝视；但良好管理与雅俗共赏的展览证明，专注观看依然可能且必要。","mainIdeaEn":"In an age of mass tourism and inattention, hurried museum visits crowd out real appreciation; yet with good management and contemplative looking, art can still offer the escape into another's vision that Proust described.","answerCode":"BACBC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先叹人潮里没法赏画，再懂细品名作需要时间，然后靠好管理疏散人流，接着娱乐也能装下严肃艺术，最后借艺术换双眼看世界。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What does the scene at the Louvre demonstrate according to the author?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The enormous appeal of a great piece of artistic work to tourists."},{"label":"B","text":"The near impossibility of appreciating art in an age of mass tourism."},{"label":"C","text":"The ever-growing commercial value of long-cherished artistic works."},{"label":"D","text":"The real difficulty in getting a glimpse at a masterpiece amid a crowd."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"The near impossibility of appreciating art in an age of mass tourism.","answerZh":"在大众旅游时代几乎不可能欣赏艺术。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到游客在卢浮宫的蒙娜丽莎前只能停留一分钟，并且有些人的时间花在自拍上，这表明在大众旅游时代，欣赏艺术几乎变得不可能。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者认为卢浮宫的场景说明了什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"Why did the late philosopher Richard Wollheim spend four hours before a picture?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It takes time to appreciate a piece of art fully."},{"label":"B","text":"It is quite common to misinterpret artistic works."},{"label":"C","text":"The longer people contemplate a picture, the more likely they will enjoy it."},{"label":"D","text":"The more time one spends before a painting, the more valuable one finds it."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It takes time to appreciate a piece of art fully.","answerZh":"充分欣赏一件艺术品需要时间。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到哲学家Richard Wollheim在卢浮宫参观时，可以在一幅画面前花费多达四个小时，他认为第一个小时是消除误解所必需的，之后画面才开始向他展示自己。这说明他花费长时间是为了充分欣赏艺术作品，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"已故哲学家 Richard Wollheim 为什么会在一幅画前待上四个小时?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does the case of the Uffizi in Florence show?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Art works in museums should be better taken care of."},{"label":"B","text":"Sites of cultural pilgrimage are always flooded with visitors."},{"label":"C","text":"Good management is key to handling large crowds of visitors."},{"label":"D","text":"Large crowds of visitors cause management problems for museums."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Good management is key to handling large crowds of visitors.","answerZh":"良好的管理是应对大批游客的关键。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章提到乌菲齐美术馆通过聪明的管理将入场队伍减少到七分钟，这说明良好的管理是处理大量游客的关键，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"佛罗伦萨 Uffizi 美术馆的例子说明了什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What do we learn from Olafur Eliasson's current Tate Modern show?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Children learn to appreciate art works most effectively while they are playing."},{"label":"B","text":"It is possible to combine entertainment with appreciation of serious art."},{"label":"C","text":"Art works about the environment appeal most to young children."},{"label":"D","text":"Some forms of art can accommodate huge crowds of visitors."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It is possible to combine entertainment with appreciation of serious art.","answerZh":"把娱乐与欣赏严肃艺术结合起来是可能的。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章提到Olafur Eliasson的泰特现代展览看起来可能只是一种娱乐，但实际上，在他最具娱乐性的地方，他也是最具严肃性的，他的迷惑性装置让人们意识到我们对地球的破坏性影响。这说明他成功地将娱乐与对严肃艺术的欣赏结合起来，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"从 Olafur Eliasson 目前在 Tate Modern 的展览中我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What can art do according to Marcel Proust?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Enable us to live a much fuller life."},{"label":"B","text":"Allow us to escape the harsh reality."},{"label":"C","text":"Help us to see the world from a different perspective."},{"label":"D","text":"Urge us to explore the unknown domain of the universe."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Help us to see the world from a different perspective.","answerZh":"帮助我们从不同的视角看世界。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章引用了Marcel Proust的话，他说'只有通过艺术我们才能逃离自我，了解另一个人如何看待宇宙，否则这些风景将和月球上的风景一样未知'，这说明艺术可以帮助我们从不同的视角看世界，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"在 Marcel Proust 看来,艺术能做什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2020_12_1-p2","title":"CET6 2020年12月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2020年12月 第1套","examDate":"2020年12月","year":"2020","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2020-12-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章批评美国农业部新膳食指南完全回避食物选择的环境代价：农业耗费大量资源、加剧气候变化，而该部门与农企关系密切；保障未来粮食安全必须重视可持续。","mainIdeaEn":"Researchers fault the USDA's new dietary guidelines for ignoring food's environmental costs; despite agriculture's huge climate and resource footprint, the agency—cozy with agribusiness—omitted sustainability, which future food security demands.","answerCode":"DADCB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先怨膳食指南不管环境，再说它有钱有权本可作为，然后揭农业吞掉大半资源，接着疑它和农企走太近，最后须抓农业可持续。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"Why are some researchers irritated at the USDA's 2016-2020 Dietary Guidelines?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It ignores the harmful effect of red meat and processed food on health."},{"label":"B","text":"Too much emphasis is given to eating less meat and buying local food."},{"label":"C","text":"The dietary recommendations are not based on medical science."},{"label":"D","text":"It takes no notice of the potential impact on the environment."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It takes no notice of the potential impact on the environment.","answerZh":"它没有考虑对环境的潜在影响。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'some researchers are annoyed that new dietary recommendations of the USDA ... seem to utterly ignore that fact'，其中'that fact'指代前文提到的'what those food choices do to the environment'，即饮食选择对环境的影响。因此，D选项'It takes no notice of the potential impact on the environment'是正确答案。","questionZh":"一些研究人员为什么对美国农业部的 2016-2020 膳食指南感到恼火?"},{"number":"52","stem":"Why does the author say the USDA could have contributed a lot to lowering the climate cost through its dietary guidelines?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has the capacity and the financial resources to do so."},{"label":"B","text":"Its researchers have already submitted relevant proposals."},{"label":"C","text":"Its agencies in charge of drafting the guidelines have the expertise."},{"label":"D","text":"It can raise students' environmental awareness through its programs."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It has the capacity and the financial resources to do so.","answerZh":"它有能力也有财力这样做。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'The government's dietary guidelines could have done a lot to lower that climate cost. Not just because of their position of authority: The guidelines drive billions of dollars of food production through federal programs'，说明USDA通过饮食指南可以影响数十亿美元的食品生产，因此A选项'Its has the capacity and the financial resources to do so'是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者为什么说美国农业部本可以通过膳食指南为降低气候成本做出很大贡献?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What do we learn from the Dietary Guidelines Advisory Committee's scientific report?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Food is easily contaminated from farm to belly."},{"label":"B","text":"Greenhouse effect is an issue still under debate."},{"label":"C","text":"Modern agriculture has increased food diversity."},{"label":"D","text":"Farming consumes most of our natural resources."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Farming consumes most of our natural resources.","answerZh":"农业消耗了我们大部分的自然资源。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'Food production is the largest user of fresh water, largest contributor to the loss of biodiversity, and a major contributor to using up natural resources'，说明农业消耗了大部分自然资源，因此D选项'Farming consumes most of our natural resources'是正确答案。","questionZh":"从膳食指南咨询委员会的科学报告中我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What may account for the neglect of sustainability in the USDA's Dietary Guidelines according to the author?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its exclusive concern with Americans' food safety."},{"label":"B","text":"Its sole responsibility for providing dietary advice."},{"label":"C","text":"Its close ties with the agriculture companies."},{"label":"D","text":"Its alleged failure to regulate the industries."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Its close ties with the agriculture companies.","answerZh":"它与农业公司的密切关系。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章倒数第三段提到'Possibly the agencies in charge of drafting the decisions are too close to the industries they are supposed to regulate'，说明USDA与农业公司关系密切，因此C选项'Its close ties with the agriculture companies'是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者认为美国农业部膳食指南忽视可持续性的原因可能是什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What should the USDA do to achieve food security according to David Wallinga?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Give top priority to things like nutrition and food security."},{"label":"B","text":"Endeavor to ensure the sustainable development of agriculture."},{"label":"C","text":"Fulfill its mission by closely cooperating with the industries."},{"label":"D","text":"Study the long-term impact of climate change on food production."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Endeavor to ensure the sustainable development of agriculture.","answerZh":"努力确保农业的可持续发展。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'You absolutely need to be worried about climate impacts and future sustainability if you want secure food in the future'，说明要实现食品安全必须关注气候影响和未来的可持续性，因此B选项'Endeavor to ensure the sustainable development of agriculture'是正确答案。","questionZh":"David Wallinga 认为美国农业部应该怎样做才能实现粮食安全?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2020_12_2-p1","title":"CET6 2020年12月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2020年12月 第2套","examDate":"2020年12月","year":"2020","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2020-12-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者批评EAT-Lancet全球植物性饮食倡议：以印度为模板忽视其饥饿与营养不良的现实，会加剧低收入国家营养危机，印度政府接纳更是牺牲民众长远利益。","mainIdeaEn":"The author criticizes the EAT-Lancet plant-based 'planetary diet' for holding up India as a model: it ignores widespread malnutrition, would worsen nutrition problems in low-income countries, and the government's embrace sacrifices its people's long-term interests.","answerCode":"BCBDA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先见印度人不愿被逼吃素，再怕报告让穷人更缺营养，然后想吃的根本吃不上，接着这套膳食坑穷国，最后政府点头卖了长远利益。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What is more visible in India than anywhere else according to the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"People's positive views on the proposals for a \"planetary diet.\""},{"label":"B","text":"People's reluctance to be compelled to eat plant-based food."},{"label":"C","text":"People's preferences for the kind of food they consume."},{"label":"D","text":"People's unwillingness to give up their eating habits."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"People's reluctance to be compelled to eat plant-based food.","answerZh":"人们不愿被迫吃植物性食物。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段中的'Yet the reverse compulsion is hidden in the proposals for a new plant-based \"planetary diet.\" Nowhere is this more visible than in India.'可知，在印度，人们对于被迫吃植物性食品的抗拒比其他任何地方都更明显。","questionZh":"根据文章,什么在印度比在其他任何地方都更明显?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What would the EAT-Lancet Commission's report do to many people in countries like India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Radically change their dietary habits."},{"label":"B","text":"Keep them further away from politics."},{"label":"C","text":"Make them even more undernourished."},{"label":"D","text":"Substantially reduce their food choices."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Make them even more undernourished.","answerZh":"使他们更加营养不良。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'In countries like India, that call could become a tool to aggravate an already tense political situation and stress already undernourished populations.'说明EAT-Lancet Commission的报告可能会使像印度这样的国家的许多人更加营养不良。","questionZh":"EAT-Lancet 委员会的报告会对印度等国的许多人产生什么影响?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about food consumption in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"People's diet will not change due to the EAT-Lancet report."},{"label":"B","text":"Many people simply do not have access to foods they prefer."},{"label":"C","text":"There is a growing popularity of a cereal-heavy vegetarian diet."},{"label":"D","text":"Policymakers help remove the barriers to people's choice of food."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Many people simply do not have access to foods they prefer.","answerZh":"许多人根本吃不到自己偏好的食物。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'there is a vast difference between what people would wish to consume and what they have to consume because of innumerable barriers around class, religion, culture, cost, geography, etc.'说明许多人根本没有机会获得他们偏好的食物。","questionZh":"关于印度的食物消费,我们从文章中可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What does the passage say about a plant-based diet modeled on India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It may benefit populations whose traditional diet is meat-based."},{"label":"B","text":"It may be another blow to the economy in developing countries."},{"label":"C","text":"It may help narrow the gap between the rich and poor countries."},{"label":"D","text":"It may worsen the nourishment problem in low-income countries."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It may worsen the nourishment problem in low-income countries.","answerZh":"它可能加剧低收入国家的营养问题。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'Which is why calls for a plant-based diet modeled on India risk offering another whip with which to beat already vulnerable communities in developing countries.'说明以印度为模型的植物性饮食可能会加剧低收入国家的营养不良问题。","questionZh":"关于以印度为样板的植物性饮食,文章说了什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"How does the Indian government respond to the EAT-Lancet Commission's proposals?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It accepts them at the expense of the long-term interests of its people."},{"label":"B","text":"It intends them to spark conversations among all Indian stakeholders."},{"label":"C","text":"It gives them approval regardless of opposition from nutrition experts."},{"label":"D","text":"It welcomes them as a tool to address chronic hunger and malnutrition."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It accepts them at the expense of the long-term interests of its people.","answerZh":"它接受这些提议,却以本国人民的长远利益为代价。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'Rather than addressing chronic hunger and malnutrition through an improved access to wholesome and nutrient-dense foods, the government is opening the door for company-dependent solutions, ignoring the environmental and economic cost, which will destroy local food systems.'说明印度政府接受了EAT-Lancet Commission的提议，牺牲了其人民的长期利益。","questionZh":"印度政府如何回应 EAT-Lancet 委员会的提议?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2020_12_2-p2","title":"CET6 2020年12月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2020年12月 第2套","examDate":"2020年12月","year":"2020","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2020-12-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章剖析长期抱怨者\"你说的都对但没用\"的心理游戏与责任/过错谬误：对付之道是热烈附和促其自省；逃避责任是牢笼，承担责任才能获得自由。","mainIdeaEn":"Analyzing chronic complainers' 'Yes But' game and the responsibility/fault fallacy, the author shows ardent over-validation stops the moaning and prompts change—evading responsibility imprisons us, while assuming it sets us free.","answerCode":"CDABC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先有人光抱怨拒绝一切建议，再分清责任不等于过错，然后用力附和堵住牢骚，接着他反倒琢磨起改变，最后担起责任才得自由。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What is characteristic of a chronic complainer, according to psychiatrist Eric Berne?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They only feel angry about their ill treatment and resent whoever tries to help."},{"label":"B","text":"They are chronically unhappy and ceaselessly find fault with people around them."},{"label":"C","text":"They constantly dismiss others' proposals while taking no responsibility for tackling the problem."},{"label":"D","text":"They lack the knowledge and basic skills required for successful conversations with their interlocutors."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They constantly dismiss others' proposals while taking no responsibility for tackling the problem.","answerZh":"他们不断否定别人的建议,却不承担解决问题的责任。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段，Eric Berne 描述了一种被称为 'Why Don't You—Yes But' 的对话模式，其中慢性抱怨者会不断地抱怨他们的关系、工作或其他情况，但会找借口拒绝任何提出的解决方案。因此，C选项 'They constantly dismiss others' proposals while taking no responsibility for tackling the problem' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"精神病学家 Eric Berne 认为,长期抱怨者有什么特点?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does the author try to illustrate with the example of the newborn on one's doorstep?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"People tend to think that one should not be held responsible for others' mistakes."},{"label":"B","text":"It is easy to become attached to the position of overlooking one's own faults."},{"label":"C","text":"People are often at a loss when confronted with a number of choices."},{"label":"D","text":"A distinction should be drawn between responsibility and fault."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"A distinction should be drawn between responsibility and fault.","answerZh":"应当区分责任与过错。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章中通过新生儿的例子来说明责任和错误之间的区别。作者指出，即使新生儿出现在门口不是作者的错，但作者有责任去处理这个问题。这个例子用来说明即使别人100%错了，逃避责任也不是长期的解决办法。因此，D选项 'A distinction should be drawn between responsibility and fault' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者用门口的新生儿这个例子想说明什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does the author advise people to do to chronic complainers?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Stop them from going further by agreeing with them."},{"label":"B","text":"Listen to their complaints ardently and sympathetically."},{"label":"C","text":"Ask them to validate their beliefs with further evidence."},{"label":"D","text":"Persuade them to clarify the confusion they have caused."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Stop them from going further by agreeing with them.","answerZh":"通过表示赞同来阻止他们继续抱怨。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到，面对慢性抱怨者，一个巧妙的方法是同意他们的观点，即 'over validation'。这样做可以避免进一步的抱怨，因为对方的动机是确认自己的信念，而你现在正在确认它们。因此，A选项 'Stop them from going further by agreeing with them' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者建议人们如何对待长期抱怨者?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What happens when chronic complainers receive over-validation?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are motivated to find ingenious ways to persuade their interlocutor."},{"label":"B","text":"They are prompted to come up with ideas for making possible changes."},{"label":"C","text":"They are stimulated to make more complaints."},{"label":"D","text":"They are encouraged to start arguing back."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They are prompted to come up with ideas for making possible changes.","answerZh":"他们会被促使想出办法来做出可能的改变。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到，当慢性抱怨者得到过度验证时，他们会重新听到他们的抱怨，并开始反驳。他们突然意识到自己并非完全无能为力，这促使他们产生可能改变现状的想法。因此，B选项 'They are prompted to come up with ideas for making possible changes' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"当长期抱怨者得到过度认同时会发生什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"How can one stop being a chronic complainer according to the author?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Analysing the so-called responsibility/fault fallacy."},{"label":"B","text":"Avoiding hazardous traps in everyday social life."},{"label":"C","text":"Assuming responsibility to free oneself."},{"label":"D","text":"Awaiting something magical to happen."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Assuming responsibility to free oneself.","answerZh":"承担起责任来解脱自己。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到，逃避责任感觉舒服，但最终会变成监狱；而承担责任感觉不舒服，但最终会带来自由。因此，C选项 'Assuming responsibility to free oneself' 是正确答案，意味着通过承担责任来解放自己。","questionZh":"作者认为怎样才能不再做一个长期抱怨者?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2020_12_3-p1","title":"CET6 2020年12月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2020年12月 第3套","examDate":"2020年12月","year":"2020","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2020-12-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章分析社交媒体为何让人孤独自卑：它本质是精心包装的形象管理，人们又爱美化他人生活；作者建议让发帖回归记录生活，多与现实朋友相处。","mainIdeaEn":"Social media breeds loneliness and inadequacy because it is curated image management and we idealize others' lives; the author advises letting posts record real moments and prioritizing face-to-face friendships over one's online image.","answerCode":"CACAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先刷到自卑又孤单，再因不信网友而报喜藏忧，然后总把别人日子想太美，接着发帖只留真实纪念，最后回归线下老友身边。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What does the author imply social media may do to our life?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It may facilitate our interpersonal relationships."},{"label":"B","text":"It may filter our negative impressions of others."},{"label":"C","text":"It may make us feel isolated and incompetent."},{"label":"D","text":"It may render us vulnerable and inauthentic."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It may make us feel isolated and incompetent.","answerZh":"它可能让我们感到孤立和无能。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章提到，社交媒体上的互动不提供与面对面交流相同的满足感，人们倾向于理想化他人的生活并比较自己的不足，导致孤独和自卑感。因此，作者暗示社交媒体可能使我们感到孤立和无能。","questionZh":"作者暗示社交媒体可能对我们的生活产生什么影响?"},{"number":"47","stem":"Why do people post comments selectively on social media?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They do not find all their online friends trustworthy."},{"label":"B","text":"They want to avoid offending any of their audience."},{"label":"C","text":"They do not want to lose their followers."},{"label":"D","text":"They are eager to boost their popularity."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They do not find all their online friends trustworthy.","answerZh":"他们并不觉得所有网友都值得信任。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到，人们在社交媒体上发布照片和帖子时不会完全真实和脆弱，因为他们并不完全信任一些所谓的'朋友'，或者与他们的信任尚未建立。因此，人们选择性地发布评论是因为他们并不认为所有在线朋友都值得信赖。","questionZh":"人们为什么在社交媒体上有选择地发表内容?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What are humans inclined to do according to the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Exaggerate their life's accomplishments."},{"label":"B","text":"Strive for perfection regardless of the cost."},{"label":"C","text":"Paint a rosy picture of other people's lives."},{"label":"D","text":"Learn lessons from other people's downfalls."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Paint a rosy picture of other people's lives.","answerZh":"把别人的生活描绘得过于美好。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章指出，人们倾向于理想化他人的生活，将自己的不足与他人最伟大的成就相比较，导致孤独和自卑感。因此，根据文章，人们倾向于描绘他人生活的乐观画面。","questionZh":"根据文章,人类倾向于做什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What is the author's view of pictures and posts on social media?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They should record the memorable moments in people's lives."},{"label":"B","text":"They should be carefully edited so as to present the best image."},{"label":"C","text":"They should be shown in a way that meets one's security needs."},{"label":"D","text":"They should keep people from the unhealthy quest for perfection."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They should record the memorable moments in people's lives.","answerZh":"它们应当记录人们生活中值得纪念的时刻。","explanation":"这是一道观点态度题。作者认为，社交媒体上的图片和帖子应该是生活宝贵时刻和乐趣时光的副产品，而不是为了填补不安全感或未满足需求而计划和计算的形象。因此，作者认为图片和帖子应该记录人们生活中难忘的时刻。","questionZh":"作者如何看待社交媒体上的图片和帖子?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does the author advise people to do when they find their online experience unconstructive?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Use social media to increase their ability to connect with various types of people."},{"label":"B","text":"Stay connected to those whom they may not otherwise get to know and befriend."},{"label":"C","text":"Try to prevent negative thoughts and feelings from getting into the online pages."},{"label":"D","text":"Strengthen ties with real-life friends instead of caring about their online image."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Strengthen ties with real-life friends instead of caring about their online image.","answerZh":"加强与现实生活朋友的联系,而不是在意自己的网络形象。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到，如果社交媒体导致消极思想和感情，那么增加与信任朋友面对面的时间，减少在线滚动的时间，将证明你的社交网络比任何'点赞'、'关注'或'分享'更有价值。因此，作者建议在发现在线体验无建设性时，加强与现实生活中朋友的关系，而不是关心他们的在线形象。","questionZh":"作者建议人们在发现自己的网络体验无益时怎么做?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2020_12_3-p2","title":"CET6 2020年12月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2020年12月 第3套","examDate":"2020年12月","year":"2020","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2020-12-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章指出黑猩猩拥有各群体独特的文化传统，而人类活动正令其行为多样性凋零；作者呼吁革新保护理念，既保物种基因，也要保存动物文化。","mainIdeaEn":"Chimpanzee communities have distinct cultural traditions, but human presence is eroding this behavioral diversity; the author calls for a new conservation approach that preserves animal cultures as well as species and genes.","answerCode":"ADBBC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先控人类毁猩猩文化，再见各群交流各有一套，然后人越多猩猩越单调，接着护住每个猩群，最后用全新思路保物种。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author say we humans have been doing to chimps?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ruining their culture."},{"label":"B","text":"Accelerating their extinction."},{"label":"C","text":"Treating them as alien species."},{"label":"D","text":"Homogenizing their living habits."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Ruining their culture.","answerZh":"毁掉它们的文化。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'That is effectively what humans have been doing to our closest relatives—chimps'，紧接着描述了人类活动导致大猩猩的艺术消失、音乐同质化和技术知识消失，这表明人类正在破坏大猩猩的文化。因此，A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者说我们人类一直在对黑猩猩做什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What is the finding of Andrew Whiten's team?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Chimps demonstrate highly developed skills of communication."},{"label":"B","text":"Chimps rely heavily upon their body language to communicate."},{"label":"C","text":"Chimps behave in ways quite similar to those of human beings."},{"label":"D","text":"Different chimp groups differ in their way of communication."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Different chimp groups differ in their way of communication.","answerZh":"不同黑猩猩群体的交流方式各不相同。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'a team of scientists led by Andrew Whiten showed that chimps from different parts of Africa behave very differently from one another'，说明不同地区的大猩猩在行为上存在差异，即不同群体之间在沟通方式上有所不同。因此，D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Andrew Whiten 团队的研究发现是什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What did Ammie Kalan and her colleagues find through their intensive fieldwork?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Whiten's classic study has little impact on the diversity of chimp behavior."},{"label":"B","text":"Chimp behavior becomes less varied with the increase of human activity."},{"label":"C","text":"Chimps alter their culture to quickly adapt to the changed environment."},{"label":"D","text":"It might already be too late to prevent animal cultures from extinction."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Chimp behavior becomes less varied with the increase of human activity.","answerZh":"随着人类活动增加,黑猩猩的行为变得不那么多样。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'Ammie Kalan and her colleagues have shown, through years of intensive fieldwork, that the very presence of humans has eroded the diversity of chimp behavior'，说明随着人类活动的增加，大猩猩的行为多样性减少。因此，B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Ammie Kalan 及其同事通过深入的实地考察发现了什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does Cat Hobaiter think we should do for chimp conservation?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Try to understand our sister species' behavior in the wild."},{"label":"B","text":"Make efforts to preserve each individual chimp community."},{"label":"C","text":"Study the unique characteristics of each generation of chimps."},{"label":"D","text":"Endeavor to restore chimp habitats to expand its total population."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Make efforts to preserve each individual chimp community.","answerZh":"努力保护每一个黑猩猩群落。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'Sometimes in the rush to conserve the species, I think we forget about the individuals,' says Cat Hobaiter... 'An event might only have a small impact on the total population of chimps, but it may wipe out an entire community—an entire culture. No matter what we do to restore habitat or support population growth, we may never be able to restore that culture.' 这表明Hobaiter强调保护每个独特的大猩猩群体的重要性。因此，B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Cat Hobaiter 认为我们应该为保护黑猩猩做什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author suggest conservationists do?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Focus entirely on culturally-based entities rather than genetically-based ones."},{"label":"B","text":"Place more stress on animal traditions than on their physical conservation."},{"label":"C","text":"Conserve animal species in a novel and all-round way."},{"label":"D","text":"Explore the cultures of species, before they vanish."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Conserve animal species in a novel and all-round way.","answerZh":"以新颖、全面的方式保护动物物种。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'Obviously conservationists need to think about saving species in a completely new way—by preserving animal traditions as well as bodies and genes.' 这表明作者建议保护者需要以一种全新的方式保护物种，即同时保护动物的传统、身体和基因。因此，C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者建议保护工作者做什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2021_06_1-p1","title":"CET6 2021年06月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2021年06月 第1套","examDate":"2021年06月","year":"2021","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2021-06-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者批评\"基因决定学业智力\"的遗传论主张：DNA与智力只是弱相关而非因果，解读数据须兼顾环境等因素，更要警惕借科学之名把歧视合理化。","mainIdeaEn":"The author challenges hereditarian claims that genes determine academic ability: DNA and intelligence show only weak correlation, not causation, and we must guard against science being used to justify discrimination.","answerCode":"DABAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先有论文称基因定成绩，再被作者质疑结论，然后指基因智力无因果，接着解读数据要看全因素，最后警惕科学包装歧视。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What did a recent research paper claim?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The type of school students attend makes a difference to their future."},{"label":"B","text":"Genetic differences between students are far greater than supposed."},{"label":"C","text":"The advantages of selective schools are too obvious to ignore."},{"label":"D","text":"Students' academic performance is determined by their genes."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Students' academic performance is determined by their genes.","answerZh":"学生的学业表现由基因决定。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段中的'a recent paper claimed differences in exam performance between pupils attending selective and non-selective schools mirror the genetic differences between them'可知，最近的研究论文声称学生的学术表现与他们所就读的学校类型之间的差异反映了他们之间的基因差异，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"最近一篇研究论文声称了什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the author think of the recent research?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its result was questionable."},{"label":"B","text":"Its implication was positive."},{"label":"C","text":"Its influence was rather negligible."},{"label":"D","text":"Its conclusions were enlightening."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Its result was questionable.","answerZh":"其结果值得怀疑。","explanation":"这是一道观点态度题。第二段作者称该研究招致大量'absurd claims'，并指出其结论只是'a glimpse of the blindingly obvious—and there's nothing to back strongly either a hereditary or environmental argument'；第三段进一步称遗传论科学'problematic on many levels'、'scientifically unsound'，DNA 与智力之间至多是'weak statistical association and not a causal link'。可见作者认为该研究的结论站不住脚、值得质疑，故选 A（其结论是有问题的/可疑的）。 - 关键句：It is a glimpse of the blindingly obvious—and there's nothing to back strongly either a hereditary or environmental argument.","questionZh":"作者如何看待这项最新研究?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does the author say about the relationship between DNA and intelligence?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is one of scientific certainty."},{"label":"B","text":"It is not one of cause and effect."},{"label":"C","text":"It is subject to interpretation of statistics."},{"label":"D","text":"It is not fully examined by gene scientists."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It is not one of cause and effect.","answerZh":"它并不是因果关系。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段中的'At best there is a weak statistical association and not a causal link between DNA and intelligence'可知，作者认为DNA和智力之间没有因果关系，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于 DNA 与智力的关系,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What do hereditarians need to do to make their claims convincing?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Take all relevant factors into account in interpreting their data."},{"label":"B","text":"Conduct their research using more sophisticated technology."},{"label":"C","text":"Gather gene data from people of all social classes."},{"label":"D","text":"Cooperate with social scientists in their research."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Take all relevant factors into account in interpreting their data.","answerZh":"在解读数据时把所有相关因素都考虑进去。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段中的'If hereditarians want to advance their cause it will require more balanced interpretation and not just acts of advocacy'可知，作者认为遗传论者需要在解释数据时考虑所有相关因素，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"遗传决定论者需要做什么才能让自己的主张令人信服?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does the author warn against in the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Exaggerating the power of technology in shaping the world."},{"label":"B","text":"Losing sight of professional ethics in conducting research."},{"label":"C","text":"Misunderstanding the findings of human cognition research."},{"label":"D","text":"Promoting discrimination in the name of science."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Promoting discrimination in the name of science.","answerZh":"以科学之名助长歧视。","explanation":"这是一道观点态度题。根据文章最后一段中的'In understanding cognitive ability, we must not elevate discrimination to a science; allowing people to climb the ladder of life only as far as their cells might suggest'可知，作者警告不要以科学的名义推广歧视，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者在文章中警告人们提防什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2021_06_1-p2","title":"CET6 2021年06月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2021年06月 第1套","examDate":"2021年06月","year":"2021","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2021-06-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章支持苏格兰开征游客税的先行之举：旅游给当地公共服务带来沉重负担，游客理应付费分担社会成本，作者盼英国其他地区也获权效仿试行。","mainIdeaEn":"The author welcomes Scotland's move to let councils tax visitors: tourism strains local services and carries social costs tourists should help pay for, and other UK places should get the chance to follow.","answerCode":"BCDAC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先闻苏格兰要收游客税，再怪执政党反对税收监管，然后收税好补公共服务钱，接着批西客不顾社会代价，最后各方吵成一团。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn from Nicola Sturgeon's speech?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The UK is set to adjust its policy on taxation."},{"label":"B","text":"Tourists will have to pay a tax to visit Scotland."},{"label":"C","text":"The UK will take new measures to boost tourism."},{"label":"D","text":"Edinburgh contributes most to Scotland's tourism."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Tourists will have to pay a tax to visit Scotland.","answerZh":"游客到苏格兰旅游将需缴税。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'Scottish councils are set to be the first in the UK with the power to levy charges on visitors, with Edinburgh likely to lead the way'可知，苏格兰议会将成为英国第一个有权向游客征税的议会，因此B选项正确。","questionZh":"从 Nicola Sturgeon 的讲话中我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"How come the UK has been slow in imposing the tourist tax?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its government wants to attract more tourists."},{"label":"B","text":"The tax is unlikely to add much to its revenue."},{"label":"C","text":"Its ruling party is opposed to taxes and regulation."},{"label":"D","text":"It takes time for local governments to reach consensus."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Its ruling party is opposed to taxes and regulation.","answerZh":"其执政党反对征税和监管。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'That the UK lags behind is due to our weak, by international standards, local government, as well as the opposition to taxes and regulation of our aggressively pro-market ruling party'可知，英国迟迟未能征收旅游税是因为其地方政府力量较弱，以及执政党强烈反对税收和监管，因此C选项正确。","questionZh":"英国为什么迟迟没有开征旅游税?"},{"number":"53","stem":"Both international and domestic visitors in the UK should pay tourist tax so as to ___.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"elevate its tourism to international standards"},{"label":"B","text":"improve the welfare of its maintenance workers"},{"label":"C","text":"promote its cultural exchange with other nations"},{"label":"D","text":"ease its financial burden of providing local services"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"ease its financial burden of providing local services","answerZh":"减轻其提供当地公共服务的财政负担","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段'There is no reason why visitors to the UK, or domestic tourists on holiday in hot spots such as Cornwall, should be exempt from taxation-particularly when vital local services including waste collection, park maintenance and arts and culture spending are under unprecedented strain'可知，向英国的国际和国内游客征收旅游税是为了减轻提供当地服务的财政负担，因此D选项正确。","questionZh":"英国的国际游客和国内游客都应缴纳旅游税,以便___。"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does the author say about Western tourists?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They don't seem to care about the social cost of tourism."},{"label":"B","text":"They don't seem to mind paying for additional services."},{"label":"C","text":"They deem travel an important part of their life."},{"label":"D","text":"They subject the effects of tourism to scrutiny."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They don't seem to care about the social cost of tourism.","answerZh":"他们似乎并不在意旅游的社会成本。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第三段'Westerners with disposable incomes have often behaved as if they have a right to go wherever they choose with little regard for the consequences'可知，西方游客似乎不太关心旅游的社会成本，因此A选项正确。","questionZh":"关于西方游客,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What are UK people's opinions about the levy of tourist tax?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Supportive."},{"label":"B","text":"Skeptical."},{"label":"C","text":"Divided."},{"label":"D","text":"Unclear."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Divided.","answerZh":"意见不一。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章最后一段'The existence of new revenue streams for some but not all councils is complicated, and businesses are often opposed, fearing higher costs will make them uncompetitive'可以推断，英国人对征收旅游税的看法是分歧的，因此C选项正确。","questionZh":"英国民众对征收旅游税持什么看法?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2021_06_2-p1","title":"CET6 2021年06月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2021年06月 第2套","examDate":"2021年06月","year":"2021","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2021-06-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者反驳\"绘画是少数人天赋\"的观念，主张把绘画重新定位为人人皆有的学习与认知工具：涂画能提升专注和记忆，练画还能磨砺观察力。","mainIdeaEn":"Challenging the notion that drawing is an inborn artistic gift, the author recasts it as a universal tool for learning and understanding: doodling boosts attention and memory, and practice sharpens visual perception.","answerCode":"ACADD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先有人当画画是天赋，再谢艺术家扮靓世界，然后教授说人人天生会画，接着涂鸦帮你专注好记，最后靠眼睛看得精准。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do people generally think about drawing?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is a gift creative people are endowed with."},{"label":"B","text":"It is a skill that is acquired with practice."},{"label":"C","text":"It is an art form that is appreciated by all."},{"label":"D","text":"It is an ability everyone should cultivate."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is a gift creative people are endowed with.","answerZh":"它是有创造力的人天生具备的一种天赋。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章开篇指出'We often think of drawing as something that takes inborn talent'，即人们普遍认为画画是天赋使然。因此选项A正确。 - 关键句：We often think of drawing as something that takes inborn talent.","questionZh":"人们普遍如何看待绘画?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What do we learn about designers and artists?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are declining gradually in number."},{"label":"B","text":"They are keen on changing shabby surroundings."},{"label":"C","text":"They add beauty and charm to the world."},{"label":"D","text":"They spend most of their lives drawing."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They add beauty and charm to the world.","answerZh":"他们为世界增添美丽与魅力。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。第三段提到'a world without designers and artists would be a very shabby one indeed'，反过来说明设计师和艺术家让世界变得美好。因此选项C正确。 - 关键句：a world without designers and artists would be a very shabby one indeed.","questionZh":"关于设计师和艺术家,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does Professor D. B. Dowd argue in his book?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Everybody is born with the capacity to draw."},{"label":"B","text":"Drawing is a skill that requires special training."},{"label":"C","text":"The value of drawing tends to be overestimated."},{"label":"D","text":"Drawing should be redefined as a realistic illusion."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Everybody is born with the capacity to draw.","answerZh":"人人生来都具有绘画的能力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。Dowd 在书中指出我们错误地把画画视为一种'professional skill instead of a personal capacity'，并提到人类天生就会画画，强调人人具备绘画能力。因此选项A正确。 - 关键句：we have misfiled the significance of drawing because we see it as a professional skill instead of a personal capacity.","questionZh":"D. B. Dowd 教授在他的书中提出了什么观点?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What have some researchers found from one study about doodling?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is a must for maintaining a base level of brain activity."},{"label":"B","text":"It can turn something boring into something interesting."},{"label":"C","text":"It is the most reliable stimulant to activate the brain."},{"label":"D","text":"It helps improve concentration and memory."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It helps improve concentration and memory.","answerZh":"它有助于提高专注力和记忆力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。第六段研究显示涂画者比不涂画者多记住29%的名字，可见涂画提升注意力与记忆力。因此选项D正确。 - 关键句：Those who doodled remembered 29 percent more of the names than those who did not.","questionZh":"一些研究人员从一项关于随手涂画的研究中发现了什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What is the characteristic of people with drawing talent?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sensitivity to cognitive stimulation."},{"label":"B","text":"Subtlety of representation."},{"label":"C","text":"Accuracy in categorization."},{"label":"D","text":"Precision in visual perception."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Precision in visual perception.","answerZh":"视觉感知的精确性。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。第七段指出'drawing talent is based on how accurately someone perceives the world... artists perceive these qualities more accurately than non-artists'，可见绘画天赋的人善于精准感知。因此选项D正确。 - 关键句：drawing talent is based on how accurately someone perceives the world. The human visual system tends to misjudge size, shape, color, and angles but artists perceive these qualities more accurately than non-artists.","questionZh":"有绘画天赋的人有什么特点?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2021_06_2-p2","title":"CET6 2021年06月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2021年06月 第2套","examDate":"2021年06月","year":"2021","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2021-06-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"作者以汽车与导航应用为例说明技术的承诺常因意外后果而落空：人人用导航反把拥堵扩散到小路；鲁莽无序的变革未必造福，创新需要审慎监管。","mainIdeaEn":"Using cars and navigation apps as examples, the author argues technology rarely delivers its full promise—everyone's rerouting just spreads congestion—so reckless, uncontrolled innovation can harm us and thoughtful regulation is essential.","answerCode":"BCABC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先拆广告吹的自由假象，再见堵车才用上慢速装备，然后导航把堵挪到小路，接着叹科技承诺常打折，最后呼吁好好管创新。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author say about car advertisements?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They portray drivers who enjoy speed on the road."},{"label":"B","text":"They present a false picture of the autonomy cars provide."},{"label":"C","text":"They pursue individuality and originality in design concepts."},{"label":"D","text":"They overestimate the potential market of autonomous cars."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They present a false picture of the autonomy cars provide.","answerZh":"它们对汽车所带来的自由呈现了一幅虚假的图景。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段中的'There is something almost delightful in the detachment from reality of advertisements showing mass-produced cars marketed as symbols of individuality and of freedom'可以判断，作者认为汽车广告呈现出一种虚假的自主性，即大规模生产的汽车被宣传为个性和自由的象征，这与现实是脱节的。","questionZh":"关于汽车广告,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does the author imply about the various gadgets on cars?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They can help to alleviate traffic jams."},{"label":"B","text":"Most of them are as effective as advertised."},{"label":"C","text":"Only some can be put to use under current traffic conditions."},{"label":"D","text":"They are constantly upgraded to make driving easier and safer."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Only some can be put to use under current traffic conditions.","answerZh":"在当前交通状况下,只有部分装置能派上用场。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'the most useful gadgets on a modern car are those which work when you're going very slowly'，说明在当前交通状况下，只有部分汽车上的装置能够被使用。","questionZh":"关于汽车上的各种小装置,作者暗示了什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does the author say about the use of navigation apps?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is likely to create traffic jams in other places."},{"label":"B","text":"It helps a great deal in easing traffic congestion."},{"label":"C","text":"It sharply reduces the incidence of traffic accidents."},{"label":"D","text":"It benefits those who are learning to drive."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is likely to create traffic jams in other places.","answerZh":"它可能在其他地方造成交通拥堵。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'When everyone is using a navigation app which tells them to avoid everyone else using the same gadget. Traffic jams often appear where no one has enough information to avoid them.'说明当每个人都使用导航应用时，交通堵塞往往会出现在其他地方。","questionZh":"关于导航应用的使用,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does the author say about technology?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its consequences are usually difficult to assess."},{"label":"B","text":"It seldom delivers all the benefits as promised."},{"label":"C","text":"It depends on the required knowledge for application."},{"label":"D","text":"Its benefits are guaranteed by collective wisdom."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It seldom delivers all the benefits as promised.","answerZh":"它很少能兑现所承诺的全部好处。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段中的'The first is that the promises of technology will never be realised as fully as we hope; they will be limited by their unforeseen and unintended consequences.'表明技术很少能像我们希望的那样完全实现其承诺。","questionZh":"关于技术,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What key message does the author try to convey in the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The consequences of technological innovation need not be exaggerated."},{"label":"B","text":"There is always a price to pay to develop technology for a better world."},{"label":"C","text":"Technological innovation should be properly regulated."},{"label":"D","text":"The culture of Silicon Valley ought not to be emulated."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Technological innovation should be properly regulated.","answerZh":"技术创新应受到适当监管。","explanation":"这是一道主旨大意题。文章最后一段提到'What traffic teaches us is that reckless and uncontrolled change is as likely to harm us as it is to benefit us, and that thoughtful regulation is necessary for a better future.'表明作者试图传达的关键信息是技术创新应该得到适当的监管。","questionZh":"作者在文章中试图传达的核心信息是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2021_06_3-p1","title":"CET6 2021年06月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2021年06月 第3套","examDate":"2021年06月","year":"2021","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2021-06-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章呼吁把创造力培养贯穿全部学校课程：创造力促进智力成长却易被应试教育扼杀，公私立学校艺术教育差距悬殊，人人平等的创造力教育刻不容缓。","mainIdeaEn":"Creativity fosters intellectual growth but is easily crushed by exam-driven schooling; the author endorses embedding creative thinking across the whole curriculum and giving all children equal access to arts education.","answerCode":"DBCBC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说创造力宝贵易夭折，再要它贯穿全部课程，然后揪出应试教学祸首，接着看私校猛砸艺术课，最后盼人人平等学艺术。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about creativity?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It develops best when people are spiritually prepared."},{"label":"B","text":"It is most often wielded by scientists and entrepreneurs."},{"label":"C","text":"It is founded on scientific knowledge and analytical skills."},{"label":"D","text":"It contributes to intellectual growth but can easily be killed."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It contributes to intellectual growth but can easily be killed.","answerZh":"它有助于智力成长,但很容易被扼杀。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段最后一句'it flourishes most fully when people are playful and childlike. Meanwhile, it works best in conjunction with deep knowledge and expertise'可知，创造力在人们精神上准备好时发展最好，并且它与深厚的知识和专业技能结合时效果最佳，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于创造力,我们从文章中可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What is the conclusion of a recently-published report?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Natural sciences should be learned the way humanities courses are."},{"label":"B","text":"Cultivation of creativity should permeate the entire school curriculum."},{"label":"C","text":"Art courses should be made compulsory for all students."},{"label":"D","text":"Students should learn more obviously creative subjects."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Cultivation of creativity should permeate the entire school curriculum.","answerZh":"创造力的培养应贯穿整个学校课程。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段第二句'the report concludes that creativity should not inhabit the school curriculum only as it relates to drama, music, art and other obviously creative subjects, but that creative thinking ought to run through all of school life'可知，报告的结论是创造力的培养应该渗透到整个学校课程中，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"最近发表的一份报告得出了什么结论?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does the report say is detrimental to the fostering of creativity?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Alleviation of pressure."},{"label":"B","text":"Teacher-led school activities."},{"label":"C","text":"Test-oriented teaching."},{"label":"D","text":"Independent learning."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Test-oriented teaching.","answerZh":"应试教学。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段第二句'When children are regarded as vessels to be filled with facts, creativity does not prosper; nor does it when teachers' sole objective is coaching children towards exams'可知，以考试为导向的教学不利于创造力的培养，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"报告认为什么不利于培养创造力?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What do we learn about the private schools in the UK?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They encourage extracurricular activities."},{"label":"B","text":"They attach great importance to arts education."},{"label":"C","text":"They prioritize arts subjects over maths and sciences."},{"label":"D","text":"They cater to students from different family backgrounds."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They attach great importance to arts education.","answerZh":"它们非常重视艺术教育。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段第一句'The value placed on them by the independent education sector is clear'以及第二句'One only has to look at the remarkable arts facilities at Britain's top private schools to comprehend this'可知，英国私立学校非常重视艺术教育，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于英国的私立学校,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What should be done to meet the future challenges?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Increasing government investment in school education."},{"label":"B","text":"Narrowing the existing gap between the rich and the poor."},{"label":"C","text":"Providing all children with equal access to arts education."},{"label":"D","text":"Focusing on meeting the needs of under-privileged students."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Providing all children with equal access to arts education.","answerZh":"让所有孩子都能平等地接受艺术教育。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段最后一句'creativity in education, and for all, must become a priority'可知，为了应对未来的挑战，必须让所有儿童都能平等地接受艺术教育，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"应该怎样做才能应对未来的挑战?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2021_06_3-p2","title":"CET6 2021年06月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2021年06月 第3套","examDate":"2021年06月","year":"2021","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2021-06-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章从交谈中无意识的\"镜像\"行为谈起，讨论模仿的双面性：它是学习和形成个人风格的途径，但抄袭他人思想作品则侵犯知识产权，有益也有害。","mainIdeaEn":"Starting from unconscious 'mirroring' in conversation, the passage explores imitation's paradox: it aids learning and helps develop one's own style, yet copying others' ideas violates intellectual property—it can both help and harm.","answerCode":"CBAAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先聊天时不自觉学对方手势，再因彼此投缘互相镜像，然后流行文化怂恿模仿，接着博采众长炼出文风，最后叹模仿利弊参半。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do people tend to do while engaging in a conversation?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Repeat what their partners say one way or another."},{"label":"B","text":"Focus as much as possible on topics of mutual interest."},{"label":"C","text":"Imitate their partners' gestures without their knowing it."},{"label":"D","text":"Observe carefully how their partners make use of gestures."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Imitate their partners' gestures without their knowing it.","answerZh":"不知不觉地模仿谈话对方的手势。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'Emulating your conversation partner's actions is a common human behavior classified as 'mirroring' and has been known and studied by psychologists for years. We all tend to subconsciously copy gestures of people we like'，表明人们在交谈时会无意识地模仿对方的手势，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"人们在交谈时往往会做什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"When does mirroring usually take place in a conversation?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"When both sides are sympathetic with each other."},{"label":"B","text":"When both sides have a lot of things in common."},{"label":"C","text":"When both sides make interesting contributions."},{"label":"D","text":"When both sides try to seek common ground."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"When both sides have a lot of things in common.","answerZh":"当双方有很多共同点时。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段说'mirroring means that conversationalists enjoy their communication and that there's a certain level of agreement between them. The topic of discussion is equally interesting for both and they know their interests meet'——镜像通常发生在双方已存在共识、话题对双方同样有趣、兴趣相投之时，即双方有很多共同点。B（双方有很多共同点）正是 'agreement between them / their interests meet' 的同义改写，故选 B。","questionZh":"在交谈中,模仿通常发生在什么时候?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What do we learn about popular culture?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It encourages people to imitate."},{"label":"B","text":"It appeals mostly to big names."},{"label":"C","text":"It acquaints young people with their idols."},{"label":"D","text":"It can change people's mode of cognition."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It encourages people to imitate.","answerZh":"它鼓励人们模仿。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'Repeating someone's behavior is typical of talented communicators, not always because the person is sympathetic, but because there is a goal to be achieved. This way new idols have been brought to the stage: politicians, celebrities, and other big names. Popular culture makes people want to look popular, and act and speak like popular people'，说明流行文化鼓励人们模仿，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于流行文化,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"Why is the saying \"copy from two, it's research\" a lesson to learn?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It facilitates the creation of one's own writing style."},{"label":"B","text":"It helps to protect one's intellectual property rights."},{"label":"C","text":"It fosters correct interpretation of professional writing."},{"label":"D","text":"It enables one to write intriguing sequels to famous stories."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It facilitates the creation of one's own writing style.","answerZh":"它有助于形成自己的写作风格。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'The correct interpretation of this statement is not about copying, but rather about creating your own style. When you study an author's writing style, don't stop on a single one, but explore numerous styles instead'，说明'copy from two, it's research'的教训是为了促进个人写作风格的创造，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"为什么说 \"copy from two, it's research\" 这句话是一个值得吸取的教训?"},{"number":"55","stem":"Why does the author say imitation is rather paradoxical?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is liable to different interpretations."},{"label":"B","text":"It is by and large a necessary evil."},{"label":"C","text":"It can give rise to endless disputes."},{"label":"D","text":"It may do harm as well as good."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It may do harm as well as good.","answerZh":"它既可能有害,也可能有益。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到'Imitation is rather paradoxical. As an integral part of learning, it brings about positive changes, making people develop and grow. However, it may do a lot of harm. Copying someone's thoughts, ideas or inventions is completely unacceptable'，说明模仿既有积极的一面也有消极的一面，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者为什么说模仿颇具矛盾性?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2021_12_1-p1","title":"CET6 2021年12月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2021年12月 第1套","examDate":"2021年12月","year":"2021","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2021-12-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者指出自动化正大规模取代美国就业岗位，其害远超贸易冲击，工人日益不安；他质疑自动化利好的乐观论调，呼吁未雨绸缪，保障民众经济安全。","mainIdeaEn":"The author warns that automation, far more than trade, is eliminating American jobs and leaving workers insecure; skeptical of its promised benefits, he urges planning ahead to ensure everyone's economic security.","answerCode":"DBBCC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先看社区饭碗渐少，再知贸易背锅实属夸大，然后工人愈发心慌，接着疑自动化好处不实，最后求保大家经济安稳。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What can we observe from the author's description of our communities?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The growing passion for automation."},{"label":"B","text":"The shift from manual jobs to IT ones."},{"label":"C","text":"Their changing views on employment."},{"label":"D","text":"Their fading employment opportunities."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Their fading employment opportunities.","answerZh":"他们日渐减少的就业机会。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'automation is increasingly replacing jobs and leaving too few good new jobs behind'可知，作者描述了社区中就业机会的减少。因此，正确答案是D选项'Their fading employment opportunities'。","questionZh":"从作者对我们社区的描述中可以观察到什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What do we learn from a recent report?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The manufacturing sector is declining at a fast rate."},{"label":"B","text":"The concerns about the effect of trade are exaggerated."},{"label":"C","text":"The fears about trade have been spreading far and wide."},{"label":"D","text":"The impact of trade on employment has been staggering."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"The concerns about the effect of trade are exaggerated.","answerZh":"对贸易影响的担忧被夸大了。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段'a recent report showed that just 13 percent of jobs lost in manufacturing are due to trade—the rest of the losses have been due to advances in technology'可知，报告指出对贸易影响的担忧被夸大了，因为大部分制造业失业是由于技术进步而非贸易。因此，正确答案是B选项'The concerns about the effect of trade are exaggerated'。","questionZh":"从最近的一份报告中我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does the passage tell us about American workers in an era of transformation?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They feel ignored by politicians."},{"label":"B","text":"They feel increasingly vulnerable."},{"label":"C","text":"They keep adapting to the changes."},{"label":"D","text":"They keep complaining but to no avail."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They feel increasingly vulnerable.","answerZh":"他们感到越来越脆弱。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'workers have made clear their feelings about their economic insecurity and desire to keep good jobs in America'可知，美国工人在变革时代感到越来越脆弱。因此，正确答案是B选项'They feel increasingly vulnerable'。","questionZh":"关于变革时代的美国劳动者,文章告诉了我们什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What does the author think of automation?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It will have the same impact as industrialization."},{"label":"B","text":"It provides sensible companies with alternatives."},{"label":"C","text":"Its alleged positive effects are doubtful."},{"label":"D","text":"Its detrimental effects are unavoidable."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Its alleged positive effects are doubtful.","answerZh":"其所谓的积极作用值得怀疑。","explanation":"这是一道观点态度题。根据文章倒数第二段'I sincerely hope that those who assert that automation will make us more effective and pave the way for new occupations are right, but the reality of automation's detrimental effects on workers makes me skeptical'可知，作者对自动化所谓的积极效果持怀疑态度。因此，正确答案是C选项'Its alleged positive effects are doubtful'。","questionZh":"作者如何看待自动化?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What should we attach importance to when dealing with automation?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"College graduates' job prospects."},{"label":"B","text":"Women's access to employment."},{"label":"C","text":"People's economic security."},{"label":"D","text":"People's social mobility"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"People's economic security.","answerZh":"人们的经济保障。","explanation":"这是一道写作目的题。文章最后一段提到'If we want an economy that allows everyone to be economically secure, we need to start thinking about how we can rightfully address automation'，表明作者强调在处理自动化问题时应该重视人们的经济安全。因此，正确答案是C选项'People's economic security'。","questionZh":"在应对自动化时,我们应该重视什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2021_12_1-p2","title":"CET6 2021年12月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2021年12月 第1套","examDate":"2021年12月","year":"2021","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2021-12-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"新研究表明国籍只能解释文化价值观差异的一小部分，职业和社会经济地位才是最强相关因素；作者主张少以国界概括人，多看收入等实际约束。","mainIdeaEn":"New research shows nationality explains little of the variation in cultural values; occupation and socioeconomic status matter far more, so we should identify people by economic circumstances rather than by country.","answerCode":"AABCD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先怪专家只看国籍，再借霍氏维度跨时空比较，然后发现钱包影响被低估，接着员工没学会跨国打交道，最后认收入更能说明人。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What error do experts often make when describing people from other places?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They tend to overly rely on nationality."},{"label":"B","text":"They often exaggerate their differences."},{"label":"C","text":"They often misunderstand their cultures."},{"label":"D","text":"They tend to dwell on national averages."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They tend to overly rely on nationality.","answerZh":"他们往往过度依赖国籍。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。第一段指出谈论他乡之人时'we seem to inevitably characterize them based on their country of origin'（不可避免地根据其原籍国来定性他们），第二段紧接着说'Statistics specialists, when they speak of national averages, often make the same mistake'——'the same mistake'回指第一段的错误，即过度依赖国籍来判断人，故专家所犯的错误本质是过于依赖国籍，对应A。D'谈论国家平均值'只是他们的做法/载体，并非题目所问的'错误'本身。 - 关键句：Statistics specialists, when they speak of national averages, often make the same mistake.","questionZh":"专家在描述来自其他地方的人时常犯什么错误?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What do we learn about Hofstede's cultural dimensions?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are useful in comparing cultural values across time and space."},{"label":"B","text":"They have brought unusual benefits to people of different cultures."},{"label":"C","text":"They are widely used to identify people's individual traits."},{"label":"D","text":"They provide valuable questions for researchers to study."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They are useful in comparing cultural values across time and space.","answerZh":"它们在跨时空比较文化价值观方面很有用。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段'Though the validity of Hofstede's dimensions has been questioned, they have the singular benefit of having been in use for decades, which allows for historical and international comparisons'可知，Hofstede的文化维度有助于跨时空比较文化价值，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于 Hofstede 的文化维度理论,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What did researchers find about previous studies on factors determining people's value?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Environmental factors were prioritized over other factors."},{"label":"B","text":"An individual's financial status was often underestimated."},{"label":"C","text":"Too much emphasis had been placed on one's occupation."},{"label":"D","text":"The impact of social progress on one's values was ignored."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"An individual's financial status was often underestimated.","answerZh":"个人的经济状况常常被低估。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'The researchers found that both demographic factors, such as age, and environmental factors, such as long-term unemployment rates, were more correlated with cultural values than nationality. Occupation and social economic status were the most strongly correlated'可知，以前的研究可能低估了个人财务状况对文化价值的影响，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"研究人员对以往关于决定人们价值观因素的研究有什么发现?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What is the impact on employees when cultures are identified with countries?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They may fail to see the cultural biases of their business partners."},{"label":"B","text":"They may fail to attach sufficient importance to cultural diversity."},{"label":"C","text":"They may not be taught how to properly interact with overseas partners."},{"label":"D","text":"They may not be able to learn the legal procedures for business transactions."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They may not be taught how to properly interact with overseas partners.","answerZh":"他们可能得不到关于如何与海外伙伴妥善交往的培训。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段'Taras says our erroneous belief that countries are cultures has caused businesses to teach their employees useless or even harmful ways of interacting with their international peers'可知，将文化等同于国家可能导致员工没有被教会如何正确地与海外合作伙伴互动，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"把文化等同于国家会对员工产生什么影响?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author suggest at the end of the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"There is sufficient reason to generalize about a country's population."},{"label":"B","text":"The majority of people are still constrained by their national identity."},{"label":"C","text":"It is arguable that the country should be regarded as the unit of authority."},{"label":"D","text":"Nationality is less useful than socio-economic status as an indicator of one's values."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Nationality is less useful than socio-economic status as an indicator of one's values.","answerZh":"作为个人价值观的指标,国籍不如社会经济地位有用。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'In the majority of cases we would be better off identifying people by the factors that constrain their lives, like income, rather than by the lines surrounding them on a map'可知，作者建议将国籍作为价值观指标不如社会经济地位有用，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者在文章结尾提出了什么建议?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2021_12_2-p1","title":"CET6 2021年12月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2021年12月 第2套","examDate":"2021年12月","year":"2021","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2021-12-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章探讨雇主是否应利用社交媒体筛查求职者：这种做法普遍但暗藏道德与法律风险，作者主张须合法、审慎地使用，并事先咨询管理与法律团队。","mainIdeaEn":"The passage weighs whether employers should screen job candidates via social media: the practice is common but carries ethical and legal risks, so it must be done lawfully, responsibly, and with expert advice.","answerCode":"DAABC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先争要不要网上查应聘者，再怕惹道德法律麻烦，然后见断章取义害人，接着只按合法路子用，最后先问管理法务专家。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What does the author mainly discuss in the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The advantage of using social media in screening job candidates."},{"label":"B","text":"The potentially invasive nature of social media in everyday life."},{"label":"C","text":"Whether the benefits of social media outweigh the drawbacks."},{"label":"D","text":"Whether social media should be used to screen job candidates."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Whether social media should be used to screen job candidates.","answerZh":"是否应该用社交媒体来筛选求职者。","explanation":"这是一道主旨大意题。文章主要讨论了社交媒体在筛选求职者时的使用问题，包括其普遍性、潜在的法律风险和道德问题，以及如何专业和负责任地使用社交媒体信息。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者在文章中主要讨论了什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What might happen when social media is used to screen job candidates?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Moral or legal issues might arise."},{"label":"B","text":"Company reputation might suffer."},{"label":"C","text":"Sensational information might surface."},{"label":"D","text":"Hiring decisions might be complicated."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Moral or legal issues might arise.","answerZh":"可能引发道德或法律问题。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章提到，不当使用社交媒体筛选可能会引发道德或法律问题，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"用社交媒体筛选求职者时可能发生什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"When could online personal information be detrimental to candidates?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"When it is separated from context."},{"label":"B","text":"When it is scrutinised by an employer."},{"label":"C","text":"When it is magnified to a ruinous degree."},{"label":"D","text":"When it is revealed to the human resources."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"When it is separated from context.","answerZh":"当信息脱离语境时。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章提到，社交媒体上的私人信息如果被断章取义可能会对求职者不利，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"网上的个人信息在什么情况下可能对求职者不利?"},{"number":"49","stem":"How can employers use social media information to their advantage while avoiding unnecessary risks?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"By tipping the delicate balance."},{"label":"B","text":"By using it in a legitimate way."},{"label":"C","text":"By keeping personal information on record."},{"label":"D","text":"By separating relevant from irrelevant data."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"By using it in a legitimate way.","answerZh":"以合法的方式使用这些信息。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章提到，使用社交媒体信息要合法，这样可以避免不必要的风险，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"雇主如何才能既利用社交媒体信息又避免不必要的风险?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does the author suggest doing before screening job candidates on social media?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hiring professionals to navigate the whole process."},{"label":"B","text":"Anticipating potential risks involved in the process."},{"label":"C","text":"Seeking advice from management and legal experts."},{"label":"D","text":"Stipulating a set of rules for asking specific questions."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Seeking advice from management and legal experts.","answerZh":"征求管理和法律专家的意见。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到，在社交媒体上筛选求职者之前，最好咨询管理和法律团队，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者建议在用社交媒体筛选求职者之前先做什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2021_12_2-p2","title":"CET6 2021年12月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2021年12月 第2套","examDate":"2021年12月","year":"2021","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2021-12-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章批评食品行业流行的\"不含XX\"标签：它迎合消费者知情需求却制造无谓恐慌，长远会侵蚀整个行业的信任并拉低销量，厂商应慎用此类声明。","mainIdeaEn":"The author criticizes the food industry's 'absence claims' labels: though they exploit consumers' demand for transparency, they stoke unfounded fears, erode trust in the whole food business, and will ultimately hurt sales.","answerCode":"DADCB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先见顾客要知情，再有商家标榜啥都不含，然后吓得人人怕食品，接着信任销量双双下滑，最后劝慎打不含牌。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What trend has been observed in a report?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Food manufacturers' rising awareness of product safety."},{"label":"B","text":"Food manufacturers' changing strategies to bolster profits."},{"label":"C","text":"Consumers' growing demand for eye-catching food labels."},{"label":"D","text":"Consumers' increasing desire for clear product information."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Consumers' increasing desire for clear product information.","answerZh":"消费者对清晰产品信息的需求日益增长。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'One report found that 39 percent of consumers would switch from the brands they currently buy to others that provide clearer, more accurate product information'，可以得出消费者越来越渴望清晰的产品信息，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"一份报告中观察到了什么趋势?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does the author say is manufacturers' new marketing strategy?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Stressing the absence of certain elements in their products."},{"label":"B","text":"Articulating the unique nutritional value of their products."},{"label":"C","text":"Supplying detailed information of their products."},{"label":"D","text":"Designing transparent labels for their products."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Stressing the absence of certain elements in their products.","answerZh":"强调其产品中不含某些成分。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'But the marketing strategy in response to this consumer demand has gone beyond articulating what is in a product, to labeling what is NOT in the food'，说明制造商的新营销策略是强调产品中没有的某些元素，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者说制造商新的营销策略是什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What point does the author make about non-GMO labels?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are increasingly attracting customers' attention."},{"label":"B","text":"They create lots of trouble for GMO food producers."},{"label":"C","text":"They should be used more for vegetables and milk."},{"label":"D","text":"They cause anxiety about food among consumers."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They cause anxiety about food among consumers.","answerZh":"它们引发消费者对食品的焦虑。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'Some dairy companies are using the 'non-GMO' label on their milk, despite the fact that all milk is naturally GMO-free, another label that creates unnecessary fear around food'，说明非转基因标签引起了消费者对食品的不必要恐慌，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于非转基因标签,作者提出了什么观点?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does the author say absence claims labels will do to food manufacturers?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cause changes in their marketing strategies."},{"label":"B","text":"Help remove stigma around their products."},{"label":"C","text":"Erode consumer trust and reduce sales."},{"label":"D","text":"Decrease support from food scientists."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Erode consumer trust and reduce sales.","answerZh":"削弱消费者信任并减少销量。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'For food manufacturers, it will mean damaged consumer trust and lower sales for everyone'，说明标签声明会削弱消费者信任并减少销售，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者说\"不含某成分\"类标签会对食品制造商产生什么影响?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author suggest food manufacturers do?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Take measures to lower the cost of food products."},{"label":"B","text":"Exercise caution about the use of absence claims."},{"label":"C","text":"Welcome new innovations in food processing."},{"label":"D","text":"Promote efficiency and increase food variety."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Exercise caution about the use of absence claims.","answerZh":"谨慎使用“不含”类声明。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'If we allow this kind of labeling to continue, we will all lose'，紧接着作者建议食品制造商在使用标签声明时应该谨慎，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者建议食品制造商怎么做?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2021_12_3-p1","title":"CET6 2021年12月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2021年12月 第3套","examDate":"2021年12月","year":"2021","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2021-12-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者借波兹曼的观点指出，电视把文字文化变成图像文化，使美国社会从理性论说滑向娱乐化、肤浅化；早期以求知为本的网络曾一度抗衡这一趋势。","mainIdeaEn":"Drawing on Neil Postman, the passage argues television shifted culture from rational, text-based discourse to image-driven entertainment, making public life superficial, while the early text-based web briefly resisted this trend as a knowledge tool.","answerCode":"ADDCB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先叹电视让理性让位娱乐，再赞读文字练批判思维，然后见交往变肤浅，接着忆早期网络为求知，最后看网民只求点赞。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What did Neil Postman say about the rise of television?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It initiated a change from dominance of reason to supremacy of pleasure."},{"label":"B","text":"It brought about a gradual shift from cinema going 1o home entertainment."},{"label":"C","text":"It started a revolution in photographic technology."},{"label":"D","text":"It marked a new age in the entertainment industry."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It initiated a change from dominance of reason to supremacy of pleasure.","answerZh":"它开启了一场从理性主导到娱乐至上的转变。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'the rise of television introduced not just a new medium but a new discourse: a gradual shift from a typographic culture to a photographic one, which in turn meant a shift from rationality to emotions, exposition to entertainment'可知，Neil Postman认为电视的兴起导致了从理性到情感，从阐释到娱乐的转变，即从理性的主导到娱乐的至高无上。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于电视的兴起,Neil Postman 说了什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"According to the passage, what is the advantage of text reading?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It gives one access to huge amounts of information."},{"label":"B","text":"It allows more information to be processed quickly."},{"label":"C","text":"It is capable of enriching one's life."},{"label":"D","text":"It is conducive to critical thinking."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is conducive to critical thinking.","answerZh":"它有利于培养批判性思维。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'Postman noted, there is no place for rational thinking because you simply cannot think with images. It is text that enables us to \"uncover lies, confusions and overgeneralizations, and to detect abuses of logic and common sense. It also means to weigh ideas, to compare and contrast assertions, to connect one generalization to another.'可知，文本阅读有助于批判性思维，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"根据文章,文字阅读的优势是什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"How has television impacted Americans?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has given them a lot more to argue about."},{"label":"B","text":"It has brought celebrities closer to their lives."},{"label":"C","text":"It has made them care more about what they say."},{"label":"D","text":"It has rendered their interactions more superficial."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It has rendered their interactions more superficial.","answerZh":"它使美国人的交往变得更加肤浅。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段'Americans don't talk to each other; we entertain each other,' Postman wrote. 'They don't exchange ideas; they exchange images. They do not argue with propositions; they argue with good looks, celebrities, and commercials.'可知，电视使美国人的互动变得更加肤浅，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"电视对美国人产生了怎样的影响?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What does the passage say about the World Wide Web?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It was developed primarily for universities worldwide."},{"label":"B","text":"It was created to connect people in different countries."},{"label":"C","text":"It was viewed as a means to quest for knowledge."},{"label":"D","text":"It was designed as a discussion forum for university students."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It was viewed as a means to quest for knowledge.","answerZh":"它曾被视为求取知识的手段。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'When it emerged towards the end of the 1980s as a purely text-based medium, it was seen as a tool to pursue knowledge, not pleasure.'可知，万维网被视为追求知识而非娱乐的工具，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于万维网,文章说了什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What do we learn about users of social media?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are bent on looking for an alternative space for escape."},{"label":"B","text":"They are constantly seeking approval from their audience."},{"label":"C","text":"They are forever engaged in hunting for new information."},{"label":"D","text":"They are unable to focus their attention on tasks for long."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They are constantly seeking approval from their audience.","answerZh":"他们不断寻求受众的认可。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章最后一段'For more than a decade, the web created an alternative space that threatened television's grip on society.'可知，万维网创造了一个替代空间，威胁到电视对社会的控制。由此可以推断，社交媒体用户可能在不断寻求观众的认可，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于社交媒体的用户,我们可以了解到什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2021_12_3-p2","title":"CET6 2021年12月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2021年12月 第3套","examDate":"2021年12月","year":"2021","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2021-12-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章讨论职场中日益增多的\"特权感\"员工：他们自视过高、消极怠工，源于童年被溺爱；研究发现要求明确、公正守信的道德型领导能缓解其负面影响。","mainIdeaEn":"A growing sense of entitlement among employees, rooted in indulgent upbringing, hurts workplace engagement; research finds ethical leaders—who set clear expectations and keep promises—can mitigate its negative effects.","answerCode":"BBDCA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先有员工嫌给得太少，再查是从小被宠坏，然后靠经理设法留住干劲，接着上司把要求讲明白，最后服说到做到的头儿。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does a recent study find about a growing number of workers?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They attempt to make more contributions."},{"label":"B","text":"They feel they deserve more than they get."},{"label":"C","text":"They attach importance to job satisfaction."},{"label":"D","text":"They try to diminish workplace dysfunction."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They feel they deserve more than they get.","answerZh":"他们觉得自己应得的比实际得到的多。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'A recent study reveals a small but growing proportion of the workforce is affected to some degree by a sense of entitlement. Work is less about what they can contribute and more about what they can take.'可知，越来越多的员工感到他们应该得到更多，而不是他们能贡献什么。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"最近一项研究对越来越多的劳动者有什么发现?"},{"number":"52","stem":"Why don't some employees work hard according to many scholars?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They lack a strong sense of self-worth."},{"label":"B","text":"They were spoiled when growing up."},{"label":"C","text":"They have received unfair treatment."},{"label":"D","text":"They are overindulged by their boss."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They were spoiled when growing up.","answerZh":"他们成长过程中被宠坏了。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'Many scholars believe this tendency begins in childhood, due to overindulgent parents, leading these individuals to expect the same kind of treatment throughout their adult lives.'可知，一些学者认为，由于父母过度溺爱，这些员工在成长过程中被宠坏了，导致他们不努力工作。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"许多学者认为一些员工为什么不努力工作?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What is a manager supposed to do to enable workers to do a better job?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Be aware of their emotions."},{"label":"B","text":"Give them timely promotions."},{"label":"C","text":"Keep a record of their performance."},{"label":"D","text":"Seek ways to sustain their motivation."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Seek ways to sustain their motivation.","answerZh":"设法维持他们的工作动力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段'Despite their feelings, it's crucial for managers to find ways to keep them motivated.'可知，管理者需要找到方法来保持员工的积极性，以使他们更好地工作。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"管理者应该怎么做才能让员工把工作做得更好?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What do the research findings reveal about ethical leaders?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are held accountable by their employees."},{"label":"B","text":"They are always transparent in their likes and dislikes."},{"label":"C","text":"They convey their requirements in a straightforward way."},{"label":"D","text":"They make it a point to be on good terms with their employees."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They convey their requirements in a straightforward way.","answerZh":"他们以直截了当的方式传达自己的要求。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'Ethical leaders communicate clear expectations, hold employees accountable, and are committed to doing the right thing.'可知，道德领导者以直接的方式传达他们的要求。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"研究结果揭示了道德型领导的什么情况?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What kind of leaders are viewed as ethical by entitled employees?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Those who can be counted on to fulfill commitments."},{"label":"B","text":"Those who can do things beyond normal expectations."},{"label":"C","text":"Those who exercise caution in making major decisions."},{"label":"D","text":"Those who know how to satisfy their employees' needs."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Those who can be counted on to fulfill commitments.","answerZh":"那些可以信赖、说到做到的领导。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'entitled employees feel more confident that ethical leaders will deliver on their promises, as they are perceived to be fair and trustworthy.'可知，被认为道德的领导者是那些能够信守承诺的人。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"在自认应得的员工眼中,什么样的领导才算有道德?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2022_06_1-p1","title":"CET6 2022年06月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2022年06月 第1套","examDate":"2022年06月","year":"2022","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2022-06-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者为美国精英大学辩护：面对\"太贵、脱离就业\"的指责和新征税，他强调通识教育助毕业生在各领域成功，助学金让教育更普惠，其价值需要被讲清。","mainIdeaEn":"Defending selective U.S. colleges against attacks and new taxes, the author argues their liberal arts education prepares graduates to excel in any field and their financial aid broadens access and opportunity.","answerCode":"BACDB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先赞名校保学生前程，再夸它推动国家发展，然后惊税案险增学费负担，接着看通识生行行出彩，最后享多元同窗之益。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What fact does the author emphasize concerning selective colleges and universities?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They have been ignoring the training of graduates for the world of work."},{"label":"B","text":"They have been doing well in ensuring their students a successful future."},{"label":"C","text":"They have been constantly attacked for being too elite and too expensive."},{"label":"D","text":"They have been actively engaged in civic life beyond the school campus."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They have been doing well in ensuring their students a successful future.","answerZh":"它们一直很好地确保了学生拥有成功的未来。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'These colleges and universities must be doing something right'，说明作者认为这些学院和大学在确保学生未来成功方面做得不错。","questionZh":"关于择优录取的高校,作者强调了什么事实?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the author say in arguing for the model of education in the U.S.?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has contributed substantially to the nation's overall development."},{"label":"B","text":"It has succeeded in maintaining sustainable financial aid programs."},{"label":"C","text":"It has given priority to innovative programs for graduate studies."},{"label":"D","text":"It has played a central role in attracting international applicants."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It has contributed substantially to the nation's overall development.","answerZh":"它为国家的整体发展做出了重大贡献。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'This model of education has long played a central role in creating opportunity, driving economic growth, and spurring innovation'，说明这种教育模式对国家的整体发展做出了重要贡献。","questionZh":"作者在为美国的教育模式辩护时说了什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What do we learn about the initial proposals concerning the recent tax reform bill?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They would have stripped many students of life's chances."},{"label":"B","text":"They would have deducted graduate student loan interest."},{"label":"C","text":"They would have added to many students' financial burden."},{"label":"D","text":"They would have increased the number of tuition waivers."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They would have added to many students' financial burden.","answerZh":"它们本会加重许多学生的经济负担。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到最初的提案'would have made education unaffordable for many by taxing tuition waivers for graduate students and ending deductions for student loan interest'，说明这些提案会增加许多学生的经济负担。","questionZh":"关于近期税改法案的最初提案,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What do the data show about elite colleges and universities?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Their graduates lack the rigor required for doing statistical analysis."},{"label":"B","text":"Their students prove to be inadequately prepared for their future careers."},{"label":"C","text":"Their focus on research is conducive to developing students' critical thinking."},{"label":"D","text":"Their liberal arts education enables graduates to excel in whatever field they are in."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Their liberal arts education enables graduates to excel in whatever field they are in.","answerZh":"其人文通识教育使毕业生在任何领域都能出类拔萃。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'The data are clear: a liberal arts education is great career preparation, both for excellent lifetime earnings and for satisfaction with the work. This education develops the skills... and the ability to keep learning. In fact, liberal arts graduates do extremely well in every imaginable field'，说明这些学院和大学的文科教育使毕业生在任何领域都能表现出色。","questionZh":"数据显示了精英高校的什么情况?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What is an advantage of providing financial aid for students?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Every student can choose the institution they wish to attend."},{"label":"B","text":"All students can benefit from a diversified student population."},{"label":"C","text":"All students will be able to earn a place on university campus."},{"label":"D","text":"Less privileged students will be more competitive at elite schools."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"All students can benefit from a diversified student population.","answerZh":"所有学生都能从多元化的学生群体中受益。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'the diversity of economic backgrounds enhances the education and experience of all of our students'，说明为学生提供财政援助的一个优势是所有学生都能从多元化的学生群体中受益。","questionZh":"为学生提供助学金有什么好处?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2022_06_1-p2","title":"CET6 2022年06月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2022年06月 第1套","examDate":"2022年06月","year":"2022","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2022-06-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"作者指出所谓\"常识\"只是感觉正确的主观判断，易受既有观念和认知偏差误导；唯有借助科学这种社会协作式验证，才能克服个人思维的局限。","mainIdeaEn":"The author argues that appeals to common sense are subjective judgments shaped by biases and prior beliefs; only socially verified, collaborative scientific inquiry can overcome individuals' cognitive limitations.","answerCode":"ADACD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先见众人不讲理性，再识常识只是主观感觉，然后知它易判错，接着靠科学共同验证，最后信合作胜过单干。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author intend to show by citing the findings from the report published last year?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"People seldom appeal to rationality in their thinking."},{"label":"B","text":"It is often the case that truth lies in the hands of a few."},{"label":"C","text":"Common sense and science are the two sides of a coin."},{"label":"D","text":"Few people know if climate change is really happening."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"People seldom appeal to rationality in their thinking.","answerZh":"人们在思考时很少诉诸理性。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到36%的澳大利亚人认为气候变化没有发生是因为'common sense'，而只有11%的人是基于科学研究。作者引用这一数据是为了说明人们在思考问题时很少诉诸理性，而是依赖于直觉或个人感受，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者引用去年发表的报告结论想要说明什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What is the appeal to common sense according to the author?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is the basis for the internalisation of individuals' ideologies."},{"label":"B","text":"It is a series of conceptions formulated from complex reasoning."},{"label":"C","text":"It is collective wisdom that helps people interact with new ideas."},{"label":"D","text":"It is something subjective based on what one perceives to be right."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is something subjective based on what one perceives to be right.","answerZh":"它是基于个人认为正确的东西而形成的主观判断。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'The appeal to common sense, however, is usually nothing more than an appeal to thinking that just feels right, but what feels right to one person may not feel right to another.'，说明常识的诉求是基于个人主观感受，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者认为诉诸常识是怎么回事?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does Daniel Kahneman think is the problem of testing new ideas with existing beliefs?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It may lead to incorrect judgment."},{"label":"B","text":"It makes no use of common sense."},{"label":"C","text":"It fails to correct mistakes through serious reasoning."},{"label":"D","text":"It can produce psychologically unacceptable outcomes."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It may lead to incorrect judgment.","answerZh":"它可能导致错误的判断。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章第三段提到'As Nobelist Daniel Kahneman notes in Thinking, Fast and Slow, when we arrive at conclusions in this way, the outcomes also feel true, regardless of whether they are.'，说明用现有信念测试新想法可能导致错误的判断，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Daniel Kahneman 认为用已有观念检验新想法的问题是什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What can we do to be less susceptible to cognitive biases?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Give equal weight to evidence of both sides in a conflict."},{"label":"B","text":"Provide convincing examples in developing an argument."},{"label":"C","text":"Establish socially shared cognition via scientific methods."},{"label":"D","text":"Avoid inconsistencies when addressing controversial issues."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Establish socially shared cognition via scientific methods.","answerZh":"通过科学方法建立社会共享的认知。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'One way we can check our internal biases and inconsistencies is through the social verification of knowledge, in which we test our ideas in a rigorous and systematic way to see if they make sense not just to us, but to other people.'，说明通过社会共享的认知，即科学方法，可以减少认知偏差，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"我们可以怎样做来减少受认知偏差的影响?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What message does the author try to convey at the end of the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Multiple perspectives stimulate people's interest in exploring the unknown."},{"label":"B","text":"Individuals can enhance their overall capabilities by interacting with others."},{"label":"C","text":"Individuals should think freely to break from the restrictions of common sense."},{"label":"D","text":"Collaborative efforts can overcome individuals limitations in scientific inquiry."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Collaborative efforts can overcome individuals limitations in scientific inquiry.","answerZh":"协作努力可以克服个人在科学探究中的局限。","explanation":"这是一道主旨大意题。文章最后一段提到'We are smarter together than we are individually, and perhaps that's just common sense.'，强调了合作努力可以克服个人在科学探究中的局限性，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者在文章结尾试图传达什么信息?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2022_06_2-p1","title":"CET6 2022年06月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2022年06月 第2套","examDate":"2022年06月","year":"2022","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2022-06-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章讨论AI用于音乐创作的争议：有人视之为激发灵感的工具，有人斥其损害音乐的人性价值；作者认为应以开放心态拥抱，AI音乐终将成为常态。","mainIdeaEn":"The passage examines the debate over AI in music creation—seen by some as a helpful creative tool and by others as a threat to music's human essence—and concludes AI-made music will likely become the norm.","answerCode":"BAADB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先有人骂AI毁音乐，再见它帮人写歌，然后嫌作品没人味，接着说音乐属于人类，最后料定它成常态。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"How do some musicians perceive using AI in creating music?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It would help to produce more music idols."},{"label":"B","text":"It would be detrimental to music production."},{"label":"C","text":"It would hinder the understanding of authentic music."},{"label":"D","text":"It would be the beginning of a new era in music creation."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It would be detrimental to music production.","answerZh":"它会不利于音乐创作。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段内容，'Contrary to seeing AI as a tool, some musicians consider it to be hugely detrimental to the music scene'，表明一些音乐家认为使用AI在创作音乐上是有害的，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"一些音乐人如何看待用 AI 创作音乐?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does Taryn Southern's story illustrate?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"AI technology is conducive to music composition."},{"label":"B","text":"Musicians will be unable to create music without high tech."},{"label":"C","text":"Musicians are often at their wits, end in their creative effort."},{"label":"D","text":"AI technology is indispensable to creating melodies and chords."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"AI technology is conducive to music composition.","answerZh":"AI 技术有助于音乐创作。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'AI software enabled her to communicate melodies and chords that she didn't know how to put together herself'，说明AI技术有助于音乐创作，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Taryn Southern 的故事说明了什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"Why are some musicians opposed to the use of AI in creating music?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Music produced with AI technology lacks humanness."},{"label":"B","text":"Music created with AI technology is easily emulated."},{"label":"C","text":"It will depreciate humans' role in music composition."},{"label":"D","text":"It will deplete young musicians, creative inspiration."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Music produced with AI technology lacks humanness.","answerZh":"用 AI 技术创作的音乐缺乏人情味。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'the music it's producing is not necessarily what we want to hear. In short, it's not of great quality'和'a computer could never emulate the work (and human touch) of a true musician'，说明一些音乐家反对使用AI创作音乐是因为AI技术制作的音乐缺乏人情味，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"一些音乐人为什么反对用 AI 创作音乐?"},{"number":"49","stem":"Why do many people think music is too precious to impart to AI technology?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It cannot be created without pains."},{"label":"B","text":"It cannot be produced at random."},{"label":"C","text":"It is part of human life."},{"label":"D","text":"It is human specific."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is human specific.","answerZh":"它是人类特有的。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'Since many people see music as such an inherently human expression, it is often considered as too precious to impart to technology'，说明很多人认为音乐是太珍贵而不能交给AI技术的东西，因为它是人类特有的表达方式，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"许多人为什么认为音乐太宝贵而不能交给 AI 技术?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does the author think of the future of AI music?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It will continue to arouse the interest of music investors."},{"label":"B","text":"It has the prospect of becoming the norm in the future."},{"label":"C","text":"It will be gradually accepted by old-school musicians."},{"label":"D","text":"It may eventually lose its freshness and appeal."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It has the prospect of becoming the norm in the future.","answerZh":"它有望在未来成为常态。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到'it's only a matter of time before AI-produced music is seen as the new norm'，说明作者认为AI音乐有成为未来常态的前景，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者如何看待 AI 音乐的未来?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2022_06_2-p2","title":"CET6 2022年06月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2022年06月 第2套","examDate":"2022年06月","year":"2022","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2022-06-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"作者认为向公众传播科学是提升其科学素养的必要之举，但科学传播本身是门学问：学者应承认知识边界、请教专家，并接受训练培养沟通技能。","mainIdeaEn":"Communicating science to the public is necessary, but it is a discipline in itself: scientists must recognize their limits, consult specialists outside their field, and train to develop real communication skills.","answerCode":"BCDCD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说科普很必要，再遇难题问专家，然后夸公众其实懂行，接着叹大学者讲不明白，最后劝去练沟通本事。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author say about communicating science to the general public?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It will help them to keep abreast of the latest scientific developments."},{"label":"B","text":"It is a necessary means to improve their understanding of scientific issues."},{"label":"C","text":"It will get them more involved in academic debates on environmental problems."},{"label":"D","text":"It is an effective way to augment scientists' influence beyond the academic circle."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It is a necessary means to improve their understanding of scientific issues.","answerZh":"这是提高公众对科学问题理解的必要手段。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'Communicating science beyond the academic bubble is necessary to augment public understanding of health and environmental issues and help individuals make well-informed personal decisions'，说明作者认为向公众传播科学知识是提高他们对科学问题理解的必要手段，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于向大众传播科学,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does the author advise scientists to do to deal with topics outside of their specialty?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Write or present them from new angles."},{"label":"B","text":"Utilize information from diverse sources."},{"label":"C","text":"Turn to a specialist for professional help."},{"label":"D","text":"Fact-check with colleagues in their field."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Turn to a specialist for professional help.","answerZh":"向专家寻求专业帮助。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'That is not to suggest that they only write or present on their own research, but rather, that they consult with an expert if the topic is outside of their discipline'，说明作者建议科学家在遇到非专业话题时，应向专家求助。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者建议科学家如何处理自己专业以外的话题?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does the author say we can learn from social media?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A solid academic foundation is essential to understanding baffling scientific principles."},{"label":"B","text":"Modern technology has facilitated communication between scientists and the public."},{"label":"C","text":"Scientific articles have gained increasing popularity among the general public."},{"label":"D","text":"The public's understanding of science is much better than some have claimed."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The public's understanding of science is much better than some have claimed.","answerZh":"公众对科学的理解远比某些人所说的要好。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'If anything, social media has shown that the public craves knowledge based on a solid scientific foundation. Even the public discourse that follows most scientific articles shows that online readers can understand even the most baffling of scientific principles'，说明社交媒体显示公众渴望基于科学基础的知识，并且能够理解复杂的科学原理，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者说我们可以从社交媒体中学到什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does the example of the biologist who shared an intricate analogy show?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is helpful to use illustrations in explaining scientific phenomena."},{"label":"B","text":"It is imperative to have appropriate titles to explain scientific issues."},{"label":"C","text":"A learned scholar is not necessarily a qualified science communicator."},{"label":"D","text":"A nonscientific audience cannot duly understand principles of science."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"A learned scholar is not necessarily a qualified science communicator.","answerZh":"博学的学者未必是合格的科学传播者。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'One biologist shared an intricate analogy involving a library, books, paper, a recipe, ingredients, and a cake to explain the process behind vaccines. Any explanation that requires a written key to keep track of what each item represents is not a clear example for public consumption'，说明即使是有学问的学者也不一定是合格的科学传播者，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"那位分享复杂类比的生物学家的例子说明了什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author suggest scientists do to close the gap between science and society?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Explain complex concepts scientifically."},{"label":"B","text":"Make appropriate use of scientific terms."},{"label":"C","text":"Take courses in public speaking."},{"label":"D","text":"Develop communication skills."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Develop communication skills.","answerZh":"培养沟通技能。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'Science communication is a science in and of itself. It requires rigorous training and instruction. A scientist should take communication courses that can teach a person how to identify and eliminate jargon and how to develop effective analogies to explain complex concepts'，说明作者建议科学家通过参加沟通课程来提高沟通技巧，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者建议科学家怎样做来缩小科学与社会之间的差距?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2022_06_3-p1","title":"CET6 2022年06月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2022年06月 第3套","examDate":"2022年06月","year":"2022","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2022-06-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章讨论AI用于音乐创作的争议：有人视之为激发灵感的工具，有人斥其损害音乐的人性价值；作者认为应以开放心态拥抱，AI音乐终将成为常态。","mainIdeaEn":"The passage examines the debate over AI in music creation—seen by some as a helpful creative tool and by others as a threat to music's human essence—and concludes AI-made music will likely become the norm.","answerCode":"BAADB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先有人骂AI毁音乐，再见它帮人写歌，然后嫌作品没人味，接着说音乐属于人类，最后料定它成常态。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"How do some musicians perceive using AI in creating music?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It would help to produce more music idols."},{"label":"B","text":"It would be detrimental to music production."},{"label":"C","text":"It would hinder the understanding of authentic music."},{"label":"D","text":"It would be the beginning of a new era in music creation."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It would be detrimental to music production.","answerZh":"它会不利于音乐创作。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段内容，'Contrary to seeing AI as a tool, some musicians consider it to be hugely detrimental to the music scene'，表明一些音乐家认为使用AI在创作音乐上是有害的，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"一些音乐人如何看待用 AI 创作音乐?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does Taryn Southern's story illustrate?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"AI technology is conducive to music composition."},{"label":"B","text":"Musicians will be unable to create music without high tech."},{"label":"C","text":"Musicians are often at their wits, end in their creative effort."},{"label":"D","text":"AI technology is indispensable to creating melodies and chords."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"AI technology is conducive to music composition.","answerZh":"AI 技术有助于音乐创作。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'AI software enabled her to communicate melodies and chords that she didn't know how to put together herself'，说明AI技术有助于音乐创作，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Taryn Southern 的故事说明了什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"Why are some musicians opposed to the use of AI in creating music?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Music produced with AI technology lacks humanness."},{"label":"B","text":"Music created with AI technology is easily emulated."},{"label":"C","text":"It will depreciate humans' role in music composition."},{"label":"D","text":"It will deplete young musicians, creative inspiration."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Music produced with AI technology lacks humanness.","answerZh":"用 AI 技术创作的音乐缺乏人情味。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'the music it's producing is not necessarily what we want to hear. In short, it's not of great quality'和'a computer could never emulate the work (and human touch) of a true musician'，说明一些音乐家反对使用AI创作音乐是因为AI技术制作的音乐缺乏人情味，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"一些音乐人为什么反对用 AI 创作音乐?"},{"number":"49","stem":"Why do many people think music is too precious to impart to AI technology?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It cannot be created without pains."},{"label":"B","text":"It cannot be produced at random."},{"label":"C","text":"It is part of human life."},{"label":"D","text":"It is human specific."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is human specific.","answerZh":"它是人类特有的。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'Since many people see music as such an inherently human expression, it is often considered as too precious to impart to technology'，说明很多人认为音乐是太珍贵而不能交给AI技术的东西，因为它是人类特有的表达方式，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"许多人为什么认为音乐太宝贵而不能交给 AI 技术?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does the author think of the future of AI music?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It will continue to arouse the interest of music investors."},{"label":"B","text":"It has the prospect of becoming the norm in the future."},{"label":"C","text":"It will be gradually accepted by old-school musicians."},{"label":"D","text":"It may eventually lose its freshness and appeal."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It has the prospect of becoming the norm in the future.","answerZh":"它有望在未来成为常态。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到'it's only a matter of time before AI-produced music is seen as the new norm'，说明作者认为AI音乐有成为未来常态的前景，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者如何看待 AI 音乐的未来?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2022_06_3-p2","title":"CET6 2022年06月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2022年06月 第3套","examDate":"2022年06月","year":"2022","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2022-06-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"作者认为向公众传播科学是提升其科学素养的必要之举，但科学传播本身是门学问：学者应承认知识边界、请教专家，并接受训练培养沟通技能。","mainIdeaEn":"Communicating science to the public is necessary, but it is a discipline in itself: scientists must recognize their limits, consult specialists outside their field, and train to develop real communication skills.","answerCode":"BCDCD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说科普很必要，再遇难题问专家，然后夸公众其实懂行，接着叹大学者讲不明白，最后劝去练沟通本事。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author say about communicating science to the general public?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It will help them to keep abreast of the latest scientific developments."},{"label":"B","text":"It is a necessary means to improve their understanding of scientific issues."},{"label":"C","text":"It will get them more involved in academic debates on environmental problems."},{"label":"D","text":"It is an effective way to augment scientists' influence beyond the academic circle."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It is a necessary means to improve their understanding of scientific issues.","answerZh":"这是提高公众对科学问题理解的必要手段。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'Communicating science beyond the academic bubble is necessary to augment public understanding of health and environmental issues and help individuals make well-informed personal decisions'，说明作者认为向公众传播科学知识是提高他们对科学问题理解的必要手段，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于向大众传播科学,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does the author advise scientists to do to deal with topics outside of their specialty?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Write or present them from new angles."},{"label":"B","text":"Utilize information from diverse sources."},{"label":"C","text":"Turn to a specialist for professional help."},{"label":"D","text":"Fact-check with colleagues in their field."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Turn to a specialist for professional help.","answerZh":"向专家寻求专业帮助。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'That is not to suggest that they only write or present on their own research, but rather, that they consult with an expert if the topic is outside of their discipline'，说明作者建议科学家在遇到非专业话题时，应向专家求助。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者建议科学家如何处理自己专业以外的话题?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does the author say we can learn from social media?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A solid academic foundation is essential to understanding baffling scientific principles."},{"label":"B","text":"Modern technology has facilitated communication between scientists and the public."},{"label":"C","text":"Scientific articles have gained increasing popularity among the general public."},{"label":"D","text":"The public's understanding of science is much better than some have claimed."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The public's understanding of science is much better than some have claimed.","answerZh":"公众对科学的理解远比某些人所说的要好。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'If anything, social media has shown that the public craves knowledge based on a solid scientific foundation. Even the public discourse that follows most scientific articles shows that online readers can understand even the most baffling of scientific principles'，说明社交媒体显示公众渴望基于科学基础的知识，并且能够理解复杂的科学原理，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者说我们可以从社交媒体中学到什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does the example of the biologist who shared an intricate analogy show?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is helpful to use illustrations in explaining scientific phenomena."},{"label":"B","text":"It is imperative to have appropriate titles to explain scientific issues."},{"label":"C","text":"A learned scholar is not necessarily a qualified science communicator."},{"label":"D","text":"A nonscientific audience cannot duly understand principles of science."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"A learned scholar is not necessarily a qualified science communicator.","answerZh":"博学的学者未必是合格的科学传播者。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'One biologist shared an intricate analogy involving a library, books, paper, a recipe, ingredients, and a cake to explain the process behind vaccines. Any explanation that requires a written key to keep track of what each item represents is not a clear example for public consumption'，说明即使是有学问的学者也不一定是合格的科学传播者，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"那位分享复杂类比的生物学家的例子说明了什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author suggest scientists do to close the gap between science and society?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Explain complex concepts scientifically."},{"label":"B","text":"Make appropriate use of scientific terms."},{"label":"C","text":"Take courses in public speaking."},{"label":"D","text":"Develop communication skills."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Develop communication skills.","answerZh":"培养沟通技能。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'Science communication is a science in and of itself. It requires rigorous training and instruction. A scientist should take communication courses that can teach a person how to identify and eliminate jargon and how to develop effective analogies to explain complex concepts'，说明作者建议科学家通过参加沟通课程来提高沟通技巧，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者建议科学家怎样做来缩小科学与社会之间的差距?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2022_09_1-p1","title":"CET6 2022年09月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2022年09月 第1套","examDate":"2022年09月","year":"2022","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2022-09-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"中美欧等国罕见一致：科技公司太大、太强、太赚钱，各国只能通过反垄断诉讼、新竞争法乃至拆分，来遏制它们不断膨胀的势力。","mainIdeaEn":"The U.S., China and Europe rarely agree, but concur that tech companies are too big, powerful and profitable, leaving governments to confront them through antitrust suits, new competition laws, even breakups.","answerCode":"DCABC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先如何阻止垄断，再人人须受监管，然后离不开科技巨头，接着已酝酿监管行动，最后巨头越发不可信。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What does the author say is the issue all major economic powers have to address?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"How to ensure the sustainable growth of their tech giants."},{"label":"B","text":"How to keep the competitiveness of their tech companies."},{"label":"C","text":"How to break up the powerful giant tech companies."},{"label":"D","text":"How to stop tech companies from gaining monopoly."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"How to stop tech companies from gaining monopoly.","answerZh":"如何阻止科技公司形成垄断。","explanation":"这是一道主旨大意题。文章第一段提到各国都认为科技公司太大、太强、太有利可图，并且这种力量只会加剧，迫使政府必须直面这个问题。因此D选项是正确答案","questionZh":"作者说所有主要经济大国都必须解决的问题是什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the suspension of Ant Group Co.'s stock offering suggest?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"All attempts to evade regulation are doomed to failure."},{"label":"B","text":"All attempts to monopolize sales must be cracked down."},{"label":"C","text":"All companies must be regulated by the government."},{"label":"D","text":"All companies, domestic or foreign, are created equal."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"All companies must be regulated by the government.","answerZh":"所有公司都必须接受政府监管。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章提到中国实施反垄断打击，暂停了蚂蚁集团370亿美元的上市计划，表明没有公司可以逃避政府的监管。因此C选项是正确答案","questionZh":"Ant Group Co. 股票发行被叫停说明了什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"How are smaller companies impacted by tech giants' business expansion?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They can no longer do business independent of tech giants."},{"label":"B","text":"They are frequently denied access to tech giants' platforms."},{"label":"C","text":"They have to change marketing strategies to keep customers."},{"label":"D","text":"They no longer have the power to price their own products."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They can no longer do business independent of tech giants.","answerZh":"它们再也无法独立于科技巨头开展业务。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章提到科技巨头在多个市场占据越来越重要的位置，迫使小企业依赖他们的平台来接触客户。因此A选项是正确答案","questionZh":"科技巨头的业务扩张给小公司带来了怎样的影响?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What have EU countries done to confront the power of digital giants?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They have imposed strict regulation over digital giants' advertising."},{"label":"B","text":"They have considered regulatory action to promote fair competition."},{"label":"C","text":"They have limited sales of digital giants' products."},{"label":"D","text":"They have sought to protect consumers' privacy."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They have considered regulatory action to promote fair competition.","answerZh":"它们已考虑采取监管行动以促进公平竞争。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章提到在欧洲，以维斯塔格为首的欧盟竞争事务主管领导各国寻求监管市场，鼓励公平竞争。因此B选项是正确答案","questionZh":"欧盟国家为对抗数字巨头的势力采取了什么措施?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What do Americans generally think of social media companies according to the author?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are invading people's privacy."},{"label":"B","text":"They are increasingly influential."},{"label":"C","text":"They are becoming untrustworthy."},{"label":"D","text":"They are growing out of control."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They are becoming untrustworthy.","answerZh":"它们正变得不值得信任。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。题干问美国公众对社交媒体公司的总体看法。原文 'the public in general have grown increasingly skeptical of social media companies' 是关键句，skeptical（怀疑、不信任）直接对应 C 选项 'They are becoming untrustworthy（变得不可信）'；后文 'More than 60% say the sector has a negative effect' 进一步印证这种不信任态度。语法/逻辑上，skeptical of 后接对象表明信任度下降，故选 C。","questionZh":"作者认为美国人普遍如何看待社交媒体公司?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2022_09_1-p2","title":"CET6 2022年09月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2022年09月 第1套","examDate":"2022年09月","year":"2022","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2022-09-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"大众航空催生的现代旅游被美化为人人受益，但过度旅游正带来社会与环境破坏；当地居民因分不到应得利益而对游客生怨，游客应尊重并惠及本地。","mainIdeaEn":"Mass tourism, romanticized as good for all, drives social and environmental harm; residents resent tourists when benefits bypass them, so travelers should respect hosts and use local businesses.","answerCode":"DBDBC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先助力当地经济，再招来居民敌意，然后觉得没分到好处，接着乐于接受新活法，最后多用本地商家。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What is the popular assumption about international tourism?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its benefits may compensate for the adverse environmental consequences."},{"label":"B","text":"Its rapid development is attributed to people's improved living standard."},{"label":"C","text":"It appeals to people in places with favorable geographical conditions."},{"label":"D","text":"It contributes to the economy of destination countries and regions."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It contributes to the economy of destination countries and regions.","answerZh":"它为目的地国家和地区的经济做出贡献。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'Travel is often portrayed as a tool for personal growth and tourism as an economic motor for destination countries and cities'可知，国际旅游被普遍认为能够促进目的地国家和地区的经济发展。","questionZh":"关于国际旅游业,人们普遍的假设是什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What do we learn from some studies about uncontrolled tourism development?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It gives rise to an increase in mass confrontations."},{"label":"B","text":"It incurs local residents' antagonism to tourists."},{"label":"C","text":"It inhibits the steady growth of local economy."},{"label":"D","text":"It brings in a large chunk of mobile population."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It incurs local residents' antagonism to tourists.","answerZh":"它会招致当地居民对游客的敌意。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段'Uncontrolled tourism development has become a primary driver of social and environmental disruption. Tourism studies provide much documentation of the many negative social impacts of tourism and resulting resentment that local populations direct toward visitors'可知，无序的旅游发展引起了当地居民对游客的敌意。","questionZh":"关于不受控制的旅游业发展,我们从一些研究中了解到什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"Why does the author say local residents of popular destinations often feel frustrated?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They fall victim to social conflicts and environmental disturbances."},{"label":"B","text":"They have little opportunity to enjoy themselves on cruise ships."},{"label":"C","text":"They cannot find employment in multinational hotel chains."},{"label":"D","text":"They do not think they benefit as much as they deserve."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They do not think they benefit as much as they deserve.","answerZh":"他们认为自己没有获得应得的那么多好处。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'Residents often become frustrated when the benefits of tourism are not felt locally'可知，当地居民感到沮丧是因为他们没有感受到旅游带来的好处。","questionZh":"作者为什么说热门目的地的当地居民常感到沮丧?"},{"number":"54","stem":"How does the author say local residents in destination communities respond to tourism activity?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They endeavor to adapt to it."},{"label":"B","text":"They readily adopt new lifestyles."},{"label":"C","text":"They immerse tourists in their culture."},{"label":"D","text":"They try to upgrade their business models."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They readily adopt new lifestyles.","answerZh":"他们乐于接受新的生活方式。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。题干问目的地社区当地居民对旅游活动如何回应。原文 'data show that tourism activity corresponds to increased social problems as local residents adopt the behaviors of tourists' 是关键句，'adopt the behaviors of tourists'（采纳游客的行为方式）对应上文 'lifestyle transformations'，直接对应 B 选项 'They readily adopt new lifestyles（欣然接受新的生活方式）'。语法上 as 引导的状语从句说明居民主动采纳游客行为，故选 B。","questionZh":"作者认为目的地社区的当地居民如何回应旅游活动?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What can tourists do to exert more positive impacts on the tourist destinations?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Show interest in local customs and lifestyles."},{"label":"B","text":"Seek possibilities to invest in local companies."},{"label":"C","text":"Use the services provided by local businesses."},{"label":"D","text":"Give favorable comments about their services."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Use the services provided by local businesses.","answerZh":"使用当地商家提供的服务。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'Informed travelers also are better able to distinguish between multinational companies and local entrepreneurs whose businesses provide direct social, environmental, and economic benefits for local residents. Such businesses are in love with the destination and are therefore deserving of market reward'可知，游客可以通过使用当地企业提供的服务来对旅游目的地产生更积极的影响。","questionZh":"游客能做些什么来对旅游目的地产生更多积极影响?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2022_12_1-p1","title":"CET6 2022年12月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2022年12月 第1套","examDate":"2022年12月","year":"2022","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2022-12-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"把自我价值绑在工作上是把双刃剑：它会催生消极动机、为成功牺牲幸福、挤压个人生活，但也带来追求情感回报的兴奋，让追逐目标变得愉悦。","mainIdeaEn":"Tying self-worth to work is double-edged: it breeds negative motivation, sacrifices well-being for success and crowds out personal life, yet also brings the excitement of pursuing rewards, making goals enjoyable.","answerCode":"ABBAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先带来消极动机，再牺牲幸福求成功，然后个人生活受挤，接着追目标也愉悦，最后有动力便积极。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What does the author say about the pursuit of work-related self-esteem?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It may result in negative motivation."},{"label":"B","text":"It contributes to one's accomplishments."},{"label":"C","text":"It can increase one's vigor as one keeps trying."},{"label":"D","text":"It costs too much emotionally and psychologically."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It may result in negative motivation.","answerZh":"它可能导致消极的动机。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'This form of motivation is widely regarded as a negative type of motivation'，表明追求工作相关的自尊可能导致负面动机。","questionZh":"关于追求与工作相关的自尊,作者怎么说?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What do employees tend to do in pursuing work-related self-esteem?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Take on tasks well beyond their actual capabilities."},{"label":"B","text":"Strive to succeed at the expense of their well-being."},{"label":"C","text":"Resort to all means regardless of the consequences."},{"label":"D","text":"Exaggerate their sense of shame and worthlessness."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Strive to succeed at the expense of their well-being.","answerZh":"以牺牲自身幸福为代价努力追求成功。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'They then take on only tasks and objectives which serve that ego-driven need. As a result, to avoid feelings of shame and worthlessness associated with failure, they extend themselves to such a degree that there's a subsequent adverse effect on their well-being'，表明员工为了追求工作相关的自尊，会牺牲自己的福祉去努力成功。","questionZh":"员工在追求与工作相关的自尊时往往会做什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What do we learn about people over-concerned with work-related self-esteem?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They may often feel inferior to their colleagues."},{"label":"B","text":"They cannot enjoy their personal life to the full."},{"label":"C","text":"They are never satisfied with their achievements."},{"label":"D","text":"They have their own view of friendship and leisure."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They cannot enjoy their personal life to the full.","answerZh":"他们无法充分享受个人生活。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'Their desire to avoid feeling inferior ends up making them feel inferior when it comes to their diminished capacity for friendship and leisure'，表明过分关注工作相关的自尊的人无法充分享受个人生活。","questionZh":"关于过度关注工作相关自尊的人,我们了解到什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What is the good news we learn from the recent research?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The pursuit of goals may turn out to be enjoyable and pleasant."},{"label":"B","text":"The emotional rewards from goal pursuit are worth the pains taken."},{"label":"C","text":"The negative consequences of goal pursuit can mostly be avoided."},{"label":"D","text":"The goal of swelling self-esteem can be achieved if one keeps trying."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"The pursuit of goals may turn out to be enjoyable and pleasant.","answerZh":"追求目标的过程可能是令人愉快和惬意的。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第五段直接说 'This excitement makes pursuing goals enjoyable and stimulates pleasure and pride that would result from success'，即追求目标会变得令人愉快、带来快乐与自豪，这正是研究发现的好消息，与选项 A『追求目标可能变得令人愉快』完全对应，故选 A。 - 关键句：This excitement makes pursuing goals enjoyable and stimulates pleasure and pride that would result from success.","questionZh":"我们从近期研究中得知的好消息是什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What can we infer from the last paragraph?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Workers have to make sacrifices to preserve self-esteem."},{"label":"B","text":"Self-esteem swells when workers are strongly motivated."},{"label":"C","text":"Pursuit of goals affects people's personal lives to an unhealthy extent."},{"label":"D","text":"People feel positive about their work as long as they are motivated."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"People feel positive about their work as long as they are motivated.","answerZh":"只要有动力，人们就会对工作抱有积极感受。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到'the way people feel about their work has less to do with whether they're motivated by the preservation of self-esteem but more with the fact that they're simply motivated'，可以推断出只要人们有动力，他们就会对工作持积极态度。","questionZh":"从最后一段我们可以推断出什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2022_12_1-p2","title":"CET6 2022年12月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2022年12月 第1套","examDate":"2022年12月","year":"2022","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2022-12-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"联合国研究警告，人类对自然资源的破坏已超出地球承受力；缺乏强力行动，水资源短缺难以缓解、环境将全球性恶化，穷国须在不损环境下改善民生。","mainIdeaEn":"A UN study warns human degradation of natural resources outpaces Earth's capacity; without radical action water scarcity will persist and the environment worsen globally, while poor nations must improve livelihoods without sacrificing it.","answerCode":"BCADD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先破坏超出承载，再没强力难解缺水，然后全球性恶化，接着追富国必伤环境，最后要护境又保民生。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What is the major finding of the UN environmental study?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Human activity has rendered Mother Earth almost uninhabitable."},{"label":"B","text":"Humans are doing more damage to the earth than it can cope with."},{"label":"C","text":"Environmental problems have considerably weakened human prosperity."},{"label":"D","text":"Environmental damage is more serious in developed countries these days."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Humans are doing more damage to the earth than it can cope with.","answerZh":"人类对地球造成的破坏已超出其承受能力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'Degradation of the world's natural resources by humans is rapidly outpacing the planet's ability to absorb the damage'，可以得出人类对地球造成的破坏速度超过了地球自我修复的能力，因此B选项'Humans are doing more damage to the earth than it can cope with'是正确答案。","questionZh":"联合国环境研究的主要发现是什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What is said about water scarcity in some of the poorest regions?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is getting so serious that there is little hope of a solution."},{"label":"B","text":"It largely accounts for their slow economic development."},{"label":"C","text":"It can hardly be relieved if no drastic measures are taken."},{"label":"D","text":"It is primarily caused by the acceleration of climate change."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It can hardly be relieved if no drastic measures are taken.","answerZh":"若不采取强力措施，水资源短缺几乎无法缓解。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'There appears little prospect of this desperate situation being remedied without radical action being taken'，可以得出如果不采取激进措施，水资源短缺问题几乎无法解决，因此C选项'It can hardly be relieved if no drastic measures are taken'是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于一些最贫困地区的缺水问题,文中说了什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does Achim Steiner say about the environmental condition?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It will deteriorate worldwide."},{"label":"B","text":"It is attracting global attention."},{"label":"C","text":"It is being slowly remedied globally."},{"label":"D","text":"It will shrink the world's population."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It will deteriorate worldwide.","answerZh":"它将在全球范围内恶化。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段'If current trends continue, and the world fails to improve patterns of production and consumption, then the state of the world's environment will continue to decline'，可以得出如果当前趋势持续，环境状况将恶化，因此A选项'It will deteriorate worldwide'是正确答案。","questionZh":"Achim Steiner 对环境状况怎么说?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What is the dilemma developing countries face?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They cannot modernise farming without causing land degradation."},{"label":"B","text":"They cannot promote industrialisation without polluting waterways."},{"label":"C","text":"They cannot boost crop yields without causing greenhouse gas emissions."},{"label":"D","text":"They cannot catch up with rich countries without sacrificing the environment."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They cannot catch up with rich countries without sacrificing the environment.","answerZh":"不牺牲环境，它们就无法赶上富裕国家。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段'In rich countries, these problems have built up over decades and centuries while economic growth was pursued at the expense of the environment. But in developing countries, the path of future development has more potential to change'，可以得出发展中国家在未来发展中不能以牺牲环境为代价来追赶发达国家，因此D选项'They cannot catch up with rich countries without sacrificing the environment'是正确答案。","questionZh":"发展中国家面临的两难困境是什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What should developing countries do in their future development according to the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They turn to developed countries for the assistance they need."},{"label":"B","text":"They remedy environmental damage by slowing economic growth."},{"label":"C","text":"They avoid damaging interference from international institutions."},{"label":"D","text":"They improve people's livelihood without harming the environment."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They improve people's livelihood without harming the environment.","answerZh":"在不损害环境的前提下改善民众生计。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'international institutions to devise more sustainable growth pathways that are supposed both to alleviate poverty and preserve the environment'，可以得出发展中国家在未来的发展中应该在不破坏环境的前提下改善民生，因此D选项'They improve people's livelihood without harming the environment'是正确答案。","questionZh":"根据文章,发展中国家在未来发展中应该怎么做?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2022_12_2-p1","title":"CET6 2022年12月 第2套 · Passage 1","examTitle":"CET6 2022年12月 第2套","examDate":"2022年12月","year":"2022","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2022-12-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"有人主张减免学生债务能刺激经济、帮助弱势，但数据显示受益最多的是富裕学生；这类政策还会诱使高校涨学费、学生盲目选专业，最终由蓝领买单。","mainIdeaEn":"Forgiving student debt is claimed to aid the economy and the needy, yet data show it mainly benefits wealthy students, encourages tuition hikes and reckless major choices, ultimately burdening blue-collar workers.","answerCode":"BBACC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说经济弱者双赢，再富人最受益，然后选专业不顾前途，接着学费配不上质量，最后蓝领替人买单。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"Why do some people advocate forgiving student loan debt?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They assert it will narrow the gap between the wealthy and the poor."},{"label":"B","text":"They believe it will benefit both the economy and the underprivileged."},{"label":"C","text":"They claim it will eliminate economic distress among college students."},{"label":"D","text":"They think the cost of education is the responsibility of the government."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They believe it will benefit both the economy and the underprivileged.","answerZh":"他们认为这将惠及经济和弱势群体双方。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'Some people in the US have asserted that forgiving student loan debt is one way to stimulate the economy and give assistance to those in need'可知，一些人主张免除学生贷款债务是刺激经济和帮助贫困人口的一种方式。因此B选项'They believe it will benefit both the economy and the underprivileged.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"为什么有些人主张免除学生贷款债务?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What do we learn from the Federal Reserve data?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Approximately 60% of student debt remains unpaid."},{"label":"B","text":"Cancelling student debt benefits wealthy families most."},{"label":"C","text":"Forgiving student debt provides little benefit to universities."},{"label":"D","text":"Low-income families owe the biggest amount of student debt."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Cancelling student debt benefits wealthy families most.","answerZh":"取消学生债务最受益的是富裕家庭。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'Federal Reserve data reveals that the highest-income 40 percent of households owe approximately 60 percent of outstanding student debt, while the lowest 40 percent owe just under 20 percent.'可知，取消学生贷款债务最有利于富裕家庭。因此B选项'Cancelling student debt benefits wealthy families most.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"我们从美联储的数据中了解到什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does the author say students are likely to do if they know they needn't repay their loans?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They will choose to study subjects without considering their job prospects."},{"label":"B","text":"They will be free to pursue their goals without being burdened financially."},{"label":"C","text":"They will over-borrow and live beyond their means."},{"label":"D","text":"They will be able to enroll in expensive universities."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They will choose to study subjects without considering their job prospects.","answerZh":"他们会选择专业时不再考虑就业前景。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章第四段'And, students will feel more comfortable making the irresponsible decision to go tens of thousands of dollars in debt to major in impractical or idealistic subjects if they know their loans will be forgiven.'可知，如果学生知道他们不需要偿还贷款，他们可能会选择不考虑就业前景的学科。因此A选项'They will choose to study subjects without considering their job prospects.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者说,如果学生知道无需偿还贷款,他们可能会做什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What does the author imply about colleges offering online education?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They cannot get away with the serious consequences."},{"label":"B","text":"They have suffered greatly from the current pandemic."},{"label":"C","text":"The tuition they charge is not justified by the quality of their service."},{"label":"D","text":"The tuition they charge has surged outrageously during the pandemic."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"The tuition they charge is not justified by the quality of their service.","answerZh":"它们收取的学费与其服务质量并不相称。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章倒数第二段'Do we really want to tell colleges that they can get away with providing below-average service for an outrageous cost?'可知，作者认为大学收取高昂的学费却没有提供相应的高质量服务。因此C选项'The tuition they charge is not justified by the quality of their service.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于提供在线教育的高校,作者暗示了什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What will happen if any of the proposed student debt plans is implemented?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Plumbers and retail workers will have a chance of becoming professionals."},{"label":"B","text":"Working-class students will have increasing access to subsidized education."},{"label":"C","text":"Blue-collar workers will have to bear the cost of educating would-be high-earners."},{"label":"D","text":"A growing number of students will be able to earn degrees in medicine and law."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Blue-collar workers will have to bear the cost of educating would-be high-earners.","answerZh":"蓝领工人将不得不承担培养未来高收入者的费用。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章最后一段'In the case of any of these student debt plans, working-class Americans who chose not to or could not afford to go to college will be subsidizing the education of the professional class. Plumbers and retail workers will be paying for the degrees of doctors and lawyers.'可知，如果实施任何提议的学生债务计划，工人阶级将不得不承担培养未来高收入者的教育成本。因此C选项'Blue-collar workers will have to bear the cost of educating would-be high-earners.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"如果任何一项拟议的学生债务方案得以实施,会发生什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2022_12_2-p2","title":"CET6 2022年12月 第2套 · Passage 2","examTitle":"CET6 2022年12月 第2套","examDate":"2022年12月","year":"2022","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2022-12-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"美国儿科学会推翻两岁前禁屏幕旧规，新指南把重点从屏幕上是什么转向房间里还有谁：视频通话是例外，独自观看有害，家长陪伴才有益。","mainIdeaEn":"The AAP scrapped its no-screens-before-age-2 rule; new guidelines shift focus from what's on screen to who else is present: video chat is fine, solo viewing harms language, and co-viewing helps.","answerCode":"DAACD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先旧规被推翻，再看屏要父母陪，然后视频通话不算，接着独看害语言，最后能联系现实情境。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn about the \"No screens under 2\" rule?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has met more and more resistance from parents."},{"label":"B","text":"It has proved helpful to children's healthy growth."},{"label":"C","text":"It confuses parents with regard to kids' education."},{"label":"D","text":"It has been discarded in line with recent research."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It has been discarded in line with recent research.","answerZh":"根据最新研究，这一规则已被摒弃。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'As of today, that rule has been thrown out the window.'可知，'No screens before age 2'这一规则已经被废弃，与D选项'it has been discarded in line with recent research'相符。","questionZh":"关于\"2岁以下不看屏幕\"的规定,我们了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What do the new AAP guidelines advocate?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Young children should be accompanied by parents during screen time."},{"label":"B","text":"Parents should be emotionally involved in their children's upbringing."},{"label":"C","text":"Young children should watch videos carefully selected by parents."},{"label":"D","text":"Parents should protect their children from too much media exposure."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Young children should be accompanied by parents during screen time.","answerZh":"幼儿看屏幕时应有父母陪伴。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'For this age group, AAP recommends no more than an hour a day of screen use. And, just as with younger children, they want care-givers to take part in screen time: 'Co-view with your children, help children understand what they are seeing, and help them apply what they learn to the world around them.''可知，新指南提倡父母在孩子屏幕时间陪伴孩子，与A选项'Young children should be accompanied by parents during screen time'相符。","questionZh":"新的 AAP 指南主张什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What do families think of live video chat according to surveys?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It should not be regarded as screen time."},{"label":"B","text":"It helps babies to develop their verbal skills."},{"label":"C","text":"It is not as harmful as playing games on laptops."},{"label":"D","text":"It is a good substitute for video viewing."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It should not be regarded as screen time.","answerZh":"它不应被视为屏幕时间。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'Surveys indicate that families already popularly believe that 'Face time doesn't count or at least that the benefit of virtual visits with grandparents or other relatives outweighs the potential cost of exposing babies to the laptop or smartphone.''可知，家庭普遍认为视频聊天不应该被视为屏幕时间，与A选项'It should not be regarded as screen time'相符。","questionZh":"根据调查,家庭如何看待实时视频聊天?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What do researchers find about kids solo viewing educational videos?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It arouses their interest in language learning."},{"label":"B","text":"It works no better than reading picture books."},{"label":"C","text":"It hampers their development of language skills."},{"label":"D","text":"It helps them acquire independent learning skills."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It hampers their development of language skills.","answerZh":"这会妨碍他们语言技能的发展。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段'The flip side of this is that many studies have actually shown poorer language skills correlated with earlier solo viewing of 'educational' videos.'可知，研究显示单独观看教育视频会阻碍儿童的语言技能发展，与C选项'It hampers their development of language skills'相符。","questionZh":"关于孩子独自观看教育视频,研究者发现了什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author say about preschoolers ages 2 to 5?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They can understand pretty well what they see on the screen."},{"label":"B","text":"They can learn on their own without much parental guidance."},{"label":"C","text":"They can make use of educational videos to develop digital literacy."},{"label":"D","text":"They can relate what they learn on the screen to real life situations."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They can relate what they learn on the screen to real life situations.","answerZh":"他们能把从屏幕上学到的东西与现实生活情境联系起来。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'For this age group, there's more evidence that they have the ability to transfer knowledge from screens to the real world, including early literacy and math.'可知，2到5岁的学龄前儿童能够将屏幕上学到的知识应用到现实世界中，与D选项'They can relate what they learn on the screen to real life situations'相符。","questionZh":"关于2至5岁的学龄前儿童,作者怎么说?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2022_12_3-p1","title":"CET6 2022年12月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2022年12月 第3套","examDate":"2022年12月","year":"2022","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2022-12-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"人们衰老速度不同源于基因、生活方式等复杂互动；染色体端粒随细胞分裂缩短决定衰老，而愤世嫉俗等心态会伤害端粒，衰老在一定程度上可控甚至逆转。","mainIdeaEn":"People age at different rates due to complex gene-lifestyle interactions; telomeres shortening with cell division drive aging, cynical hostility harms them, and aging is partly controllable, even reversible.","answerCode":"ABCBD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先为何衰老不同，再端粒左右基因，然后缩短可逆转，接着敌意害端粒，最后衰老可以调控。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What have scientists come to know better today?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Why people age at different rates."},{"label":"B","text":"How genes influence the aging process."},{"label":"C","text":"How various genes express themselves in aging."},{"label":"D","text":"Why people have long been concerned about aging."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Why people age at different rates.","answerZh":"人们衰老速度为何各不相同。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'it's becoming clearer and clearer to scientists that the differences between people's rates of aging lie in the complex interactions among genes, social relationships, environments and lifestyles'，表明科学家们现在对人们衰老速度不同的原因有了更好的了解，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"如今科学家对什么有了更深入的了解?"},{"number":"47","stem":"Why are some lifestyle factors considered extremely important?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They may shorten the process of cell division."},{"label":"B","text":"They may determine how genes function."},{"label":"C","text":"They may affect the lifespan of telomeres."},{"label":"D","text":"They may account for the stresses on cells."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They may determine how genes function.","answerZh":"它们可能决定基因如何发挥作用。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。题干定位词'some lifestyle factors'对应第一段原句'Even though you were born with a particular set of genes, the way you live can influence how they express themselves. Some lifestyle factors may even turn genes on or shut them off.'——生活方式能开启或关闭基因，即决定基因如何运作，故选 B (They may determine how genes function)。 - 关键句：Some lifestyle factors may even turn genes on or shut them off.","questionZh":"为什么某些生活方式因素被认为极其重要?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What have the author and his colleagues discovered about telomeres?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Their number affects the growth of cells."},{"label":"B","text":"Their length determines the quality of life."},{"label":"C","text":"Their shortening process can be reversed."},{"label":"D","text":"Their health impacts the division of cells."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Their shortening process can be reversed.","answerZh":"它们的缩短过程可以被逆转。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'one extraordinary discovery from our labs is that telomeres can actually lengthen'，表明作者和同事发现端粒的缩短过程可以逆转，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者及其同事关于端粒发现了什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What have scientists learned about cynical hostility?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It may lead to confrontational thought patterns."},{"label":"B","text":"It may produce an adverse effect on telomeres."},{"label":"C","text":"It may cause people to lose their temper frequently."},{"label":"D","text":"It may stir up agitation among those in long lines."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It may produce an adverse effect on telomeres.","answerZh":"它可能对端粒产生不利影响。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'Scientists have learned that several thought patterns appear to be unhealthy for telomeres, and one of them is cynical hostility... People who score high on measures of cynical hostility tend to get more heart disease, metabolic disease and often die at younger ages. They also have shorter telomeres'，表明科学家发现愤世嫉俗的敌意对端粒有不利影响，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于愤世嫉俗的敌意,科学家了解到了什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What do we learn from the last paragraph about the process of aging?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It may vary from individual to individual."},{"label":"B","text":"It challenges scientists to explore further."},{"label":"C","text":"It depends on one's genetic code."},{"label":"D","text":"It may be controlled to a degree."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It may be controlled to a degree.","answerZh":"它在一定程度上是可以控制的。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'aging is a dynamic process that could possibly be accelerated or slowed—and, in some aspects, even reversed'，表明衰老过程在一定程度上可以被控制，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于衰老过程,我们从最后一段了解到什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2022_12_3-p2","title":"CET6 2022年12月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2022年12月 第3套","examDate":"2022年12月","year":"2022","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2022-12-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"科学家意外改良出一种能分解塑料饮料瓶的酶，有望首次实现瓶到瓶的完全回收，减少石油开采和塑料污染，厂商也开始探索规模化应用。","mainIdeaEn":"Scientists accidentally engineered an enzyme that breaks down plastic bottles, potentially enabling full bottle-to-bottle recycling, cutting oil use and pollution, as manufacturers begin exploring large-scale application.","answerCode":"BAADC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先能全回收塑料，再天生会分解，然后意外更高效，接着厂商在探索，最后评估环境影响。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about an enzyme scientists have created?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It was identified during a lab experiment accident."},{"label":"B","text":"It may make full recycling of plastic bottles a reality."},{"label":"C","text":"It was a breakthrough made with persistent efforts."},{"label":"D","text":"It may initiate a radical reform in the plastic industry."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It may make full recycling of plastic bottles a reality.","answerZh":"它可能使塑料瓶的完全回收成为现实。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段，科学家意外创造了一种酶，这种酶能够分解塑料饮料瓶，并且这项突破可能帮助解决全球塑料污染危机，因为它首次使得瓶子的完全回收成为可能。因此，B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于科学家创造出的一种酶,我们从文中了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does the passage say about the bug that produces the important enzyme?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has a natural ability to consume plastics."},{"label":"B","text":"It is a bacterium that reproduces at a high rate."},{"label":"C","text":"It is essential to the recycling of plastic bottles."},{"label":"D","text":"It has a chemical structure unknown to scientists."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It has a natural ability to consume plastics.","answerZh":"它天生具有分解塑料的能力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段，科学家在2016年在日本的一个垃圾场发现了第一种自然进化到可以吃掉塑料的细菌。因此，A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于产生这种重要酶的细菌,文章说了什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"By adjusting the enzyme produced by the bug, the scientists .","options":[{"label":"A","text":"made it more effective by chance"},{"label":"B","text":"discovered an extraordinary chemical"},{"label":"C","text":"altered its basic molecular composition"},{"label":"D","text":"found its evolutionary process sped up"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"made it more effective by chance","answerZh":"偶然间使它变得更有效","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段，一个国际团队调整了这种酶，想看看它是如何进化的，但测试显示他们意外地使分子在分解用于饮料瓶的塑料方面变得更加有效。因此，A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"通过调整这种细菌产生的酶,科学家们____。"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does Prof. McGeehan say about the recycling of plastic bottles?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Manufacturers are implementing it on an increasingly larger scale."},{"label":"B","text":"It generates huge business opportunities for plastic manufacturers."},{"label":"C","text":"It has aroused persistent interest among the general public."},{"label":"D","text":"Manufacturers are beginning to explore ways of doing it."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Manufacturers are beginning to explore ways of doing it.","answerZh":"制造商正开始探索实现这一目标的方法。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段，McGeehan教授说，制造商开始探索如何正确回收这些瓶子。因此，D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"McGeehan 教授对塑料瓶的回收利用怎么说?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What is Prof. Adisa Azapagic's advice concerning the application of the enzyme?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Developing technologies to address greenhouse gas emissions."},{"label":"B","text":"Considering the extra cost involved in producing the enzyme."},{"label":"C","text":"Assessing its possible negative impact on the environment."},{"label":"D","text":"Studying the full life cycle of the enzyme as the first step."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Assessing its possible negative impact on the environment.","answerZh":"评估其对环境可能造成的负面影响。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段，Azapagic教授同意这种酶可能是有用的，但补充说需要进行全面的生命周期评估，以确保这项技术不会以牺牲其他环境问题，包括额外的温室气体排放为代价，解决一个环境问题——废物。因此，C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于这种酶的应用,Adisa Azapagic 教授有什么建议?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2023_03_1-p1","title":"CET6 2023年03月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2023年03月 第1套","examDate":"2023年03月","year":"2023","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2023-03-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"数十年来饮食多样化被视为健康建议，但新研究发现它其实缺乏共识、也无益健康，反而会让人摄入更多热量、增加肥胖风险。","mainIdeaEn":"Long a standard health recommendation, dietary diversity actually lacks a clear definition and scientific support; new research links it to eating more calories, poorer eating patterns and higher obesity risk.","answerCode":"ACABC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先劝饮食多样，再多样吃得更多，然后定义没共识，接着未必更健康，最后吃过量才觉饱。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What has been a standard piece of dietary advice for decades?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"People should diversify what they eat."},{"label":"B","text":"People should have a well-balanced diet."},{"label":"C","text":"People should cultivate a healthy eating habit."},{"label":"D","text":"People should limit calorie intake to avoid obesity."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"People should diversify what they eat.","answerZh":"人们应当使饮食多样化。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段中的'The suggestion that people should aim for dietary diversity by trying to eat a variety of foods has been a basic public health recommendation for decades in the United States and elsewhere'可以确定，标准的饮食建议是人们应该多样化饮食。","questionZh":"几十年来标准的饮食建议一直是什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What did the new research by the American Heart Association find?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Unhealthy food makes people gain weight more easily."},{"label":"B","text":"Dietary diversity is positively related to good health."},{"label":"C","text":"People seeking dietary diversity tend to eat more."},{"label":"D","text":"Big eaters are more likely to become overweight."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"People seeking dietary diversity tend to eat more.","answerZh":"追求饮食多样化的人往往吃得更多。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'Researchers found a greater prevalence of obesity amongst people with a greater dietary diversity'，说明追求饮食多样性的人倾向于摄入更多的食物。","questionZh":"美国心脏协会的新研究发现了什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What could help to explain the contradiction between the new findings and the common public health recommendation?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"There is little consensus on the definition of dietary diversity."},{"label":"B","text":"The methods researchers use to measure nutrition vary greatly."},{"label":"C","text":"Conventional wisdom about diet is seldom supported by science."},{"label":"D","text":"Most dietary guidelines around the world contradict one another."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"There is little consensus on the definition of dietary diversity.","answerZh":"关于饮食多样化的定义几乎没有共识。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章第三段提到'But this advice does not seem to be supported by science, possibly because there is little agreement about the meaning of 'dietary diversity''，说明对饮食多样性的定义缺乏共识可能是新发现与公共健康建议相矛盾的原因。","questionZh":"什么有助于解释新发现与常见公共健康建议之间的矛盾?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What did Dr. Rao find after 20 years of research on obesity?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"There is no clear definition of optimal eating patterns."},{"label":"B","text":"Diversified food intake may not contribute to health."},{"label":"C","text":"Eating patterns and weight gain go hand in hand."},{"label":"D","text":"Dietary diversity promotes healthy body weight."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Diversified food intake may not contribute to health.","answerZh":"多样化的饮食摄入未必有益健康。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'he has observed that people who have a regimented lifestyle and diet tend to be thinner and healthier than people with a wide variety of consumption'，说明多样化的食物摄入可能并不促进健康。","questionZh":"经过20年的肥胖研究,Rao 博士发现了什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does the passage say about people who eat a great variety of food?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are more likely to eat foods beneficial to their health."},{"label":"B","text":"They don't have any problems getting sufficient nutrition."},{"label":"C","text":"They don't feel they have had enough until they overeat."},{"label":"D","text":"They tend to consume more sweets, sugar and red meat."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They don't feel they have had enough until they overeat.","answerZh":"他们不吃到过量就不觉得吃够了。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'there is some evidence that a greater variety of food options in a single meal may delay people's feeling of fullness and actually increase how much they eat'，说明吃很多种类食物的人可能不会感到饱直到他们吃得过多。","questionZh":"关于饮食种类繁多的人,文章说了什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2023_03_1-p2","title":"CET6 2023年03月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2023年03月 第1套","examDate":"2023年03月","year":"2023","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2023-03-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"曾被认为人类独有的辨同辨异抽象能力，在刚出生、未受训练的小鸭身上也被发现，这颠覆了人们对鸟类智力的认识。","mainIdeaEn":"Same-different discrimination, once thought uniquely human, appears in untrained newborn ducklings, overturning the notion of the birdbrain and showing animals can learn abstract relationships without training.","answerCode":"ADBCD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先会辨同与异，再鸟脑认知全错，然后能分辨异同，接着动物没受训，最后研究大有进展。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"In what way were humans thought to be unique?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Being capable of same-different discrimination."},{"label":"B","text":"Being able to distinguish abstract from concrete."},{"label":"C","text":"Being a major source of animal intelligence."},{"label":"D","text":"Being the cornerstone of the creative world."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Being capable of same-different discrimination.","answerZh":"具备辨别相同与不同的能力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段中的'The ability to make inferences from the same and different, once thought to be unique to humans, is viewed as a cornerstone of abstract intelligent thought'可知，人类被认为独特的能力是能够进行相同与不同的推断，即same-different discrimination。","questionZh":"人类曾在哪方面被认为是独一无二的?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What do we learn from the study published in Science?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Our understanding of the bird world was biased."},{"label":"B","text":"Our communication with birds was far from adequate."},{"label":"C","text":"Our knowledge about bird psychology needs updating."},{"label":"D","text":"Our conception of birds' intelligence was wrong."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Our conception of birds' intelligence was wrong.","answerZh":"我们对鸟类智力的认识是错误的。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段中的'The study, published Thursday in Science, challenges our idea of what it means to have a birdbrain'可知，这项研究挑战了我们对鸟类智力的看法，即我们的关于鸟类智力的概念是错误的。","questionZh":"我们从发表在 Science 上的研究中了解到什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What did the researchers discover about most ducklings from their experiment?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They could associate shape with color."},{"label":"B","text":"They could tell whether the objects were the same."},{"label":"C","text":"They preferred colored objects to colorless ones."},{"label":"D","text":"They reacted quickly to moving objects."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They could tell whether the objects were the same.","answerZh":"它们能分辨物体是否相同。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第五段'The researchers found that about 70% of the ducklings preferred to move toward the pair of objects that had the same shape or color relationship as the first objects they saw'以及紧接的举例：先看到两个绿色球的小鸭更倾向于移向两个蓝色球（同-同关系）而非橙紫不匹配组合（异-异关系），可知小鸭分辨的是『两物体之间是否相同』这一抽象关系，对应全文主题 same-different discrimination。故选 B。 - 关键句：The researchers found that about 70% of the ducklings preferred to move toward the pair of objects that had the same shape or color relationship as the first objects they saw.","questionZh":"研究者在实验中关于大多数小鸭发现了什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What was novel about the experiment in the study reported in Science?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The ducklings were compared with other animals."},{"label":"B","text":"It was conducted by experimental psychologists."},{"label":"C","text":"The animals used received no training."},{"label":"D","text":"It used a number of colors and shapes."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"The animals used received no training.","answerZh":"实验所用的动物未经任何训练。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段中的'By studying imprinting, the authors of this study have shown for the first time that an animal can learn relationships between concepts without training'可知，这项研究的新颖之处在于使用的动物没有接受训练。","questionZh":"Science 报道的这项研究中的实验有什么新颖之处?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What do we learn from Dr. Wasserman's comment on the study of animal minds at the end of the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Research methods are being updated."},{"label":"B","text":"It is getting more and more intricate."},{"label":"C","text":"It is attracting more public attention."},{"label":"D","text":"Remarkable progress is being made."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Remarkable progress is being made.","answerZh":"正在取得显著进展。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段中的'\"We are in a revolutionary phase in terms of our ability to understand the minds of other animals.\"'可知，Dr. Wasserman认为我们在理解其他动物心智方面正在取得显著进展。","questionZh":"从文末 Wasserman 博士对动物思维研究的评论中,我们了解到什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2023_06_1-p1","title":"CET6 2023年06月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2023年06月 第1套","examDate":"2023年06月","year":"2023","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2023-06-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"技术从非中立工具，人工智能正在重塑人类：它替代人的判断，使人丧失锻炼实践判断力的机会，还通过推荐算法收窄选择，让日常生活越来越可预测。","mainIdeaEn":"Technology is never neutral; AI is reshaping humanity by substituting for human judgment, denying people the chance to develop practical judgment, and narrowing choices until everyday life becomes utterly predictable.","answerCode":"DAACB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先AI重塑人类，再没机会练判断，然后选择被收窄，接着一切可预测，最后人类不再难料。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do we learn about the deeper implications of AI?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is causing catastrophic levels of unemployment."},{"label":"B","text":"It is doing physical harm to human operators."},{"label":"C","text":"It is altering moral judgments."},{"label":"D","text":"It is reshaping humanity."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is reshaping humanity.","answerZh":"它正在重塑人类。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'Technological innovations reshape people as they use these innovations to control their environment'，表明人工智能正在改变人类。选项D 'It is reshaping humanity' 与原文表述一致，因此是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于人工智能更深层的影响,我们了解到什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What is the consequence of algorithmic prescription replacing human judgment?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"People lose the chance to cultivate the ability to make practical judgments."},{"label":"B","text":"People are prevented from participating in making major decisions in the workplace."},{"label":"C","text":"Managers no longer have the chance to decide which loan to approve."},{"label":"D","text":"Managers do not need to take the trouble to determine who to hire or fire."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"People lose the chance to cultivate the ability to make practical judgments.","answerZh":"人们失去了培养实际判断能力的机会。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'We see the emergence of machines as substitute judges in a variety of everyday contexts as a potential threat to people learning how to effectively exercise judgment themselves'，说明算法处方取代人类判断会导致人们失去培养实际判断能力的机会。选项A 'People lose the chance to cultivate the ability to make practical judgments' 与原文表述一致，因此是正确答案。","questionZh":"算法指令取代人类判断的后果是什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What may result from increasing application of recommendation engines in our consumption of culture?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Consumers will have much limited choice."},{"label":"B","text":"Consumers will actually enjoy better luck."},{"label":"C","text":"It will be easier to decide on what to enjoy."},{"label":"D","text":"Humans will develop tastes similar to machines'."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Consumers will have much limited choice.","answerZh":"消费者的选择将大受限制。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'By presenting consumers with algorithmically selected choices of what to watch, read, stream and visit next, companies are replacing human taste with machine taste'，说明推荐引擎的广泛应用会限制消费者的选择。选项A 'Consumers will have much limited choice' 与原文表述一致，因此是正确答案。","questionZh":"在文化消费中越来越多地应用推荐引擎可能导致什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What is likely to happen to larger parts of our daily life as machine learning algorithms improve?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They will turn out to be more pleasant."},{"label":"B","text":"They will repeat our past experience."},{"label":"C","text":"They can be completely anticipated."},{"label":"D","text":"They may become better and better."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They can be completely anticipated.","answerZh":"它们可以被完全预测。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'As machine learning algorithms improve and as they train on more extensive data sets, larger parts of everyday life are likely to become utterly predictable'，说明随着机器学习算法的改进，日常生活的大部分可以被完全预测。选项C 'They can be completely anticipated' 与原文表述一致，因此是正确答案。","questionZh":"随着机器学习算法的改进,我们日常生活的更大部分可能会发生什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"Why does the author say the creatures living in the more and more AI-mediated world will become increasingly unlike us?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They will have lost the most significant human element of being intelligent."},{"label":"B","text":"They will no longer possess the human characteristic of being unpredictable."},{"label":"C","text":"They will not be able to understand themselves as we can do today."},{"label":"D","text":"They will be deprived of what their predecessors were proud of about themselves."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They will no longer possess the human characteristic of being unpredictable.","answerZh":"他们将不再具备人类不可预测这一特性。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'But to the extent that unpredictability is part of how people understand themselves and part of what people like about themselves, humanity is in the process of losing something significant'，说明在越来越受AI影响的世界中，人类将失去不可预测性这一重要特征。选项B 'They will no longer possess the human characteristic of being unpredictable' 与原文表述一致，因此是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者为什么说生活在日益由 AI 主导的世界里的生物将越来越不像我们?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2023_06_1-p2","title":"CET6 2023年06月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2023年06月 第1套","examDate":"2023年06月","year":"2023","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2023-06-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"自然拼读法是教孩子阅读的最佳途径，却长期被污名化；美国深陷阅读教学法之争，密西西比州靠系统、明确的阅读科学取得显著进步。","mainIdeaEn":"Phonics is the best way to teach reading yet has been stigmatized; amid America's decades-long reading wars, Mississippi's systematic, explicit science-of-reading approach produced remarkable gains.","answerCode":"ABBCD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先拼读法名声差，再教学法长期争，然后须系统明确教，接着改用阅读科学，最后是沉浸式教学法。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn about phonics in many American classrooms?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is ill reputed."},{"label":"B","text":"It is mostly misapplied."},{"label":"C","text":"It is arbitrarily excluded."},{"label":"D","text":"It is misrepresented."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is ill reputed.","answerZh":"它名声不佳。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'But in many classrooms, this can be a dirty word'，说明phonics在许多美国教室中名声不佳。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于许多美国课堂中的自然拼读法,我们了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What has America been witnessing for decades?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"An obsession with innovating teaching methodologies of reading."},{"label":"B","text":"An enduring debate over the approach to teaching children to read."},{"label":"C","text":"An increasing concern with many children's inadequacy in literacy."},{"label":"D","text":"An ever-forceful advocacy of a combined method for teaching reading."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"An enduring debate over the approach to teaching children to read.","answerZh":"一场关于儿童阅读教学方法的旷日持久的争论。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'America is stuck in a debate about teaching children to read that has been going on for decades'，说明美国几十年来一直在进行关于如何教孩子阅读的辩论。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"美国几十年来一直目睹着什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"Why does Tenette Smith think a combination of teaching methods is ineffective?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Elementary school children will be frustrated when taught with several methods combined."},{"label":"B","text":"Phonics has to be systematically applied and clearly taught to achieve the desired effect."},{"label":"C","text":"Sprinkling in a little phonics deters the progress of even adequately motivated children."},{"label":"D","text":"Balanced literacy fails to sustain children's interest in developing a good reading habit."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Phonics has to be systematically applied and clearly taught to achieve the desired effect.","answerZh":"自然拼读法必须系统运用、明确教授才能达到预期效果。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'\"You can't sprinkle in a little phonics,\" says Tenette Smith, executive director of elementary education and reading at Mississippi's education department. \"It has to be systematic and explicitly taught.\"'，说明Tenette Smith认为phonics必须系统地应用并明确地教授才能达到预期效果。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Tenette Smith 为什么认为多种教学方法结合起来是无效的?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does the author say Mississippi's success is attributed to?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Convening a National Reading Panel to synthesize research evidence."},{"label":"B","text":"Placing sufficient emphasis upon both fluency and comprehension."},{"label":"C","text":"Adopting scientifically grounded approaches to teaching reading."},{"label":"D","text":"Obtaining support from Congress to upgrade teaching methods."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Adopting scientifically grounded approaches to teaching reading.","answerZh":"采用有科学依据的阅读教学方法。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'Mississippi's success is attributed to implementing reading methods supported by a body of research known as the science of reading.'，说明密西西比州的成功归因于采用科学研究支持的阅读方法。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者说密西西比州的成功归因于什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What have advances in statistics and brain imaging proved ineffective?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The teaching of symbol-sound relationships."},{"label":"B","text":"Explicit instruction in phonemic awareness."},{"label":"C","text":"Efforts to end the reading wars."},{"label":"D","text":"The immersive approach."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The immersive approach.","answerZh":"沉浸式教学法。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'Yet over two decades on, \"balanced literacy\" is still being taught in classrooms. But advances in statistics and brain imaging have disproved the whole-language method.'，说明统计学和脑成像技术的进步已经证明沉浸式方法无效。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"统计学和脑成像方面的进步被证明对什么无效?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2023_06_3-p1","title":"CET6 2023年06月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2023年06月 第3套","examDate":"2023年06月","year":"2023","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2023-06-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章介绍莫斯的观点：加工食品像烟酒一样被设计得使人上瘾，食品公司利用记忆和速度让人不停吃零食，如今却难以满足消费者健康饮食的新需求。","mainIdeaEn":"Michael Moss argues processed food is engineered to be as addictive as alcohol or cigarettes—companies exploit memory and speed to keep us hooked, and now struggle to meet consumers' demand for healthier food.","answerCode":"ADACD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说加工食品如烟酒会上瘾，再靠记忆勾起我们的馋，然后厂商拼命塑造食物记忆，接着一切讲究快字当头，最后自己也戒不掉方便食品。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"In what way does Michael Moss think processed food is comparable to alcohol and cigarettes?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are all addictive."},{"label":"B","text":"They are all necessary evils."},{"label":"C","text":"They are all engineered to be enjoyed."},{"label":"D","text":"They are all in increasingly great demand."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They are all addictive.","answerZh":"它们都会让人上瘾。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'processed food is engineered to hook you, not unlike alcohol, cigarettes, or other harmful substances'可知，Moss认为加工食品、酒精和香烟都是让人上瘾的，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Michael Moss 认为加工食品在哪方面可与酒精和香烟相提并论?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the author say plays a key role in the foods we crave?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The food environment."},{"label":"B","text":"Aggressive marketing."},{"label":"C","text":"Convenience."},{"label":"D","text":"Memory."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Memory.","answerZh":"记忆。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段'Memory, nostalgia in particular, plays a big role in the foods we crave'可知，在我们渴望的食物中，记忆尤其是怀旧起着重要作用，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者说什么在我们渴望的食物中起关键作用?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What do food companies do to capitalize on consumers' association with their food products?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They strive to influence how consumers remember their products."},{"label":"B","text":"They attempt to use consumers' long-term memories to promote addiction."},{"label":"C","text":"They try to exploit consumers' memories for their products as early as possible."},{"label":"D","text":"They endeavor to find what consumers remember about their products."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They strive to influence how consumers remember their products.","answerZh":"它们竭力影响消费者对其产品的记忆。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'Knowing this, the food industry spends lots of time trying to shape the memories that we have for their products'可知，食品公司努力影响消费者对他们产品的记忆，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"食品公司做什么来利用消费者对其食品的联想?"},{"number":"49","stem":"How does the food industry operate from manufacturing to packaging, according to Moss?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Placing the idea of fast food in an entirely new light."},{"label":"B","text":"Setting no limit to the number of fast food chains."},{"label":"C","text":"Focusing on how quickly the work is done."},{"label":"D","text":"Prioritizing the quality of their products."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Focusing on how quickly the work is done.","answerZh":"注重工作完成的速度。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段'Everything in the industry is about speed, from manufacturing to packaging'可知，食品行业从制造到包装都注重速度，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"据 Moss 所说,食品行业从生产到包装是如何运作的?"},{"number":"50","stem":"Why are companies finding it difficult to satisfy consumers' demand for healthier food products?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They think the speed of production outweighs consumers' health."},{"label":"B","text":"They believe their industry would perish without fast foods."},{"label":"C","text":"They have to strike a balance between taste and nutrition."},{"label":"D","text":"They are hooked on manufacturing convenience foods."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They are hooked on manufacturing convenience foods.","answerZh":"它们沉迷于生产方便食品。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'these companies are finding it really difficult to meet that new demand because of their own addiction to making these convenience foods'可知，公司之所以难以满足消费者对健康食品产品的需求，是因为它们沉迷于制造这些方便食品，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"为什么各公司发现很难满足消费者对更健康食品的需求?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2023_06_3-p2","title":"CET6 2023年06月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2023年06月 第3套","examDate":"2023年06月","year":"2023","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2023-06-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"人类进化上的成功并非源于超凡智力与独立创新，而是靠忠实模仿他人；研究显示儿童会不加判断地过度模仿，这种照搬能力正是人类繁衍壮大的关键。","mainIdeaEn":"Humans thrive not through raw intelligence or innovation but by faithfully copying others; studies show children over-imitate irrationally, and this copying ability underlies our species' evolutionary success.","answerCode":"DDABB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先哪都能活，再靠模仿闯关，然后小孩照搬每一步，接着源于学复杂技术，最后模仿是人类天性。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What might explain humans' having the largest population of almost all mammals?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are equipped with raw strength for solving the most challenging problems."},{"label":"B","text":"They cope with the outside world more effectively than their animal relatives."},{"label":"C","text":"They possess the most outstanding ability to think."},{"label":"D","text":"They know how to survive everywhere on earth."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They know how to survive everywhere on earth.","answerZh":"他们懂得如何在地球上任何地方生存。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'while humans have colonized every corner of the globe'可知人类在地球上的各个角落都能生存，因此D选项'They know how to survive everywhere on earth'是正确答案。","questionZh":"什么或许能解释人类在几乎所有哺乳动物中拥有最多的数量?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What accounts for humans' evolutionary successes according to a growing number of cognitive scientists and anthropologists?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are better at innovating solutions."},{"label":"B","text":"They thrive through creative strategies."},{"label":"C","text":"They are naturally adaptive to ecological contexts."},{"label":"D","text":"They meet challenges by imitating others carefully."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They meet challenges by imitating others carefully.","answerZh":"他们通过细致地模仿他人来应对挑战。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'They think that, rather than making our living as innovators, we survive and thrive precisely because we don't think for ourselves. Instead, people cope with challenging climates and ecological contexts by carefully copying others.'可知，人类通过仔细模仿他人来应对挑战，因此D选项'They meet challenges by imitating others carefully'是正确答案。","questionZh":"据越来越多的认知科学家和人类学家所言,是什么造就了人类的进化成功?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does the author think is odd about the findings of the study by Victoria Horner and Andrew Whiten?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Children irrationally imitated every action of the experimenters."},{"label":"B","text":"Chimpanzees could tell the transparent box from the opaque one."},{"label":"C","text":"Chimpanzees could retrieve the treat more quickly than children did."},{"label":"D","text":"Children omitted the step of tapping on the box with a stick to open it."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Children irrationally imitated every action of the experimenters.","answerZh":"儿童不加理性判断地模仿实验者的每个动作。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'Oddly, the children carefully copied all the steps to open the box, even when they could see that the stick had no practical effect. That is, they copied irrationally: Instead of doing only what was necessary to get their reward, children slavishly imitated every action they'd witnessed.'可知，作者认为奇怪的是孩子们不理性地模仿了实验者的所有动作，因此A选项'Children irrationally imitated every action of the experimenters'是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者认为 Victoria Horner 和 Andrew Whiten 研究的发现有什么奇怪之处?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What is anthropologist Joseph Henrich's explanation for the human preference for copying?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It originates in the rationality of people around the world."},{"label":"B","text":"It stems from the way people learn complex technologies."},{"label":"C","text":"It results from people distrusting their own wisdom."},{"label":"D","text":"It derives from the desire to acquire knowledge step by step."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It stems from the way people learn complex technologies.","answerZh":"它源于人们学习复杂技术的方式。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段'Anthropologist Joseph Henrich points out that people around the world rely on technologies that are often so complex that no one can learn them rationally. Instead, people must learn them step by step, trusting in the wisdom of more experienced elders and peers.'可知，人类偏好模仿的原因是人们学习复杂技术的方式，因此B选项'It stems from the way people learn complex technologies'是正确答案。","questionZh":"人类学家 Joseph Henrich 对人类偏好模仿的解释是什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What point does the author want to emphasize when he says \"We're not chimpanzees\"?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is arguable whether everyone should avoid imitation."},{"label":"B","text":"It is characteristic of human beings to copy others."},{"label":"C","text":"It is desirable to trust in more knowledgeable peers."},{"label":"D","text":"It is naive to laugh at someone embracing nonconformity."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It is characteristic of human beings to copy others.","answerZh":"模仿他人是人类的特性。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章最后一段'So the next time you hear someone arguing passionately that everyone should embrace nonconformity and avoid imitating others, you might laugh a little bit. We're not chimpanzees, after all.'可知，作者想要强调的是人类模仿他人是其特性，因此B选项'It is characteristic of human beings to copy others'是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者说\"We're not chimpanzees\"时想强调什么观点?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2023_12_1-p1","title":"CET6 2023年12月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2023年12月 第1套","examDate":"2023年12月","year":"2023","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2023-12-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者批评\"减税促增长\"的公式无效却流行，主张把提高工人工资作为经济政策优先项：工资上涨带动消费，进而驱动美国经济增长。","mainIdeaEn":"The author argues the popular tax-cut formula for growth doesn't work; instead, raising workers' wages should be the policy priority, since higher pay fuels consumption and thus drives economic growth.","answerCode":"BCABA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说减税没对手才流行，再开涨工资新药方，然后工资涨带火经济，接着旧论只认生产率，最后生产率翻倍工资掉队。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"Why does the formula of tax cuts remain popular though ineffective?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its critics' voice has not been heard throughout the country."},{"label":"B","text":"There seem to be no other options available to replace it."},{"label":"C","text":"The cult of tax cuts has been relentlessly propagated by all policymakers."},{"label":"D","text":"There appears to be a misunderstanding of the formula among the public."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"There seem to be no other options available to replace it.","answerZh":"似乎没有其他可行方案能取代它。","explanation":"原文'it lacks for obvious rivals'，即减税公式缺乏明显的替代方案，故选 B。 - 关键句：And while the cult of tax cuts has attracted many critics, it lacks for obvious rivals.","questionZh":"为什么减税的方式虽然无效却依然流行?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the author think is a more effective measure for driving economic growth in the U.S.?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Aiding people left behind by economic growth."},{"label":"B","text":"Prioritizing the growth of the nation's GDP."},{"label":"C","text":"Increasing the compensation for labor."},{"label":"D","text":"Introducing even more extensive tax cuts."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Increasing the compensation for labor.","answerZh":"提高劳动报酬。","explanation":"原文指出更有效的途径是 higher wages（提高工资即提高劳动报酬），故选 C。 - 关键句：The painful lessons of recent decades point to a promising candidate: higher wages.","questionZh":"作者认为推动美国经济增长更有效的措施是什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What is the logic underlying the author's viewpoint?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The growth of workers' paychecks ultimately boosts the nation's economy."},{"label":"B","text":"Paying a premium to maintain a reliable workforce attracts more customers."},{"label":"C","text":"Consumption stimulates the desire for higher wages."},{"label":"D","text":"Familiar arguments for higher wages are outdated."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"The growth of workers' paychecks ultimately boosts the nation's economy.","answerZh":"工人工资的增长最终会促进国家经济发展。","explanation":"作者借福特案例说明'consumption drives the economy, and workers who are paid more can spend more'，即工资增长最终拉动经济，故选 A。 - 关键句：Consumption drives the American economy, and workers who are paid more can spend more.","questionZh":"作者观点背后的逻辑是什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What is the basis for higher wages according to the conventional wisdom?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fairness in distribution."},{"label":"B","text":"Increase in productivity."},{"label":"C","text":"The priority of economic policymakers."},{"label":"D","text":"The unerring judgment of market forces."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Increase in productivity.","answerZh":"生产率的提高。","explanation":"原文'productivity growth was the only route to higher wages'，传统观点认为生产率增长是涨薪的唯一途径，故选 B。 - 关键句：The conventional wisdom held that productivity growth was the only route to higher wages.","questionZh":"根据传统观念,更高工资的基础是什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What do we learn about things in the real world in America for the past 50 years or so?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"People have failed to see a corresponding increase in wages and in productivity."},{"label":"B","text":"People have been disheartened by the widening gap between the haves and have-nots."},{"label":"C","text":"People have witnessed a tug of war between Republicans and Democrats over tax cuts."},{"label":"D","text":"People have seen the link disappearing between productivity and workers' well-being."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"People have failed to see a corresponding increase in wages and in productivity.","answerZh":"人们没有看到工资与生产率的相应增长。","explanation":"原文指出自1970年以来生产率翻倍而工资远远落后，即工资增长未与生产率增长同步，故选 A。 - 关键句：the widening gap between productivity growth and wage growth since roughly 1970. Productivity has more than doubled; wages have lagged far behind.","questionZh":"关于过去大约50年美国现实世界中的情况,我们了解到什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2023_12_1-p2","title":"CET6 2023年12月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2023年12月 第1套","examDate":"2023年12月","year":"2023","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2023-12-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"一项新研究发现顶级心理学与神经科学期刊编委会由男性主导，女性代表性严重不足；作者认为这源于结构性障碍，呼吁主动破除而非归咎传统。","mainIdeaEn":"A new study finds top psychology and neuroscience journal editorial boards are male-dominated, underrepresenting women; the author blames structural barriers and calls for actively dismantling them rather than blaming tradition.","answerCode":"DCBAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先盼编委会多元化，再曝男编辑占大头，然后女编辑比例严重失衡，接着女性声音没人代表，最后来场结构大改革。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What would we expect an editorial board of an academic journal to exhibit in view of its important responsibilities?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Insight."},{"label":"B","text":"Expertise."},{"label":"C","text":"Integrity."},{"label":"D","text":"Diversity."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Diversity.","answerZh":"多元化。","explanation":"原文期望期刊建立 a diverse editorial board，体现多样性，故选 D。 - 关键句：journals would do everything they can to establish a diverse editorial board, reflecting a variety of voices, experiences, and identities.","questionZh":"鉴于学术期刊编委会的重要职责,我们期望它表现出什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What do we learn from the findings of a new study in Nature Neuroscience?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The majority of top psychology and neuroscience journals reflect a variety of voices, experiences and identities."},{"label":"B","text":"The editorial boards of most psychology and neuroscience journals do influence the direction their field takes."},{"label":"C","text":"The editorial boards of the most important journals in psychology and neuroscience are male-dominated."},{"label":"D","text":"The majority of editors in top psychology and neuroscience journals have relevant backgrounds."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"The editorial boards of the most important journals in psychology and neuroscience are male-dominated.","answerZh":"心理学和神经科学最重要期刊的编委会由男性主导。","explanation":"研究发现顶级期刊编辑多为男性，即编委会男性主导，故选 C。 - 关键句：the majority of editors in top psychology and neuroscience journals are male and based in the United States: a situation that may be amplifying existing gender inequalities in the field","questionZh":"我们从 Nature Neuroscience 一项新研究的发现中了解到什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What fact does the author highlight concerning the gender differences in editors of psychology journals?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"There were quite a few female editors who also distinguished themselves as influential psychology researchers."},{"label":"B","text":"The number of female editors was simply disproportionate to that of women engaged in psychology research."},{"label":"C","text":"The proportion of female editors was increasingly lower at senior levels."},{"label":"D","text":"There were few female editors who could move up to senior positions."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"The number of female editors was simply disproportionate to that of women engaged in psychology research.","answerZh":"女性编辑的数量与从事心理学研究的女性数量根本不成比例。","explanation":"原文强调女编辑比例显著低于女性心理学研究者比例，即不成比例，故选 B。 - 关键句：the proportion of female editors was significantly lower than the overall proportion of women psychology researchers.","questionZh":"关于心理学期刊编辑中的性别差异,作者强调了什么事实?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What can we infer from the conclusion drawn by the team of the new study on the basis of their findings?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Women's views are underrepresented in the editorial boards of top psychology and neuroscience journals."},{"label":"B","text":"Male editors of top psychology and neuroscience journals tend to be biased against their female colleagues."},{"label":"C","text":"Male researchers have enough representation in the editorial boards to ensure their publications."},{"label":"D","text":"Female editors have to struggle to get women's research articles published in academic journals."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Women's views are underrepresented in the editorial boards of top psychology and neuroscience journals.","answerZh":"女性的观点在顶级心理学和神经科学期刊编委会中代表性不足。","explanation":"团队结论是男性的观念在编委会中被过度代表，可推断女性观点代表不足，故选 A。 - 关键句：the ideas, values and decision-making biases of men are overrepresented in the editorial positions of the most recognized academic journals in psychology and neuroscience.","questionZh":"从这项新研究团队基于其发现得出的结论中,我们可以推断出什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author suggest we do instead of simply blaming the inequality of editorial boards on tradition?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Strike a balance between male and female editors."},{"label":"B","text":"Increase women's employment in senior positions."},{"label":"C","text":"Enlarge the body of female academics."},{"label":"D","text":"Implement overall structural reforms."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Implement overall structural reforms.","answerZh":"实施全面的结构性改革。","explanation":"作者指出存在结构性原因，应主动打破这些壁垒，即进行整体结构性改革，故选 D。 - 关键句：there are structural reasons that women are disadvantaged in science. Women receive lower salaries and face greater childcare demands, for instance, which can result in fewer publications and grants","questionZh":"作者建议我们做什么,而不是简单地将编委会的不平等归咎于传统?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2023_12_2-p1","title":"CET6 2023年12月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2023年12月 第2套","examDate":"2023年12月","year":"2023","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2023-12-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"借赛琳娜·戈麦斯戒社交媒体的例子，作者指出主动断网是一种特权：数字鸿沟令弱势群体难以上网，社会既要允许人们下线，更要保障人人能联网。","mainIdeaEn":"Using Selena Gomez's social media break, the author argues opting out of the internet is a privilege: digital exclusion harms the underprivileged, so society must let some switch off while enabling others to switch on.","answerCode":"CCDBA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先是她多年不碰社交媒体，再叹数字时代离网难活，然后英国不少家庭没稳宽带，接着平台让人有归属感，最后关键是人人能上网。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do we learn about singer and actress Selena Gomez in the past four and a half years?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"She has had worsening mental problems."},{"label":"B","text":"She has won Instagram's most followers."},{"label":"C","text":"She has refrained from using social media."},{"label":"D","text":"She has succeeded in a bid on the internet."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"She has refrained from using social media.","answerZh":"她一直克制不使用社交媒体。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'Could you get by without using the internet for four and a half years? That's exactly what singer and actress Selena Gomez has done in a bid to improve her mental health.'可知，Selena Gomez在过去四年半里没有使用社交媒体，所以选项C正确。","questionZh":"关于歌手兼演员 Selena Gomez 过去四年半的情况,我们了解到什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"Why does actively opting out of using the internet become a matter of privilege?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Most people find it subtle and complicated to give up using the internet."},{"label":"B","text":"Most people can hardly ditch the web while avoiding hate and comparisons."},{"label":"C","text":"Most people can hardly get by without the internet due to growing digitisation."},{"label":"D","text":"Most people have been seriously addicted to the web without being aware of it."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Most people can hardly get by without the internet due to growing digitisation.","answerZh":"由于数字化日益加深，大多数人离开互联网几乎无法生活。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'The increasing digitisation of our society means that everything from paying a gas bill to plotting a route to a friend's house and even making a phone call is at the mercy of your internet connection. Actively opting out of using the internet becomes a matter of privilege.'可知，由于社会数字化程度的提高，人们越来越依赖互联网，所以主动放弃使用互联网成为一种特权。因此选项C正确。","questionZh":"为什么主动选择不使用互联网成了一种特权?"},{"number":"48","stem":"Why does the author say \"witnessing companies⋯feels particularly irritating\"(Lines 2-4, Para.6)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The UK digital divide would further worsen due to the metaverse."},{"label":"B","text":"The concept of the metaverse is believed to be still quite illusory."},{"label":"C","text":"School children would be drawn farther away from the real world."},{"label":"D","text":"Most families in the UK do not have stable broadband connections."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Most families in the UK do not have stable broadband connections.","answerZh":"英国大多数家庭没有稳定的宽带连接。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章第六段'The UK's digital divide has worsened over the past two years, leaving poorer families without broadband connections in their homes. Digital exclusion is a major threat to wider societal equality in the UK, so witnessing companies like Facebook championing the metaverse as the next great frontier when school children are struggling to complete their homework feels particularly irritating.'可知，由于英国数字鸿沟的加剧，许多家庭没有宽带连接，而Facebook等公司却在推广元宇宙，这使得作者感到特别恼火。因此选项D正确。","questionZh":"作者为什么说\"witnessing companies…feels particularly irritating\"(第6段第2-4行)?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What is worth bearing in mind concerning social media platforms?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are conducive to promoting societal equality."},{"label":"B","text":"They help many people feel connected with others."},{"label":"C","text":"They provide a necessary device for a digital detox."},{"label":"D","text":"They create a virtual community on the internet."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They help many people feel connected with others.","answerZh":"它们帮助许多人感受到与他人的联结。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'Consequently, it's worth bearing in mind that while deleting all social media accounts will undoubtedly make some feel infinitely better, many other people benefit from the strong sense of community that sharing platforms can breed.'可知，许多人从社交媒体平台上获得的强烈社区感中受益，所以选项B正确。","questionZh":"关于社交媒体平台,什么值得记住?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does the author think is really important for those living in digital exclusion?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Having access to the internet."},{"label":"B","text":"Edging further towards web 3.0."},{"label":"C","text":"Getting more educational resources."},{"label":"D","text":"Opening more social media accounts."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Having access to the internet.","answerZh":"能够接入互联网。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'Internet access will continue to grow in importance as we edge further towards web 3.0, and greater resources and initiatives are needed to provide the underprivileged with the connectivity they desperately need to learn, work and live.'可知，对于生活在数字排斥中的人来说，获得互联网接入是非常重要的，所以选项A正确。","questionZh":"作者认为对处于数字排斥中的人来说真正重要的是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2023_12_2-p2","title":"CET6 2023年12月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2023年12月 第2套","examDate":"2023年12月","year":"2023","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2023-12-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章探讨竞争是天性还是习得：弗洛伊德与达尔文传统视竞争为本能，但达尔文本人并不排斥合作，米德的跨文化研究表明竞争性其实是文化塑造的。","mainIdeaEn":"Is competitiveness innate or learned? Though Freud and Darwinian tradition cast it as instinct, Darwin himself allowed for cooperation, and Mead's cross-cultural studies show competitiveness is culturally created.","answerCode":"DDCBD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先见竞争影响无处不在，再学会守规矩里求满足，然后自然界本无理性插手，接着求生也能互相扶持，最后态度全看文化怎么教。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author think is easy to see in many areas of contemporary life?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The disagreement on the inevitability of competition."},{"label":"B","text":"The consequence of psychological investigation."},{"label":"C","text":"The effect of human drives."},{"label":"D","text":"The impact of competition."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The impact of competition.","answerZh":"竞争的影响。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'you cannot but recognize the effect competition is exerting in academics and many other areas of contemporary life'，表明作者认为在当代生活的许多领域中，竞争的影响是显而易见的。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者认为在当代生活的许多领域中,什么很容易看到?"},{"number":"52","stem":"According to psychology, what do people strive to do following the initial stage of their life?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fulfill individual needs without incurring adverse effects of human drives."},{"label":"B","text":"Indulge in cultural pursuits while keeping their base impulses at bay."},{"label":"C","text":"Gain extensive recognition without exposing pure indulgence."},{"label":"D","text":"Satisfy their own desires while observing social conventions."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Satisfy their own desires while observing social conventions.","answerZh":"在遵守社会规范的同时满足自身欲望。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'we are at the mercy of a battle between our base impulses for self-fulfillment and social and cultural norms which prohibit pure indulgence'，表明在人生的最初阶段之后，人们努力在满足自己的欲望的同时遵守社会规范。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"根据心理学,人们在人生初始阶段之后努力去做什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What do we learn about the \"natural world\" characterized by Thomas Hobbes?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It gets misrepresented by philosophers and anthropologists."},{"label":"B","text":"It gets distorted in Darwin's The Origin of Species."},{"label":"C","text":"It is free from the rational intervention of humans."},{"label":"D","text":"It is the pre-rational world rarely appreciated nowadays."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It is free from the rational intervention of humans.","answerZh":"它不受人类理性的干预。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'Thomas Hobbes... characterized the 'natural world,' that is, the world before the imposition of the will of humanity, as being 'nasty, brutish, and short.''，表明霍布斯描述的自然世界是人类意志强加之前的世界，即没有人类理性干预的世界。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于 Thomas Hobbes 所描述的\"natural world\",我们了解到什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What can we conclude from Darwin's assertion in The Origin of Species?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"All species inherently depend on others for survival."},{"label":"B","text":"Struggles for survival do not exclude mutual support."},{"label":"C","text":"Competition weighs as much as cooperation as a survival strategy."},{"label":"D","text":"The strongest species proves to be the fittest in natural selection."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Struggles for survival do not exclude mutual support.","answerZh":"生存竞争并不排斥相互扶持。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章第四段提到'Darwin asserted in The Origin of Species that the struggles he was describing should be viewed as metaphors and could easily include dependence and cooperation.'，表明达尔文认为生存斗争可以被看作是隐喻，可以很容易地包括依赖和合作。因此可以推断出生存斗争不排除相互支持。所以B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"从达尔文在 The Origin of Species 中的论断,我们可以得出什么结论?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What conclusion did Margaret Mead reach after studying dozens of different cultures?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is characteristic of humans to be competitive."},{"label":"B","text":"Americans are uniquely opposed to cooperation."},{"label":"C","text":"Competition is relatively more prevalent in Western societies."},{"label":"D","text":"People's attitude towards competition is actually culture-bound."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"People's attitude towards competition is actually culture-bound.","answerZh":"人们对竞争的态度实际上受文化制约。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'Mead's final conclusion was that competitiveness is a culturally created aspect of human behavior, and that its prevalence in a particular society is relative to how that society values it.'，表明米德得出的结论是竞争性是人类行为中由文化创造的方面，其在特定社会的普遍性与该社会对它的评价有关。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"Margaret Mead 研究了数十种不同文化后得出了什么结论?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2023_12_3-p1","title":"CET6 2023年12月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2023年12月 第3套","examDate":"2023年12月","year":"2023","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2023-12-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者认为研究成果必须走出学术圈、以通俗易懂的方式传播给公众才能真正造福社会，并分析了传播不足的原因，呼吁机构支持研究者对外分享成果。","mainIdeaEn":"Research only fulfills its purpose when findings are communicated accessibly beyond academia; the author analyzes why researchers fail to do so and urges institutions to support broader public sharing of results.","answerCode":"DABAC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先要成果传出学术圈，再叹大众看不懂学术话，然后学者只顾评终身教职，接着分享能带来新方向，最后请写手让公众读得懂。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"How can research serve its full purpose according to the author?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"With researchers being aware of public interests."},{"label":"B","text":"With its findings published in prominent journals."},{"label":"C","text":"With researchers creating products that enhance social development."},{"label":"D","text":"With its findings properly communicated beyond the academic circle."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"With its findings properly communicated beyond the academic circle.","answerZh":"将研究成果恰当地传播到学术圈之外。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'For research to serve its full purpose, the results must leave the confines of research laboratories and academic journals'可知，研究要发挥其全部作用，其发现必须走出实验室和学术期刊的局限。因此，正确答案是D选项'With its findings properly communicated beyond the academic circle'。","questionZh":"作者认为研究如何才能充分发挥其作用?"},{"number":"47","stem":"Why do ordinary readers find it difficult to access the results of researchers'studies?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They cannot understand the academic language used for reporting these results."},{"label":"B","text":"They feel intimidated by the jargon researchers use to describe their findings."},{"label":"C","text":"They do not attend conferences where these results are freely available."},{"label":"D","text":"They have few chances to locate the journals that publish these findings."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They cannot understand the academic language used for reporting these results.","answerZh":"他们看不懂报告这些成果所用的学术语言。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'Even articles freely available are usually written in academic language incomprehensible to the average reader'可知，即使文章免费提供，通常也是用普通读者难以理解的学术语言写成的。因此，正确答案是A选项'They cannot understand the academic language used for reporting these results'。","questionZh":"为什么普通读者难以获取研究人员的研究成果?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What is one of the reasons some researchers won't prioritise communicating their findings to the public?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They can thrive on the papers published."},{"label":"B","text":"Their top consideration is to win tenure."},{"label":"C","text":"Their main goal is gaining recognition in their field."},{"label":"D","text":"They have to struggle to reach out to the community."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Their top consideration is to win tenure.","answerZh":"他们的头等大事是获得终身教职。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'For researchers in the tenure-track system, their main goal is winning tenure, which in part can be achieved by getting a number of papers published in prominent journals'可知，一些研究者不会优先考虑向公众传达他们的发现，因为他们的主要目标是获得终身教职，这在一定程度上可以通过在知名期刊上发表多篇论文来实现。因此，正确答案是B选项'Their top consideration is to win tenure'。","questionZh":"一些研究人员不优先向公众传达其研究发现的原因之一是什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"How can sharing findings benefit researchers themselves?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"By helping them to identify new research directions."},{"label":"B","text":"By enabling them to understand crises plaguing society."},{"label":"C","text":"By enabling them to effectively address social discrepancies."},{"label":"D","text":"By helping them to forge ties with government agencies."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"By helping them to identify new research directions.","answerZh":"帮助他们发现新的研究方向。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段'Engaging with other researchers and the public can lead to unexpected new connections and new ideas that could suggest fruitful new directions for research'可知，与其他人和公众接触可以带来意想不到的新联系和新想法，这些可能为研究提供富有成果的新方向。因此，正确答案是A选项'By helping them to identify new research directions'。","questionZh":"分享研究发现如何使研究人员自身受益?"},{"number":"50","stem":"Why are researchers advised to engage the services of professional writers or communication officers?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"To satisfy ethics committees' mandatory requirements of researchers."},{"label":"B","text":"To translate their study into languages accessible to readers overseas."},{"label":"C","text":"To make their publications correctly understood by the public."},{"label":"D","text":"To render their findings acceptable by prominent journals."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"To make their publications correctly understood by the public.","answerZh":"使他们的发表成果被公众正确理解。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'But this can be resolved by researchers engaging the services of professional writers or communication officers to help with translating their study into more accessible language and share it widely with media outlets and the public'可知，研究人员被建议聘请专业作家或传播官员，以帮助将他们的研究翻译成更易于理解的语言，并与媒体和公众广泛分享。因此，正确答案是C选项'To make their publications correctly understood by the public'。","questionZh":"为什么建议研究人员聘请专业作家或传播人员的服务?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2023_12_3-p2","title":"CET6 2023年12月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2023年12月 第3套","examDate":"2023年12月","year":"2023","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2023-12-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章为蜘蛛正名：它们长期被误解、与邪恶挂钩且缺乏研究，如今又因昆虫减少和栖息地丧失而受威胁，作者呼吁更多人欣赏蜘蛛的美妙价值。","mainIdeaEn":"Long misunderstood and linked with evil, spiders are under-studied and now threatened by shrinking insect prey and habitat loss; the author hopes more people will appreciate how terrific spiders truly are.","answerCode":"ABCBD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说蜘蛛一直被误解，再被当成邪恶化身，然后杀虫剂断了它口粮，接着失了家园快灭绝，最后盼大家赏识蛛之美。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn about spiders in the UK since the middle ages?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They have been generally misconceived."},{"label":"B","text":"They have adversely impacted crop growth."},{"label":"C","text":"They have been a constant reminder of bad luck."},{"label":"D","text":"They have made their presence felt when spinning webs."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They have been generally misconceived.","answerZh":"它们普遍遭到误解。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'But they are a constant source of human anxieties—with a cultural association with witches and wickedness dating back to the middle ages'可知，自中世纪以来，蜘蛛在英国一直被误解，与巫术和邪恶联系在一起。","questionZh":"关于中世纪以来英国的蜘蛛,我们了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What have spiders been associated with in the UK for centuries?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Harm."},{"label":"B","text":"Evil"},{"label":"C","text":"Suffering."},{"label":"D","text":"Aggression."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Evil","answerZh":"邪恶","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'with a cultural association with witches and wickedness dating back to the middle ages'可知，在英国几个世纪以来，蜘蛛一直与邪恶联系在一起。","questionZh":"几个世纪以来,蜘蛛在英国一直与什么联系在一起?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What partly accounts for the reduction in spiders'food supply?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The long tradition of collecting insects."},{"label":"B","text":"Fast reproduction of their competitors."},{"label":"C","text":"Chemicals used for killing insects."},{"label":"D","text":"The extinction of a lot of wildlife."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Chemicals used for killing insects.","answerZh":"用于杀灭昆虫的化学品。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'A recent landmark study identified a 75% fall in insect populations between 1989 and 2016, with pesticide use thought to be to blame along with the destruction of wild areas for development'可知，蜘蛛食物供应减少的部分原因是杀虫剂的使用。","questionZh":"什么部分导致了蜘蛛食物供应的减少?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does the passage say is conservationists' biggest worry?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A variety of spiders are threatened due to pollution of marshes and wasteland."},{"label":"B","text":"Certain species of spiders are endangered due to loss of their natural homes."},{"label":"C","text":"An increasing number of spiders are being killed by deadly pesticides."},{"label":"D","text":"More and more spider species are found losing their ability to migrate."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Certain species of spiders are endangered due to loss of their natural homes.","answerZh":"某些蜘蛛物种因失去自然栖息地而濒临灭绝。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'But conservationists are most concerned about those varieties that are threatened due to habitat loss and fragmentation, which makes it impossible for them to migrate'可知，保护主义者最担心的是某些物种因栖息地丧失和破碎化而受到威胁。","questionZh":"文中说保护主义者最大的担忧是什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What wish does the author express close to the end of the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"More people would recognise spiders'unique status in the ecosystem."},{"label":"B","text":"People would show greater enthusiasm for spiders than for butterflies."},{"label":"C","text":"There would be sufficient corridors for spiders to move along."},{"label":"D","text":"There would be more people appreciating spiders' splendour."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"There would be more people appreciating spiders' splendour.","answerZh":"希望有更多人欣赏蜘蛛的美妙之处。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'it would be a good thing if more animal lovers recognised the ways in which spiders are simply terrific'可知，作者希望更多的人能认识到蜘蛛的美妙之处。","questionZh":"作者在文章接近结尾处表达了什么愿望?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2024_06_1-p1","title":"CET6 2024年06月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2024年06月 第1套","examDate":"2024年06月","year":"2024","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2024-06-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"文章探讨员工目睹职场危险行为却不干预的原因——旁观者效应、恐惧与不良安全文化，并主张主管和全员共同营造鼓励及时干预的安全氛围。","mainIdeaEn":"The passage examines why employees fail to intervene against unsafe workplace behavior—bystander effect, fear, and poor safety culture—and urges supervisors and everyone to build a climate supporting timely intervention.","answerCode":"BDADC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先怪职场文化不给安全感，再是人越多越没人出手，然后领导不管大家都学样，接着怕干预要多干活，最后靠主管造氛围敢发声。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What is one of the factors contributing to failure of intervention in face of risky behavior in the workplace?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Slack supervision style."},{"label":"B","text":"Unfavorable workplace culture."},{"label":"C","text":"Unforeseeable risk."},{"label":"D","text":"Blocked communication."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Unfavorable workplace culture.","answerZh":"不良的职场文化。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段提到的'the company's culture needs to make them feel safe to speak up'可知，不利的公司文化是导致在面对工作场所危险行为时未能干预的一个因素。","questionZh":"面对工作场所的危险行为,导致干预失败的因素之一是什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the author mean by \"diffusion of responsibility\" (Line 4, Para. 3)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The more people are around, the more they need to worry about their personal safety."},{"label":"B","text":"The more people who witness an event, the less likely anyone will venture to participate."},{"label":"C","text":"The more people idling around on the street, the more likely they need taking care of."},{"label":"D","text":"The more people are around, the less chance someone will step forward to intervene."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The more people are around, the less chance someone will step forward to intervene.","answerZh":"周围的人越多，有人站出来干预的可能性就越小。","explanation":"这是一道词义猜测题。根据文章第三段中'the more people assume that someone else will take care of it—meaning no one effectively intervenes or acts in a moment of need'可知，'diffusion of responsibility'指的是当周围人越多时，越少有人会站出来干预。","questionZh":"作者所说的\"diffusion of responsibility\"(第3段第4行)是什么意思?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What happens when unsafe behavior at the workplace is not addressed by the leaders?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"No one will intervene when they see similar behaviors."},{"label":"B","text":"Everyone will see it as the easiest way to deal with crisis."},{"label":"C","text":"Workers have to take extra caution executing their duties."},{"label":"D","text":"Workers are left to take care of the emergency themselves."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"No one will intervene when they see similar behaviors.","answerZh":"人们看到类似行为时没有人会出面干预。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段提到的'When a group of employees sees unsafe behavior not being addressed at a leadership level it creates the precedent that this is how these situations should be addressed, thus defining the safety culture for everyone'可知，当领导者不处理不安全行为时，员工不会干预他们看到的类似行为。","questionZh":"当工作场所的不安全行为未被领导者处理时会发生什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What is the ultimate reason workers won't act when they see unsafe operations?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Preference of deferring the action to others."},{"label":"B","text":"Anticipation of leadership intervention."},{"label":"C","text":"Fear of being isolated by coworkers."},{"label":"D","text":"Fear of having to do more work."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Fear of having to do more work.","answerZh":"害怕不得不承担更多工作。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第三段提到的'Fear is the ultimate factor in not intervening. There is a fear of penalty, a fear that they'll have to do more work if they intervene'可知，工人不采取行动的最终原因是害怕要做更多的工作。","questionZh":"工人看到不安全操作时不采取行动的根本原因是什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What is critical to ensuring workplace safety?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Workers are trained to operate their equipment properly."},{"label":"B","text":"Workers exhibiting at-risk behavior are strictly disciplined."},{"label":"C","text":"Supervisors create a safety environment for timely intervention."},{"label":"D","text":"Supervisors conduct effective communication with frontline workers."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Supervisors create a safety environment for timely intervention.","answerZh":"主管营造有利于及时干预的安全氛围。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段提到的'Supervisors also play a critical role... build a safety climate within their team that supports intervening and open communication among them'可知，确保工作场所安全的关键因素是主管创建一个支持及时干预和沟通的安全环境。","questionZh":"确保工作场所安全的关键是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2024_06_1-p2","title":"CET6 2024年06月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2024年06月 第1套","examDate":"2024年06月","year":"2024","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2024-06-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"围绕核能，科学界因对环保主义的不同理解而分裂：纯粹派只信可再生能源，另一派认为需核能兜底；德国的经验显示完全依赖可再生能源困难重重。","mainIdeaEn":"Scientists split over nuclear power due to differing views of environmentalism: purists back renewables only, others see nuclear as necessary backup; Germany's stalled transition shows 100% renewables remains contentious.","answerCode":"DCABA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先因环保理解不同起分歧，再有人说必要时就用核能，然后全靠可再生仍有争议，接着德国算推绿能好榜样，最后电网却拖了后腿。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What accounts for the divide within the scientific community about nuclear energy?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Attention to combating human-made climate change."},{"label":"B","text":"Emphasis on protecting wildlife and natural ecosystems."},{"label":"C","text":"Evolution of the term 'green energy' over the last century."},{"label":"D","text":"Adherence to different interpretations of environmentalism."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Adherence to different interpretations of environmentalism.","answerZh":"对环保主义不同理解的坚持。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'the distinction between these two strands of environmentalism is the cause of a split within the scientific community about nuclear energy'，表明科学界对核能的分歧是由于对环保主义的不同解释，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"是什么造成了科学界对核能的分歧?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What is the solution to energy shortage proposed by purists' opponents?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Relying on renewables firmly and exclusively."},{"label":"B","text":"Using fossil fuel and green energy alternately."},{"label":"C","text":"Opting for nuclear energy when necessary."},{"label":"D","text":"Limiting people's non-basic consumption."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Opting for nuclear energy when necessary.","answerZh":"必要时选择核能。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'Nuclear energy, being far cleaner than oil, gas and coal, is a natural option, especially where hydroelectric capacity is limited'，表明反对者提出在必要时选择核能作为解决方案，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"纯粹主义者的反对者提出的能源短缺解决方案是什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What point does the author want to make with cities like Burlington as an example?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is controversial whether the goal of the whole world's exclusive dependence on renewables is attainable."},{"label":"B","text":"It is contentious whether cities with large populations have renewable resources at their immediate disposal."},{"label":"C","text":"It is arguable whether cities that manage to run off renewables have sustainable hydroelectric capabilities."},{"label":"D","text":"It is debatable whether traditional fossil fuel energy can be done away with entirely throughout the world."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is controversial whether the goal of the whole world's exclusive dependence on renewables is attainable.","answerZh":"全世界完全依赖可再生能源这一目标能否实现尚有争议。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章第五段提到'The achievability of universal 100% renewability is similarly contentious'，并通过Burlington的例子说明即使是小城市也难以完全依赖可再生能源，暗示全球范围内实现100%可再生能源的争议性，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者以 Burlington 等城市为例想说明什么观点?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What do we learn about Germany regarding renewable energy?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has increased its wind and solar power generation four times over the last two decades."},{"label":"B","text":"It represents a good example of a major industrialized country promoting green energy."},{"label":"C","text":"It relies on renewable energy to generate more than half of its electricity."},{"label":"D","text":"It has succeeded in reaching the goal of energy transition set by Merkel."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It represents a good example of a major industrialized country promoting green energy.","answerZh":"它是主要工业化国家推广绿色能源的一个好范例。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'Germany stands as the best case study for a large, industrialized country pushing into green energy'，表明德国是推动绿色能源的大型工业化国家的典范，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于德国在可再生能源方面的情况,我们了解到什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What may be one of the reasons for Germany's progress having halted in recent years?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its grid infrastructure's capacity has fallen behind its development of green energy."},{"label":"B","text":"Its overabundance of green energy has forced power plants to suspend operation during daytime."},{"label":"C","text":"Its industrial south is used to running factories on conventional energy supplies."},{"label":"D","text":"Its renewable energy supplies are unstable both at night and during the day."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Its grid infrastructure's capacity has fallen behind its development of green energy.","answerZh":"其电网基础设施的容量已跟不上绿色能源的发展。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'Lagging grid infrastructure struggles to transport this overabundance of green energy from Germany's north to its industrial south'，表明电网基础设施的落后是德国近年来进展停滞的原因之一，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"德国近年来进展停滞的原因之一可能是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2024_06_2-p1","title":"CET6 2024年06月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2024年06月 第2套","examDate":"2024年06月","year":"2024","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2024-06-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"研究发现逆袭类真人秀强化了美国人对向上流动神话的信念，尽管现实中阶层跃升艰难；这种被娱乐媒体维系的信念还会削弱人们对反不平等政策的支持。","mainIdeaEn":"A study finds rags-to-riches reality TV perpetuates Americans' belief in the American Dream despite stagnant upward mobility, and this belief makes viewers less supportive of policies combating inequality.","answerCode":"BCAAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先是年轻人难往上爬，再看真人秀更信美国梦，然后新闻没真人秀观众多，接着共和党人信得最深，最后信梦者不挺反不平等政策。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about young Americans of today?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They have greater ambitions than their parents."},{"label":"B","text":"They find it difficult to achieve upward mobility."},{"label":"C","text":"They have overtaken their parents in terms of earnings."},{"label":"D","text":"They envy the opportunities in other industrialised nations."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They find it difficult to achieve upward mobility.","answerZh":"他们发现向上流动很难实现。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'young Americans today are struggling to earn more than their parents did at the same age, and upward mobility in the US actually compares unfavourably to that of other industrialised nations'可知，当今美国年轻人发现向上流动比他们的父母更难，因此B选项'They find it difficult to achieve upward mobility'是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于当今的美国年轻人,我们从文中了解到什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does Kim's team find about reality TV shows in America?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They reinterpret the essence of the popular rags-to-riches culture."},{"label":"B","text":"They urge people to achieve economic success through hard work."},{"label":"C","text":"They help strengthen people's conviction in the American Dream."},{"label":"D","text":"They feature ordinary Americans striving for social recognition."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They help strengthen people's conviction in the American Dream.","answerZh":"它们有助于强化人们对美国梦的信念。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段'The results showed that those who'd watched a rags-to-riches clip did indeed have a significantly greater belief in the American Dream'可知，观看这类节目的人确实对美国梦有更大的信仰，因此C选项'They help strengthen people's conviction in the American Dream'是正确答案。","questionZh":"Kim 的团队关于美国的真人秀节目发现了什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does the author say about news broadcasts in America?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They attract far fewer viewers than reality TV."},{"label":"B","text":"They are bent on reporting the dark side of life."},{"label":"C","text":"They stand in striking contrast with reality TV."},{"label":"D","text":"They focus on Americans' economic hardships."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They attract far fewer viewers than reality TV.","answerZh":"它们吸引的观众远少于真人秀。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'news broadcasts—which paint a more realistic view of the economic hardship faced by millions of Americans—get a much smaller proportion of the viewership'可知，新闻广播的观众比例远小于真人秀节目，因此A选项'They attract far fewer viewers than reality TV'是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于美国的新闻广播,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What can we infer from the passage about Republicans in general?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They believe strongly in the American Dream."},{"label":"B","text":"They strive to climb the socio-economic ladder."},{"label":"C","text":"They have a very strong affiliation with their party."},{"label":"D","text":"They tend to watch more rags-to-riches TV shows."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They believe strongly in the American Dream.","answerZh":"他们坚信美国梦。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章第四段'when participants were separated by party affiliation, this effect was significant among Republicans but not Democrats'可以推断出，共和党人普遍更相信美国梦，因此A选项'They believe strongly in the American Dream'是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于共和党人,我们可以从文中总体上推断出什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What is stated about people who believe in upward mobility?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are likely to blame the government for their plight."},{"label":"B","text":"They regard political consequences as anything but trivial."},{"label":"C","text":"They respect individuals striving to climb the social ladder."},{"label":"D","text":"They are less likely to approve of policies to fight inequality."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They are less likely to approve of policies to fight inequality.","answerZh":"他们更不可能支持对抗不平等的政策。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章最后一段'if people mistakenly believe that hard work is all that is needed for individuals to make a better life for themselves, they may be less supportive of policies that could actually combat inequality'可以推断出，相信向上流动的人不太可能支持打击不平等的政策，因此D选项'They are less likely to approve of policies to fight inequality'是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于相信向上流动的人,文中陈述了什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2024_06_2-p2","title":"CET6 2024年06月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2024年06月 第2套","examDate":"2024年06月","year":"2024","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2024-06-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"作者指出许多人以职业定义自我，失业便引发身份危机；但身份远比想象复杂且不断演变，我们应改变自我认知、学会管理不确定性，由自己定义自己。","mainIdeaEn":"Many people define themselves by their jobs, so job loss triggers identity crises; the author argues identity is complex and evolving, urging us to revise self-beliefs and manage uncertainty—we define who we are.","answerCode":"CDBDA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先是丢了工作不知自己是谁，再发现身份比想的复杂，然后职场身份随时间变，接着学着跟不确定共处，最后改写自我认知拓宽路。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about one's loss of a job?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It compels them to visit a clinical psychologist."},{"label":"B","text":"It offers them a chance to play different roles."},{"label":"C","text":"It renders them puzzled about who they are."},{"label":"D","text":"It forces them to redefine their life's goals."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It renders them puzzled about who they are.","answerZh":"它使人们对自己是谁感到困惑。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到'This loss provokes an identity crisis much greater than the loss of the job itself'，说明失去工作会导致人们对于自我身份的困惑，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于失业,我们从文中了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What has the author come to understand about our identity?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is crucial to our emotional wellbeing."},{"label":"B","text":"It plays a big role in many facets of life."},{"label":"C","text":"It reflects our changing status in society."},{"label":"D","text":"It is more complicated than it appears."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is more complicated than it appears.","answerZh":"它比表面看起来更复杂。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到'One of the things I have come to understand, however, is that our identity is much more complex than we recognise at first glance'，表明作者认为我们的身份比第一眼看到的要复杂得多，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于我们的身份,作者逐渐明白了什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does the passage say about our identities at work?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are essential to our self-esteem."},{"label":"B","text":"They evolve with the passage of time."},{"label":"C","text":"They overrule all other self-perceptions."},{"label":"D","text":"They are key to understanding ourselves."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They evolve with the passage of time.","answerZh":"它们会随着时间的推移而演变。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到'Our identities at work are not static. They change over time'，说明我们在工作中的身份会随着时间的推移而变化，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于我们在工作中的身份,文中说了什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What do we have to do in today's ever-changing job market?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Strive to develop our social identity."},{"label":"B","text":"Prepare for different career paths."},{"label":"C","text":"Try to be assertive at all times."},{"label":"D","text":"Learn to manage uncertainty."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Learn to manage uncertainty.","answerZh":"学会应对不确定性。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到'At each stage my ability to adapt to and develop my career identity has been crucial to my wellbeing...we have to manage uncertainty, especially in today's volatile and ever-shifting job market'，说明在不断变化的就业市场中，我们需要学会管理不确定性，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"在当今瞬息万变的就业市场中,我们必须做什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What should we do to expand our career options?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Alter our perceptions of ourselves."},{"label":"B","text":"Compare various job opportunities."},{"label":"C","text":"Look into newly emerging sectors."},{"label":"D","text":"Exercise self-discipline consciously."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Alter our perceptions of ourselves.","answerZh":"改变我们对自己的认知。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章中提到'...you can create a new experience of your identity by changing the beliefs you hold about yourself in order to expand your career options'，说明为了扩大职业选择，我们需要改变对自己的看法，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"为拓展职业选择,我们应该做什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2024_06_3-p1","title":"CET6 2024年06月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2024年06月 第3套","examDate":"2024年06月","year":"2024","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2024-06-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者认为讽刺实为伪装成幽默的敌意，既伤害听者也加深说者的敌意与不安，主张少用讽刺、改用无恶意的机智，以让自己更快乐并改善人际关系。","mainIdeaEn":"Sarcasm is hostility disguised as humor that hurts listeners and deepens the speaker's own insecurity; the author urges cutting sarcasm and using harmless wit instead to improve happiness and relationships.","answerCode":"ABBCD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说讽刺像爵士一听就懂，再让听者觉得被贬低，然后说者越发不安含敌意，接着戒掉后利己又利人，最后靠意图分清机智与讽刺。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"Why does the author say sarcasm and jazz have something surprisingly in common?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Both are recognized when heard."},{"label":"B","text":"Both have exactly the same tone."},{"label":"C","text":"Both mean the opposite of what they appear to."},{"label":"D","text":"Both have hidden in them an evident irritation."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Both are recognized when heard.","answerZh":"两者都是一听就能辨认出来。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'Sarcasm and jazz have something surprisingly in common: You know them when you hear them'，说明作者认为讽刺和爵士乐有一个共同点，那就是一听就能识别出来。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者为什么说讽刺和爵士乐有着令人意外的共同之处?"},{"number":"47","stem":"How do many people feel when they hear sarcastic comments?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They feel hostile towards the sarcastic person."},{"label":"B","text":"They feel belittled and disrespected."},{"label":"C","text":"They feel a strong urge to retaliate."},{"label":"D","text":"They feel incapable of disguising their irritation."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They feel belittled and disrespected.","answerZh":"他们感到被贬低和不受尊重。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第三段提到'Despite smiling outwardly, many people who receive sarcastic comments feel put down and often think the sarcastic person is rude, or contemptible'，说明很多人听到讽刺的评论会感到被贬低和不受尊重。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"许多人听到讽刺性评论时有什么感受?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What happens when a person consistently acts sarcastically?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They feel their dignity greatly heightened."},{"label":"B","text":"They feel increasingly insecure and hostile."},{"label":"C","text":"They endure hostility under the disguise of humor."},{"label":"D","text":"They taste bitterness even in pleasant interactions."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They feel increasingly insecure and hostile.","answerZh":"他们会越来越缺乏安全感并充满敌意。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第五段提到'when a person consistently acts sarcastically it may only serve to heighten their underlying hostility and insecurity'，说明一个人如果持续讽刺，会增强他们潜在的敌意和不安全感。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"当一个人持续表现得爱讽刺时会发生什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What does the author say about people quitting sarcastic comments?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It makes others happier and more self-confident."},{"label":"B","text":"It restrains them from being irritating and bullying."},{"label":"C","text":"It benefits not only themselves but also those around them."},{"label":"D","text":"It shields them from negative comments and outright hostility."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It benefits not only themselves but also those around them.","answerZh":"这不仅有益于他们自己，也有益于身边的人。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'when a person stops voicing negative comments, especially sarcastic ones, they may soon start to feel happier and more self-confident. Also, other people in their life benefit even more because they no longer have to hear the emotionally hurtful language of sarcasm'，说明一个人停止发表负面评论，尤其是讽刺的评论，不仅他自己会感觉更快乐和自信，他周围的人也会受益，因为他们不再需要听到情感上伤人的讽刺语言。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于人们戒掉讽刺性评论,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What is the chief difference between a speaker's wit and sarcasm?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Their clarity."},{"label":"B","text":"Their appreciation."},{"label":"C","text":"Their emphasis."},{"label":"D","text":"Their intention."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Their intention.","answerZh":"他们的意图。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'the main difference between wit and sarcasm is that, as already stated, sarcasm is often hostility disguised as humor. It can be intended to hurt and is often bitter and biting. Witty statements are usually in response to someone's unhelpful remarks or behaviors, and the intent is to untangle and clarify the issue by emphasizing its absurdities'，说明讽刺和机智的主要区别在于讽刺通常是伪装成幽默的敌意，可能故意伤人，常常苦涩尖刻。而机智的陈述通常是对某人无益的评论或行为的回应，目的是通过强调其荒谬性来解开和澄清问题。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"说话者的机智与讽刺之间的主要区别是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2024_06_3-p2","title":"CET6 2024年06月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2024年06月 第3套","examDate":"2024年06月","year":"2024","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2024-06-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章介绍变异性对学习新技能至关重要：多样化输入虽起步较慢却更利于泛化，研究者综述多领域研究探讨其类型与机制，并呼吁更多相关探索。","mainIdeaEn":"Variable practice, though slower at first, promotes better generalization in learning; researchers reviewed studies across fields to identify the types and mechanisms of variability and call for further research.","answerCode":"ADBDC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先是只见吉娃娃学狗有困难，再说哪种变异最利学习未定，然后变着练需重组记忆，接着社区大小影响认脸，最后盼激起兴趣多研究。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the passage say about infants learning the category \"dog\" if they are exposed to Chihuahuas only?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They will encounter some degree of difficulty."},{"label":"B","text":"They will try to categorise other objects first."},{"label":"C","text":"They will prefer Chihuahuas to other dog species."},{"label":"D","text":"They will imagine Chihuahuas in various conditions."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They will encounter some degree of difficulty.","answerZh":"它们会遇到一定程度的困难。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段，如果婴儿只接触到吉娃娃，他们将难以学习'狗'这一类别。因此，A选项'They will encounter some degree of difficulty.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于只接触吉娃娃的婴儿学习\"dog\"这一类别,文中说了什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does Raviv say about the four different kinds of variability?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Which of them is most relevant to the task at hand is to be confirmed."},{"label":"B","text":"Why they have an impact on learning is far from being understood."},{"label":"C","text":"Why they have never been directly compared remains a mystery."},{"label":"D","text":"Which of them is most conducive to learning is yet to be identified."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Which of them is most conducive to learning is yet to be identified.","answerZh":"四种变异性中哪一种最有利于学习尚待确定。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第五段，Raviv提到四种不同种类的变异性从未被直接比较过，这意味着我们目前不知道哪一种对学习最有效。因此，D选项'Which of them is most conducive to learning is yet to be identified.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"Raviv 对四种不同类型的可变性有何看法?"},{"number":"53","stem":"How does one of the theories explain the importance of variability for learning new skills?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Learners regard variable training as typical of what happens in the real world."},{"label":"B","text":"Learners receiving variable training are compelled to reorganise their memories."},{"label":"C","text":"Learners pay attention to the relevant aspects of a task and ignore those irrelevant."},{"label":"D","text":"Learners focus on related skills instead of wasting time and effort on unrelated ones."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Learners receiving variable training are compelled to reorganise their memories.","answerZh":"接受变异性训练的学习者不得不重组自己的记忆。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段，其中一个理论解释了变异性对学习新技能的重要性，即当训练是可变的时，学习者被迫积极重建他们的记忆。因此，B选项'Learners receiving variable training are compelled to reorganise their memories.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"其中一种理论如何解释可变性对学习新技能的重要性?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does the passage say about face recognition?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"People growing up in a small community may find it easy to remember familiar faces."},{"label":"B","text":"Face recognition has a significant impact on literally every aspect of our social lives."},{"label":"C","text":"People growing up in a large community can readily recognise any individual faces."},{"label":"D","text":"The size of the community people grow up in impacts their face recognition ability."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The size of the community people grow up in impacts their face recognition ability.","answerZh":"人们成长所在社区的规模会影响其面孔识别能力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段，Raviv解释说，人们在成长过程中所在的社区大小会影响他们的面部识别能力。因此，D选项'The size of the community people grow up in impacts their face recognition ability.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于人脸识别,文章说了什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does Raviv hope to do with their research work?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Highlight which aspects of a task are relevant and which are not to learning a skill."},{"label":"B","text":"Use the principle of variability in teaching seemingly unrelated skills in education."},{"label":"C","text":"Arouse people's interest in variability and stimulate more research on the topic."},{"label":"D","text":"Apply the principle of variability to such fields of study as the immune system."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Arouse people's interest in variability and stimulate more research on the topic.","answerZh":"唤起人们对变异性的兴趣,激发更多相关研究。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段，Raviv希望他们的研究工作能够激发人们对变异性的兴趣，并刺激更多关于该主题的研究。因此，C选项'Arouse people's interest in variability and stimulate more research on the topic.'是正确答案。","questionZh":"Raviv 希望用他们的研究工作做什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2024_12_1-p1","title":"CET6 2024年12月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2024年12月 第1套","examDate":"2024年12月","year":"2024","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2024-12-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者探讨\"恐怖悖论\"——人为何主动寻求恐怖娱乐：人类进化出在安全情境中体验负面情绪的乐趣，恐怖片让我们练习恐惧、习得应对，并获得掌控感。","mainIdeaEn":"Exploring the paradox of horror, the author argues humans evolved to enjoy experiencing negative emotions safely: horror lets us rehearse fear, develop coping strategies, and finish with a rewarding sense of mastery.","answerCode":"BBACD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先见影厅观众嗨到飞起，再懂人爱安全地吓自己，然后捉迷藏教你别当猎物，接着恐怖片练胆学应对，最后收获满满掌控感。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"The alien finds the audience in the movie theatre clearly in a state of ______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"total mindfulness"},{"label":"B","text":"extreme excitement"},{"label":"C","text":"spiritual elevation"},{"label":"D","text":"intense curiosity"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"extreme excitement","answerZh":"极度兴奋","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段描述，'They are clearly in a state of high arousal.' 以及 'They sometimes jump collectively in their seats, and emit high-pitched warning calls.' 可以判断观众处于极度兴奋的状态，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"外星人发现电影院里的观众明显处于一种什么状态?"},{"number":"47","stem":"Why do many people seek out scary entertainment, according to the author's research?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They gain experience in overcoming horror in real life."},{"label":"B","text":"They find joy in going through simulated horrible experiences."},{"label":"C","text":"They have learned from hide-and-seek as kids the thrill involved."},{"label":"D","text":"They have evolved to gain pleasure in escaping life-threatening situations."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They find joy in going through simulated horrible experiences.","answerZh":"他们从经历模拟的恐怖体验中获得乐趣。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段，'My research suggests that we humans evolved to find pleasure in situations that allow us to experience negative emotions in a safe context.' 表明人们寻求恐怖娱乐是因为在安全的环境中体验负面情绪能带来快乐，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"根据作者的研究,为什么很多人会主动寻找恐怖娱乐?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What do children learn from hide-and-seek?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"How to avoid falling prey to an attacker."},{"label":"B","text":"How to simulate a predator-prey interaction."},{"label":"C","text":"How to keep themselves from catastrophic errors."},{"label":"D","text":"How to turn a dangerous scenario into a safe one."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"How to avoid falling prey to an attacker.","answerZh":"如何避免沦为攻击者的猎物。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段，'This simulation gives the child crucial information about how to avoid becoming prey,' 明确指出孩子们从hide-and-seek游戏中学习如何避免成为猎物，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"孩子们从捉迷藏中学到了什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"Why is horror gratifying to many people?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It reminds them of an ancient set of biological defence mechanisms."},{"label":"B","text":"It triggers their imagination to travel into dangerous virtual worlds."},{"label":"C","text":"It allows them to learn what fear feels like and how to tackle it."},{"label":"D","text":"It activates their evolved fear system and their unique fantasy."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It allows them to learn what fear feels like and how to tackle it.","answerZh":"恐怖让人们得以体会恐惧的感觉并学会如何应对。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段，'Horror is pleasurable to many people because it lets us play with negative emotions and develop coping strategies. We learn what it feels like to be truly afraid, and we learn how to handle negative emotion.' 表明恐怖电影让人愉悦是因为它能让我们体验恐惧并学习如何应对，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"为什么恐怖对很多人来说是令人满足的?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What will one experience if they watch a horror film through without being hurt?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A strong sense of clear relevance."},{"label":"B","text":"A profound sense of good fortune."},{"label":"C","text":"A profound sense of intense relief."},{"label":"D","text":"A strong sense of being in control."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"A strong sense of being in control.","answerZh":"一种强烈的掌控感。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段，'If you make it through the film in one piece, you'll probably experience a strong sense of mastery, a sense that you were able to make it through an appalling experience.' 表明如果观众完整地看完恐怖电影，他们会体验到一种强烈的掌控感，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"一个人毫发无伤地看完一部恐怖片后会体验到什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2024_12_1-p2","title":"CET6 2024年12月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2024年12月 第1套","examDate":"2024年12月","year":"2024","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2024-12-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"文章指出，现实世界正在反抗不切实际的审美压力，但社交媒体却塑造并强化了新的数字审美理想，滤镜痴迷损害用户心理健康，最终需靠心理干预来解决。","mainIdeaEn":"While the physical world fights unrealistic beauty pressure, social media imposes a new digital beauty ideal; obsessive filtering harms users' mental health, requiring psychological care rather than cosmetic fixes.","answerCode":"DCACB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先是网上美由社媒说了算，再有人抗争荒谬审美压力，然后Ins脸成新理想，接着把自己当物来评判，最后要靠心理干预解瘾。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn about beauty in the digital arena?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It dictates the taste of digital media."},{"label":"B","text":"It has been in the making for years."},{"label":"C","text":"It has ushered in a new awakening."},{"label":"D","text":"It is defined by social media."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is defined by social media.","answerZh":"数字领域的美由社交媒体来定义。","explanation":"根据文章第一段'But in the digital arena, social media determines what is considered beautiful'可知，在数字领域，是社交媒体定义了什么是美。因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于数字领域中的美,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does the passage say about beauty in the physical world?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Women are under constant pressure to keep up with beauty models."},{"label":"B","text":"Women are encouraged to pursue a beauty ideal that has never existed."},{"label":"C","text":"A fight is going on to remove pressure on women to conform to an absurd beauty ideal."},{"label":"D","text":"Media outlets have begun to present as beauty models trendy women without any makeup."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"A fight is going on to remove pressure on women to conform to an absurd beauty ideal.","answerZh":"一场斗争正在进行,以消除迫使女性迎合荒谬审美理想的压力。","explanation":"根据文章第二段'In the physical world, the struggle goes against the underlying pressure exerted on women to conform to an unrealistic beauty ideal'可知，在物理世界中，斗争是为了消除对女性施加的压力，使她们不再追求不切实际的美丽理想。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于现实世界中的美,文章说了什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about the Instagram face?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is now regarded as the new beauty ideal."},{"label":"B","text":"It is what most women will go after in 2050."},{"label":"C","text":"It is being much talked about on social media."},{"label":"D","text":"It is a perfect illustration of the ultimate beauty."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is now regarded as the new beauty ideal.","answerZh":"Instagram 脸如今被视为新的审美理想。","explanation":"根据文章第四段'Today, however, the Instagram face has become the new beauty ideal'可知，Instagram脸现在被视为新的美丽理想。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于 Instagram 脸,我们可以从文章中了解到什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What has obsessive filtering resulted in?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A good many women striving to reach an impossible level of perfection."},{"label":"B","text":"An urge to turn the entire game played on the network to one's advantage."},{"label":"C","text":"A tendency to regard one's body as an object of observation and judgment."},{"label":"D","text":"An increasing number of women filtering their images before uploading them."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"A tendency to regard one's body as an object of observation and judgment.","answerZh":"一种把自己的身体当作观察和评判对象的倾向。","explanation":"根据文章倒数第二段'One of the significant consequences of obsessive filtering is the emerging tendency to treat oneself as an object to be observed and valued, in the same way another person observes and judges from the side'可知，过度过滤导致人们倾向于将自己视为被观察和评价的对象。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"过度使用滤镜导致了什么结果?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author want to emphasize at the end of the passage regarding Americans' obsession with looks?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cosmetic surgery should be made more accessible to the masses."},{"label":"B","text":"Psychological intervention should be introduced to alleviate it."},{"label":"C","text":"Their time spent on social media should be strictly controlled."},{"label":"D","text":"Its root cause should be meticulously examined and analyzed."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Psychological intervention should be introduced to alleviate it.","answerZh":"应引入心理干预来缓解这种痴迷。","explanation":"根据文章最后一段'The time spent on social media creates an urge to achieve an impossible beauty ideal so powerful that the only thing that can fix it is not cosmetic intervention, but mental health care'可知，作者强调需要心理干预来缓解美国人对外貌的迷恋。因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于美国人对外貌的痴迷,作者在文末想强调什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2024_12_2-p1","title":"CET6 2024年12月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2024年12月 第2套","examDate":"2024年12月","year":"2024","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2024-12-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"随着人口涌向城市，乡村日渐冷清；作者指出乡村生活能耗高、又受市场力量冲击，其演变不可避免，与城市相比，乡村的未来更加难以预料。","mainIdeaEn":"As people flock to cities, the countryside is emptying; the author argues rural life is energy-inefficient and constantly evolving, so change is inevitable and the countryside's future is far less clear than cities'.","answerCode":"ABDAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先见乡村人去屋空，再嫌乡下生活费能源，然后富人买房坏了保护，接着承认乡村必然变迁，最后前路比城市更难料。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What has become of the rural areas nowadays?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are becoming somewhat deserted."},{"label":"B","text":"They are being increasingly urbanised."},{"label":"C","text":"They are closely-knit communities."},{"label":"D","text":"They are haunted by conservation."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They are becoming somewhat deserted.","answerZh":"农村地区正变得有些荒凉冷清。","explanation":"第二段指出乡村居民因城市经济更好而外迁，\"leaving the countryside in desolation\"，即乡村日渐荒芜，故选A。","questionZh":"如今的乡村地区变成了什么样子?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the author think of the rural lifestyle?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is unlikely to survive given the on-going changes."},{"label":"B","text":"It is less energy-efficient compared to that in cities."},{"label":"C","text":"It is highly dependent upon heavy automobiles."},{"label":"D","text":"It is a choice more affluent people will endorse."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It is less energy-efficient compared to that in cities.","answerZh":"与城市相比,乡村生活方式的能源效率更低。","explanation":"第三段指出乡村人均碳排放高于城市，城市\"brings energy efficiency that the countryside cannot match\"，即乡村生活能效更低，故选B。","questionZh":"作者如何看待乡村生活方式?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does the author think of rich urban residents buying a second home in the countryside?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is bound to mar the traditional rural life."},{"label":"B","text":"It adversely impacts rural social stability."},{"label":"C","text":"It hinders rural economies' revitalisation."},{"label":"D","text":"It is detrimental to rural preservation."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is detrimental to rural preservation.","answerZh":"这不利于乡村的保护。","explanation":"第四段指出富人买第二套房推高房价，逼走本地居民，\"For those who believe in rural preservation, this is deplorable\"，即不利于乡村保护，故选D。","questionZh":"作者如何看待富裕的城市居民在乡下购置第二套住房?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What do we learn about the countryside with industrialisation and technological advances?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is destined to change gradually."},{"label":"B","text":"It will present an idealised way of life."},{"label":"C","text":"It is likely to embrace foreign cultures."},{"label":"D","text":"It will become increasingly diversified."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is destined to change gradually.","answerZh":"乡村注定会逐渐发生改变。","explanation":"第五段指出工业化和技术进步使乡村持续演变，\"surely an evolving countryside is inevitable\"，即乡村注定会逐渐改变，故选A。","questionZh":"随着工业化和技术进步,乡村发生了什么变化?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does the author think of the future of the countryside compared with cities?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is going to be harder for the locals."},{"label":"B","text":"It is going to resemble that of cities."},{"label":"C","text":"It is less likely to stay static."},{"label":"D","text":"It is less easy to envisage."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is less easy to envisage.","answerZh":"乡村的未来更难以预见。","explanation":"末段指出城市未来明确（成为megacities），\"but the future of the countryside is less clear\"，即乡村前景更难预料，故选D。","questionZh":"与城市相比,作者如何看待乡村的未来?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2024_12_2-p2","title":"CET6 2024年12月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2024年12月 第2套","examDate":"2024年12月","year":"2024","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2024-12-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"作者借一项审美研究质疑\"情人眼里出西施\"：人们对自然景观的审美高度一致，对人造物分歧较大，说明美可能存在普遍的客观原则，并非纯属主观。","mainIdeaEn":"Citing research showing people agree on natural beauty but diverge on artifacts, the author challenges the saying that beauty is in the eye of the beholder, suggesting general objective principles of beauty may exist.","answerCode":"ACDBC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说老话没人质疑，再发现人造物分歧大，然后因它露脸比自然少，接着夕阳处处美得相似，最后匠人手法未必都爱。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the passage say about the statement \"beauty is in the eye of the beholder\"?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has hardly ever been disputed."},{"label":"B","text":"It can be interpreted aesthetically."},{"label":"C","text":"Many people have found it absurd."},{"label":"D","text":"People have long been misled by it."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It has hardly ever been disputed.","answerZh":"这一说法几乎从未受到质疑。","explanation":"首段指出该说法\"are rarely questioned\"，几乎无人质疑，故选A。","questionZh":"关于 \"beauty is in the eye of the beholder\" 这一说法,文章说了什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does a recent study exploring aesthetic taste show?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Aesthetic tastes tend to differ from person to person."},{"label":"B","text":"Natural beauty is rarely surpassed by artificial beauty."},{"label":"C","text":"There is less consensus on objects shaped by human craft."},{"label":"D","text":"There is general agreement on what is pleasing to the eye."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"There is less consensus on objects shaped by human craft.","answerZh":"对人工制造的物品,人们的审美共识更少。","explanation":"研究显示人们对自然物审美高度一致，但\"they disagree more about artifacts, or human-made objects\"，即对人造物共识较少，故选C。","questionZh":"一项探究审美品味的最新研究表明了什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"Why do people differ in their aesthetic appraisal of artifacts?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They come out in a great variety of designs."},{"label":"B","text":"They lead to varying behavioral consequences."},{"label":"C","text":"They take up much less natural space than landscapes."},{"label":"D","text":"They come into people's view less often than natural spaces."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They come into people's view less often than natural spaces.","answerZh":"人工制品进入人们视野的频率低于自然景观。","explanation":"原文\"Art and architecture, unlike natural spaces, do not have the same level of exposure. So, people do not have the same level of shared taste\"，即人造物曝光度低，故选D。","questionZh":"为什么人们对人造物品的审美评价各不相同?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does the example of sunset tell about nature?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It creates a powerful appeal through its brilliant radiance."},{"label":"B","text":"It displays aesthetic traits in a similar way the world over."},{"label":"C","text":"It embodies beauty with a wide array of aesthetic features."},{"label":"D","text":"It establishes the principles of beauty in a number of ways."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It displays aesthetic traits in a similar way the world over.","answerZh":"自然在世界各地以相似的方式展现其审美特质。","explanation":"原文以日落为例说明\"Nature exhibits some of the universal aesthetic features... in a common way throughout the world\"，即自然在全球以相似方式呈现审美特征，故选B。","questionZh":"日落的例子说明了自然的什么特点?"},{"number":"55","stem":"Why do artifacts not always hold universal appeal?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The appreciation of their beauty is not subject to objective standards."},{"label":"B","text":"The universal principle of beauty prevents a wide array of embodiments."},{"label":"C","text":"The way their creators apply the principle of beauty may not be pleasing to everybody."},{"label":"D","text":"Their creators interpret the universal principle of beauty each in their preferred way."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"The way their creators apply the principle of beauty may not be pleasing to everybody.","answerZh":"其创作者运用美的原则的方式未必人人喜欢。","explanation":"原文\"they apply these very general concepts in unique ways. But the way they applied the principle may not have universal appeal\"，即创作者运用美的原则的方式未必人人喜爱，故选C。","questionZh":"为什么人造物品并不总能获得普遍的喜爱?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2024_12_3-p1","title":"CET6 2024年12月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2024年12月 第3套","examDate":"2024年12月","year":"2024","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2024-12-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者驳斥流行的\"左脑型/右脑型\"人格说：两半球确有分工差异，但与性格无关，神经科学界从未支持这种说法，对相关在线测试应保持怀疑。","mainIdeaEn":"The author debunks the popular left-brained versus right-brained personality myth: brain hemispheres do differ in function, but this has nothing to do with personality, and online quizzes claiming otherwise deserve deep skepticism.","answerCode":"BCAAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先见测试号称分左右脑，再看两脑协作更离奇，然后分工打破对称假设，接着左右型性格说纯属编，最后对测验多留个心眼。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do numerous personality quizzes online claim they are able to do?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Distinguish between the two hemispheres of one's brain."},{"label":"B","text":"Determine whether one is left-brained or right-brained."},{"label":"C","text":"Tell if one is more of a linguist or of a mathematician."},{"label":"D","text":"Ascertain how one's brain performs different tasks."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Determine whether one is left-brained or right-brained.","answerZh":"判定一个人是左脑型还是右脑型。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'There are hundreds of personality quizzes online that assert they can ascertain whether the right or left half of your brain is dominant'可知，众多在线性格测试声称能够判断一个人是左脑型还是右脑型，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"网上众多性格测试声称自己能做什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the author say is sometimes stranger than fiction?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"How one hemisphere of the brain impacts creativity."},{"label":"B","text":"How the two halves of our brains work alternately."},{"label":"C","text":"How the two hemispheres of our brains cooperate."},{"label":"D","text":"How one half of the brain dominates the other."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"How the two hemispheres of our brains cooperate.","answerZh":"大脑两个半球如何协同工作。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'But the actual science of how the two halves of our brains work together is sometimes stranger than fiction'可知，作者认为大脑两半球如何协同工作有时比小说还要奇异，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者说什么有时比虚构小说还离奇?"},{"number":"48","stem":"Why did many scientists have difficulty endorsing the idea that different areas of the brain do different things?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It contradicts the assumption that the two hemispheres of the brain are symmetrical."},{"label":"B","text":"It dismisses the view that the universe has been evolving in a consistent manner."},{"label":"C","text":"It is in conflict with the suggestion that the left and right halves of the brain work together."},{"label":"D","text":"It disrupts the idea that the right hemisphere of the brain controls the left side of the body."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It contradicts the assumption that the two hemispheres of the brain are symmetrical.","answerZh":"它与大脑两半球是对称的这一假设相矛盾。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第五段'But many scientists struggled with this idea, because the very suggestion that the left and right halves of the brain operate differently disrupted the idea that nature tends toward perfect symmetry'可知，许多科学家难以接受大脑左右两半球功能不同的观点，因为这打破了自然界倾向于完美对称的理念，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"为什么许多科学家难以认同大脑不同区域各司其职的观点?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What belief have neuroscientists long rejected according to the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"There are left-dominant people and right-dominant people with different personalities."},{"label":"B","text":"There are noticeable differences between the left and right hemispheres of the brain."},{"label":"C","text":"One's personality is hardly related to the different halves of the brain."},{"label":"D","text":"Different areas of the brain are responsible for different activities."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"There are left-dominant people and right-dominant people with different personalities.","answerZh":"存在左脑主导型和右脑主导型的人,且二者性格不同。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段'The idea that we have left-dominant people and right-dominant people, and that this is related to personality, is categorically false. That's never been supported in the neuroscience community'可知，神经科学家长期拒绝接受存在左脑型人和右脑型人以及这与个性有关的观点，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"根据文章,神经科学家长期以来拒绝接受什么观念?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What are we advised to do with an online quiz that tells us something about ourselves?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Challenge its authority."},{"label":"B","text":"Scrutinize its originality."},{"label":"C","text":"Evaluate its popularity."},{"label":"D","text":"Question its reliability."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Question its reliability.","answerZh":"质疑其可靠性。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'But you have to take it with an enormous grain of salt'可知，对于告诉我们关于自己的在线测试，我们应该质疑其可靠性，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"面对一个声称能揭示我们自身特点的在线测试,我们被建议怎么做?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2024_12_3-p2","title":"CET6 2024年12月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2024年12月 第3套","examDate":"2024年12月","year":"2024","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2024-12-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"亚利桑那一所中学试行多名教师共管百余学生的协作教学模式：看似混乱实则精心编排，初步研究显示它能提振教师士气与合作，尽管仍有考核等难题。","mainIdeaEn":"An Arizona high school pilots team teaching, where teachers share large groups of students; despite seeming chaotic, early results show improved teacher morale and collaboration, though challenges like evaluating individual teachers remain.","answerCode":"DBCCD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先看乱中有序的合班课，再听初步研究说有戏，然后督学叹单干拖慢进步，接着互评知道学生咋接受，最后愁咋考核每位老师。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn about team teaching from the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is generally conducted in classrooms without walls."},{"label":"B","text":"It allows students to choose teachers they favor most."},{"label":"C","text":"It prioritizes peer work over classroom instruction."},{"label":"D","text":"It is closely coordinated despite seeming confusion."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is closely coordinated despite seeming confusion.","answerZh":"尽管看似混乱,协作教学其实配合紧密。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到，尽管看起来像混乱，但实际上是一种精心策划的计划，每位老师每天都会制定针对每个学生的个性化计划。因此，D选项 'It is closely coordinated despite seeming confusion.' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于团队教学,我们可以从文章中了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does initial research suggest regarding Westwood's innovative teaching model?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It could help raise teachers' pay."},{"label":"B","text":"It could turn out to be a success."},{"label":"C","text":"It could cut down overall costs."},{"label":"D","text":"It could end up like a gamble."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It could turn out to be a success.","answerZh":"这一模式可能会取得成功。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到，初步研究显示，这种创新教学模式可能取得成功，因为参与团队教学的老师们报告了更高的工作满意度、更频繁的同事合作和更积极的与学生互动。因此，B选项 'It could turn out to be a success.' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于 Westwood 的创新教学模式,初步研究表明了什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What did superintendent Andi Fourlis say about the teaching profession?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Morale cannot be boosted until teaching models are overhauled."},{"label":"B","text":"Teachers are simply too busy to visit classes of their colleagues."},{"label":"C","text":"Progress is slow due to lack of collaboration among teachers."},{"label":"D","text":"Teachers often do fantastic things without being noticed."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Progress is slow due to lack of collaboration among teachers.","answerZh":"由于教师之间缺乏协作,进步十分缓慢。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第五段引用了Andi Fourlis的话，指出教师职业进步缓慢是因为我们在孤立中工作，意味着缺乏合作。因此，C选项 'Progress is slow due to lack of collaboration among teachers.' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"学区总监 Andi Fourlis 对教师职业说了什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does the author want to show by citing English teacher Jeff Hall's experience?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"English teachers and science teachers are complementary in performing their tasks."},{"label":"B","text":"A teacher of arts and letters is completely puzzled by what a science teacher teaches."},{"label":"C","text":"The new teaching model helps inform the teacher how their instruction is received."},{"label":"D","text":"Science teachers will hardly know the confusion they create without a performance appraisal."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"The new teaching model helps inform the teacher how their instruction is received.","answerZh":"新教学模式有助于教师了解自己的教学被学生接受的情况。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到了英语老师Jeff Hall的经历，他通过与其他老师分享绩效评估了解到自己的教学可能给学生带来的困惑。这说明新模式帮助老师了解他们的教学是如何被接受的。因此，C选项 'The new teaching model helps inform the teacher how their instruction is received.' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者引用英语教师 Jeff Hall 的经历想说明什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author think is one of the difficult problems in implementing the new teaching model?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"What to do with teachers working alone."},{"label":"B","text":"What to include in teaching schedules."},{"label":"C","text":"How to recruit volunteers for a team."},{"label":"D","text":"How to assess each teacher's performance."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"How to assess each teacher's performance.","answerZh":"如何评估每位教师的表现。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到了新模式实施中的困难问题，包括如何评估四位老师对135名学生的表现。因此，D选项 'How to assess each teacher's performance.' 是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者认为推行新教学模式的难题之一是什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2025_06_1-p1","title":"CET6 2025年06月 第1套 · Passage 1","examTitle":"CET6 2025年06月 第1套","examDate":"2025年06月","year":"2025","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2025-06-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"官方把学业差归咎于缺课，但研究者发现经准假的缺课几乎无碍学习，无故缺课主要是家庭校外危机的信号；应据此把资源投向最需要帮助的孩子。","mainIdeaEn":"Officials blame missed instruction for low achievement, but the authors find excused absences barely hurt learning; unexcused absences mainly signal family crises, so resources should go to the children who need them most.","answerCode":"CABAC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先听官方怪缺课误学业，再发现请假缺课没啥事，然后旷课暴露家中难处，接着政策迷信少缺课就好，最后把资源送给困难娃。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What does the U.S. secretary of education say in his open letter?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is of vital importance to respond promptly to the school absence crisis."},{"label":"B","text":"The academic performance of chronically absent students is deplorable."},{"label":"C","text":"Low academic achievement is mainly attributed to school absences."},{"label":"D","text":"The effect of school absences on American education is worrisome."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Low academic achievement is mainly attributed to school absences.","answerZh":"学业成绩差主要归因于缺课。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段中的'His open letter stated that missing 10% of school days in a year for any reason—excused or unexcused—is a primary cause of low academic achievement'，可以确定美国教育部长在其公开信中提到，缺课是低学术成就的主要原因，因此选项C是正确答案。","questionZh":"美国教育部长在公开信中说了什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What do the authors find about school absences?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Excused school absences have little impact on children's learning."},{"label":"B","text":"There is little difference between unexcused and excused absences."},{"label":"C","text":"Excused absences lead to comparatively better school performance."},{"label":"D","text":"Unexcused absences are a big challenge to both schools and families."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Excused school absences have little impact on children's learning.","answerZh":"经准假的缺课对孩子的学习影响很小。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'We find that absences excused by a parent do little to harm children's learning'，表明家长批准的缺课对儿童学习影响很小，因此选项A是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于学生缺课,作者们有什么发现?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What do the authors believe concerning unexcused school absences?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are likely to cause a decrease in students' academic achievements due to missed instruction."},{"label":"B","text":"They point directly to many of the out-of-school challenges confronting children and their families."},{"label":"C","text":"They are matters the American government typically ignores when formulating educational policies."},{"label":"D","text":"They give a clear signal to children and their families of the crises they are likely to face in the future."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They point directly to many of the out-of-school challenges confronting children and their families.","answerZh":"无故缺课直接反映了孩子及其家庭面临的许多校外困境。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第五段提到'unexcused absence is a strong signal of the many challenges children and families face'，表明无故缺课直接指向儿童及其家庭面临的许多挑战，因此选项B是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于无故缺课,作者们持什么看法?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What is the assumption underlying education policies in the U.S.?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Children's academic performance depends on reducing the number of absences."},{"label":"B","text":"Schools can boost children's academic performance by effective intervention."},{"label":"C","text":"Schools as well as families should be held responsible for out-of-school crises."},{"label":"D","text":"Children's academic performance is closely related to the quality of instruction."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Children's academic performance depends on reducing the number of absences.","answerZh":"孩子的学业表现取决于减少缺课次数。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'These policies assume that missing school for any reason harms children academically because they are missing classroom instruction'，表明美国教育政策的基本假设是缺课会因为错过课堂指导而损害儿童的学术表现，因此选项A是正确答案。","questionZh":"美国教育政策背后的假设是什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What do the authors suggest doing regarding school absences?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Identifying their underlying causes."},{"label":"B","text":"Reframing school attendance policies."},{"label":"C","text":"Directing resources to helping needy children."},{"label":"D","text":"Pressuring schools to reduce unexcused ones."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Directing resources to helping needy children.","answerZh":"把资源用于帮助有需要的孩子。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章最后一段提到'we suggest using unexcused absence from school as a signal to channel resources to the children and families who need them most'，表明作者建议将资源引导到最需要帮助的儿童和家庭，因此选项C是正确答案。","questionZh":"针对学生缺课问题,作者们建议怎么做?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2025_06_1-p2","title":"CET6 2025年06月 第1套 · Passage 2","examTitle":"CET6 2025年06月 第1套","examDate":"2025年06月","year":"2025","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2025-06-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"作者研究\"追随热情\"的职业信条后大为震惊：把热情变成稳定好工作需要经济与人脉支撑，盲目鼓吹它会延续社会不平等，还让雇主借机剥削热情员工。","mainIdeaEn":"Researching the popular follow-your-passion advice, the author found it perpetuates overwork and socioeconomic inequality, since turning passion into a good job takes money and connections, while employers exploit passionate workers' devotion.","answerCode":"DADCB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先劝人爱啥就干啥，再被研究结果吓一跳，然后发现要靠钱和人脉，接着不平等只会延续，最后老板白赚你的热情。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What did the author advise people to do for almost a decade?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Figure out what is the most fascinating job."},{"label":"B","text":"Follow widely accepted career counsel."},{"label":"C","text":"Pursue their careers with passion."},{"label":"D","text":"Do whatever they are zealous for."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Do whatever they are zealous for.","answerZh":"去做自己热衷的任何事情。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。第一段作者说获得学士学位后'I was determined to do what I love'（决心做自己热爱的事）；第二段'For almost a decade, I told everyone I encountered that they should do the same. \"Follow your passion,\" I counseled. \"You can figure out the employment stuff later.\"'——'do the same'即指做自己热爱的事，配上直接引语'Follow your passion'，可知作者近十年建议的核心是：追随热情、做自己热衷之事，就业问题先放一边。D项'Do whatever they are zealous for'中 zealous 意为'热情的、热衷的'，正是'follow your passion / do what I love'的对应表达，故选D。","questionZh":"近十年来作者一直建议人们做什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"How did the author feel about the passion principle through his research?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"He was astonished by its consequences."},{"label":"B","text":"He was further convinced of its soundness."},{"label":"C","text":"He was actually right to follow it through."},{"label":"D","text":"He was struck by its broad popularity."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"He was astonished by its consequences.","answerZh":"他对其带来的后果感到震惊。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段'It wasn't until I began to research this widely accepted career advice that I understood how problematic it really was.'以及第四段'I was stunned by what I found out about this principle in the research for my new book.'可知，作者通过研究发现追随热情原则的后果令人震惊，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"通过研究,作者对激情原则有何感受?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What is important to turning one's passion into a stable, good-paying job?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Willingness to take unpaid internships and low-paying jobs."},{"label":"B","text":"Full academic preparedness and sound career counseling."},{"label":"C","text":"Hard work and sacrifice of leisure time."},{"label":"D","text":"Financial backing and social connections."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Financial backing and social connections.","answerZh":"经济支持和社会人脉。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段'While the passion principle is broadly popular, not everyone has the necessary resources to turn their passion into a stable, good-paying job. Passion-seekers from wealthy families are better able to wait until a job they are passionate about comes along without worrying about student loans in the meantime. They are also better situated to take unpaid internships to get their foot in the door while their parents pay their rent. And they often have access to parents' social networks to help them find jobs.'可知，将热情转化为稳定、高薪工作的重要因素是经济支持和社会关系。","questionZh":"要把激情变成一份稳定且高薪的工作,什么是重要的?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What happens when everyone is encouraged to follow their passion?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Many more career aspirants end up unemployed."},{"label":"B","text":"People are less concerned with socioeconomic inequality."},{"label":"C","text":"Socioeconomic inequality is likely to persist."},{"label":"D","text":"Career counselors are going to lose credibility."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Socioeconomic inequality is likely to persist.","answerZh":"社会经济不平等很可能会持续存在。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。根据文章倒数第二段'Colleges, workplaces and career counselors who promote the 'follow your passion' path for everyone, without leveling the playing field, help perpetuate socioeconomic inequalities among career aspirants.'可知，鼓励所有人追随热情，而不创造公平的竞争环境，会加剧社会经济不平等。因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"当人人都被鼓励追随自己的激情时,会发生什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author say about employers of passionate workers?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They provide these workers with job stability and a good salary."},{"label":"B","text":"They exploit these workers' passion to benefit themselves."},{"label":"C","text":"They level the playing field for these workers to reach their goals."},{"label":"D","text":"They encourage these workers to realize their aspirations."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They exploit these workers' passion to benefit themselves.","answerZh":"他们利用这些员工的热情为自己谋利。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'Potential employers showed greater interest in passionate applicants in part because they believed the applicants would work hard at their jobs without expecting an increase in pay. They even sacrifice a good salary, job stability and leisure time to work in a job they love.'可知，雇主利用热情工作者的热情来为自己谋利，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于雇用充满激情员工的雇主,作者说了什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2025_06_2-p1","title":"CET6 2025年06月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2025年06月 第2套","examDate":"2025年06月","year":"2025","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2025-06-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"组织变革成功离不开员工的热情拥抱；作者论证模拟培训优于讲座：它让学员无风险地探索试验、转变行为，但学员须把所学立即用于工作才能收效最大。","mainIdeaEn":"Successful organizational change requires an enthusiastic workforce; unlike lectures, simulations let learners explore and practice risk-free to shift behavior, provided they immediately apply what they learn to real work.","answerCode":"CAADB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说变革要全员热捧，再带学员看见可能性，然后讲座改不了行为，接着模拟里无险随便练，最后学完马上用到活上。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do we learn about successful changes in organizations?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They can be immediately implemented with great ease."},{"label":"B","text":"They are usually led by organization leaders of vision."},{"label":"C","text":"They call for enthusiastic support from the workforce."},{"label":"D","text":"They often result from simulation learning experiences."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They call for enthusiastic support from the workforce.","answerZh":"成功的变革需要员工队伍的热情支持。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第二段'successful change requires more than a vision; it requires a workforce that not only doesn't resist change, but embraces it'可知，成功的变革需要员工的热情支持，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于组织中成功的变革,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What should learning leaders do to arouse learners' passion for change?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Allow them to see what could possibly be achieved."},{"label":"B","text":"Help them break free from their old paradigms."},{"label":"C","text":"Encourage them to rethink their thought models."},{"label":"D","text":"Stimulate them to embrace fresh opportunities."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Allow them to see what could possibly be achieved.","answerZh":"让学习者看到可能实现的目标。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第三段'learning leaders must expose the workforce to what could be, which will enable them to rethink their mental models'可知，学习领导者应该让员工看到可能实现的未来，以激发他们对变革的热情，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"学习负责人应该怎么做才能激发学习者对变革的热情?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does the passage say about lectures, training programs and workshops?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are generally incapable of changing workers' behaviors on the job."},{"label":"B","text":"They are interventions different from simulations in creating stimuli for change."},{"label":"C","text":"They aim at transforming the behaviors of the workers in an organization."},{"label":"D","text":"They help managers achieve the full effect of employee development efforts."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They are generally incapable of changing workers' behaviors on the job.","answerZh":"它们通常无法改变员工在工作中的行为。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第五段'Lectures, training programs and workshops can explain the intellectual elements of transformation, but they are seldom effective at getting to the behavioral aspects that lie at the heart of a significant change initiative'可知，讲座、培训项目和研讨会通常无法改变员工的在职行为，因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于讲座、培训项目和研讨会,文章说了什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What makes simulation one of the most fruitful forms of learning?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its capability of saving time by accelerating the immersive learning experience."},{"label":"B","text":"Its potential for learners to examine their skills, knowledge and learning process."},{"label":"C","text":"Its capability of providing all participants with a practical learning experience."},{"label":"D","text":"Its potential for learners to explore, experiment and practice without any risk."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Its potential for learners to explore, experiment and practice without any risk.","answerZh":"它让学习者能够毫无风险地探索、试验和练习。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第六段'The ability to explore, experiment and repeatedly apply new knowledge in unlimited, risk-free models is what makes simulation one of the most productive forms of learning'可知，模拟之所以是最有效的学习形式之一，是因为学习者可以在无风险的模型中探索、实验和反复应用新知识，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"是什么让模拟演练成为最富成效的学习形式之一?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What should participants do in a simulation to reap the greatest benefits possible?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Take the experience as a mere game."},{"label":"B","text":"Apply promptly what they learn to their jobs."},{"label":"C","text":"Develop a deep level of understanding."},{"label":"D","text":"Strive to connect closely with their leaders."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Apply promptly what they learn to their jobs.","answerZh":"把所学及时运用到工作中。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'To maximize benefits from simulation, participants should immediately apply the learning from the experience to forge a smooth link between learning and doing'可知，为了获得最大的好处，参与者应该立即将从模拟中学到的东西应用到工作中，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"参与者在模拟演练中应该怎么做才能获得最大收益?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2025_06_2-p2","title":"CET6 2025年06月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2025年06月 第2套","examDate":"2025年06月","year":"2025","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2025-06-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"作者主张GDP增长不应是政府首要目标：尽管幸福难以衡量，政府仍应创造促进民众福祉的条件，把公民本身当作目的，实现以人为本的施政。","mainIdeaEn":"GDP growth should not be governments' primary goal; despite doubts about measuring happiness, the author argues governments should create conditions for citizens' wellbeing and treat people as ends in themselves.","answerCode":"ACBDB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先提增长要可持续，再有人说幸福因人而异，然后给人人用得上的资源，接着政府仍把经济排第一，最后目标该以人为本。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the passage say is the more recent thinking of economic growth?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It should be made sustainable."},{"label":"B","text":"It is vital to the future of humanity."},{"label":"C","text":"It should be governments' chief concern."},{"label":"D","text":"It is an indicator of government performance."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It should be made sustainable.","answerZh":"经济增长应当是可持续的。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'economic thinking is moving toward the idea that we should aim for sustainability in our economic models'，表明经济增长的最新思考是使其可持续。因此A选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"文章说关于经济增长的较新观点是什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"Why are some people opposed to the idea that governments should focus on happiness?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Governments cannot impose happiness on citizens."},{"label":"B","text":"People's happiness is built upon their own endeavor."},{"label":"C","text":"Happiness means different things to different people."},{"label":"D","text":"Happiness depends on sustainable economic growth."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Happiness means different things to different people.","answerZh":"幸福对不同的人意味着不同的东西。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段提到'There are concerns about how happiness can be measured'和'people want different things'，表明不同人对幸福有不同的理解，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"为什么有些人反对政府把重心放在幸福上?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What does philosopher Julian Baggini suggest governments do in a recently published article?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Try to reduce inequality between the rich and the poor."},{"label":"B","text":"Provide people with access to resources for a better life."},{"label":"C","text":"Change people's behaviors to put social wealth to better use."},{"label":"D","text":"Make use of advanced technologies to improve people's lives."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Provide people with access to resources for a better life.","answerZh":"让人们能够获得改善生活所需的资源。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到philosopher Julian Baggini的观点'people do not need to own, but rather access things that enable them to live well'，表明他建议政府让人们能够接触到使他们生活更好的资源，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"哲学家 Julian Baggini 在最近发表的文章中建议政府做什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"Why does the WHO feel the need to appeal to the economic benefits of improving mental health to justify its recommendations?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Mental health programs cannot be executed without GDP growth."},{"label":"B","text":"Psychological interventions are conducive to people's wellbeing."},{"label":"C","text":"Poor mental health is detrimental to a nation's economic system."},{"label":"D","text":"Governments still take economic development as their priority."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Governments still take economic development as their priority.","answerZh":"各国政府仍把经济发展作为优先事项。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到'As long as the economy is their priority, governments need go no further than ensuring citizens' continued productivity'，表明只要经济是政府的优先事项，他们就不需要超出确保公民持续生产力的范围。因此WHO需要强调改善心理健康的经济利益来说服政府，所以D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"为什么世卫组织觉得需要借助改善心理健康的经济效益来论证其建议的合理性?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What message does the author try to convey at the end of the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Governments' goal should be prosperity-driven."},{"label":"B","text":"Governments' goal should be people-oriented."},{"label":"C","text":"Governments should consider citizens' views in decision-making."},{"label":"D","text":"Governments should set sustained productivity as their top priority."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Governments' goal should be people-oriented.","answerZh":"政府的目标应当以人为本。","explanation":"这是一道主旨大意题。文章最后一段提到'To demand that governments set the 'happiness of citizens' as their highest priority is to demand that they view citizens as ends in themselves'，表明作者试图传达的信息是政府应该以人民为中心，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"作者在文章结尾想传达什么信息?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2025_06_3-p1","title":"CET6 2025年06月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2025年06月 第3套","examDate":"2025年06月","year":"2025","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2025-06-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者剖析职业焦虑的心理根源——怕被势利眼以职业评判：人们追逐名利实为渴求尊重与爱；应对势利的答案是善待并好奇地看待每一个偶遇之人。","mainIdeaEn":"Career anxiety stems partly from fear of snobs who judge us by our jobs; our chase for status goods is really a hunger for respect, and the answer is kindness and curiosity toward everyone we meet.","answerCode":"ACDAB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先怕被势利眼打量，再看他们只问你干啥的，然后买豪车实为求认可，接着势利眼只敬名利双收，最后善待好奇每个路人。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What gives rise to our worry about careers apart from money?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fear of being judged in a snobbish manner."},{"label":"B","text":"The prospect of facing fault-finding managers."},{"label":"C","text":"The ruthless way employees are often treated."},{"label":"D","text":"Fright at the difficulty in hunting for a job."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Fear of being judged in a snobbish manner.","answerZh":"害怕被人以势利的眼光评判。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第一段提到'we worry because we suspect—not wrongly—that the world is full of a frightening sort of person ready to judge us ruthlessly and swiftly: a person we can call a snob'，表明我们对职业的担忧部分源于害怕被势利小人以势利的方式评判。","questionZh":"除了钱,还有什么引发我们对职业的担忧?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about today's snobs?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They try hard to dig into a person's past."},{"label":"B","text":"They draw a rigid conclusion about people."},{"label":"C","text":"They judge a person by their occupation."},{"label":"D","text":"They tend to place people in a social context."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They judge a person by their occupation.","answerZh":"他们以职业来评判一个人。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第二段明确指出'Nowadays, the snob cares about one thing only: what you do for a living'，说明当今的势利小人通过一个人的工作来评判一个人。","questionZh":"关于如今的势利者,我们可以从文章中了解到什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What does the author say about people's interest in material goods?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is the cause for condemnation of their greed."},{"label":"B","text":"It has a lot to do with the comforts they provide."},{"label":"C","text":"It arouses pity rather than respect from the wealthy."},{"label":"D","text":"It arises from their craving for social recognition."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It arises from their craving for social recognition.","answerZh":"它源于人们对社会认可的渴望。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章第四段提到'A lot of our interest in fancy cars, jobs and houses has nothing to do with materialism. It has to do with a hunger for the respect and esteem that is only available in our societies through the acquisition of material goods'，表明人们对物质商品的兴趣源于对社会认可的渴望。","questionZh":"关于人们对物质商品的兴趣,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What kind of people do snobs deem worth respect and esteem?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Those with fame and fortune."},{"label":"B","text":"Those with regimented minds."},{"label":"C","text":"Those with intelligence and imagination."},{"label":"D","text":"Those with qualities lying hidden in disguise."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Those with fame and fortune.","answerZh":"有名有钱的人。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。文章倒数第二段提到'For snobs, it is the already acclaimed and already successful who are the only ones worthy of respect'，说明势利小人认为只有已经获得赞誉和成功的人才值得尊重。","questionZh":"势利者认为什么样的人值得尊重和敬重?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does the author imply we should do to avoid being snobbish?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Be aware there has never been such a thing as a better or worse person."},{"label":"B","text":"Be kind to and curious about those who we happen to meet in our lives."},{"label":"C","text":"Realize that better or worse keeps hanging in unexpected ways."},{"label":"D","text":"Judge people on the basis of their distinctive character traits."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Be kind to and curious about those who we happen to meet in our lives.","answerZh":"善待生活中偶然相遇的人,并对他们抱有好奇心。","explanation":"这是一道推理判断题。文章最后一段提到'our ultimate duty remains to be kind, good, curious and imaginative about pretty much everyone who ever crosses our path'，暗示我们应该对遇到的每个人保持善意、好奇和想象力，以避免变得势利。","questionZh":"作者暗示我们应该怎么做才能避免势利?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2025_06_3-p2","title":"CET6 2025年06月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2025年06月 第3套","examDate":"2025年06月","year":"2025","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2025-06-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"美国性别薪酬差距在1980年代快速缩小，却因家庭休假政策出台后趋同停滞至今；研究认为生育与育儿负担是女性薪酬难以追平男性的根本原因。","mainIdeaEn":"The U.S. gender pay gap narrowed fast in the 1980s but stalled after family leave policies were introduced; ultimately, bearing and caring for children is what keeps women's pay behind men's.","answerCode":"BBCDB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先看八十年代差距猛缩，再遇休假政策趋同放缓，然后顾家耗掉时间精力，接着若延续早该同酬，最后卡在生娃带娃上。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn about the gender pay gap in the US during the 1980s?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It was being slowly closed."},{"label":"B","text":"It was shrinking rapidly."},{"label":"C","text":"It started to yawn."},{"label":"D","text":"It remained substantial."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It was shrinking rapidly.","answerZh":"当时性别薪酬差距正在迅速缩小。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第一段'During that decade, the gender pay gap closed by about one percentage point a year'可知，80年代美国性别工资差距正在快速缩小，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于 20 世纪 80 年代美国的性别薪酬差距,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What happened with the introduction of state and federal family leave policies?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The process towards salary equity at work began to reverse."},{"label":"B","text":"The rate of gender wage convergence started to fall noticeably."},{"label":"C","text":"The trend of women returning to work after childbirth started."},{"label":"D","text":"The narrowing of the gender pay gap attracted more attention."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"The rate of gender wage convergence started to fall noticeably.","answerZh":"性别工资趋同的速度开始明显下降。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章第四段'After family leave was introduced in the US, in fact, the rate of gender wage convergence fell to just 0.03 percentage points per year, and has remained there ever since'可知，家庭休假政策实施后，性别工资差距缩小的速度明显下降，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"州和联邦家庭休假政策出台后发生了什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What partly accounts for the slip in women's salaries?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The insufficient motivation women generally have for career advancement."},{"label":"B","text":"The opportunities numerous women give up for pay raise and promotion."},{"label":"C","text":"The huge amounts of time and energy women spend taking care of the family."},{"label":"D","text":"The lack of policy support from government and business corporations."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"The huge amounts of time and energy women spend taking care of the family.","answerZh":"女性照顾家庭所花费的大量时间和精力。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章倒数第二段'Part of this is because women take on more of the unpaid labor at home, which can eat into time available for work and energy for career advancement'可知，女性花费大量时间和精力在家庭无偿劳动上，是她们工资下降的部分原因，因此C选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"女性薪资下滑的部分原因是什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does the new study say about wage parity?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It would have stalled if those controllable problems had not been addressed."},{"label":"B","text":"It would have halted if company and government had not worked together."},{"label":"C","text":"It would have been achieved with the complete erasure of gender biases."},{"label":"D","text":"It would have been attained with the continuation of the 1980s trend."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It would have been attained with the continuation of the 1980s trend.","answerZh":"若 1980 年代的趋势得以延续,薪酬平等本可实现。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'if the 1980s trend continued, we would have been at parity by now'可知，如果80年代的趋势持续下去，现在应该已经实现了工资平等，因此D选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"关于薪酬平等,这项新研究说了什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What prevents women from achieving parity with men in the final analysis?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ignoring biases against women in the workplace."},{"label":"B","text":"Giving birth to children and taking care of them."},{"label":"C","text":"Failing to mandate breaks for childbirth and care."},{"label":"D","text":"Lacking resources to address biological problems."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Giving birth to children and taking care of them.","answerZh":"生育并照顾孩子。","explanation":"这是一道细节理解题。根据文章最后一段'it's also because mothers are passed over for raises and promotion, and because time out of the workplace sets women back, even if that time is taken voluntarily, and supported by company or government policy'可知，女性因为生育和抚养孩子而无法实现与男性的平等，因此B选项是正确答案。","questionZh":"归根结底,是什么阻碍女性实现与男性的平等?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2025_12_1-p1","title":"CET6 2025年12月 第1套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2025年12月 第1套","examDate":"2025年12月","year":"2025","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2025-12-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者批评推崇\"为成功舍弃朋友\"的激进个人主义文化，指出友谊是人生的锚，追求成功时更应珍视并用心维护亲密关系，而非独自打拼。","mainIdeaEn":"The author criticizes the individualist culture that normalizes losing friends on the road to success, arguing friendships are our anchors and nurturing them matters more than any achievement won alone.","answerCode":"DADBB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先见追成功冷落朋友，再劝重审个人主义之害，然后社会以为赢靠拼命，接着鸡汤喊工作别社交，最后谁都离不开好朋友。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What often happens when people are eager to pursue individual success?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They lack a shoulder to cry on."},{"label":"B","text":"They have no soul to confide in."},{"label":"C","text":"They cannot find reliable friends."},{"label":"D","text":"They ignore their ties with friends."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They ignore their ties with friends.","answerZh":"他们忽视了与朋友的联系。","explanation":"文章第一段明确指出：\"in our eagerness to seek individual success, we lose friends along the way and that has become part of the process.\" 在追求个人成功的过程中，我们失去了朋友，这说明人们忽视了与朋友的联系。D选项\"忽视与朋友的关系\"准确概括了这一现象。 - 关键句：However, more often than not, in our eagerness to seek individual success, we lose friends along the way and that has become part of the process.","questionZh":"当人们急于追求个人成功时,往往会发生什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What does the author advise people to do in their pursuit of radical individualism?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Reexamine its detrimental effects."},{"label":"B","text":"Shrug off the loss of their loved ones."},{"label":"C","text":"Avoid the chaos and turmoil involved."},{"label":"D","text":"Remove aggressive obstacles in the way."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Reexamine its detrimental effects.","answerZh":"重新审视激进个人主义的有害影响。","explanation":"第三段作者建议：\"We must reevaluate the harm of radical, individual freedom.\" reevaluate the harm意为\"重新评估其危害\"，与A选项\"重新审视其有害影响\"(reexamine its detrimental effects)含义一致。detrimental effects对应harm，reexamine对应reevaluate。 - 关键句：We must reevaluate the harm of radical, individual freedom.","questionZh":"在追求极端个人主义的过程中,作者建议人们怎么做?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What is American society's assumption of personal achievement?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is to be duly celebrated and highly commended."},{"label":"B","text":"It is a sure way to fulfill a person's dream."},{"label":"C","text":"It revolves around an individualistic culture."},{"label":"D","text":"It reflects a person's exceptional endeavor."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It reflects a person's exceptional endeavor.","answerZh":"个人成就反映了一个人非凡的努力。","explanation":"第五段指出：\"Society tends to celebrate personal achievement and commend it based on the assumption that winning or succeeding is a consequence of working harder than the next person.\" 社会的假设是成功是比别人更努力工作的结果，即个人成就反映了个人的超凡努力。D选项中的\"exceptional endeavor\"（杰出的努力）对应\"working harder than the next person\"。 - 关键句：Society tends to celebrate personal achievement and commend it based on the assumption that winning or succeeding is a consequence of working harder than the next person.","questionZh":"美国社会对个人成就的假设是什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What is preached in many success stories?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Attaching importance to academic gains on the road to success."},{"label":"B","text":"Investing one's time in work instead of connecting with friends."},{"label":"C","text":"Trying to strengthen friendships in one's pursuit of personal success."},{"label":"D","text":"Excelling in academic performance to get into a prestigious college."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Investing one's time in work instead of connecting with friends.","answerZh":"把时间投入工作,而不是用来与朋友交往。","explanation":"第六段列举了成功故事中宣扬的观点：\"Invest time in your relationships? Invest time in your work instead.\" 以及\"Spend too much time with friends? You're losing time better utilized on your achievements.\" 这些都在宣扬把时间投入工作而非维系友谊，与B选项一致。 - 关键句：Invest time in your relationships? Invest time in your work instead.","questionZh":"许多成功故事宣扬的是什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What can we infer from the passage regarding the pursuit of success?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"No one can succeed without pushing limits."},{"label":"B","text":"No one can afford to neglect close friends."},{"label":"C","text":"Collectivism is superior to individualism."},{"label":"D","text":"Success experts often lead people to ruin."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"No one can afford to neglect close friends.","answerZh":"任何人都不能忽视亲密的朋友。","explanation":"文章最后两段强调：\"We cannot be complacent with losing friendships because they are our anchors\"以及\"having people to support and love you on the way is far more important than any end result.\" 全文主旨就是不能为了追求成功而忽视友谊，因此可以推断出没有人能承受忽视亲密朋友的代价。 - 关键句：Put effort into fostering healthy relationships, and maintaining them through your busy schedule that seems like it leaves no time for anyone else.","questionZh":"关于对成功的追求,我们可以从文章中推断出什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2025_12_1-p2","title":"CET6 2025年12月 第1套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2025年12月 第1套","examDate":"2025年12月","year":"2025","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2025-12-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"作者指出美国距真正的公平仍有很长的路，种族不平等代价惨重、社会分裂加深；呼吁继承马丁·路德·金的遗志，正视问题、携手共建更包容的国家。","mainIdeaEn":"America still falls far short of true equity: racial inequity has cost dearly and divisions are deepening. Honoring Martin Luther King Jr.'s legacy, Americans must confront these issues together and build a more inclusive nation.","answerCode":"CACDB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先叹公平之路还很长，再看黑人学生上学吃亏，然后接过金博士的旗，接着国家越来越撕裂，最后携手共解公平难题。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What does the author think about today's America?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is struggling to transform fiction into reality."},{"label":"B","text":"It has been the focus of many vital conversations."},{"label":"C","text":"It still has a long way to go before equity can be truly realized."},{"label":"D","text":"It has got to a point where people disagree on nearly every issue."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It still has a long way to go before equity can be truly realized.","answerZh":"要真正实现公平,美国还有很长的路要走。","explanation":"文章第二段指出美国社会\"still struggling to separate truth from fantasy\"，并说\"the battle for equity is at the heart of these vital conversations\"。第四段进一步提到\"We're missing out on valuable opportunities to bridge the differences that divide us\"。全文主旨表明美国在实现真正公平方面仍有很长的路要走，C选项准确概括了作者的观点。 - 关键句：More than five decades later, our society is still struggling to separate truth from fantasy, fact from fiction.","questionZh":"作者如何看待今天的美国?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about black students in the past 20 years?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They have been unfairly treated regarding higher education."},{"label":"B","text":"They have been battling hard to address equity issues."},{"label":"C","text":"They have boosted their lifetime incomes by billions of dollars."},{"label":"D","text":"They have come to see the consequences of racial discrimination."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They have been unfairly treated regarding higher education.","answerZh":"他们在高等教育方面受到了不公正的对待。","explanation":"第三段引用2020年花旗报告指出：黑人学生本可以增加900-1130亿美元的终身收入，\"if equity issues related to higher education had been adequately addressed over the past two decades\"。这说明过去20年间高等教育方面的公平问题未得到充分解决，即黑人学生在高等教育方面受到了不公平对待。 - 关键句：Black students could have increased their lifetime incomes $90-$113 billion if equity issues related to higher education had been adequately addressed over the past two decades.","questionZh":"关于过去 20 年里的黑人学生,我们可以从文章中了解到什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"How can Americans bridge the differences that divide them?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"By dealing with the thorny issues confronting them."},{"label":"B","text":"By seizing every chance to enhance racial harmony."},{"label":"C","text":"By continuing to pursue Martin Luther King Jr.'s cause."},{"label":"D","text":"By striving to identify exceedingly valuable opportunities."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"By continuing to pursue Martin Luther King Jr.'s cause.","answerZh":"继续推进 Martin Luther King Jr. 的事业。","explanation":"第四段明确指出：\"by honoring King's legacy, we can get our country back on the path toward true equity.\" 通过继承马丁·路德·金的遗志，美国可以重回通往真正公平的道路。C选项\"继续追求马丁·路德·金的事业\"与原文\"honoring King's legacy\"含义一致。 - 关键句：However, by honoring King's legacy, we can get our country back on the path toward true equity.","questionZh":"美国人如何才能弥合彼此间的分歧?"},{"number":"54","stem":"How do most Americans view America as a nation according to a recent survey?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is compelled to address its historical social issues."},{"label":"B","text":"It is delaying advancements toward racial equality."},{"label":"C","text":"It has kept itself from polarization."},{"label":"D","text":"It has become increasingly split."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It has become increasingly split.","answerZh":"美国已变得日益分裂。","explanation":"第七段明确引用调查数据：\"A recent survey found that 77 percent of Americans believe the nation is 'more divided than ever before'.\" 77%的美国人认为国家比以往任何时候都更加分裂，D选项\"变得越来越分裂\"(increasingly split)准确对应\"more divided than ever before\"。 - 关键句：A recent survey found that 77 percent of Americans believe the nation is \"more divided than ever before\".","questionZh":"根据一项最新调查,大多数美国人如何看待美国这个国家?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author suggest Americans do?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ensure the wellbeing of their children and grandchildren."},{"label":"B","text":"Make joint efforts to tackle the nation's equity issues."},{"label":"C","text":"Restrain their intolerance and discrimination."},{"label":"D","text":"Restore social order for a harmonious nation."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Make joint efforts to tackle the nation's equity issues.","answerZh":"共同努力解决国家的公平问题。","explanation":"文章最后一段作者呼吁：\"let's commit to working together to disrupt the status quo. Let's continue to build a better, more inclusive nation.\" 作者建议美国人共同努力打破现状，建设一个更好、更包容的国家。B选项\"共同努力解决国家的公平问题\"准确概括了作者的建议，working together对应make joint efforts。 - 关键句：On this Martin Luther King Day and beyond, let's commit to working together to disrupt the status quo.","questionZh":"作者建议美国人怎么做?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2025_12_2-p1","title":"CET6 2025年12月 第2套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2025年12月 第2套","examDate":"2025年12月","year":"2025","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2025-12-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者阐述\"团结\"的多重面向：人类相互依存、离不开合作，团结既可能压抑个性，也是对极端个人主义的反拨，理论家视其为社会秩序与进步的关键。","mainIdeaEn":"The author explores solidarity's many facets: as interdependent beings humans need it to thrive, and despite tensions with individuality, theorists see genuine, inclusive solidarity as key to social order and progress.","answerCode":"ABCBC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说不合作难繁荣，再叹团结复杂多面，然后社群里舍小我为大家，接着反对极端个人主义，最后团结撑起秩序与进步。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What does the author say about human beings?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They cannot prosper without cooperating with each other."},{"label":"B","text":"They share a common interest and believe in a just cause."},{"label":"C","text":"They think and behave alike in different social groups."},{"label":"D","text":"They cannot gain independence without fighting for it."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They cannot prosper without cooperating with each other.","answerZh":"人类不相互合作就无法繁荣。","explanation":"文章开篇指出人类是相互依存的存在，不能脱离他人而繁荣（As interdependent beings we cannot thrive independent of others）。A选项中的cannot prosper without cooperating是对原文的同义转述。thrive对应prosper，interdependent对应cooperating with each other。 - 关键句：As interdependent beings we cannot thrive independent of others.","questionZh":"关于人类,作者说了什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What do we learn about solidarity in an increasingly diverse society?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It gives rise to a complicated division of labour."},{"label":"B","text":"It involves many aspects with great complexity."},{"label":"C","text":"It brings individuals together as environment changes."},{"label":"D","text":"It embraces the characteristics of different individuals."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It involves many aspects with great complexity.","answerZh":"团结涉及诸多方面,极为复杂。","explanation":"第四段指出在日益多元化的社会中，团结具有复杂和多面的特征（a complex and multifaceted character）。B选项中的many aspects对应multifaceted，great complexity对应complex，是原文的准确转述。 - 关键句：solidarity takes on a complex and multifaceted character as it forms bonds of interdependence among unique individuals living in a fast-changing environment and working within a complex division of labour.","questionZh":"在一个日益多元的社会里,关于团结我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What would we witness in the setting of communitarianism?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ruling of social norms and ridding of individuality."},{"label":"B","text":"Emphasis on the adherence to individual differences."},{"label":"C","text":"Sacrifice of personal interests for the common good."},{"label":"D","text":"Elimination of individualism and personal choices."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Sacrifice of personal interests for the common good.","answerZh":"为共同利益而牺牲个人利益。","explanation":"第五段明确指出，在社群主义的背景下，个人放弃自己的利益来服务于公共利益（individuals give up their own interests to serve the common good）。C选项是对这句话的直接转述，sacrifice对应give up，personal interests对应own interests。 - 关键句：In this setting, individuals give up their own interests to serve the common good.","questionZh":"在社群主义的环境中,我们会看到什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What does solidarity entail according to the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A limit to personal differences."},{"label":"B","text":"An opposition to individualism."},{"label":"C","text":"A hindrance to social advancement."},{"label":"D","text":"An inevitable end to liberal pursuits."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"An opposition to individualism.","answerZh":"对个人主义的反对。","explanation":"第六段指出团结也被视为对极端个人主义和选择自由的过度强调的一种回应（a reaction to the extreme emphasis on individualism）。它反对不受约束的个人将社会视为自由障碍的自由主义观点。B选项中的opposition to individualism准确概括了这一含义。 - 关键句：Solidarity is also viewed as a reaction to the extreme emphasis on individualism and freedom of choice.","questionZh":"根据文章,团结意味着什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What do social theorists think of solidarity?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is especially relevant to the most vulnerable."},{"label":"B","text":"It is most effective in protecting human dignity."},{"label":"C","text":"It is essential to progress and order in society."},{"label":"D","text":"It is indispensable to avoiding shallow relationships."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It is essential to progress and order in society.","answerZh":"团结对社会的进步与秩序至关重要。","explanation":"最后一段开头明确指出社会理论家将团结视为带来社会秩序和进步的关键因素（a key factor in bringing about order and progress in society）。C选项中essential to progress and order是对原文key factor in bringing about order and progress的同义转述。 - 关键句：social theorists have viewed solidarity as a key factor in bringing about order and progress in society.","questionZh":"社会理论家如何看待团结?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2025_12_2-p2","title":"CET6 2025年12月 第2套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2025年12月 第2套","examDate":"2025年12月","year":"2025","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2025-12-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"爱给人不请自来建议的人往往出于权力欲和情感脆弱；作者建议接受者不要严厉拒绝，而应体谅对方动机、温和设界，才能避免冲突并获得情绪安全。","mainIdeaEn":"People who give unwanted advice often crave power and are emotionally fragile; rather than rejecting them harshly, the author advises validating their intent and setting gentle boundaries to avoid conflict.","answerCode":"DBDAC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先看建议狂多爱权力，再知他们内心脆弱，然后你想骂他控制欲，接着他把拒绝当威胁，最后先懂他为何爱支招。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What is the finding of one study about people who keep giving unsolicited advice?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They turn out to be well-meaning."},{"label":"B","text":"They are genuinely kind-hearted."},{"label":"C","text":"They are capable of influencing others."},{"label":"D","text":"They are inclined to crave for power."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They are inclined to crave for power.","answerZh":"他们往往渴望权力。","explanation":"第一段提到一项研究发现，那些有强烈寻求权力倾向的人更可能给出建议（people with a high tendency to seek power were more likely to give advice）。D选项中的inclined to crave for power对应原文的high tendency to seek power。 - 关键句：One study found that people with a high tendency to seek power were more likely to give advice than those with an opposite tendency.","questionZh":"关于总爱主动提建议的人,一项研究有什么发现?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What is the problem with people who are driven to give you unsolicited advice?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They may be quick to upset others."},{"label":"B","text":"They may be emotionally vulnerable."},{"label":"C","text":"They want their voice to be the loudest."},{"label":"D","text":"They respond to discomfort excessively."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They may be emotionally vulnerable.","answerZh":"他们可能在情感上很脆弱。","explanation":"第三段指出这些人可能表现出一种有问题的情感脆弱程度（a problematic degree of emotional vulnerability），很快就会变得不安，且需要很长时间才能平静下来。B选项直接对应原文的emotional vulnerability。 - 关键句：These people may also display a problematic degree of emotional vulnerability, becoming upset very quickly, and taking a long time to calm down.","questionZh":"那些热衷于向你提供不请自来的建议的人有什么问题?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What is the advice receiver tempted to do when noticing the advice giver's underlying anxiety?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Reveal the undesirable result of their approach."},{"label":"B","text":"Refuse their advice in an undisguised manner."},{"label":"C","text":"Bring their real motives to the surface."},{"label":"D","text":"Accuse them of trying to control others."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Accuse them of trying to control others.","answerZh":"指责对方企图控制别人。","explanation":"第四段指出，当建议接收者注意到建议者的潜在焦虑时，很容易会对建议者做出严厉回应并指责他们具有操控性（accuse them of being manipulative）。D选项中的accuse them of trying to control others是对being manipulative的同义转述。 - 关键句：It can be tempting in this situation to react harshly to the advice giver and to accuse them of being manipulative","questionZh":"当察觉到建议者潜在的焦虑时,接受建议的一方会忍不住想做什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"How is the advice giver likely to react to the rejection of their advice?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They may regard it as a threat."},{"label":"B","text":"They may modify their behavior."},{"label":"C","text":"They get ready for a larger conflict."},{"label":"D","text":"They begin to doubt their self-worth."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They may regard it as a threat.","answerZh":"他们可能把拒绝视为一种威胁。","explanation":"第五段指出，如果给建议这个行为积极地支撑着某人的自我价值感，那么直接拒绝可能被视为一种威胁（an outright rejection may be perceived as a threat）。A选项中的regard it as a threat直接对应原文的perceived as a threat。 - 关键句：an outright rejection may be perceived as a threat, activating their fight-or-flight response","questionZh":"建议被拒绝后,建议者可能作何反应?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What should the advice receiver do to avoid unnecessary conflict?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Concede the advice is perfectly reasonable."},{"label":"B","text":"Give their reasons for not taking the advice."},{"label":"C","text":"Understand why the advice giver offers the advice."},{"label":"D","text":"Explain their chosen way of handling the situation."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Understand why the advice giver offers the advice.","answerZh":"理解建议者为何要提出建议。","explanation":"文章最后一段指出，最好以考虑到对方行为背后原因的方式来设定边界（takes into account the individual's underlying reasons for doing what they are doing），以避免不必要的冲突。C选项中的understand why对应takes into account the underlying reasons。 - 关键句：It is best to set boundaries in a way that takes into account the individual's underlying reasons for doing what they are doing to avoid unnecessary conflict and more stress.","questionZh":"为避免不必要的冲突,接受建议的一方应该怎么做?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2025_12_3-p1","title":"CET6 2025年12月 第3套 · Passage One","examTitle":"CET6 2025年12月 第3套","examDate":"2025年12月","year":"2025","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2025-12-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"正念让人不加评判地专注当下，能对抗把注意力当商品的\"注意力经济\"；作者提倡把正念用于他人——放下手机、不评判地专注倾听，改善人际关系。","mainIdeaEn":"Mindfulness, attending to the present without judgment, helps us resist the attention economy's constant distractions; practiced toward others through fully attentive, nonjudgmental listening, it becomes a precious gift that strengthens relationships.","answerCode":"BBACC","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先学不评判专注当下，再看注意力被买卖，然后手机总拽人离开此刻，接着正念帮你处好关系，最后专心倾听忍住不评判。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about practicing mindfulness?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It triggers our mind to reflect on past experiences or anticipate future events."},{"label":"B","text":"It focuses our attention on the present moment without making judgments."},{"label":"C","text":"It concentrates our mind on our personal feelings, happy or scary."},{"label":"D","text":"It helps our mind to stay calm when facing judgments from others."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It focuses our attention on the present moment without making judgments.","answerZh":"正念让我们不加评判地把注意力集中在当下。","explanation":"文章第二、三段指出正念的核心是观察体验而不被卷入其中，不以喜恶或好坏来评判，从而更全面地活在当下。B选项\"专注当下且不做评判\"准确概括了正念练习的要义。A选项说触发回忆或预想未来事件，恰恰是正念要避免的；C选项说集中注意个人感受，缩小了正念的范围；D选项说面对他人评判时保持冷静，原文未提及。 - 关键句：This practice of mindfulness can help calm the mind and the body as we learn not to react to experience with likes and dislikes or judgments of good and bad.","questionZh":"关于练习正念,我们可以从文章中了解到什么?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What do we see in today's \"attention economy\" according to Jenny Odell?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Focus on technological advances continuously updates products and services."},{"label":"B","text":"People's attention is turned into something that can be bought and sold."},{"label":"C","text":"Businesses profit from selling mobile phones and revolutionizing social media."},{"label":"D","text":"People tend to purchase products and services without careful thinking."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"People's attention is turned into something that can be bought and sold.","answerZh":"人们的注意力被变成了可以买卖的东西。","explanation":"第四段引用Jenny Odell的观点，指出在\"注意力经济\"中，人类注意力已被转化为一种大企业买卖的商品。B选项\"人们的注意力被变成可以买卖的东西\"是对原文的准确转述。A选项讨论技术更新产品，偏离主题；C选项说企业从卖手机和革新社媒中获利，曲解了原文；D选项说人们不经思考就购物，原文未涉及。 - 关键句：The artist Jenny Odell argues that in our \"attention economy\" human attention has been transformed into a commodity that big corporations buy and sell.","questionZh":"根据 Jenny Odell 的说法,在如今的 \"attention economy\" 中我们看到了什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What happens with the prevalent use of mobile phones or social media?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They keep distracting users from the here and now."},{"label":"B","text":"They render users incapable of resisting temptation."},{"label":"C","text":"They rob users of their ability to observe experience."},{"label":"D","text":"They tempt users to endorse the attention economy."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They keep distracting users from the here and now.","answerZh":"它们不断使用户从当下分心。","explanation":"第五段指出大多数人使用的设备是对当下时刻的持续干扰，结果是我们专注和活在当下的能力似乎被偷走了。A选项\"它们不断使用户从此时此刻分心\"准确概括了这一影响。B选项说无法抵抗诱惑，过度引申；C选项说剥夺观察体验的能力，原文说的是专注能力；D选项说诱使用户支持注意力经济，原文未提及。 - 关键句：The devices most people use are a perpetual diversion from the present moment.","questionZh":"随着手机或社交媒体的普遍使用,发生了什么?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What benefit can practicing mindfulness bring to us according to some scholars?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It prevents us from making arbitrary judgments about others."},{"label":"B","text":"It shifts our attention from material things to spiritual pursuits."},{"label":"C","text":"It is conducive to our forging better interpersonal relationships."},{"label":"D","text":"It is helpful in regaining our ability to enjoy what we have in life."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It is conducive to our forging better interpersonal relationships.","answerZh":"它有助于我们建立更好的人际关系。","explanation":"第六段指出一些学者认为我们不仅可以为自己练习正念，还可以为他人练习，这有助于建立更强健的人际关系。C选项\"有助于建立更好的人际关系\"直接对应原文。A选项说防止对他人做武断判断，虽有关联但不是原文强调的主要益处；B选项说将注意力从物质转向精神追求，原文未提及；D选项说重获享受生活的能力，也并非此处论述重点。 - 关键句：It can help us build stronger, healthier relationships.","questionZh":"一些学者认为练习正念能给我们带来什么益处?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does the author suggest we do in another person's presence?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Share each other's experience frankly and compassionately."},{"label":"B","text":"Pay full attention to establishing close relationships with them."},{"label":"C","text":"Be attentive listeners while refraining from making judgments."},{"label":"D","text":"Remind them of the distraction from mobile phones and social media."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Be attentive listeners while refraining from making judgments.","answerZh":"专心倾听,同时克制自己不作评判。","explanation":"第八段指出正念的礼物是带着同情心倾听他人描述其经历，要放下手机、关掉社媒，全神贯注地倾听而不做评判，也不要让互动围绕自己展开。C选项\"做专注的倾听者，同时不做评判\"最为准确。A选项说坦诚分享经历，原文强调的是倾听而非分享；B选项说全神贯注建立亲密关系，扭曲了原文含义；D选项说提醒他们手机和社媒的干扰，原文是对自己的要求而非提醒他人。 - 关键句：It means practicing being fully present in another person's presence and listening to them with complete attention without judgment, while resisting the urge to make the interaction about you.","questionZh":"作者建议我们在与他人相处时怎么做?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2025_12_3-p2","title":"CET6 2025年12月 第3套 · Passage Two","examTitle":"CET6 2025年12月 第3套","examDate":"2025年12月","year":"2025","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2025-12-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"作者由验证码测试引出反思：数字技术已反客为主，把人当作实现自身目的的工具，而人类如温水中的青蛙，可能无法及时意识到这种危险。","mainIdeaEn":"Starting from a Captcha that made him do unpaid labeling work, the author argues digital technology now uses humans as means to its own ends, and like boiling frogs we may not wake up in time.","answerCode":"DCBAD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先乖乖点图过验证，再惊测机器的反测人类，然后温水青蛙浑然不觉，接着科技拿人当工具使，最后怕我们醒来已太迟。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"How did the author respond to the Captcha test?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"He clicked on the cells randomly."},{"label":"B","text":"He accepted the challenge readily."},{"label":"C","text":"He completed it confidently."},{"label":"D","text":"He worked on it submissively."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"He worked on it submissively.","answerZh":"他顺从地完成了测试。","explanation":"第二段描述作者面对验证码时虽然有些恼怒（a bit irritated），但还是像绵羊一样照做了（Like a lamb, I complied）。\"Like a lamb\"比喻顺从地服从，D选项\"顺从地完成\"最为准确。A选项说随机点击，与原文矛盾；B选项说欣然接受挑战，忽略了作者的不情愿；C选项说自信地完成，原文未体现自信。 - 关键句：Like a lamb, I complied.","questionZh":"作者对 Captcha 测试作何反应?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What is ironic about the Captcha test?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A machine can respond to the test as well as humans do."},{"label":"B","text":"A machine can outperform humans in object identification."},{"label":"C","text":"A test designed to test machines is now used by machines to test humans."},{"label":"D","text":"A test conceived to tell a human from a robot can now do tricks humans can't."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"A test designed to test machines is now used by machines to test humans.","answerZh":"一个原本用来测试机器的测试,如今被机器用来测试人类。","explanation":"第四段解释了验证码被称为\"自动图灵测试\"的讽刺之处：图灵测试最初是让人类判断机器能否像人一样回应，而现在验证码却是机器让人类做把戏来证明自己是人。C选项\"一个设计来测试机器的测试现在被机器用来测试人类\"准确概括了这一讽刺。A选项说机器能像人一样回应测试，偏离主题；B选项说机器识别物体比人强，原文未提及；D选项说测试能做人类做不到的把戏，曲解原文。 - 关键句：So we have wandered into a world in which machines make us do tricks to prove that we are humans!","questionZh":"Captcha 测试的讽刺之处是什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"Why does the author use the metaphor of the boiling frog?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"To show that humans are unwilling to trade convenience for control by smart tech."},{"label":"B","text":"To show that humans are unaware of the potential danger brought by smart tech."},{"label":"C","text":"To question whether humans are conditioned to accept digital tech."},{"label":"D","text":"To question whether humans are as vulnerable as the boiling frog."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"To show that humans are unaware of the potential danger brought by smart tech.","answerZh":"为了说明人类没有意识到智能技术带来的潜在危险。","explanation":"第五段用\"温水煮蛙\"的比喻来说明人类可能已被数字技术悄然影响而不自知。作者提问\"我们是否已被微妙地驯化以至于看不到发生在自己身上的事？\"B选项\"表明人类没有意识到智能技术带来的潜在危险\"最为准确。A选项说人类不愿用便利换取被控制，与原文意思相反（人们恰恰在不知不觉中这样做了）；C选项只是部分表述；D选项把人类与青蛙做简单类比，缺乏对比喻深层含义的理解。 - 关键句：Have we become so subtly conditioned by digital technology that we don't see what's been happening to us?","questionZh":"作者为什么使用温水煮青蛙的比喻?"},{"number":"54","stem":"Why does the author think that Brett Frischmann and Evan Selinger are right?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A large part of digital tech is now making use of humans to meet its own ends."},{"label":"B","text":"Humans are now fast locked in a race against digital tech to control the world."},{"label":"C","text":"Digital tech can serve human needs in ways previously thought impossible."},{"label":"D","text":"Digital tech is now doing thinking while humans are doing repetitive work."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"A large part of digital tech is now making use of humans to meet its own ends.","answerZh":"很大一部分数字技术如今正在利用人类来达成自身目的。","explanation":"第七段作者解释说相当大比例的数字技术现在把人类当作实现其目的的手段，而这些目的并非我们的目的，把我们变成了在跑步轮上跑的快乐老鼠。A选项\"大部分数字技术正在利用人类来满足自己的目的\"准确对应原文。B选项说人类与数字技术竞争控制世界，原文未提及；C选项说数字技术以不可思议的方式服务人类需求，与原文观点相反；D选项说数字技术在思考而人类做重复劳动，过度简化了原文。 - 关键句：A significant proportion of digital tech now sees (and uses) humans as means to ends that are not ours.","questionZh":"作者为什么认为 Brett Frischmann 和 Evan Selinger 是对的?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What does the author imply by asking \"Are we smart enough to jump out before it's too late?\" at the end of the passage?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is not sensible to expect digital tech to take humans' interest to heart."},{"label":"B","text":"It is hard to say whether technology or humans will get the upper hand."},{"label":"C","text":"We may have to search the web to get the answer to the question."},{"label":"D","text":"We may not awake in time to the danger digital tech poses to us."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"We may not awake in time to the danger digital tech poses to us.","answerZh":"我们可能无法及时觉醒,意识到数字技术对我们构成的危险。","explanation":"文章末尾作者问\"我们是否足够聪明能在为时已晚之前跳出来？\"紧接着说\"你甚至不用谷歌搜索就知道答案\"，暗示答案是否定的。结合\"温水煮蛙\"的比喻，作者暗示我们可能无法及时醒悟数字技术对我们构成的危险。D选项\"我们可能无法及时警醒数字技术对我们的危害\"最为准确。 - 关键句：Are we smart enough to jump out before it's too late? You don't even have to Google it to know the answer.","questionZh":"作者在文末问 \"Are we smart enough to jump out before it's too late?\" 意在暗示什么?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2026_06_1-p1","title":"CET6 2026年06月 第1套 · Passage 1","examTitle":"CET6 2026年06月 第1套","examDate":"2026年06月","year":"2026","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2026-06-01-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者认为禁止青少年使用社交媒体不现实，但其与少女抑郁的关联不容低估，呼吁尽快监管数字巨头，同时不应忽视教育医疗投入不足等其他诱因。","mainIdeaEn":"Banning teens from social media is unrealistic, but its link to girls' depression must be taken seriously; the author urges overdue regulation of tech giants while noting other pressures also fuel youth depression.","answerCode":"ABCDA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说一刀切禁网行不通，再指越刷越易抑郁，然后强调发现别小看，接着嫌限时新规太简单，最后别忘学校医疗缺钱。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What does the author believe regarding social media?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"To stop children using it is unrealistic and inadvisable."},{"label":"B","text":"It helps both adults and children to organise their lives."},{"label":"C","text":"It poses problems to both parents and children."},{"label":"D","text":"A world without it is really hard to imagine."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"To stop children using it is unrealistic and inadvisable.","answerZh":"禁止孩子使用社交媒体既不现实也不可取。","explanation":"细节理解题。第一段指出儿童使用社交媒体是问题'但并不意味着应当禁止'，并称设想一个青少年被禁止使用相关平台的世界'既不现实也不可取（neither practical nor desirable）'，与 A（阻止儿童使用既不现实也不可取）一致。 - 关键句：it is neither practical nor desirable to imagine a world in which teenagers are prevented from accessing the platforms...","questionZh":"关于社交媒体,作者持什么看法?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about British teenage girls?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The more frequently they interact on social media, the more they experience harassment."},{"label":"B","text":"The more time they spend on social media, the more likely they suffer from depression."},{"label":"C","text":"Most of them are engaged on social media for at least three hours a day."},{"label":"D","text":"They spend half as many hours on social media as British teenage boys."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"The more time they spend on social media, the more likely they suffer from depression.","answerZh":"她们花在社交媒体上的时间越多,患抑郁的可能性就越大。","explanation":"细节理解题。第二段指出英国少女的高抑郁率'is closely correlated to time spent on social media'，即在社交媒体上花的时间越多越可能抑郁，与 B 一致。 - 关键句：the alarmingly high rate of depression in British teenage girls is closely correlated to time spent on social media","questionZh":"关于英国十几岁的女孩,我们可以从文章中了解到什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What is the author's view on the research finding about British teenage girls?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its implications about online abuse are obvious."},{"label":"B","text":"Its key message calls for immediate attention."},{"label":"C","text":"Its importance should not be undervalued."},{"label":"D","text":"Its uncertainty should not go unnoticed."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Its importance should not be undervalued.","answerZh":"这一发现的重要性不应被低估。","explanation":"观点态度题。第三段指出尽管研究未证明因果，但'the importance of the finding that there is a connection should not be underestimated'，与 C（其重要性不应被低估）几乎同义。 - 关键句：the importance of the finding that there is a connection should not be underestimated","questionZh":"作者如何看待关于英国少女的这项研究发现?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What do experts think of health secretary Matt Hancock's idea?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its implementation requires prompt action."},{"label":"B","text":"It is a welcome initiative but is long overdue."},{"label":"C","text":"Its success depends on how it is implemented."},{"label":"D","text":"It is too simplistic to produce the desired effect."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It is too simplistic to produce the desired effect.","answerZh":"这一想法过于简单化,难以产生预期效果。","explanation":"细节理解题。第四段说该想法优点在于'simplicity'，但'some experts question its effects'并呼吁更多区分，认为上网时间本身不坏、关键在于做什么，即专家认为它过于简单、难以奏效，与 D 一致。 - 关键句：some experts question its effects and call for a greater degree of differentiation","questionZh":"专家们如何看待卫生大臣 Matt Hancock 的想法?"},{"number":"50","stem":"Besides social media companies, what factors contribute to young people's psychological health problems?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Poorly financed schools and health services."},{"label":"B","text":"Politicians' eagerness to divert public attention."},{"label":"C","text":"Bad statutory regulation of digital media giants."},{"label":"D","text":"Their parents' educational background and life."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Poorly financed schools and health services.","answerZh":"经费不足的学校和医疗卫生服务。","explanation":"细节理解题。末段指出社交媒体公司并非万恶之源，年轻人抑郁上升还有其他原因，其中提到政客借此转移人们对'inadequately resourced schools and health services'的注意力，即资源不足的学校与医疗服务也是相关因素，与 A 一致。 - 关键句：politicians keen to divert attention from inadequately resourced schools and health services","questionZh":"除社交媒体公司外,还有哪些因素导致了年轻人的心理健康问题?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2026_06_1-p2","title":"CET6 2026年06月 第1套 · Passage 2","examTitle":"CET6 2026年06月 第1套","examDate":"2026年06月","year":"2026","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2026-06-01-02","mainIdeaZh":"尽管G20曾承诺打击跨国公司利用避税天堂，利润转移问题反而愈演愈烈；作者认为设立全球最低企业税才是治本之策，但美国不配合使问题难以解决。","mainIdeaEn":"Despite the G-20's pledge, corporate profit-shifting to tax havens has only worsened; the author argues a global minimum corporate tax would end it, but U.S. noncooperation keeps the problem alive.","answerCode":"CBADD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说协议没管住避税，再怪美国政策太宽松，然后各国只会慢慢减税，接着开出全球最低税药方，最后美国不干问题拖着。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn about the G-20's agreement on curbing the use of tax havens?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has aggravated the problem in non-G-20 countries."},{"label":"B","text":"It has taken a toll on countries such as Cayman Islands."},{"label":"C","text":"It has failed to achieve the expected outcome."},{"label":"D","text":"It has failed to result in any long-term plan."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"It has failed to achieve the expected outcome.","answerZh":"该协议未能达到预期效果。","explanation":"细节推断题。第一、二段指出 G-20 曾同意打击避税天堂并制定了计划，但'instead of reining in the use of tax havens... the problem has only gotten worse'，说明协议未达到预期效果，与 C 一致。 - 关键句：instead of reining in the use of tax havens... the problem has only gotten worse.","questionZh":"关于 G-20 遏制利用避税天堂的协议,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What mainly accounted for the large increase in the world's biggest multinational corporations' shift of profits to tax havens?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fluctuating tax rates globally."},{"label":"B","text":"Lenient policies of the U.S."},{"label":"C","text":"Heavy taxes imposed on them."},{"label":"D","text":"Rapid growth of their business."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Lenient policies of the U.S.","answerZh":"美国的宽松政策。","explanation":"细节理解题。第四段指出大幅增长的主要原因是80年代避税产业的兴起，以及'U.S. policies that made it easier to shift profits'，即美国的宽松政策，与 B 一致。 - 关键句：U.S. policies that made it easier to shift profits from high-tax countries to tax havens.","questionZh":"全球最大跨国公司向避税天堂转移利润大幅增加,主要原因是什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What have policymakers been doing to prevent government tax loss?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Reducing corporate taxes step by step."},{"label":"B","text":"Scrapping consumption taxes gradually."},{"label":"C","text":"Making joint efforts to levy corporate taxes."},{"label":"D","text":"Adjusting global effective corporate tax rates."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Reducing corporate taxes step by step.","answerZh":"逐步降低企业税。","explanation":"细节理解题。第六段指出世界一直'by cutting or scrapping corporate taxes in a very gradual way'来试图解决问题，即逐步削减企业税，与 A 一致。 - 关键句：the world as a whole has been trying to solve this problem by cutting or scrapping corporate taxes in a very gradual way.","questionZh":"为防止政府税收流失,政策制定者一直在做什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does the author say would bring tax havens to an end?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The alignment of corporate taxes with consumption taxes."},{"label":"B","text":"The implementation of generous tax rates in all countries."},{"label":"C","text":"The agreement on the root cause of global profit-shifting."},{"label":"D","text":"The imposition of a global minimum corporate tax rate."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The imposition of a global minimum corporate tax rate.","answerZh":"征收全球最低企业税率。","explanation":"细节理解题。第七段指出若各国能就'a global minimum corporate tax rate'达成一致，利润转移问题将基本消失，'as tax havens would simply cease to exist'，即全球最低企业税率会终结避税天堂，与 D 一致。 - 关键句：If countries could agree on a global minimum corporate tax rate... as tax havens would simply cease to exist.","questionZh":"作者说什么会让避税天堂走向终结?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What could be expected of the global problem of profit-shifting in the near future?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It would be solved with more countries cutting tax rates."},{"label":"B","text":"It would end with governments' awareness of its severity."},{"label":"C","text":"It would cease to exist with worldwide corporate support."},{"label":"D","text":"It would continue because of noncooperation from the U.S."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"It would continue because of noncooperation from the U.S.","answerZh":"由于美国不合作,这一问题将继续存在。","explanation":"推断题。第八段指出130多个国家已签署最低税率机制、即将实施，但'The U.S. has notably not been able to pass this legislation'，末段强调改革的必要性，暗示美国不合作会使利润转移问题继续存在，与 D 一致。 - 关键句：The U.S. has notably not been able to pass this legislation.","questionZh":"在不久的将来,利润转移这一全球性问题可能会怎样?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2026_06_2-p1","title":"CET6 2026年06月 第2套 · Passage 1","examTitle":"CET6 2026年06月 第2套","examDate":"2026年06月","year":"2026","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2026-06-02-01","mainIdeaZh":"作者指出你对自律本质的看法决定自律表现：把自律当会耗尽的资源它就会衰减，把它当越用越强的力量并像肌肉一样锻炼，意志力就会不断增强。","mainIdeaEn":"Your mindset about self-discipline shapes how much you have: viewing willpower as self-replenishing rather than depletable, and exercising it like a muscle, makes it grow stronger with each act of persistence.","answerCode":"CABCD","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先看你怎么看自律，再提旧论说越用越亏，然后忆往昔证明自补可行，接着咬牙把活干下去，最后自律如肌肉越练越壮。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"What plays an important role in determining how much self-discipline people experience?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Their belief about the nature of motivation."},{"label":"B","text":"Their use of internal energy for persisting."},{"label":"C","text":"Their conception of self-discipline."},{"label":"D","text":"Their ability to resist temptation."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Their conception of self-discipline.","answerZh":"他们对自律的认知。","explanation":"细节理解题。第二段问人们如何看待'自身自律的本质'，第三段紧接着说'Your answer matters, as it determines how much self-discipline you experience'，即人们对自律的看法/观念决定其拥有多少自律，与 C（他们对自律的观念）一致。 - 关键句：Your answer matters, as it determines how much self-discipline you experience.","questionZh":"什么在很大程度上决定了人们感受到的自律程度?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What did years of research suggest about self-discipline?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is a depletable resource."},{"label":"B","text":"It is bolstered through use."},{"label":"C","text":"Its strength is dependent on willpower."},{"label":"D","text":"Its exercise is an exhausting experience."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It is a depletable resource.","answerZh":"自律是一种会被耗尽的资源。","explanation":"细节理解题。第三段指出多年来心理学研究把自控视为'a resource that is depleted with use and needs to be restored through breaks'，即一种可耗尽的资源，与 A 一致。 - 关键句：research in psychology pointed to self-control as a resource that is depleted with use","questionZh":"多年的研究对自律给出了什么结论?"},{"number":"48","stem":"Why does the author ask us to reflect on our experience of meeting the goal despite initial difficulty?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"To show the urgency of abandoning outdated beliefs about self-control."},{"label":"B","text":"To show the feasibility of viewing self-discipline as a force fueling itself."},{"label":"C","text":"To support the argument for persistence in workplace accomplishments."},{"label":"D","text":"To add evidence to consistent findings in previous psychological research."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"To show the feasibility of viewing self-discipline as a force fueling itself.","answerZh":"为了说明把自律视为一种自我补给的力量是可行的。","explanation":"写作意图题。第四段让读者回想起初困难却最终坚持完成的经历，并说'you've already had such an experience, so you've shown that it's possible'，意在证明把自律视为一种自我供给的力量是可行的，与 B 一致。 - 关键句：you've already had such an experience, so you've shown that it's possible.","questionZh":"作者为什么让我们回想那些起初艰难但最终达成目标的经历?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What are we advised to do if we cannot afford to take breaks to recharge?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Figure out what has gone wrong."},{"label":"B","text":"Focus on the hardest part of our task."},{"label":"C","text":"Exert ourselves to go on with the work."},{"label":"D","text":"Gather new energy from people around."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Exert ourselves to go on with the work.","answerZh":"努力坚持把工作做下去。","explanation":"细节理解题。第五段指出如果负担不起休息，就应'focus on gathering more energy at this point rather than focusing on how difficult it is to continue'，即振作精神、继续工作，与 C 一致。 - 关键句：focus on gathering more energy at this point rather than focusing on how difficult it is to continue","questionZh":"如果我们没有条件通过休息来恢复精力,我们被建议怎么做?"},{"number":"50","stem":"Why does the author compare our self-discipline to a muscle?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The more it is applied, the more resistance it encounters."},{"label":"B","text":"The more it is exerted, the more proud we become."},{"label":"C","text":"The more it is enforced, the stronger our willpower proves."},{"label":"D","text":"The more it is exercised, the more strengthened it gets."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"The more it is exercised, the more strengthened it gets.","answerZh":"自律越锻炼就越强大。","explanation":"推断题。末段将自律比作肌肉，指出每次抵制诱惑或坚持任务'you strengthen that muscle, leading to less effort and resistance in similar instances in the future'，即越锻炼越强，与 D 一致。 - 关键句：Your self-discipline is akin to a muscle... you strengthen that muscle, leading to less effort and resistance","questionZh":"作者为什么把我们的自律比作肌肉?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2026_06_2-p2","title":"CET6 2026年06月 第2套 · Passage 2","examTitle":"CET6 2026年06月 第2套","examDate":"2026年06月","year":"2026","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2026-06-02-02","mainIdeaZh":"智能手机和社交媒体给青少年家长带来挑战：过度使用损害孩子心理健康，作者结合自身经历指出，如今父母必须同时警惕现实与网络两个世界的危险。","mainIdeaEn":"Smartphones and social media pose real challenges for parents of teens: excessive use fuels anxiety, depression and loneliness, and parents must now guard against dangers in both the real and online worlds.","answerCode":"CBDBA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先愁孩子看不良内容，再叹刷屏越刷越孤单，然后作者心情很纠结，接着影星怕屏幕里未知，最后现实网络两头都要防。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do around half of parents of teens do according to a new study?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They set their kids' phones to filter out obscene information."},{"label":"B","text":"They try to alleviate the spread of explicit scenes on the internet."},{"label":"C","text":"They feel concerned about their kids' viewing indecent content online."},{"label":"D","text":"They strive to prevent their kids from spending excessive screen time."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They feel concerned about their kids' viewing indecent content online.","answerZh":"他们担心孩子在网上浏览不良内容。","explanation":"细节理解题。第二段指出新研究表明约一半父母'are worried about their teens being exposed to explicit content online'，即担心孩子在网上接触露骨内容，与 C（担心孩子在网上观看不雅内容）一致。 - 关键句：about half of parents of teens are worried about their teens being exposed to explicit content online.","questionZh":"一项新研究显示,约半数青少年的父母在做什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What does a large amount of research show about teens' excessive smartphone use?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It allows them less time for meaningful activities."},{"label":"B","text":"It renders them more lonely and low-spirited."},{"label":"C","text":"It gives them less time for social interactions."},{"label":"D","text":"It makes them more alert to online bullying."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It renders them more lonely and low-spirited.","answerZh":"这使他们更加孤独和情绪低落。","explanation":"细节理解题。第五段指出'Ample research shows too much smartphone use produces significant anxiety, depression, and feelings of isolation in teens'，depression 对应 low-spirited，isolation 对应 lonely，与 B 一致。 - 关键句：too much smartphone use produces significant anxiety, depression, and feelings of isolation in teens.","questionZh":"关于青少年过度使用智能手机,大量研究表明了什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What do we learn about the author's feelings regarding smartphones and screen time?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are deep-seated."},{"label":"B","text":"They are instinctive."},{"label":"C","text":"They are unique."},{"label":"D","text":"They are mixed."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"They are mixed.","answerZh":"作者的感受是复杂的。","explanation":"观点态度题。第六段作者一方面想把孩子手机扔进湖里、为屏幕时间较劲，另一方面又承认通讯的便利、理解这种成瘾、坦言自己也在与过度使用作斗争，情感复杂矛盾，与 D（复杂/矛盾的）一致。 - 关键句：The convenience of communication... often feels like it isn't worth the battle... I understand the addiction... I too, struggle with overuse.","questionZh":"关于智能手机和屏幕时间,作者的感受如何?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What does actress Kate Winslet think about the world of social media?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It poses increasing challenges to parents trying to ensure internet safety."},{"label":"B","text":"It scares parents because they don't really know what is on the screen."},{"label":"C","text":"It is a sphere difficult for parents and their teens to navigate."},{"label":"D","text":"It is full of uncertainties frightful to parents and their teens."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It scares parents because they don't really know what is on the screen.","answerZh":"它让父母害怕,因为他们并不真正知道屏幕上有什么。","explanation":"细节理解题。第七段中 Winslet 说'the world of social media is frightening to parents because we don't really know what's there'，即令父母害怕是因为不了解其中有什么，与 B 一致。 - 关键句：the world of social media is frightening to parents because we don't really know what's there","questionZh":"女演员 Kate Winslet 如何看待社交媒体的世界?"},{"number":"55","stem":"What message does the author try to convey in the last paragraph?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Parents have to be concerned about dangers to their teens in both real and virtual worlds."},{"label":"B","text":"Governments have responsibilities in regulating social media and teens' smartphone use."},{"label":"C","text":"Parents should provide guidance to their teens in the use of social media."},{"label":"D","text":"Online dangers are as serious as problems with teenagers' mental health."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Parents have to be concerned about dangers to their teens in both real and virtual worlds.","answerZh":"父母必须同时关注现实世界和虚拟世界中孩子面临的危险。","explanation":"主旨题。末段指出如今父母'don't just have to worry about real-world dangers, but all the ones sneaking online'，即既要担心现实世界的危险，也要担心潜藏于网络的危险，与 A 一致。 - 关键句：parents don't just have to worry about real-world dangers, but all the ones sneaking online","questionZh":"作者在最后一段想传达什么信息?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2026_06_3-p1","title":"CET6 2026年06月 第3套 · Passage 1","examTitle":"CET6 2026年06月 第3套","examDate":"2026年06月","year":"2026","passageLabel":"Passage One","passageNumber":1,"sortKey":"2026-06-03-01","mainIdeaZh":"三位艺术家起诉AI绘图公司未经许可用受版权保护的作品训练模型；作者指出支持者搬出\"合理使用\"辩护，但该条款因个案而异，未必适用本案。","mainIdeaEn":"Artists are suing text-to-image AI companies for training on copyrighted works without consent; while supporters invoke fair use, the author notes this doctrine applies case by case and may not cover the lawsuit.","answerCode":"BCDCB","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先告侵权讨说法，再叹画家没饭吃，然后气AI偷懒抄近道，接着挺派搬出合理使用，最后合理使用未必管用。","questions":[{"number":"46","stem":"Why have three artists brought a lawsuit against Stability AI, DeviantArt, and Midjourney?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They claim that the use of the Stable Diffusion tool is a violation of law."},{"label":"B","text":"They claim these companies infringed their intellectual property rights."},{"label":"C","text":"They want to stop the use of all AI tools in the creation of art works."},{"label":"D","text":"They want to prevent artists from being compelled to rely on AI tools."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"They claim these companies infringed their intellectual property rights.","answerZh":"他们声称这些公司侵犯了其知识产权。","explanation":"细节理解题。首段与第二段指出艺术家起诉是因为这些 AI 工具'infringed the rights of thousands of artists'，且在数十亿张受版权保护的图像上训练'without compensation or consent'，即侵犯了艺术家的知识产权，与 B 一致。 - 关键句：alleging that the text-to-image AI tools have infringed the rights of thousands of artists","questionZh":"三位艺术家为什么起诉 Stability AI、DeviantArt 和 Midjourney?"},{"number":"47","stem":"What will happen if Stable Diffusion and similar products are allowed to continue to operate as they do now, according to the law firm?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Intellectual property laws will be hard to enforce."},{"label":"B","text":"Fewer artists will invest talent in artistic creation."},{"label":"C","text":"Artists will lose their means of subsistence."},{"label":"D","text":"Copied works will flood the art market."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Artists will lose their means of subsistence.","answerZh":"艺术家们将失去谋生手段。","explanation":"细节理解题。第四段律所指出可预见结果是这些产品'will replace the very artists'，并'eliminate \"artist\" as a viable career path'（让“艺术家”这一职业道路消失），即艺术家将失去谋生手段，与 C 一致。 - 关键句：they will eliminate 'artist' as a viable career path","questionZh":"据该律师事务所称,如果允许 Stable Diffusion 及类似产品照现在这样继续运营,会发生什么?"},{"number":"48","stem":"What makes artists furious aside from copyright infringement?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Art works produced with AI tools are not banned from art-sharing platforms."},{"label":"B","text":"Text-to-image generators have won such great popularity in the past year."},{"label":"C","text":"Their distorted signatures appear more and more frequently in AI art."},{"label":"D","text":"AI tools can bypass the considerable labor involved in creating art works."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"AI tools can bypass the considerable labor involved in creating art works.","answerZh":"AI 工具可以绕过创作艺术作品所需的大量劳动。","explanation":"细节理解题。第六段指出艺术家除对版权侵犯愤怒外，还'frustrated by how AI tools are able to sidestep the labor and art processes'（AI 工具能绕过他们必须经历的劳动与创作过程），与 D 一致。 - 关键句：they have also been frustrated by how AI tools are able to sidestep the labor and art processes they are required to go through","questionZh":"除版权侵权外,还有什么让艺术家们愤怒?"},{"number":"49","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about many AI enthusiasts?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They look forward to AI tools creating good-quality art works."},{"label":"B","text":"They claim artists can use copyrighted materials just as teachers do."},{"label":"C","text":"They support AI's limited use of copyrighted images without permission."},{"label":"D","text":"They wish the \"fair use\" clause would be applicable to all works in a dataset."}],"answer":"C","answerText":"They support AI's limited use of copyrighted images without permission.","answerZh":"他们支持 AI 在未经许可的情况下有限度地使用受版权保护的图像。","explanation":"细节理解题。第八段指出科技爱好者以'fair use'条款为依据，认为该工具可使用受版权保护的图像；而'合理使用'允许在未经许可下对版权材料进行有限度使用，即他们支持 AI 未经许可地有限度使用版权图像，与 C 一致。 - 关键句：using the \"fair use\" clause as the basis for why copyrighted images could be used by the tool","questionZh":"关于许多 AI 爱好者,我们可以从文章中了解到什么?"},{"number":"50","stem":"What does the author think of the \"fair use\" clause in copyright law?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It may determine the final verdict of the case."},{"label":"B","text":"It may not apply to the present legal case."},{"label":"C","text":"It does not cover the works of all artists."},{"label":"D","text":"It is subject to different interpretations."}],"answer":"B","answerText":"It may not apply to the present legal case.","answerZh":"它可能不适用于当前这起法律案件。","explanation":"观点态度题。末段指出'fair use applies differently to each case'，且'it's hard to make a blanket statement about all works in a dataset as being applicable'，暗示合理使用未必适用于本案这种整批数据的情形，与 B 一致。 - 关键句：since fair use applies differently to each case, it's hard to make a blanket statement about all works in a dataset as being applicable","questionZh":"作者如何看待版权法中的 \"fair use\" 条款?"}]},{"id":"cet6_2026_06_3-p2","title":"CET6 2026年06月 第3套 · Passage 2","examTitle":"CET6 2026年06月 第3套","examDate":"2026年06月","year":"2026","passageLabel":"Passage Two","passageNumber":2,"sortKey":"2026-06-03-02","mainIdeaZh":"撒哈拉以南非洲电力供应不可靠制约经济发展，政府主导的电气化收效甚微；作者主张借助私营部门快速大规模建设现代电网，释放非洲经济潜力。","mainIdeaEn":"Unreliable electricity holds back sub-Saharan Africa's economy; since government-led electrification has fallen short, the author argues partnering with the fast-growing private sector is key to rapidly building modern grids at scale.","answerCode":"AADDA","answerMnemonic":"小剧场：先说缺电拖累经济，再叹官办电网不给力，然后要快建大电网，接着政府拉私企合伙，最后私企有钱赚才肯干。","questions":[{"number":"51","stem":"What do we learn about the current electric supply system in Africa?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It curbs the economic development of the continent."},{"label":"B","text":"It mainly depends on the polluting diesel generators."},{"label":"C","text":"It is the primary cause of inequitable distribution of wealth."},{"label":"D","text":"It deprives many Africans of the opportunity to use computers."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"It curbs the economic development of the continent.","answerZh":"它制约着非洲大陆的经济发展。","explanation":"细节理解题。第二段指出'The current system keeps a lid on the economic talents of people like Agok'，且首段称不公平的能源获取'put their livelihood and future at risk'，即现行供电体系抑制了非洲的经济发展，与 A 一致。 - 关键句：The current system keeps a lid on the economic talents of people like Agok and his students.","questionZh":"关于非洲目前的电力供应系统,我们可以了解到什么?"},{"number":"52","stem":"What do we learn from the passage about Africa's past electrification efforts?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They have failed to meet most Africans' need of a reliable power supply."},{"label":"B","text":"They have failed to build a national grid to provide electric power."},{"label":"C","text":"They have unleashed the true economic potential of the continent."},{"label":"D","text":"They have aimed at wiring Africa with clean, dependable energy."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"They have failed to meet most Africans' need of a reliable power supply.","answerZh":"这些努力未能满足大多数非洲人对可靠电力供应的需求。","explanation":"细节理解题。第三段指出各国政府主导电气化，但'fewer than half of the people surveyed say that the national grid is providing a reliable supply of electricity'，即过去的努力未能为多数非洲人提供可靠电力，与 A 一致。 - 关键句：fewer than half of the people surveyed say that the national grid is providing a reliable supply of electricity","questionZh":"关于非洲过去的电气化努力,我们可以从文章中了解到什么?"},{"number":"53","stem":"What is essential to tackling the power supply shortage in Africa?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Replacing temporary solutions with long-term strategies."},{"label":"B","text":"Accelerating economic growth with sustainable policies."},{"label":"C","text":"Restructuring national power generation companies."},{"label":"D","text":"Putting in place a large-scale modern power grid speedily."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Putting in place a large-scale modern power grid speedily.","answerZh":"迅速建成大规模的现代化电网。","explanation":"细节理解题。第四段指出'Deploying modern grid infrastructure with speed and at scale is essential'，即快速、大规模地部署现代电网基础设施是关键，与 D 一致。 - 关键句：Deploying modern grid infrastructure with speed and at scale is essential to replacing these temporary solutions","questionZh":"解决非洲电力供应短缺的关键是什么?"},{"number":"54","stem":"What are many governments in Africa doing to solve the electricity supply problem?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Focusing on building world-class infrastructures."},{"label":"B","text":"Relying on the private sector for scale economy."},{"label":"C","text":"Launching sustainable business models."},{"label":"D","text":"Cooperating with private companies."}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Cooperating with private companies.","answerZh":"与私营企业合作。","explanation":"细节理解题。第五、六段指出许多政府'have begun to embrace the private sector as partners'，且'governments are increasingly turning to private partners'，即与私营企业合作，与 D 一致。 - 关键句：many governments agree and have begun to embrace the private sector as partners in providing reliable power at scale","questionZh":"为解决电力供应问题,非洲许多政府正在做什么?"},{"number":"55","stem":"Why will private companies be motivated to join the effort of electrifying sub-Saharan Africa?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"There is big money to be made."},{"label":"B","text":"They have enough funding in place."},{"label":"C","text":"South Africa has set a successful example."},{"label":"D","text":"Governments are turning to them for help."}],"answer":"A","answerText":"There is big money to be made.","answerZh":"其中有丰厚的利润可赚。","explanation":"细节理解题。第七段指出'electrifying sub-Saharan Africa is a $350 billion opportunity'（为撒哈拉以南非洲通电是一个价值3500亿美元的商机），即有巨额利润可赚，是私营企业的动力所在，与 A 一致。 - 关键句：electrifying sub-Saharan Africa is a $350 billion opportunity","questionZh":"为什么私营企业会有动力参与撒哈拉以南非洲的电气化事业?"}]}];
